nes, vestiges of the island''s first farmers, and attests to human occupation linked to the exploitation of the fertile lands at the mouth of the Liamone River [2] [3]. A rock shelter on the site was also used as a tomb and contained metalwork dating from the early Iron Age [2] [5].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234461", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234462", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
