r its ancient stone millstones, vestiges of the island''s first farmers, and attests to human occupation linked to the exploitation of the fertile lands at the mouth of the Liamone River [2] [3]. A rock shelter on the site was also used as a tomb and contained metalwork dating from the early Iron Age [2] [5].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234461", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234462", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0011452e-b306-49d7-92a2-4044cf1ca5ec'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:0011452e-b306-49d7-92a2-4044cf1ca5ec:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Pedra das Cabras', '44e6bed794211ed375c143b3747c04ac', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Petroglyphs'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 5 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32963", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0010:chunk-0001: description \"Pedra das Cabras (Stone of the Goats) is a Bronze Age petroglyph located near Figueirido in the municipality of Ribeira, in the Barbanza region of Galicia, Spain. Over 4,000 years old, the engravings on a large granite rock depict two animals resembling deer, each carved with six legs rather than four -- an artistic choice believed to represent the figures in motion. The site is one of Galicia''s notable examples of open-air prehistoric rock art from the Metal Age.\" -> ''The Stone of the Goats (Galician: Pedra das Cabras) is a petroglyph located in a pine forest near the village of Figueirido, in the Barbanza Region of Galicia [1]. The zoomorphic motifs are scratched into the side of a large solitary rock and depict two animals, possibly goats [1]. Each animal has six legs, which might have been a deliberate choice to represent movement in the figures [1]. The engravings have been tentatively dated to the Neolithic [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83056", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26c_fields-wd1-s001: period_nam