cavations have recovered over 2,200 flint tools from Mousterian and Gravettian periods, a braided mat of natural fibres dated to 6,500 years ago (the oldest in Italy), and Neolithic paintings discovered in 1955. Artifacts are displayed at the Museo Civico Archeologico in Bisceglie.'' -> ''A major 1955 discovery yielded a Neanderthal femur [1] [2]. Artifacts are displayed at the Museo Civico Archeologico in Bisceglie [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304598", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/010a33fa/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/010a33fa/Grotta_Santa_Croce_Bisceglie_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/010a33fa/Grotta_Santa_Croce_Bisceglie_01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/010a33fa/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/010a33fa/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/010a33fa/Grotta_Santa_Croce_Bisceglie_01.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
