ians believe the caves were carved during the time of Emperor Ashoka. A later Hindu shrine to Goddess Tulja was built in one of the abandoned caves, giving the site its current name.'' -> ''The caves belong to the Hinayana phase of Buddhism [1]. The most notable feature is a circular chaitya hall with twelve octagonal pillars surrounding a central stupa, topped by a dome [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234470", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234471", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-50''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304607", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0185cd5a/Tulja Budhhist Caves Junnar Pune (1) 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0185cd5a/Tulja_Caves_from_distant_(_Pratik_Butte_Patil_).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305817", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0185cd5a/Tulja_Caves_from_distant_(_Pratik_Butte_Patil_).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0185cd5a/Tulja Budhhist Caves Junnar Pune (1) 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306693", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0185cd5a/Tulja Budhhist Caves Junnar Pune (1) 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0185cd5a/Tulja_Caves_from_distant_(_Pratik_Butte_Patil_).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
