s the full transition from Paleolithic hunter-gatherers to Neolithic farmers, with domesticated plants and animals appearing around 7,000 BC [1] [2]. Finds include stone tools, pottery, and Mesolithic child burials now displayed in the Nafplion Archaeological Museum [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304616", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/01b50bc7/Franchthi_Cave_from_Koilada_Argolidas.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/01b50bc7/014Σπήλαιο_Φράχθι_Ερμιονίδας.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/01b50bc7/014Σπήλαιο_Φράχθι_Ερμιονίδας.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/01b50bc7/Franchthi_Cave_from_Koilada_Argolidas.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306702", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/01b50bc7/Franchthi_Cave_from_Koilada_Argolidas.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/01b50bc7/014Σπήλαιο_Φράχθι_Ερμιονίδας.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
