s, storage pits, fire pits, ivory ornaments, and a schematic map carved on a mammoth tusk -- the oldest known map from Ukraine. Reconstructed dwellings are displayed at museums in Kyiv and New York.'' -> ''Mezhyrich is an Upper Palaeolithic site in Cherkasy Oblast, central Ukraine, famous for four mammoth-bone dwellings dating to approximately 18,200-17,400 years ago [1] [2]. The structures measure 12-24 square metres each and were built from hundreds of mammoth bones and tusks as shelters from extreme cold [1] [3]. Excavations by Ivan Pidoplichko (1966-74) and later teams uncovered flint and bone tools, storage pits, fire pits, ivory ornaments, and a schematic map carved on a mammoth tusk [1] [2]. Reconstructed dwellings are displayed at museums in Kyiv and New York [2] [4] [5].''"}]'::jsonb),
