co that served as a Roman military fort (castrum) [1] [2]. It was one of five forts that protected the city of Volubilis from incursions over the Limes Africanus frontier [1] [2]. The fort housed the Cohors IV Gallorum equitata, an auxiliary unit recruited from Gaul [1] [3] [4]. Roman control of the region ended following the Crisis of the Third Century, when internal instability weakened imperial authority in North Africa [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234477", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234478", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''101''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('01ef71b0-4942-486e-bb0e-f13fffd9ebda'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '9', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:01ef71b0-4942-486e-bb0e-f13fffd9ebda:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''7'' restored on Pikestones', '4e44371ade80a6344e6363ad04c0a6bd', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 9 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 5 content link(s), 2 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81558", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2036:chunk-0001: description ''Pikestones is the remains of a Neolithic burial cairn on Anglezarke moor in Lancashire, England. The site measures approximately 45\\u202fm (150\\u202fft) long and 18\\u202fm (60\\u202fft) wide, with a single burial chamber built from large upright slabs capped by two lintels, forming a chamber about 4.5\\u202fm long, 0.9\\u202fm wide and 0.9\\u202fm high, originally covered by a massive stone and turf mound. The cairn is aligned almost exactly north‑south, with the burial chamber situated beneath the wider northern end. A double wall at the northern edge curves inward to form a forecourt entrance.'' -> ''Pikestones is the remains of a Neolithic Burial Cairn, located on Anglezarke moor in Lancashire [1]. The site is approximately 150 feet long and 60 feet across at its widest point [1]. It consisted of one burial chamber constructed of large upright slabs, capped by two lintel slabs, forming a chamber of 15 feet long, 3 feet wide and 3 feet high, covered by a huge mound of stones and turves [1]. The cairn was aligned almost exactly North-South, with the burial chamber under the wider northern end [1]. Today the cairn has been badly robbed and the main features are the five large gritstone slabs, the remains of the burial chamber [1]. Pikestones is the earliest man-made structure in the area and only one other chambered tomb has been found in Lancashire [1]. The monument must have taken an immense amount of labour to construct and like most long barrows was erected in a prominent position, located on a ridge at a height of just over 900 feet [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92413", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141972", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/Pikestones_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1892027.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245565", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245566", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/01ef71b0/Pikestones - geograph.org.uk - 1892027.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
