" -> \"The Tomb of Tin Hinan is a monumental Berber mausoleum on a hilltop near the oasis of Abalessa in the Hoggar Mountains, southern Algeria [1] [2]. First opened by Byron Khun de Prorok in 1925, excavators found a female skeleton adorned with seven silver bracelets on one arm and seven gold on the other [2]. The tomb is attributed to Tin Hinan (''she of the tents'') [1] [3].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338654", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-06-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/021307e1/Tin Hinan Tomb 13.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
