haeological excavations have been conducted since 1995 by Sapienza University of Rome.\" -> \"Elaiussa Sebaste is an ancient Cilician city founded in the 2nd century BC on a small island near present-day Ayas, 55 km from Mersin on Turkey''s Mediterranean coast [1]. The ruins include a 2nd-century AD theatre, an agora with lion-shaped monumental fountains, baths with mosaic floors, a Corinthian-columned pagan temple, and a Byzantine church [1] [2]. Its necropolis on a northern hill preserves approximately 100 monumental tombs and sarcophagi, the richest in ancient Cilicia [1] [3]. Archaeological excavations have been conducted since 1995 [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304628", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0255f640/Elaiussa_Sebaste_Aqueduct_2015_6700_panorama.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0255f640/Elaiussa_Sebaste_Theatre_1302.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305838", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0255f640/Elaiussa_Sebaste_Theatre_1302.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0255f640/Elaiussa_Sebaste_Aqueduct_2015_6700_panorama.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306714", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0255f640/Elaiussa_Sebaste_Aqueduct_2015_6700_panorama.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0255f640/Elaiussa_Sebaste_Theatre_1302.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355556", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
