e the sophistication of Roman hydraulic engineering within Toletum, which during the Imperial era featured large public works including bath buildings and two aqueducts.'' -> ''Located beneath Calle Nuncio Viejo, these Roman vaults consist of a system of walls and barrel vaults dating to the Roman era according to archaeological studies [1] [2]. They sit near two of the city\\''s most important Roman remains: the Roman baths and cisterns of the water distribution network [3] [4]. Restored and enhanced by the Toledo Consortium by April 2008, they are now accessible to visitors through the \"Unknown Heritage\" (Patrimonio Desconocido) guided routes programme [1] [5] [6].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245576", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346236", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346237", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0294d74b-0e97-4509-913a-475e3c21e1a7'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:0294d74b-0e97-4509-913a-475e3c21e1a7:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''9'' restored on Punic Building, Żurrieq', '57d824b0cc9b9a33a24331ce01068577', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Minaret/tower'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0011:chunk-0001: description ''The Punic building in Zurrieq is the most substantial surviving example of Phoenician-Punic architecture in Malta, featuring a 5.5 m-high tower of ashlar limestone blocks laid without mortar, crowned by an Egyptian-style cavetto cornice. Possibly dating to the late 6th century BC, its purpose remains debated -- theories include a monumental tomb, or the temple of Melqart described by Ptolemy. A 1964 excavation revealed stepped foundations and pottery spanning Punic to modern periods. Scheduled as a Class A archaeological site in 1998, it sits within the private garden of the Domus Curialis.'' -> \"The remains of an unidentified Punic building exist incorporated into several properties in Żurrieq, Malta [1]. They include a well-preserved structure commonly known as the Punic Tower or the Żurrieq Tower which is found inside the private garden of the Domus Curialis, the house of the town''s archpriest [1]. The site consists of a well-preserved 5.6 m-high tower with a square plan topped by a cavetto cornice showing inspiration from ancient Egyptian architecture, along with some adjacent walls which are believed to have originally formed part of a larger building [1]. Both the tower and the walls are constructed out of ashlar limestone masonry without mortar, with each block having dimensions of up to 66 cm × 180 cm [1]. The building''s age and purpose are not known, but it might date back to around the late 6th century BC [1]. The building is not believed to have been a defensive tower [1]. The building''s existence was first recorded by Bishop Miguel Jerónimo de Molina in 1680 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92431", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92432", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92433", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Minaret/tower''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141985", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Misra%C4%A7_ir-Repubblika_%28%C5%BBurrieq%29_01.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Punic building, Żurrieq 02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234486", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-600''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304637", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Punic building, Żurrieq 02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Misraħ_ir-Repubblika_(Żurrieq)_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305847", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Misraħ_ir-Repubblika_(Żurrieq)_01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Punic building, Żurrieq 02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306723", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Punic building, Żurrieq 02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Misraħ_ir-Repubblika_(Żurrieq)_01.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
