ure, along with some adjacent walls which are believed to have originally formed part of a larger building [1]. Both the tower and the walls are constructed out of ashlar limestone masonry without mortar, with each block having dimensions of up to 66 cm × 180 cm [1]. The building''s age and purpose are not known, but it might date back to around the late 6th century BC [1]. The building is not believed to have been a defensive tower [1]. The building''s existence was first recorded by Bishop Miguel Jerónimo de Molina in 1680 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92431", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92432", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92433", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Minaret/tower''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141985", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5e/Misra%C4%A7_ir-Repubblika_%28%C5%BBurrieq%29_01.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Punic building, Żurrieq 02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234486", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-600''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304637", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Punic building, Żurrieq 02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0294d74b/Misraħ_ir-Repubblika_(Żurrieq)_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305847", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-h