alia [1]. It has been described as \"gender-bending\" and \"showing that the social roles depicted by these standardized iconographies were more fluid than previously thought\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92434", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92435", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234487", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234488", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-2700''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-06-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/02a9d200/IGLESIA DE SAN JOSE DE CAPELLANIA (2).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
