 inhabitants of both villages, which had disputed a water source.'' -> ''Yanaque-Quilcamarca is an archaeological complex of two adjacent hilltop settlements at 3,820 meters elevation in Ancash Region, Peru (Ocros Province, Acas District) [1] [2]. Stone structures with clay mortar span from summit to slopes, featuring rectangular and semicircular forms reaching up to 2 meters in height [2]. According to local legend, a woman called Pichanamaria swept through the streets with a broom, causing an illness that killed the inhabitants of both villages, which had disputed a water source [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234493", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: site_type None -> ''Village''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245579", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245580", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346238", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346239", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
