the existence of a late prehistoric settlement beneath the town, dating from the mid-2nd to early 1st millennium BCE [1]. Pliny the Elder is the earliest European writer to mention Adulis [1]. Adulis is also mentioned in the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea, a guide of the Red Sea and the Indian Ocean [1]. Adulis was one of the first Axumite sites to undergo excavation, when a French mission to Eritrea under Vignaud and Petit performed an initial survey in 1840, and prepared a map which marked the location of three structures they believed were temples [1]. The first scientific excavations at Adulis were undertaken in 1906, under the supervision of Richard Sundström [1]. Sundström worked in the northern sector of the site, exposing a large structure, which he dubbed the \"palace of Adulis\", as well as recovering some examples of Axumite coinage [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84145", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: lat ''15.273933181644413'' -> ''15.2636''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: lon ''39.69111438105472'' -> ''39.6606''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84147", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141994", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0349db41/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0349db41/ADOULIS Canal Sud détail.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304649", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0349db41/ADOULIS Canal Sud détail.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0349db41/Byzantine_Basilica_(8527948107).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305859", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url