    ('057ed947-18f5-45f5-b4c6-6bc1e29264d7'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:057ed947-18f5-45f5-b4c6-6bc1e29264d7:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''6'' restored on Dinedor Camp', 'eee82aa747491cd25a0f3638a0e62d94', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 7 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 0 content link(s), 3 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2001:chunk-0001: description ''Dinedor Camp is an Iron Age univallate hillfort on a spur of Dinedor Hill, about 3 km south of Hereford, overlooking the confluence of the Wye and Lugg rivers. The sub-rectangular enclosure measures approximately 337 m long by 160 m wide, enclosing around 9.5 acres. Its rampart averages 3 m high, increasing to nearly 7 m at the northeast, with stone revetments on both faces and a quarry ditch. Excavations revealed permanent, dense occupation immediately behind the rampart, with Iron Age pottery and evidence dating the latest phase to the 2nd century BC. The site is a scheduled monument and was transferred to Dinedor Parish Council as a community asset in 2016.'' -> ''Dinedor Camp is an Iron Age hillfort, about 1 kilometre west of the village of Dinedor and about 3 kilometres south of Hereford in England [1]. The fort is on a spur of Dinedor Hill; it overlooks to the east the River Wye at the confluence with the River Lugg [1]. It is about 337 metres long and 160 metres wide, enclosing an area of about 3.8 hectares [1]. There is an out-turned entrance at the east [1]. There is a steep natural slope on the south side, and a single rampart, about 3 metres high, around the rest of the fort, rising to about 8 metres in the north-east [1]. There was some excavation in 1951 at the north-east of the fort, a trench being cut from the edge of the rampart for about 35 metres towards the centre of the camp [1]. Sherds of Iron Age and Roman pottery, part of an iron axehead and other iron fragments were found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92496", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/057ed947/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/057ed947/Dinedor Camp, Hereford (geograph 5993134).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
