. There is a steep natural slope on the south side, and a single rampart, about 3 metres high, around the rest of the fort, rising to about 8 metres in the north-east [1]. There was some excavation in 1951 at the north-east of the fort, a trench being cut from the edge of the rampart for about 35 metres towards the centre of the camp [1]. Sherds of Iron Age and Roman pottery, part of an iron axehead and other iron fragments were found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92496", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/057ed947/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/057ed947/Dinedor Camp, Hereford (geograph 5993134).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
