 stones were maidens turned to stone for dancing on the Sabbath. The site lies on the Michael Line, a ley line passing through St Michael''s Mount and Glastonbury Tor.\" -> ''The Nine Maidens, also called the Seventeen Brothers, is a Bronze Age cairn circle on Belstone Common on northern Dartmoor, Devon, England [1] [2] [3] [4]. Local folklore claims the stones were maidens turned to stone for dancing on the Sabbath [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245607", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245608", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346258", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346259", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('068a88b3-505e-4998-add2-6b985b255371'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:068a88b3-505e-4998-add2-6b985b255371:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Ancient Theatre of Fourvière', 'bf163a7ea4ffb47f643253e376663681', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Theatre'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 28 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28390", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0122:chunk-0003: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Theatre''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81662", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2039:chunk-0001: description ''The Ancient Theatre of Fourviere is a Roman theatre in Lyon, France, built on the hillside of Fourviere in the ancient city of Lugdunum[1]. The theatre was constructed in two main phases: the original structure was built around 15 BC, possibly under Emperor Augustus, with a diameter of approximately 90 metres[2]. At the end of the 1st century or beginning of the 2nd century AD, the theatre was significantly expanded, reaching a diameter of 108 metres and increasing its capacity to approximately 10,000 spectators[1][2]. The theatre was positioned against the hill, below its summit, placing it near the centre of the Roman colony[1]. This expansion made it one of the largest Roman theatres in Gaul and a major cultural venue for the ancient city.'' -> ''The Ancient Theatre of Fourvière is a Roman theatre in Lyon, France [1]. It was built on the hill of Fourvière, which is situated in the center of the Roman city [1]. The theatre is part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site that protects the historic center of Lyon [1]. The theatre was constructed in two phases: around 15 BC, a theatre with a 90 m diameter was built next to the hill [1]. At the beginning of the 2nd century, the final construction added a last section for the audience [1]. The diameter is 108 m, and there were seats for 10,000 people [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142056", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Ancient Theatre of Fourvière (18059340520).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304711", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Ancient Theatre of Fourvière (18059340520).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Lyon_-_Lugdunum_-_Théatre_Romain.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305921", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Lyon_-_Lugdunum_-_Théatre_Romain.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Ancient Theatre of Fourvière (18059340520).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306797", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Ancient Theatre of Fourvière (18059340520).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/068a88b3/Lyon_-_Lugdunum_-_Théatre_Romain.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
