-known Aboriginal sites in Queensland: Nonda Rock and Ngarrabullgan Cave [1]. Here Aboriginal cultural deposits have been radiocarbon dated, and dated by optically stimulated luminescence, back to 40,000+ years ago [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113483", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113484", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Cave Structures'' -> ''Sacred site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142078", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Ngarrabullgin001.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/06a1c527/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245611", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245612", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}]'::jsonb),
