istry of Public Building and Works and carried out in May 1965 under the directorship of Geoffrey J. Wainwright [1]. The excavation revealed that the location of the stones was not their original prehistoric position [1]. The original location of the circle was identified as existing a few feet to the west [1]. The original circle had either eight or possibly nine sockets for stones and was oval shaped [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92523", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245631", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245632", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333623", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/082935cc/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/082935cc/Hampton Down stone circle - geograph.org.uk - 242207.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346272", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346273", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2050''"}]'::jsonb),
