    ('08d4b7da-794b-4cb7-9ed8-714758ae4487'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '7', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:08d4b7da-794b-4cb7-9ed8-714758ae4487:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''5'' restored on Cunetio', '6713d8165f566277824b4f6568d73124', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 7 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 0 content link(s), 15 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43905", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0082:chunk-0001: description ''Cunetio was a large walled Romano-British town in the River Kennet valley in Wiltshire, England, occupied from the 2nd century AD until the early 5th century [1]. Located near modern-day Mildenhall, about 2.4 km (1.5 mi) east of Marlborough, the settlement was unknown until aerial photography revealed it in the 1940s [1]. Excavations uncovered a substantial urban area defended by large masonry walls, with artefacts including kitchenware, personal effects, and two hoards of Roman coinage [1].'' -> ''Cunetio was a large walled town in a valley of the River Kennet in modern-day Wiltshire, England [1]. Occupied from the 2nd century AD by Romano-British people, the settlement was abandoned in the early 5th century, the emerging post-Roman period [1]. It lay near what is now the village of Mildenhall, about 1+1⁄2 miles (2.4 km) east of the market town of Marlborough [1]. Artefacts recovered from Cunetio have included kitchenware, personal effects, and two hoards of Roman coinage [1]. In the 1960s, a small coin hoard was found, followed in 1978 by the much larger Cunetio Hoard of over 55,000 coins [1]. The town grew around a mansio that had been built near the crossing of two Roman roads: the east–west road from Speen in Berkshire to Aquae Sulis (Bath), and the south-east to north road from Winchester to Wanborough [1]. As the town grew, it developed a regular grid of streets and stone buildings on its eastern side but retained less regular and substantial structures in the west part [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142645", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304747", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/East of Mildenhall - geograph.org.uk - 1225767.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305480", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/East of Mildenhall - geograph.org.uk - 1225767.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/East of Mildenhall - geograph.org.uk - 1225767.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
