followed in 1978 by the much larger Cunetio Hoard of over 55,000 coins [1]. The town grew around a mansio that had been built near the crossing of two Roman roads: the east–west road from Speen in Berkshire to Aquae Sulis (Bath), and the south-east to north road from Winchester to Wanborough [1]. As the town grew, it developed a regular grid of streets and stone buildings on its eastern side but retained less regular and substantial structures in the west part [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142645", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304747", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/East of Mildenhall - geograph.org.uk - 1225767.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305480", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/East of Mildenhall - geograph.org.uk - 1225767.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/08d4b7da/East of Mildenhall - geograph.org.uk - 1225767.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
