 settlements on the island. The site is part of the rich prehistoric heritage of the Alta Rocca region, which also includes the Bronze Age sites of Cucuruzzu and Capula. The Musee Departemental de l''Alta Rocca in Levie houses collections from the site, documenting the prehistory of southern Corsica from its earliest human occupation.\" -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234541", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304063", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338469", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4325:chunk-0001: description None -> ''Currachjaghju is an archaeological site in the Corsican commune of Levie, in France [1]. Currachjaghju is counted among the Middle Neolithic monuments of Corsica, a period that on the island lasted from 5000 BC to 4000 BC [2].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('09fcbc60-19c1-4742-a69d-3cb7afe19443'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:09fcbc60-19c1-4742-a69d-3cb7afe19443:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Kingston Russell Stone Circle', 'ebfde3ce56062439f2333c2572657b62', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -2500"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33039", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0012:chunk-0001: description ''Kingston Russell Stone Circle, also known as the Gorwell Circle, is the largest surviving stone circle in Dorset, located on a chalk ridge between Abbotsbury and Littlebredy at 189 m above sea level. The late Neolithic or early Bronze Age monument consists of 18 sarsen stones arranged in an oval measuring 24 by 27 m. All stones are now recumbent; records from 1815 note one stone on the southern side was still upright at that time. The site has never been formally excavated. It is a scheduled monument under the Ancient Monuments and Archaeological Areas Act 1979, managed by English Heritage.'' -> ''Kingston Russell Stone Circle, also known as the Gorwell Circle, is a stone circle located between the villages of Abbotsbury and Littlebredy in the south-western English county of Dorset [1]. Archaeologists believe that it was likely erected during the Bronze Age [1]. The Kingston Russell ring is part of a tradition of stone circle construction that spread throughout much of Britain, Ireland, and Brittany during the Late Neolithic and Early Bronze Age, over a period between 3,300 and 900 BCE [1]. The site has not been excavated or been subject to in-depth archaeological investigation [1]. Kingston Russell is the largest surviving stone circle in Dorset [1]. The stones are arranged in an oval with a diameter measuring from 24 by 27 metres (79 by 89 feet) [1]. The ring consists of eighteen stones, the longest of which are located at the north of the circle [1]. As of 1939, all the stones were lying on the ground, although there is a record that in 1815 one stone on the southern side was still standing upright [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92555", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92556", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142685", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/09fcbc60/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/09fcbc60/Kingston Russell stone circle I.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245653", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245654", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346288", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346289", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
