al Heritage of Peru in 2003. A 2015 restoration initiative involving the Cusco Department of Culture and local communities began clearing vegetation to reveal the site\\''s full structural extent.'' -> ''Wat\\''a (Quechua for \"island\") is an archaeological zone in the Cusco Region, Anta Province, Huarocondo District, situated atop the Pachar ravine north of Huarocondo [1] [2]. The complex comprises five sections: Wat\\''aq\\''asa, Willkapata, Qhawarina, Qullqa, and Saksaywaman Pata, featuring enclosures, platforms, and ceremonial sites [1] [2]. Saksaywaman Pata was declared National Cultural Heritage of Peru in 2003 [1]. A 2015 initiative involving the Cusco Department of Culture and local communities began clearing vegetation to reveal the site\\''s full structural extent [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304064", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}]'::jsonb),
