h stone slabs that leads into a central chamber. This architectural style is also found in the neighbouring Isles of Scilly, suggesting cultural links between these regions during prehistory[1].'' -> ''The Tregiffian Burial Chamber is a Neolithic or early Bronze Age chambered cairn located near Lamorna in west Cornwall, England [1] [2]. It is a rare type of passage grave known as an Entrance grave, featuring an entrance passage lined with stone slabs that leads into a central chamber [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245659", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245660", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333632", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0a82ea91/Tregiffian burial chamber westCornwall England.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0a82ea91/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346292", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346293", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> ''-2900''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0a8f4bd4-8115-4b64-b20c-0014b2458106'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:0a8f4bd4-8115-4b64-b20c-0014b2458106:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Dorset Cursus', '922ef8e6a1cdd63fee5f35d7304b5510', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Earthwork'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 13 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0159:chunk-0001: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-3300''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35646", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-3300'' -> ''-4500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81750", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2042:chunk-0001: description ''The Dorset Cursus is a Neolithic linear earthwork stretching 10 km across the chalk downland of Cranborne Chase in east Dorset, England [1]. It is better interpreted as a pair of same-length cursus constructed end to end, with the more southerly cursus pre-dating the northerly one [1].'' -> \"The Dorset Cursus is a Neolithic cursus monument that spans across 10 km of the chalk downland of Cranborne Chase in east Dorset, United Kingdom [1]. Its extreme length makes it a notable example of this class of linear earthwork; it is better interpreted as a pair of same-length cursus constructed end to end, with the more southerly cursus (the Gussage Cursus) pre-dating the northerly one (the Pentridge Cursus) [1]. The Cursus dates from 3300 BCE which makes it contemporary with the earthen long barrows on Cranborne Chase: many of these are found near, on, or within the Cursus and since they are still in existence they help trace the Cursus'' course in the modern landscape [1]. The relationship between the Cursus and the alignment of these barrows suggests that they had a common ritual significance to the Neolithic people who spent an estimated 0.5 million worker-hours in its construction [1]. The Cursus consisted of a pair of parallel banks (1.5 m tall) running about 82 m apart, with external ditches 1.5 m deep and 2 m wide [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0a8f4bd4/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0a8f4bd4/Dorset_cursus_bank_on_bottlebush_down.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333635", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0a8f4bd4/Dorset_cursus_bank_on_bottlebush_down.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0a8f4bd4/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
