metery at Tower Hill contained both cremation and inhumation burials, along with high-status finds including lead coffins, bronze bowls, and a rare oculist''s stamp. Evidence of Saxon occupation was also discovered outside the town walls.\" -> ''Sandy was a significant Romano-British small town in Central Bedfordshire [1] [2]. Recent excavations uncovered the first Roman town wall found in Bedfordshire, built from local ironstone and mortar, enclosing an area of about 11 hectares [1] [3]. A large cemetery at Tower Hill contained both cremation and inhumation burials [4]. Evidence of Saxon occupation was also discovered outside the town walls [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245667", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245668", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346297", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
