ion burials, along with high-status finds including lead coffins, bronze bowls, and a rare oculist''s stamp. Evidence of Saxon occupation was also discovered outside the town walls.\" -> ''Sandy was a significant Romano-British small town in Central Bedfordshire [1] [2]. Recent excavations uncovered the first Roman town wall found in Bedfordshire, built from local ironstone and mortar, enclosing an area of about 11 hectares [1] [3]. A large cemetery at Tower Hill contained both cremation and inhumation burials [4]. Evidence of Saxon occupation was also discovered outside the town walls [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245667", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245668", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346297", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0b2d26e4-2441-4333-900d-fc4119c03166'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:0b2d26e4-2441-4333-900d-fc4119c03166:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Spathes', 'aace478196ba2f2ae5b63fb7f814c693', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 24 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29012", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0225:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30341", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2002:chunk-0001: description ''Spathes (Greek Σπάθες, \"swords\") is a Late Bronze Age necropolis on Mount Olympus, among the first archaeological sites discovered there[1]. The oldest tombs date to the 14th century BC, with the last traces of use found from the end of the 13th century BC to the beginning of the 12th century BC[1]. The associated settlement has not been discovered[1]. Many burial offerings were made in the Mycenaean style, suggesting the Mycenaean cultural circle extended beyond Thessaly into Pieria[1].'' -> ''Among the first archaeological sites discovered in Mount Olympus was the excavation site Spathes [1]. It is a necropolis from the Late Bronze Age [1]. Many of the burial offerings were made in the Mycenaean style, so that the Mycenaean cultural circle probably also extended over the border of Thessaly to Pieria [1]. The excavations brought to light 34 tombs, which were partly destroyed and plundered [1]. The most important finds were made in a tomb, in which apparently high ranking personalities were buried [1]. Remnants of a spear, a bronze sword, painted and unpainted vases and perfume bottles, jewelry and stone seals (partly with animal motifs) were discovered [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142751", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Spathes.jpg/400px-Spathes.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0b2d26e4/Spathes.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
