ean style, so that the Mycenaean cultural circle probably also extended over the border of Thessaly to Pieria [1]. The excavations brought to light 34 tombs, which were partly destroyed and plundered [1]. The most important finds were made in a tomb, in which apparently high ranking personalities were buried [1]. Remnants of a spear, a bronze sword, painted and unpainted vases and perfume bottles, jewelry and stone seals (partly with animal motifs) were discovered [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142751", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Spathes.jpg/400px-Spathes.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0b2d26e4/Spathes.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0b34fdec-f221-40f9-8238-2d78d7ce6638'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:0b34fdec-f221-40f9-8238-2d78d7ce6638:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''7'' restored on Cranon', 'ad9978c3d5ece2408918e67bbf73ce90', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0012:chunk-0001: description ''Cranon (Κραννών) was an ancient Greek polis (city-state) in the region of Pelasgiotis, Thessaly, Greece [1]. The settlement was situated southwest of Larissa at a distance of 100 stadia from Gyrton, as recorded by the geographer Strabo [1]. Cranon was bounded by the territory of Atrax to the west and Scotussa to the east, while the ridges of Revenia to the south separated it from the valley of the river Enipeus [1].'' -> ''Cranon or Crannon was a town and polis (city-state) of Pelasgiotis, in ancient Thessaly, situated southwest of Larissa, and at the distance of 100 stadia from Gyrton, according to Strabo [1]. After the Battle of Chaeronea (338 BCE), the Phocians fought in Lamia and in the Battle of Crannon against Antipater and his army [1]. This was the decisive battle of the Lamian War between Macedon and Athens with its allies [1]. In 191 BCE, Crannon was taken by Selecuid king Antiochus III [1]. The first epigraphic reference to the polis of the Cranionians is in an honorific decree of the 3rd century BCE [1]. At an indeterminate date Cranon was a walled and fortified city, but almost nothing is known about the urban centre and the acropolis, except for a possible temple of Athena Polias erected on it [1]. There were also temples of Aesclepius, Apollo, Poseidon and Zeus [1]. The city minted silver coins in the fifth century BCE (480-400 BCE) and bronze coins in the fourth century BCE [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346298", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346299", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
