es in 1961. Today it hosts summer performances with acoustics ranked among the finest of any open-air theatre worldwide.\" -> \"Greco-Roman theatre built in the late 2nd century BC in the ancient city-kingdom of Kourion on Cyprus''s southwestern coast [1] [2]. It seated up to 3,500 spectators [1] [2]. In the early 3rd century AD it was converted for wild animal combat before reverting to theatrical use by century''s end [1]. Today it hosts summer performances [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
