unded by a dry-stone revetting wall [1]. The barrow was archaeologically excavated in 1821, revealing the remains of fifteen skeletons and a later, intrusive Roman age burial above the northeast chamber [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142813", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/Uley_Long_Barrow.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley Long Barrow (42082931545).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304795", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley Long Barrow (42082931545).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley_Long_Barrow.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305996", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley_Long_Barrow.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley Long Barrow (42082931545).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306881", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley Long Barrow (42082931545).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0cd2e708/Uley_Long_Barrow.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
