l earthwork enclosure on the steep southeast-facing slopes of Rodhuish Common in Somerset, England [1] [2] [3]. The enclosure measures 31.7 m north-south by 28.3 m east-west, defined by a stony bank averaging 0.6 m high, with a 1.7 m cut into the natural slope on the western side [1]. Designated as a Scheduled Monument in 2003 [1]. Listed on Historic England''s Heritage at Risk register [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246039", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246040", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/0db059e7/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346306", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346307", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0de3da9b-5aeb-45a2-8f72-31ac1ad74a13'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:0de3da9b-5aeb-45a2-8f72-31ac1ad74a13:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Beeley Moor', 'e6fac456281cde78d1971e210a1799c9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81794", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2043:chunk-0001: description \"Beeley Moor is a gritstone upland in the Derbyshire Peak District, rising to 371 m, preserving a rich prehistoric landscape of Bronze Age cairns, cairn fields, burial mounds, stone circles, and guidestones, all protected as Scheduled Ancient Monuments. Notable features include Hob Hurst''s House, an unusual square Bronze Age burial cairn on nearby Harland Edge, excavated by Thomas Bateman in 1853, which yielded a stone cist containing cremated remains. The moor became Open Access land following the Countryside and Rights of Way Act 2000.\" -> ''Beeley Moor is a small gritstone upland area in the Derbyshire Peak District of central and northern England, near the villages of Beeley and Baslow [1]. Its highest point is 371 metres above sea level [1]. Beeley Moor is a prehistoric landscape with many protected scheduled monuments including individual cairns, cairn fields, burial mounds and guidestones [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84158", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:8