l site within a rock shelter was documented by Sandra Bowdler, an archaeologist from the Australian Museum in 1964 [1]. Until 1916, the Balls Head area was frequented by the local Aboriginal community and sites including middens, art sites and rock engravings remain today [1]. The Aboriginal name for Balls Head is Yerroulbine [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113545", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113546", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/(1)Balls_Head_Reserve-3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246046", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304816", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/(1)Balls_Head_Reserve-3.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/Angophora_costata_Balls_Head.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306017", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/Angophora_costata_Balls_Head.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/(1)Balls_Head_Reserve-3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306902", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/(1)Balls_Head_Reserve-3.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0dfe2efe/Angophora_costata_Balls_Head.webp''"}, {"sou