 the cardinal points [1]. It has been considered by some to be a male initiation ground, mainly on the basis of comparison with other similar sites in NSW [1]. This arrangement is believed to fall within the traditional land of the Wurn balug clan of the Djadjawurrung [1]. Following its rediscovery in 1963, interest was focussed on its interpretation and protection, with initial protection provided under the Archaeological Relics Office [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93298", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93299", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93300", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: site_type ''Stone circle'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234571", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246049", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246050", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346313", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
