n 1983 when a farmer''s plough struck a mosaic. The site comprises the Villa of Maternus with elaborate floor mosaics depicting scenes including the death of Adonis and the god Oceanus, a basilica originally featuring 32 monolithic marble columns, and a mausoleum. The villa included luxury amenities such as hypocaust under-floor heating and running water, with mosaics assembled by at least three workshops, two of which signed their work. The complex is attributed to Maternus Cynegius, an Iberian-born adviser to Emperor Theodosius, and later saw Visigothic, Islamic, and Knights Templar occupation.\" -> \"Carranque Archaeological Park in Toledo province, Spain, preserves a lavish 4th-century Roman villa complex rediscovered in 1983 when a farmer''s plough struck a mosaic [1]. The site comprises the Villa of Maternus with elaborate floor mosaics depicting scenes including the death of Adonis and the god Oceanus, a basilica originally featuring 32 monolithic marble columns, and a mausoleum [1] [2] [3]. The villa included luxury amenities such as hypocaust under-floor heating and running water, with mosaics assembled by at least three workshops, two of which signed their work [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304836", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0ecacadb/Carranque.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0ecacadb/Carranque-basilica.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306037", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0ecacadb/Carranque-basilica.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0ecacadb/Carranque.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306922", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0ecacadb/Carranque.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0ecacadb/Carranque-basilica.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355567", "url": "remediatio