1]. In the 13th century BC, the Annals of Hattusili III mentions the city as a part of Lukka and conquered by the Hittites [1]. Telmessos was a flourishing city in the west of Lycia, on the Gulf of Fethiye [1]. It was famed for its school of diviners, consulted among others by the Lydian king Croesus, prior to declaring war against Cyrus [1]. Telmessos was a member of the Delian League in the 5th century BC [1]. It was taken by Alexander the Great in 334 BC, when he came to the town after the siege of Halicarnassus [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93326", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142891", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/185A7357.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234585", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234586", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/185A7357.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/Tomb of Amyntas.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345658", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
