ian city situated on a steep mountain over 900 m above sea level near modern Uzumlu, 19 km northeast of Fethiye, Turkey. Monuments and inscriptions date back to the 5th century BC, with the Lycian name Kadawanti. Remains include a stadium with six rows of seating, a theatre with 18 rows, baths from Vespasian''s reign, a Doric temple, and polygonal city walls. A member of the Lycian League during the Hellenistic and Roman periods. First official excavations began in 2022.\" -> \"Ancient Lycian city situated on a steep mountain over 900 m above sea level near modern Uzumlu, Turkey [1] [2]. Monuments and inscriptions date back to the 5th century BC, with the Lycian name Kadawanti [1]. Remains include a stadium with six rows of seating, a theatre with 18 rows, baths from Vespasian''s reign, a Doric temple, and polygonal city walls [1] [2]. A member of the Lycian League during the Hellenistic and Roman periods [3] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307555", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/105d50fa/Kadyanda City Wall 7552.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/105d50fa/Kadyanda_Theatre_7563.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355570", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
