1: description \"Ancient Lycian city situated on a steep mountain over 900 m above sea level near modern Uzumlu, 19 km northeast of Fethiye, Turkey. Monuments and inscriptions date back to the 5th century BC, with the Lycian name Kadawanti. Remains include a stadium with six rows of seating, a theatre with 18 rows, baths from Vespasian''s reign, a Doric temple, and polygonal city walls. A member of the Lycian League during the Hellenistic and Roman periods. First official excavations began in 2022.\" -> \"Ancient Lycian city situated on a steep mountain over 900 m above sea level near modern Uzumlu, Turkey [1] [2]. Monuments and inscriptions date back to the 5th century BC, with the Lycian name Kadawanti [1]. Remains include a stadium with six rows of seating, a theatre with 18 rows, baths from Vespasian''s reign, a Doric temple, and polygonal city walls [1] [2]. A member of the Lycian League during the Hellenistic and Roman periods [3] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307555", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/105d50fa/Kadyanda City Wall 7552.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/105d50fa/Kadyanda_Theatre_7563.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355570", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1065be39-af74-4a22-8f95-ffc846068367'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:1065be39-af74-4a22-8f95-ffc846068367:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Rudston Monolith', '7c20e6dcf9910c1e1c979d9c9fe0587b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 17 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33083", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0013:chunk-0001: description \"The tallest megalith in the United Kingdom at nearly 8 metres high with a circumference of 5 metres, standing in the churchyard of All Saints Church in Rudston, East Riding of Yorkshire. Dating to the Late Neolithic or Early Bronze Age, the stone was hewn from Moorstone grit quarried near Scarborough and transported roughly 40 miles, likely by river. It stands at the convergence of three cursus monuments, suggesting it was a focal point for prehistoric assembly or ceremony. The name Rudston derives from Old English ''rood-stane'' meaning cross-stone.\" -> ''The Rudston Monolith, at over 25 feet, is the tallest monolith in the United Kingdom, originating in the U.K. It is situated in the churchyard of All Saints Church, in the village of Rudston in the East Riding of Yorkshire [1]. The stone is slender, with two large flat faces [1]. It is over 25 feet (7.6 m) tall, is approximately 5 feet 9 inches (1.75 m) wide and just under 3 feet 3 inches (1 m) thick [1]. The top appears to have broken off [1]. In 1773 the stone was capped in lead; this was later removed, although the stone is currently capped [1]. The weight is estimated at 40 tonnes [1]. Eighteenth-century antiquarian William Stukeley found \"the dimensions of the monolith within ground as large as those without\" [1]. Stukeley found many skulls during his dig and suggested they might have been sacrificial [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93356", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Rudston_Monolith.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1065be39/Rudston_Monolith.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-3500''"}]'::jsonb),
