ne was capped in lead; this was later removed, although the stone is currently capped [1]. The weight is estimated at 40 tonnes [1]. Eighteenth-century antiquarian William Stukeley found \"the dimensions of the monolith within ground as large as those without\" [1]. Stukeley found many skulls during his dig and suggested they might have been sacrificial [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93356", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Rudston_Monolith.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1065be39/Rudston_Monolith.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-3500''"}]'::jsonb),
