tes to the Late Horizon period (1438-1530 AD) and preserves remains associated with Inca settlement in the Urubamba Valley region.'' -> ''Mawk\\''ataray (Quechua: mawk\\''a \"ancient\" + Taray, meaning \"old Taray\") is an Inca-period archaeological site in the Cusco Region of Peru, situated in Calca Province, Taray District [1] [2]. The name refers to the nearby town of Taray [1] [2]. The site preserves remains associated with Inca settlement in the Urubamba Valley region [2] [3] [4].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246075", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246076", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
