gonal masonry characterizes the oldest surviving structures, while later constructions used smooth cut stone. The ruins also contain cisterns, sarcophagi, and remnants of churches, reflecting the site''s importance as a settlement along ancient Mediterranean travel routes between Silifke and Erdemli.\" -> ''Okuzlu Oren Yeri is an archaeological site in the Erdemli district of Mersin Province, Turkey [1]. The site was occupied during the Hellenistic, Roman, and Byzantine periods, featuring remains including a basilica structure from the Byzantine phase [1] [2]. Polygonal masonry characterizes the oldest surviving structures, while later constructions used smooth cut stone [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246081", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246082", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/11aae1cf/ÖküzlüTür2Sturz.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355573", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
