aracterizes the oldest surviving structures, while later constructions used smooth cut stone. The ruins also contain cisterns, sarcophagi, and remnants of churches, reflecting the site''s importance as a settlement along ancient Mediterranean travel routes between Silifke and Erdemli.\" -> ''Okuzlu Oren Yeri is an archaeological site in the Erdemli district of Mersin Province, Turkey [1]. The site was occupied during the Hellenistic, Roman, and Byzantine periods, featuring remains including a basilica structure from the Byzantine phase [1] [2]. Polygonal masonry characterizes the oldest surviving structures, while later constructions used smooth cut stone [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246081", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246082", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/11aae1cf/ÖküzlüTür2Sturz.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355573", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('11d5d105-4613-4bd5-9e52-b17ce6a5c87d'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:11d5d105-4613-4bd5-9e52-b17ce6a5c87d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Bhaja Caves', 'b81fa087074e84b53ff2092ac9ea6482', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cave Structures'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 19 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33103", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0014:chunk-0001: description ''Bhaja Caves are a group of 22 rock-cut Buddhist caves dating to the 2nd century BC, situated 400 feet above the village of Bhaja on an ancient trade route from the Arabian Sea eastward into the Deccan Plateau [1]. The caves belong to the Early Buddhist schools in Maharashtra and are protected as a Monument of National Importance by the Archaeological Survey of India [1]. The complex features a prominent chaitya (prayer hall) with a vaulted horseshoe ceiling, representing an early development from wooden architecture [1]. A vihara with a pillared verandah and unique reliefs also forms part of the excavation [1]. The caves contain several stupas, one of their most significant features [1].'' -> ''Bhaja Caves are a group of 22 rock-cut caves dating back to the 2nd century BC located off the Mumbai - Pune expressway near the city of Pune [1]. The caves are 400 feet above the village of Bhaja [1]. The most prominent excavation is its chaitya, a good example of the early development of this form from wooden architecture, with a vaulted horseshoe ceiling [1]. Its vihara has a pillared verandah in front and is adorned with unique reliefs [1]. A cistern inscription shows the name of a donor from the 2nd century AD [1]. A notable part of the monument is a group of 14 stupas, five inside and nine outside an irregular excavation [1]. The stupas are relics of resident monks, who died at Bhaja, and display an inscription with the names of three monks, Ampinika, Dhammagiri and Sanghdina [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113595", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Cave Structures''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/11d5d105/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/11d5d105/Bhaja_Caves_IMG_5481.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307572", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/11d5d105/Bhaja_Caves_IMG_5481.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/11d5d105/The_Bhaje_Caves_05.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
