    ('1268a0fc-ad34-46f1-878c-4cb4402d9cfa'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:1268a0fc-ad34-46f1-878c-4cb4402d9cfa:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''7'' restored on Moel y Gaer, Rhosesmor', 'ba86ecc7ded44d5d3d80b0a0ea41388e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start -800"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81934", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2047:chunk-0001: description ''Moel y Gaer is an Iron Age hillfort situated on a summit at the southern end of Halkyn Mountain overlooking the Dee Estuary near Rhosesmor, Flintshire, Wales[1]. Excavations in the early 1970s uncovered a complex sequence of timber defensive structures and multiple phases of building work within the ramparts[1]. The site is exceptionally well-preserved, with its earthworks remaining visible across the hilltop[1].'' -> ''Moel y Gaer is an Iron Age hillfort located on a summit at the southern end of Halkyn Mountain, overlooking the village of Rhosesmor, Flintshire [1]. It is a well-preserved hillfort overlooking the Dee Estuary [1]. Excavations in the early 1970s revealed a sequence of defensive structures made of timber and several phases of building work inside the ramparts [1]. Excavations suggest that the site was occupied, perhaps sporadically, from the Neolithic period to sometime before the Roman conquest of the area [1]. Remains of a timber long house on the hill summit have been dated to the third millennium BC and may represent the earliest human occupation of the region [1]. D