 reliefs depicting condors, a puma, a falcon, a human head, and small animals in a style showing clear Chavin cultural influence. Large quantities of ceramics suggest it functioned as a place of worship. The site also serves as a natural viewpoint but remains largely unexcavated and under-researched.'' -> ''Condorcaga is a Chavin-influenced archaeological zone in the Chota Province, Lajas District, Cajamarca region of Peru [1] [2]. The hilltop site features a pre-Inca chullpa (stone tower) with carved reliefs depicting condors, a puma, a falcon, a human head, and small animals in a style showing Chavin cultural influence [2]. Large quantities of ceramics suggest it functioned as a place of worship [2]. The site also serves as a natural viewpoint but remains under-researched [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234627", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246087", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246088", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346342", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346343", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1374c196-3e09-44d3-b2a8-ac326f6bd14c'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:1374c196-3e09-44d3-b2a8-ac326f6bd14c:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Rempstone Stone Circle', 'd183f6947af505f7d2e444b3953c2898', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -2500"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0083:chunk-0001: description ''Rempstone Stone Circle is a Bronze Age monument near Corfe Castle on the Isle of Purbeck in Dorset, England. The surviving stones form an arc suggesting an original diameter of about 26 metres (85 feet), which would make it the second largest stone circle in Dorset. Unusually for the region, the stones are reddish hard stone rather than sarsen, and it is the only Dorset circle not located on the chalk hills west of Dorchester. In 1957, a row of 23 stones forming a possible avenue was discovered 800 metres west of the circle but subsequently removed. The site is a scheduled monument under legal protection.'' -> ''Rempstone Stone Circle is a stone circle near to Corfe Castle on the Isle of Purbeck in the south-western English county of Dorset [1]. Archaeologists believe that it was likely erected during the Bronze Age [1]. The southern half of the circle has been destroyed, with five upright and three recumbent stones remaining extant [1]. In 1957, a possible avenue of stones leading to the circle was discovered by ploughing but subsequently removed [1]. The incomplete stone circle lies in a dense wood just to the south of the B3351 road, 4 kilometres east of Corfe Castle and 5 kilometres west of Studland [1]. The stones are sandstone boulders which geologically belong to the Bagshot Beds, on which the circle is located [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93401", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93402", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143395", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/Part_of_the_Rempstone_stone_circle_in_birch_woodland%2C_Purbeck_-_geograph.org.uk_-_25149.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1374c196/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246091", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246092", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307596", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1374c196/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1374c196/Part of the Rempstone stone circle in birch woodland, Purbeck - geograph.org.uk - 25149.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346345", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
