e burial cairn in the Carneddau mountains of north Wales, occupying a summit northeast of Foel-fras [1]. The summit features two large shelter cairns hollowed from a massive prehistoric burial cairn [1] [2]. Its eastern slopes drain via Afon Tafolog to Afon Roe, flowing through Rowen before joining the River Conwy [1]. The site forms the final top on Carnedd Llewelyn''s long northern spur, with Tal y Fan to the northeast [1] [3].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246099", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246100", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346348", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346349", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2300''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('14aacb74-9cd3-4766-b74b-4911d804c415'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:14aacb74-9cd3-4766-b74b-4911d804c415:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Welsh Road', 'fbc08d3b6b15ae963a22d7c4595a4be5', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81964", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2048:chunk-0001: description \"A drover''s road running through the English Midlands used to transport cattle from North Wales to South East England. Many stretches coincide with parish boundaries, suggesting pre-Roman origins as an ancient trackway. The route followed Watling Street from Shrewsbury to Brownhills, then ran through Castle Bromwich, Kenilworth, Southam, and on to Buckingham. Between 1700 and 1850, an estimated two million animals annually used this corridor. The northern section was turnpiked in 1759, now followed by the A452.\" -> ''The Welsh Road, also known as the Welshman\\''s Road or the Bullock Road, was a drover\\''s road running through the English Midlands, used for transporting cattle from North Wales to the markets of South East England [1]. Drovers and their herds would follow the line of Watling Street from Shrewsbury and over Cannock Chase to Brownhills, from where the Welsh Road ran through Stonnall, Castle Bromwich, Stonebridge, Kenilworth, Cubbington, Offchurch, Southam, Priors Hardwick, Boddington, Culworth, Sulgrave, Syresham, Biddlesden, and Buckingham [1]. The age of the route is not known [1]. The parish records of Helmdon record money being given in 1687 \"to a poor Welshman who fell sick on his journey driving beasts to London\", but many lengths of the road coincide with parish or manorial boundaries, suggesting that it probably formed an ancient trackway dating to the pre-Roman era [1]. The northern section of the route from Brownhills to Stonebridge was made a turnpike by the Broughton, Chester and Stonebridge Turnpike Trust in 1759 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93415", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246101", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/14aacb74/Welsh Road lock and cottage - geograph.org.uk - 7279320.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346351", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
