and cultural boundary [1]. It was cut through by a Roman Road in the 1st century [1]. In the 4th century it was remodelled and brought back into use, and excavations show that the Roman road was blocked [1]. A coin of Valens dates this activity to shortly after 364 AD [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113612", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113613", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246107", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246108", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346354", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
