 Anatolia, located at the mouth of the Şeytan deresi valley [1] [2]. The settlement flourished during the Hellenistic and Roman periods [2]. The site is now occupied by the town of Kızkalesi in Mersin Province, Turkey [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246111", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246112", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/15c7e942/Korykos Zisterne01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346358", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346359", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
