ient city in Cilicia Trachaea, Anatolia, located at the mouth of the Şeytan deresi valley [1] [2]. The settlement flourished during the Hellenistic and Roman periods [2]. The site is now occupied by the town of Kızkalesi in Mersin Province, Turkey [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246111", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246112", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/15c7e942/Korykos Zisterne01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346358", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346359", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('15d5774e-1934-42db-85d8-5f990e7afe50'::uuid, 'antiquity', '3', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:15d5774e-1934-42db-85d8-5f990e7afe50:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''5'' restored on Coggabata', '115aeed5c9ecc53f488d1f316c5dd2d9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 3 from period_start 43"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33141", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0015:chunk-0001: description \"Coggabata (modern Drumburgh) was a Roman fort on Hadrian''s Wall in Cumbria, built to guard two important Solway Firth fords, the Stonewath and Sandwath. The stone fort measured approximately 82 by 96 meters, occupying just under 2 acres. Excavations in 1899 revealed the stone fort and a buttressed granary, while 1947 digs showed the stone fort was built within a slightly larger earthwork fort with clay ramparts, likely added to the original Turf Wall. Recent excavations uncovered a remarkably well-preserved section of Hadrian''s Wall surviving up to four courses high. The Notitia Dignitatum records the garrison as the Second Cohort of Lingones. A medieval pele tower, Drumburgh Castle, was later built across the fort''s north wall using Roman stones.\" -> \"Coggabata, or Congavata / Concavata, was a Roman fort on Hadrian''s Wall, between Aballava to the east and Mais to the west [1]. It was built on a hill commanding views over the flatter land to the east and west and to the shore of the Solway Firth to the north [1]. Its purpose was to guard the southern end of two important Solway fords, the Stonewath and the Sandwath [1]. The fort was an oblong and built of stone, with the Wall running along its northern side, and measured 270 feet north to south by 316 feet east to west, occupying an area of just less than 2 acres [1]. A Roman road has been proved by LIDAR photography to have linked Coggabata with the nearby Roman fort at Kirkbride to the south-west [1]. The Notitia Dignitatum gives the garrison as the Second Cohort of Lingones but only a detachment could be accommodated in such a small fort [1]. Excavations in 1947 revealed that the stone fort had been built within a slightly larger fort whose clay ramparts had been levelled [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93442", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143431", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/15d5774e/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246115", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246116", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333659", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/15d5774e/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> ''43''"}]'::jsonb),
