n Poseidon, surrounded by a grove of wild olives [1]. It was the centre of the religious worship of the six Triphylian cities, all of whom contributed to its support [1]. The ruins of Samicum are found at Kleidi Hill near Kato Samiko [1]. The ruined walls are 6 feet (2 m) thick, and about 1.5 miles (2.4 km) in circumference [1]. The remains found on Kleidi Hill include cyclopean walls and remnants of a settlement that was occupied in the middle and late Helladic periods [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94326", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143463", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/Samiko.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/16d9eae9/Samia acropolis.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246128", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321080", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/16d9eae9/Samia acropolis.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/16d9eae9/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324956", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/16d9eae9/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/16d9eae9/Samiko.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346370", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_ch