    ('16edc297-75f0-471e-a82a-fc3dc46d6c8f'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:16edc297-75f0-471e-a82a-fc3dc46d6c8f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Castleshaw Roman Fort', '6a115d82415c0b66ff33192b7184b7d7', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fort'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28288", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0106:chunk-0001: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fortification''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35667", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Fortification'' -> ''Fortress/citadel''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37663", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-wrong-both: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82020", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2049:chunk-0001: description ''Castleshaw Roman Fort was a 1st-century AD Roman fortification in Britannia, located on Castle Hill overlooking the Castleshaw Valley at the foot of Standedge in Greater Manchester [1]. Constructed c. AD 79, the fort operated until the 90s AD before being replaced by a smaller fortlet built c. 105 AD around which a civilian settlement grew [1]. The site may have served as a logistical and administrative centre before abandonment in the 120s [1]. While unverified, scholars have suggested Castleshaw could be the location of Rigodunum, a major Brigantian settlement [1].'' -> \"Castleshaw Roman fort was a castellum in the Roman province of Britannia [1]. The remains of the fort are located on Castle Hill on the eastern side of Castleshaw Valley at the foot of Standedge but overlooking the valley [1]. The fort was constructed in c. AD 79, but fell out of use at some time during the 90s [1]. It was replaced by a smaller fortlet, built in c. 105, around which a civilian settlement grew [1]. The site has been the subject of antiquarian and archaeological investigation since the 18th century, but the civilian settlement lay undiscovered until the 1990s [1]. The location of the fort''s granary, stables, the principia, the praetorium, and six long narrow buildings which are possibly workshops or storerooms are all known [1]. After being abandoned by the Romans, Castleshaw was rediscovered by antiquarian Thomas Percival in 1752 [1]. The fort was rectangular in shape and had sides of 115 metres and 100 metres, covering an area of approximately 1.2 hectares [1].\""}]'::jsonb),
