ples from the Eurasian steppes to the Balkans. Rescue excavations began in 1999 under the Greek Ephorate of Antiquities.'' -> ''Pigi Athinas (Source of Athena) is an archaeological site at the eastern foot of Mount Olympus near Platamonas, Greece, with evidence of human presence from the 7th millennium BC [1] [2]. A Neolithic settlement with successive occupation phases was established, yielding finds including a female figurine [3]. During the Bronze Age (c. 1620-1500 BC), a monumental tumuli cemetery was created with circular and elliptical burial mounds containing 17 individuals aged 20-50, interred with pottery grave goods [1] [3]. The tumuli expansion is associated with the spread of Indo-European peoples from the Eurasian steppes to the Balkans [3]. Rescue excavations began in 1999 under the Greek Ephorate of Antiquities [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234651", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234652", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-7000''"}]'::jsonb),
