e spread of Indo-European peoples from the Eurasian steppes to the Balkans. Rescue excavations began in 1999 under the Greek Ephorate of Antiquities.'' -> ''Pigi Athinas (Source of Athena) is an archaeological site at the eastern foot of Mount Olympus near Platamonas, Greece, with evidence of human presence from the 7th millennium BC [1] [2]. A Neolithic settlement with successive occupation phases was established, yielding finds including a female figurine [3]. During the Bronze Age (c. 1620-1500 BC), a monumental tumuli cemetery was created with circular and elliptical burial mounds containing 17 individuals aged 20-50, interred with pottery grave goods [1] [3]. The tumuli expansion is associated with the spread of Indo-European peoples from the Eurasian steppes to the Balkans [3]. Rescue excavations began in 1999 under the Greek Ephorate of Antiquities [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234651", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234652", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-7000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1724deb2-8bac-4a38-971b-4d1542745e0b'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:1724deb2-8bac-4a38-971b-4d1542745e0b:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Bant''s Carn', '83b403d5ab8dfd0744555f68dc888a82', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''Undated'') is shared by 18 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2049:chunk-0001: description \"(3000–1500 BC) Bant''s Carn is a Bronze Age entrance grave on St Mary''s in the Isles of Scilly, England. One of the finest Scillonian entrance graves, it measures approximately 8 metres in diameter and sits on a 12‑metre platform. The passage is 4.5 metres long and 1 metre high, lacking a roof. Below lies the Iron Age settlement of Halangy Down[1][2][3].\" -> \"Bant''s Carn is a Bronze Age entrance grave located on a steep slope on the island of St Mary''s in the Isles of Scilly, England [1]. The tomb is one of the best examples of a Scillonian entrance grave [1]. The tomb measures around 8 metres (26 ft) in diameter and stands on a low platform 12 metres (39 ft) across [1]. The entrance is 4.5 metres (15 ft) long and 1 metre (3.3 ft) high, with no roof [1]. It is separated from the burial chamber by a jamb [1]. The chamber itself measures around 5 metres (16 ft) in length and 1.5 metres (4.9 ft) in width and height, with four large capstones serving as a roof [1]. The tomb was excavated in 1900 by archaeologist, George Bonsor [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94336", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94337", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246133", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246134", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307656", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1724deb2/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/1724deb2/Bant''s Cairn, St Mary''s - geograph.org.uk - 1197663.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346375", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
