ka\" refers to the Inca Empire and \"raqay\" means a ruin, shed, storehouse, or dormitory for farm laborers. The site features stone wall structures demonstrating Inca architectural and engineering methods. It likely functioned as a storage and administrative facility serving the Inca road network during the empire\\''s height (c. 1438-1530 AD).'' -> ''An Inca archaeological site in Peru\\''s Ayacucho Region, Huanta Province, Iguain District, situated on top of the mountain Allqu Willka [1] [2]. The name derives from Quechua, where \"Inka\" refers to the Inca Empire and \"raqay\" means a ruin, shed, storehouse, or dormitory for farm laborers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235483", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246457", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246458", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346385", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1877a303-0731-4ad3-9814-2b852ff93242'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:1877a303-0731-4ad3-9814-2b852ff93242:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''2'' restored on Dun Beag Broch', 'ae2db0b25f1eb8721b8465e92840ee6f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43947", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0083:chunk-0001: description ''Dun Beag is one of the best-preserved Iron Age brochs on the Isle of Skye, perched on a rocky outcrop near Struan overlooking Loch Bracadale. Built in the last centuries BC, the drystone tower has an interior diameter of approximately 11 metres with walls 4.3 metres thick, and originally stood over 10 metres tall. The structure features a narrow entrance with door-checks for a timber door, possible guard cells, and an impressive stone staircase of which 20 steps survive within the hollow walls. Excavated from 1914 to 1920 by Countess Vincent Baillet de Latour, finds included medieval and later coins, indicating intermittent use well beyond the Iron Age. Scholars now believe brochs were built primarily as status symbols reflecting the prestige of their inhabitants.'' -> ''Dun Beag is an iron-age broch located about 1 kilometre northwest of the village of Struan on the west coast of the island of Skye, in Scotland [1]. Dun Beag is situated at the north end of a small rocky knoll [1]. The broch consists of a drystone tower with a diameter of around 18.6 metres with walls about 4 metres thick at the base [1]. The broch currently stands to a maximum height of 2 metres [1]. Internally three openings are visible in the broch wall [1]. One leads to a small chamber; a second leads to a long narrow gallery within the wall; and a third leads to the stone stair of which some twenty steps survive [1]. The broch was visited by Thomas Pennant in 1772, and it was still a substantial structure, with a height of perhaps 4 metres [1]. The broch was excavated by the Countess Vincent Baillet de Latour between 1914 and 1920 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94363", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94364", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1877a303/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1877a303/Dun_Beag_Broch,_Struan.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246461", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246462", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346386", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346387", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
