hat make it \"the richest and most significant example of a Bronze Age burial monument not only in the Normanton group or in association with Stonehenge, but arguably in the whole of Britain\" [1]. The items date the burial to the early Bronze Age, circa 1950 BC, and include a large \\''lozenge\\''-shaped sheet of gold, a sheet gold belt plate, three bronze daggers, a bronze axe, a stone macehead and bronze rivets, all held by the Wiltshire Museum, Devizes [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143887", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/18c1589b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/18c1589b/Bush Barrow - geograph.org.uk - 1622275.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('18f488c0-fce6-4ea4-b732-d23fe5759cd1'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:18f488c0-fce6-4ea4-b732-d23fe5759cd1:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Tell Yunatsite', '97465cdc68ff428cb58337b4338148b1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82088", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2051:chunk-0001: description ''Tell Yunatsite (Ploskata mogila) is a multi-period archaeological tell in Pazardzhik Province, southern Bulgaria, located 8 km west of Pazardzhik[1]. The mound rises 12 m above modern ground level and spans 110 m in diameter[1]. Situated on a low terrace at the former Topolnitsa riverbed near its confluence with the Maritsa River, the site contains layers from the Copper Age (associated with the Karanovo culture), Early Bronze Age, Iron Age, Roman, and Medieval periods[1].'' -> ''Tell Yunatsite, also known as Ploskata mogila, is situated in the Pazardzhik Province of southern Bulgaria, some 8 kilometres to the west of the district capital Pazardzhik [1]. The tell stands 12 metres above modern ground level and has a diameter of 110 m [1]. It is situated on a low terrace at the right bank of the former Topolnitsa riverbed near to its confluence with the Maritsa River (ca. 5 km or 3 mi away from the site) [1]. Medieval, Roman, Iron Age, Early Bronze Age, and Copper Age periods have all been attested at the site [1]. The Copper Age tell is associated with the Karanovo culture [1]. The tell contains the remains of at least 30 settlements placed one over the other [1]. Various peoples had settled at the tell altogether for more than 6,000 years, at least from the Early Chalcolithic (5000 BCE) onwards [1]. Tell Yunatsite is one of the most important sites for revealing the cultural development of the Early Bronze Age in Thrace [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143900", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/TellYunatsite.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/18f488c0/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
