he Copper Age tell is associated with the Karanovo culture [1]. The tell contains the remains of at least 30 settlements placed one over the other [1]. Various peoples had settled at the tell altogether for more than 6,000 years, at least from the Early Chalcolithic (5000 BCE) onwards [1]. Tell Yunatsite is one of the most important sites for revealing the cultural development of the Early Bronze Age in Thrace [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143900", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/TellYunatsite.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/18f488c0/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
