o rock-cut cisterns and remnants of other structures [1]. Caves are carved out of a solid black basalt rock [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94371", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143908", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/191e7642/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/191e7642/Buddha with attendents in Mahakali Caves.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235492", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235493", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307704", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/191e7642/Buddha with attendents in Mahakali Caves.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/191e7642/Mahakali_caves.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
