gionary camp by 15 AD, covering 20 hectares with a 1.8-km encircling wall. The site hosted Switzerland''s largest Roman amphitheatre, seating 10,000 spectators. A 1.2-mile Roman underground water canal still functions today, supplying the later Konigsfelden Monastery. The last garrison, Legio XI Claudia, departed in 101 AD when Trajan redeployed it to the Danube region. Listed as a Swiss heritage site of national significance.\" -> \"The only Roman legionary fortress of the 1st century AD in Switzerland, located at modern Windisch at the confluence of the Aare and Reuss rivers [1] [2] [3]. Established as a military post around 15 BC during Augustus''s Alpine campaign, it grew into a full legionary camp by 15 AD, covering 20 hectares with a 1.8-km encircling wall [1] [2] [3]. The site hosted Switzerland''s largest Roman amphitheatre [2] [4]. A Roman underground water canal still functions today, supplying the later Konigsfelden Monastery [2] [5]. The last garrison, Legio XI Claudia, departed in 101 AD when Trajan redeployed it to the Danube region [1] [2]. Listed as a Swiss heritage site of national significance [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307719", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/19ecf84c/Restaurierte Ruinen des Legionslagers Vindonissa.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/19ecf84c/Vindonissa.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355578", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Fortress'' -> ''Fortress/citadel''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('19f1118c-190f-47f7-a161-8d6cd52277e7'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:19f1118c-190f-47f7-a161-8d6cd52277e7:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Vela Spila Cave', '032d3aa1eed62b8eb23dec10f59dfa87', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43951", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0083:chunk-0001: description \"Vela Spila is a large elliptical cave above the town of Vela Luka on Korcula island, Croatia, measuring 40 metres long, 17 metres high, and 40 metres wide. One of Europe''s most important prehistoric sites, it contains a stratigraphic sequence spanning from the Late Upper Palaeolithic to the Bronze Age, with evidence of seasonal human presence from around 20,000 BC. Among only five European sites with Palaeolithic fired clay figurines, its 36 ceramic artifacts date to 17,500-15,000 years ago. Mesolithic child burials and secondary adult inhumations found here are rare examples of mortuary practices from that period.\" -> ''The Vela Spila cave is situated above the town of Vela Luka on the island of Korčula, in Croatia on Pinski Rat hill at an elevation of approximately 130 m [1]. The cave consists of an elliptically shaped cavern that measures 40 m in length, 17 m in height, and is approximately 40 m wide [1]. There are two openings in the roof of the cave which were caused by collapse at an as yet undetermined time [1]. The cave has been mentioned in the Korčula Statute back in the 15th century [1]. Scientific research of the cave started in the late 1940s [1]. Marinko Gjivoje took up work at the site in 1949 [1]. Further excavations between 2001 and 2006, produced 36 ceramic artifacts dated to the late Upper Palaeolithic period, about 17,500 to 15,000 years ago [1]. These finds are the only examples of ceramic figurative art in southeastern Europe during the Upper Palaeolithic [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94387", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94388", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-21000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143928", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Vela_Luka_Vela_spila_2002.jpg/400px-Vela_Luka_Vela_spila_2002.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/19f1118c/Vela spila 01518.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235499", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235500", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-20000''"}]'::jsonb),
