a Statute back in the 15th century [1]. Scientific research of the cave started in the late 1940s [1]. Marinko Gjivoje took up work at the site in 1949 [1]. Further excavations between 2001 and 2006, produced 36 ceramic artifacts dated to the late Upper Palaeolithic period, about 17,500 to 15,000 years ago [1]. These finds are the only examples of ceramic figurative art in southeastern Europe during the Upper Palaeolithic [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94387", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94388", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-21000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143928", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Vela_Luka_Vela_spila_2002.jpg/400px-Vela_Luka_Vela_spila_2002.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/19f1118c/Vela spila 01518.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235499", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235500", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-20000''"}]'::jsonb),
