tion [1]. This dolmen from the New Stone Age is believed to have been destroyed in the 17th or 18th century, because its large stones lay scattered on the fields [1]. Several of the stones were sunk into the ground, others had been carried away [1]. Excavations revealed that the burial chamber originally comprised 20 to 24 upright stones and about 8 capstones [1]. It had a side entrance; this type of grave is known as a passage grave [1]. The open space between the uprights and the capstones was sealed in with dry stonework [1]. The dead were laid on the floor of the burial chamber and prepared for the afterlife by being buried with their traditional jewellery, earthenware jars and everyday implements [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94415", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b48aaf6/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b48aaf6/Großsteingrab bei Siddernhausen Seiteneingang 20210912.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235514", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307746", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b48aaf6/Großsteingrab bei Siddernhausen Seiteneingang 20210912.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b48aaf6/GroßsteingrabSidd2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
