d Condover area was established as a Royal hunting forest.'' -> ''Bayston Hill is a village in Shropshire, England, located 5 km south of Shrewsbury, with evidence of both an Iron Age hillfort and a Roman settlement on its high grounds [1]. Archaeological surveys from 2001 identified six previously unknown historical sites including sections of at least one Roman road, medieval trackways, cropmarks suggesting historical earthworks, and medieval parish boundary stones [1]. The area also preserves remains of a Roman villa at Chapel Field near Whitley [2] [3] [4]. In the Middle Ages, the surrounding Bayston Hill and Condover area was established as a Royal hunting forest [1] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246491", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246492", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347151", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347152", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
