ety of animal species during extensive periods and is now home to nearly 30,000 bats [1]. Devetashka Cave is located approximately 2 km from the village of Devetaki [1]. The site is 35 m wide and 30 m high at the entrance [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b7b98d0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b7b98d0/Devetàshka_peshterà_(Devetàshka_cave).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321132", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b7b98d0/Devetàshka_peshterà_(Devetàshka_cave).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b7b98d0/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324964", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b7b98d0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b7b98d0/Devetaki cave.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
