an bridge. Its most famous feature is the monumental Epicurean inscription by 2nd-century AD philosopher Diogenes, originally approximately 25,000 words spanning over 200 feet of wall. By 2007, 299 fragments had been recovered, estimated at only 20-25% of the original text. The city joined the Lycian League in 84 BC.'' -> ''Oinoanda (or Oenoanda) was an ancient Lycian city on an isolated hilltop in the upper Xanthus valley, near modern Incealiler in Mugla Province, Turkey [1] [2]. The city joined the Lycian League in 84 BC [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1c0baadb/Oinoanda 4.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1c0baadb/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355582", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
