ogical excavations between 1960 and 1966 uncovered Roman walls dated to 180 AD along with the first Christian church from the 4th-5th century. The Lauriacum Museum, founded in 1892, displays over 1,200 artefacts including military equipment, funerary monuments, and a rare Roman ceiling fresco.'' -> ''Enns, in Upper Austria, stands on the site of Lauriacum, a major Roman legionary base on the Danube Limes [1] [2]. An extensive civilian settlement grew to the north and southwest, likely achieving municipal status in the early 3rd century and becoming the episcopal seat of northern Noricum in the 5th century [1] [2]. Archaeological excavations between 1960 and 1966 uncovered Roman walls dated to 180 AD [2] [3] [4].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331471", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1c4ac177/Stadtturm_von_Enns_mit_Wappen.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1c4ac177/Enns - Hauptplatz mit Stadtturm.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
