s and was designated a \"millennial find\". It is now displayed in the permanent archaeological exhibition at the Museum of the City of Skopje.'' -> ''Cerje is a Neolithic archaeological site located near the village of Govrlevo, south of Skopje, North Macedonia [1] [2] [3] [4]. Excavations uncovered houses from the Early and Middle Neolithic periods, built with sophisticated architectural techniques typical of the Balkan Neolithic [5]. The site\\''s most renowned find is the \"Adam of Macedonia,\" a ceramic male torso in a seated position excavated by archaeologist Milos Bilbija [5] [6] [7]. This figurine, noted for its accentuated anatomy and realistic art form, is considered one of the earliest prehistoric male figurines and was designated a \"millennial find\" [1] [2] [6]. It is now displayed in the permanent archaeological exhibition at the Museum of the City of Skopje [6] [7].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235532", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: lat ''41.99627851589683'' -> ''41.9325''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235533", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: lon ''21.431698883197658'' -> ''21.36222''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235534", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235535", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-6000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355583", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
