 Gupta script mentioning Jain sage Vairadeva, though some scholars suggest Maurya Empire origins as early as 319 BC [1]. The main cave has a rectangular interior with trapezoidal entrance reminiscent of the earlier Barabar Caves [1]. The name means ''store of gold,'' reflecting a persistent legend of hidden treasure within the cave walls [2] [3].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:339014", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-001-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/1cef558f/Swarn Bhandar Caves.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
