built in the 1st century AD [1]. Through the centuries Dun Carloway remained in use until the floor level was too high due to build-up of the occupation layers [1]. The broch was occasionally used in later times as a stronghold [1]. Dun Carloway is built on a rock on a steep south slope at the height of 50 metres [1]. It is the best preserved broch in the Outer Hebrides [1]. The wall of the broch rises on the south side to 9.2 metres [1]. Only Mousa Broch and Dun Telve have walls that are higher [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Fortification'' -> ''Minaret/tower''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94470", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94471", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144047", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1db1cb71/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1db1cb71/Carloway - Dun Carloway - 20180411092749.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235560", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235561", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307812", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1db1cb71/Carloway - Dun Carloway - 20180411092749.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1db1cb71/Dun_Carloway.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347169", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_c