s a Bronze Age funerary naveta on Menorca, Spain, dated to 1500-1000 BC, where collective inhumations were practised [1]. The structure has a circular layout with walls built using Cyclopean masonry [1]. It is classified as an \"intermediate naveta,\" potentially representing a transitional form between earlier megalithic tombs and later elongated navetas [1]. Archaeologist Maria Luisa Serra Belabre conducted a brief excavation in the 1960s [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307821", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1ddc9784/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1ddc9784/Biniac_oriental.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
