    ('1e9f1c86-dabd-4cf8-90f8-87c64a8ccc5c'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:1e9f1c86-dabd-4cf8-90f8-87c64a8ccc5c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Cave of Zeus, Naxos', '653c9e4a5f9a9ab885c2e26fd7d2a94b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82206", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2055:chunk-0001: description \"A large cave on the western slope of Mount Zas on Naxos, the highest peak in the Cyclades at 1,003 m, situated at 630 m elevation. The cave entrance widens to approximately 10 meters and extends about 75 meters deep, featuring impressive stalactites and stalagmites. Systematic excavations beginning in 1962 revealed artifacts spanning the Late Neolithic to the Early Cycladic III period, including copper tools now displayed in the Naxos Archaeological Museum. Greek mythology holds that the infant Zeus was hidden here from his father Kronos, and an archaic inscription on the path reads ''Oros Dios Milosiou'' (Mountain of Zeus of Milon), attesting to ancient shepherd worship of Zeus.\" -> ''The Cave of Zas, or Cave of Zeus, is an ancient Greek cave located on Mount Zas on the island of Naxos [1]. The cave was occupied from the Late Neolithic to Early Cycladic III periods [1]. Due to the lack of crop processing residue found, archaeologists suggest that the cave was not used for year-round settlement, but for herding animals during the driest period of the year [1]. Excavations of the cave were carried out in 1985-1986 and 1994 [1]. The Cave of Zas is 630m above sea level and located southeast of Filoti, a village at the foot of the mountain [1]. Large stalactites and stalagmites have been found inside the cave [1]. In Agathosthenes\\'' telling of the history of Naxos, Zeus spent his childhood in the cave, in hiding from his father, Cronus [1]. A rock carving found near the cave reads \"Zeus Melosios,\" referring to Zeus as the protector of the sheep [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114823", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-5000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144071", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1e9f1c86/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1e9f1c86/Between source of Arion and Cave of Zas, Coming to Cave, Naxos, 11H2195.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
