ng animals during the driest period of the year [1]. Excavations of the cave were carried out in 1985-1986 and 1994 [1]. The Cave of Zas is 630m above sea level and located southeast of Filoti, a village at the foot of the mountain [1]. Large stalactites and stalagmites have been found inside the cave [1]. In Agathosthenes\\'' telling of the history of Naxos, Zeus spent his childhood in the cave, in hiding from his father, Cronus [1]. A rock carving found near the cave reads \"Zeus Melosios,\" referring to Zeus as the protector of the sheep [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114823", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-5000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144071", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1e9f1c86/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1e9f1c86/Between source of Arion and Cave of Zas, Coming to Cave, Naxos, 11H2195.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
