pottery decorated in incised geometric patterns filled with white and red pigment [3] [4] [5]. The culture''s hallmark vessel is the rhyton, a four-legged decorated container with a large carrying handle, believed to have played an important role in Neolithic ritual practices [1] [3] [5].\""}]'::jsonb),
