ile limited archaeological excavations have been conducted at the site, the identification of Pyrri contributes to understanding the distribution of Roman settlements and road infrastructure in the Zagreb region during antiquity [1].\" -> \"Pyrri was an ancient Roman settlement in the Roman province of Pannonia, situated along a road connecting Poetovio (modern Ptuj, Slovenia) in the north to Siscia (modern Sisak, Croatia) in the south [1] [2] [3] [4]. Archaeological evidence and scholarly research suggest the settlement''s location corresponds to the present-day village of Komin in the Sveti Ivan Zelina area of Zagreb County, Croatia [1] [5].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235586", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246541", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246542", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355588", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2101b2c7-9dd5-4dbf-b140-9c24ae364da8'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2101b2c7-9dd5-4dbf-b140-9c24ae364da8:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Coppa Nevigata', '12f3898be09853f4b7b2941b078d166a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82242", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2056:chunk-0001: description ''Coppa Nevigata is a multi-period archaeological site on the Apulian coast of the Gargano peninsula in Foggia province, southern Italy. The earliest occupation dates to the Neolithic period, between the 7th and 5th millennia BC, when the site sat at the edge of a coastal lagoon with easy access to marine resources. During the Bronze Age, it developed into a significant fortified settlement with contacts reaching the Aegean world, evidenced by fragments of Mycenaean ceramics. The site provides early evidence for the extraction of purple dye from murex shells and olive oil pressing from the Protoapennine phase onward.'' -> ''Coppa Nevigata is an archaeological site in the province of Foggia, southern Italy, southwest of Manfredonia, on the Apulian coast of the Gargano peninsula [1]. The earliest recorded human presence on the site, which was situated on the edge of a coastal lagoon, with easy access to the sea and numerous natural resources, dates back to the Neolithic, between the 7th and 5th millennia BC [1]. During the Bronze Age, a significant settlement arose that had contacts with the civilizations of the Aegean; these contacts are most visible during the Subapennine phase, when fragments of Mycenaean ceramics are found at the site [1]. From the beginning of the Protoapennine phase, there is evidence for the extraction of purple dye from murex shells and for pressing of olives to extract olive oil [1]. The purple dye production, starting around 1800 BC, is the earliest yet attested in Italy [1]. This dye production increased through the 14th century BC, but sharply dropped off by the 12th century in the Subapennine phase [1]. The site was defended by dry stone fortification walls [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95179", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95180", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-6000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235589", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235590", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-6000''"}]'::jsonb),
