 the Bronze Age, a significant settlement arose that had contacts with the civilizations of the Aegean; these contacts are most visible during the Subapennine phase, when fragments of Mycenaean ceramics are found at the site [1]. From the beginning of the Protoapennine phase, there is evidence for the extraction of purple dye from murex shells and for pressing of olives to extract olive oil [1]. The purple dye production, starting around 1800 BC, is the earliest yet attested in Italy [1]. This dye production increased through the 14th century BC, but sharply dropped off by the 12th century in the Subapennine phase [1]. The site was defended by dry stone fortification walls [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95179", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95180", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-6000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235589", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235590", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-6000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2121c097-4bc4-4763-9534-ba57efa1437d'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2121c097-4bc4-4763-9534-ba57efa1437d:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Torralba and Ambrona - Archaeological Site', '99cbc9cf37fd7543b3b4e80aa9b11b1f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -398050"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82244", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2056:chunk-0001: description ''Two Lower Paleolithic archaeological and paleontological sites in the Province of Soria, Castile and Leon, Spain, at least 350,000 years old. The sites preserve Acheulean stone tool assemblages including hand axes, cleavers, and racloirs, made from flint, quartzite, limestone, and quartz. Elephant remains are the most represented fauna across most levels. First excavated by the Marquis of Cerralbo (1909-1914), later by F. Clark Howell in the 1960s, and CENIEH campaigns continue to the present. Research has shown the sites were not contemporaneous, with Torralba dating 300,000-200,000 years ago.'' -> ''Torralba and Ambrona are two paleontological and archaeological sites that correspond to various fossiliferous levels with Acheulean lithic industry associated, at least about 350,000 years old [1]. The sites, traditionally studied together, are about 3 km distant [1]. From these sites have been obtained fossils of large mammals, mainly elephants, with remains of nearly fifty individuals from each site, in addition to large bovines and horses [1]. The sites show evidence of successive occupations by human beings, who had a hunting station or, more likely, scavanged carrion and carried out quartering [1]. The American anthropologist Francis Clark Howell conducted six excavation campaigns in Torralba and Ambrona, between 1961 and 1963 and in 1980, 1981 and 1983 [1]. The abundant accumulations of elephant remains in Ambrona are similar to the modern sites popularly known as \"Elephants\\'' graveyards\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95183", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95184", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-350000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144621", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/Palaeoloxodon_antiquus_-_in_situ_fossil_bones_-_Ambrona.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2121c097/Ambrona - sala de la exposición permanente vista hacia el NO.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246543", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246544", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308468", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2121c097/Ambrona - sala de la exposición permanente vista hacia el NO.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2121c097/Palaeoloxodon_antiquus_-_in_situ_fossil_bones_-_Ambrona.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347181", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347182", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-