rom each site, in addition to large bovines and horses [1]. The sites show evidence of successive occupations by human beings, who had a hunting station or, more likely, scavanged carrion and carried out quartering [1]. The American anthropologist Francis Clark Howell conducted six excavation campaigns in Torralba and Ambrona, between 1961 and 1963 and in 1980, 1981 and 1983 [1]. The abundant accumulations of elephant remains in Ambrona are similar to the modern sites popularly known as \"Elephants\\'' graveyards\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95183", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95184", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-350000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144621", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/Palaeoloxodon_antiquus_-_in_situ_fossil_bones_-_Ambrona.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2121c097/Ambrona - sala de la exposición permanente vista hacia el NO.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246543", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246544", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308468", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2121c097/Ambrona - sala de la exposición permanente vista hacia el NO.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2121c097/Palaeoloxodon_antiquus_-_in_situ_fossil_bones_-_Ambrona.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347181", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remedia