    ('23242c3f-c221-4689-a166-af4f464f5c1b'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:23242c3f-c221-4689-a166-af4f464f5c1b:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Necropolis of Fossa', 'd28a3958cd41e150fc0b03edd1f522cb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 24 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27820", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0014:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1000'' -> ''-900''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35693", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-900'' -> ''-1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82286", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2057:chunk-0001: description ''The Necropolis of Fossa, known as \"Abruzzo\\''s Little Stonehenge,\" is an Italic burial ground in the commune of Fossa, Province of L\\''Aquila, discovered in 1992. Covering 3,500 square meters with about 500 graves, it spans nearly 1,000 years (9th-1st century BC) across three phases: Iron Age, Orientalizing-Archaic, and Hellenistic. Used by the Vestini people and later by Romans, the site features tumuli with stone circles, chamber tombs, and pit graves. Finds include ceramics, jewelry, funerary beds, bronze razors, and iron weapons.'' -> \"Necropolis of Fossa was an Italic necropolis, the ruins of which are located in the comune of Fossa, in the province of L''Aquila in the Abruzzo region of Italy [1]. The origins of the necropolis of Fossa are attributed to the first population residing in the area, the Vestini on Monte Cerro, where remains of a fortified village dating back to between the 9th and 8th century BC can be found [1]. Later, the development of Aveia during the Roman era continued its use until around the 1st century BC [1]. The area is located in an alluvial zone on the eastern bank of the Aterno river [1]. It was discovered accidentally in 1992 during excavations for the construction of an industrial warehouse [1]. The excavated area covers 3,500 m², with approximately 500 tombs of different types (tumuli, pits, chamber tombs, and infant burials in ceramic tiles) dating back to three main periods [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144678", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Fossa_AQ_-_Necropoli_15.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/23242c3f/Fossa AQ - Necropoli 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321187", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/23242c3f/Fossa AQ - Necropoli 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/23242c3f/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324972", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/23242c3f/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/23242c3f/Fossa AQ - Necropoli 15.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
