ing tree. Similar rock signs are common across Southern Azerbaijan and Eastern Anatolia.'' -> ''The Nakhchivan Rock Signs were discovered in 2016 at Agsal, between the villages of Erefse and Milax in the Culfa (Julfa) region of Azerbaijan [1] [2]. Three rock signs were found featuring drainage channels directed towards the canyon, suggesting fluid flow [1]. Similar rock signs are common across Southern Azerbaijan and Eastern Anatolia [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246885", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246886", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347192", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347193", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('23cd75bc-22da-4f28-aa83-f527fdf84e2e'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '1', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:23cd75bc-22da-4f28-aa83-f527fdf84e2e:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''1'' restored on Qilakitsoq', 'e9b2a672c0c56d9bd6059fa254484207', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0086:chunk-0001: description \"Qilakitsoq (Greenlandic for ''that which has very little sky'') is an archaeological site on Greenland''s Nuussuaq Peninsula near Uummannaq, famous for the 1972 discovery of eight naturally mummified Inuit bodies dated to approximately 1475 AD. Found by hunters Hans and Jokum Gronvold in two graves a metre apart, the corpses were stacked with animal hide layers between them and freeze-dried by Arctic conditions. The mummies -- all women and children -- are the best-preserved human remains found in North America, retaining skin, hair, tattoos, and intestinal contents showing a diet of 75% marine products. Four of the mummies are now displayed at the Greenland National Museum in Nuuk.\" -> ''Qilakitsoq is an abandoned settlement and an important archaeological site in Greenland [1]. It is the location of the discovery of eight mummified corpses from the Thule period [1]. These Inuit mummies offer important insights into the lives of Inuit about 500 years ago [1]. Qilakitsoq is located in Kitaa near the city of Uummannaq on the northern coast of the Nuussuaq peninsula in a sheltered cove of the Karrat Fjord [1]. In the time of the Thule culture, which lasted until about 1800, a settlement of about thirty hunter-gatherers was located here [1]. On October 9, 1972, two hunters discovered a grave containing several mummies while they were out hunting for rock ptarmigans [1]. Radiocarbon dating yielded a probable time of death around 1475 with a margin of error of about ±50 years [1]. A total of 78 articles of clothing were discovered [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95257", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95258", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Qilakitsoq_I-1.jpg/400px-Qilakitsoq_I-1.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/23cd75bc/Qilakitsoq mummies (Kenny McFly).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246889", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246890", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347194", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347195", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''1000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
