oeotian city on a ledge 300 m above sea level on the north slope of Mount Cithaeron [1] [2]. Allied with Athens from c. 519 BC, Plataea sent 1,000 soldiers to the Battle of Marathon in 490 BC [2] [3]. In 479 BC, Greek forces under Pausanias defeated the Persian army of Mardonius, decisively ending Persian expansion into mainland Greece [4] [5]. The city was repeatedly destroyed by Thebes and Sparta before Philip II and Alexander rebuilt it after 338 BC [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347198", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347199", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355590", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
