d Sparta before Philip II and Alexander rebuilt it after 338 BC.'' -> ''Ancient Boeotian city on a ledge 300 m above sea level on the north slope of Mount Cithaeron [1] [2]. Allied with Athens from c. 519 BC, Plataea sent 1,000 soldiers to the Battle of Marathon in 490 BC [2] [3]. In 479 BC, Greek forces under Pausanias defeated the Persian army of Mardonius, decisively ending Persian expansion into mainland Greece [4] [5]. The city was repeatedly destroyed by Thebes and Sparta before Philip II and Alexander rebuilt it after 338 BC [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347198", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347199", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355590", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('23ee2849-5bee-4742-91b1-29a35361fcf7'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:23ee2849-5bee-4742-91b1-29a35361fcf7:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Barrow Clump', '0363376d81c924555fe4ecfd397ea2a5', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Barrow'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 34 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44047", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0086:chunk-0001: description ''Barrow Clump is a Neolithic and Early Bronze Age barrow on Salisbury Plain in Wiltshire, England, located about 5.6 km (3.5 mi) north of Amesbury[1]. The site, a scheduled monument, represents over 5,000 years of human activity—originally a Neolithic settlement, later used as a burial mound in the Early Bronze Age, and re-used as a cemetery in the Anglo-Saxon period[2]. Other barrows in the group have been lost to ploughing[1].'' -> ''Barrow Clump is an archaeological site in Figheldean parish, Wiltshire, England, about 3+1⁄2 miles north of the town of Amesbury [1]. Barrow Clump lies on the northwestern slope of rising ground about 700 metres east of the village of Ablington [1]. The surviving part of the monument is a bowl barrow about 30 metres in diameter [1]. The barrow was constructed in the early Bronze Age on the site of a Neolithic settlement, and much later, around the 6th century, it was re-used as an Anglo-Saxon cemetery [1]. Partial excavations were carried out in the 19th century, in the early 20th century by Lt Col William Hawley, and in 2003–2004 by English Heritage [1]. Permission was granted for full excavation in 2012–2014 in order to record the site, which was being extensively damaged by badgers [1]. Many Bronze Age items were found, with a smaller quantity from the Neolithic period [1]. Many Saxon graves were uncovered, together with items including a bucket-shaped drinking vessel, made from pieces of yew wood bound together with bronze [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95263", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95264", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235617", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}]'::jsonb),
