    ('24553e33-f5bd-409d-bf2f-04c193eb63cf'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:24553e33-f5bd-409d-bf2f-04c193eb63cf:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Judeir-jo-daro', 'edf998013896576e46026ecd678302e8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 130 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82316", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2058:chunk-0001: description \"Judeir-jo-daro (also Damb Judeir) is a Mature Harappan period (c. 2600-1900 BCE) archaeological site in the Kachhi plain of Nasirabad District, Balochistan, Pakistan. The site consists of five small mounds divided by rainwater gullies, with surface surveys identifying Harappan-style pottery sherds. Located between the Indus River basin and the Balochistan highlands, it likely functioned as a trade node connecting core Indus regions to the highland interior. It is a federally protected site under Pakistan''s Antiquities Act of 1975, though it faces significant conservation challenges from erosion.\" -> ''Judeir-jo-daro, also known as Damb Judeir, is an archaeological site dating back to the Harappan period in Balochistan, Pakistan [1]. The city, during its time, was a moderate sized settlement with a population of around 20,240 and an area of 2,700,000 square feet (62 acres) [1]. The present day site is a federally protected archaeological site located between Jhatpat and Dera Murad Jamali in the Nasirabad District of Balochistan [1].''"}, {