ite, but this only lasted about forty years, then was decommissioned [1]. There was extensive Roman activity prompted by the fort, which was connected westward by a road to the Icknield Street, and to the east by a road to Sawley on the River Trent [1]. A fort-vicus which manufactured pottery and worked iron was founded 600m to the east on the Sawley Road [1]. The fort was later re-occupied and re-used for a further twenty five years [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95281", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fort''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('251ac618-a557-4c31-9129-65afc47b649d'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:251ac618-a557-4c31-9129-65afc47b649d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Sybaris on the Traeis', '7a7727e501492970ec9f1f63039652e9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 316 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33449", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0019:chunk-0001: description ''Sybaris on the Traeis was an ancient Greek colony of Magna Graecia located on the Traeis river (modern Trionto) in southern Italy[1]. It was founded around 444 BC by Sybarite refugees who fled Thurii after most of them were killed by other Greek settlers in a violent conflict[1]. The city shared its name with the original Sybaris, which had been destroyed in 510 BC[1]. Sybaris on the Traeis lasted only about a century before being destroyed by the Bruttii around 356/355 BC[1].'' -> ''Sybaris on the Traeis was an ancient city situated on the Traeis river, now known as the Trionto [1]. It shares its name with the original city of Sybaris which was destroyed in 510 BC [1]. Its former inhabitants built a new city, Thurii, not far from the site of Sybaris [1]. This new colony was founded together with other Greek settlers in 446/445 BC [1]. Soon a conflict arose between the two groups and most of the Sybarites were killed by the other Greek colonists of Thurii [1]. Some of them managed to flee and founded Sybaris on the Traeis [1]. John Wo