 [1]. Its dimensions are 36 metres north-west to south-east by 30 metres north-east to south-west [1]. There are 16 stones of local pink granite, set about 5.5 metres apart; a larger gap on the east side is thought to be an original entrance [1]. Four of these are upright, with heights 0.7 to 1.3 metres; the rest are recumbent [1]. A thick layer of peat was found above the ground surface [1]. A flint tool was found, and spreads of charcoal which may be the traces of fire-rituals [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95294", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95295", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144713", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Threestoneburn_Stone_Circle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1836990.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/257fe33f/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246912", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347206", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347207", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2900''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2590803d-1be8-4d57-abc5-2b10da46806d'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2590803d-1be8-4d57-abc5-2b10da46806d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Tomb of Menecrates', '8ee9667a48719ae1255e1502632877fb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 24 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82348", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2059:chunk-0001: description ''The Tomb of Menecrates is an Archaic-period cenotaph in Corfu, Greece, built around 600 BC in the ancient city of Korkyra[1]. The tomb and its funerary lion sculpture were discovered in 1843 during demolition of a Venetian-era fortress at Garitsa hill by British forces of the United States of the Ionian Islands[1]. Dated to the sixth century BC, the monument represents a rare example of Archaic funerary architecture in the western Greek world[1].'' -> ''The Tomb of Menecrates or Monument of Menecrates is an Archaic-period cenotaph in Corfu built around 600 BC in the ancient city of Korkyra [1]. The tomb and the funerary sculpture of a lion were discovered in 1843 during demolition works by the British army in the United States of the Ionian Islands who were demolishing a Venetian-era fortress in the site of Garitsa hill in Corfu [1]. According to an Ancient Greek inscription found on the grave, the tomb was a monument built by the ancient Korkyreans in honour of their proxenos Menecrates, son of Tlasias, from Oiantheia [1]. Both the tomb and the sculpture are made of local limestone [1]. The tomb is cylindrical with a conical roof [1]. The cylindrical part consists of five circular rings made of stones of equal thickness featuring isodomic construction [1]. The monument is 1.4 m in height and 4.7–4.9 m in diameter [1]. The inscription is one of the oldest extant in Greece [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144714", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/Tomb_of_Menekrates_in_Corfu.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2590803d/Tomb of Menecrates in Corfu.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2590803d/Tomb of Menecrates in Corfu.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2590803d/Tomb_of_Menekrates_in_Corfu.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
