nal number [1]. The stones are broad rather than tall, and are less than 1 metre tall [1]. Prior to 1909 most of the stones had fallen [1]. It was restored in that year, and a trial excavation is said to have yielded a small amount of charcoal and one rough flint flake [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95305", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95306", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246917", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246918", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308567", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/262b6a28/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/262b6a28/Stone Circle at Brisworthy - geograph.org.uk - 9820.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347212", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347213", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('264ac74e-f5bc-4b73-b28a-c2db99132c50'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:264ac74e-f5bc-4b73-b28a-c2db99132c50:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Wednesbury', '87ea13d82accda3eb626ded4993a4084', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82376", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2060:chunk-0001: description ''A market town in the West Midlands whose name derives from Old English meaning \"Woden\\''s Fort,\" one of the few English places named after a pre-Christian deity. Church Hill is believed to have hosted an Iron Age hillfort, and a large ditch excavated at St Mary\\''s Road in 2008 predating the early medieval period supports this interpretation. The fortification may have been reused by Aethelflaed, Lady of the Mercians, as an Anglo-Saxon burh in the early 10th century.'' -> ''Wednesbury is situated five miles southeast of Wolverhampton, three miles southwest of Walsall and seven miles northwest of Birmingham [1]. The substantial remains of a large ditch excavated in St Mary\\''s Road in 2008 has been interpreted as part of a hilltop enclosure and possibly the Iron Age hillfort long suspected on the site [1]. The first authenticated spelling of the name was Wodensbyri, written in an endorsement on the back of the copy of the will of Wulfric Spot, dated 1004 [1]. Wednesbury (\"Woden\\''s borough\") is one of a number of places in England to be named after the pre-Christian deity Woden, the leader of the Old English pantheon [1]. During the Anglo-Saxon period there are believed to have been two battles fought in Wednesbury, in 592 and 715 [1]. According to The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle there was \"a great slaughter\" in 592 and \"Ceawlin was driven out\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95307", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95308", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144726", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/St_Bartholomew%27s_Wednesbury.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/264ac74e/Wednesbury_-_the_High_Street.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246919", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246920", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308570", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/264ac74e/Wednesbury_-_the_High_Street.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/264ac74e/St_Bartholomew''s_Wednesbury.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347215", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
