 cairn with unique stone causeways radiating to standing stones [2]. The passages align to the midwinter sunset, and the standing stones are graded in height with the tallest facing the setting sun [1] [2]. The site is the type-site for about 50 similar Clava-type cairns found across the Moray Firth region [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308579", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/26b6f958/2018 07 10 Schottland (54) Balnuaran of Clava.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/26b6f958/Ring_Cairn.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347217", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: lat ''57.477915335686546'' -> ''57.473115''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347218", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: lon ''-4.224785833093299'' -> ''-4.073982''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('26c567ca-9af0-486b-9599-dcb0b7792628'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:26c567ca-9af0-486b-9599-dcb0b7792628:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Anakeion', '351ed35622e1a9087f86b68e7e318305', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2060:chunk-0001: description ''A 5th-century BC sanctuary in Athens dedicated to the Dioskouroi (Castor and Pollux), located on the east slope of the Acropolis near the cave of Aglauros. It served as a key military assembly point, as described by Thucydides when soldiers gathered there during the oligarchic unrest of 411 BC. The annual Anakeia festival held here featured animal sacrifices for military protection. Its exact location remains debated, with limited archaeological remains identified.'' -> ''The Anakeion or Anacaeum, also known as the Sanctuary of the Dioskouroi, was a temple in Athens [1]. The name of the temple derives from the Greek Ἄνακες (an archaic form of ἄνακτες, \"lords\" or \"kings\"), the title by which the Dioskouroi, Castor and Pollux, twin sons of Zeus and Leda, were commonly known in Attica [1]. The Old Agora, the predecessor of the Classical Agora, was used in the fifth century and before as a rallying point, and references in Andokides and Thucydides to musters at the Anakeion in 415 and 411 BCE have led scholars to conclude that the Anakeion may have lain within the vicinity of the Old Agora, perhaps to the east of the Acropolis [1]. The decoration of the Anakeion, according to Pausanias, fell to Mikon and Polygnotos [1]. The former depicted the Argonauts, the followers of Jason, with particular attention to Akastos and his horses [1]. Polygnotos depicted the Rape of the Leukippides: the forcible abduction and marriage of Phoebe and Hilaeira, daughters of Leukippos, by the Dioskouroi [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95309", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95310", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144744", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/26c567ca/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246921", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246922", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347219", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347220", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
