e bowl, and harp fragments, now held in the British Museum. It was the richest Anglo-Saxon burial known until the discovery of Sutton Hoo in the 1930s. The village name derives from Old English meaning \"Taeppa\\''s barrow\".'' -> ''Taplow is best known for the Taplow Barrow, a 7th-century Anglo-Saxon burial mound [1] [2]. Excavated in 1883, it contained the lavishly furnished grave of a chieftain or prince [2]. Grave goods included a sword, spears, shields, a gold buckle, drinking horns, glass beakers, now held in the British Museum [2]. It was the richest Anglo-Saxon burial known until the discovery of Sutton Hoo in the 1930s [2]. The village name derives from Old English meaning \"Taeppa\\''s barrow\" [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246927", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246928", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347221", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347222", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('270c2134-0bdc-4874-a038-d1b7c0bd80a4'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:270c2134-0bdc-4874-a038-d1b7c0bd80a4:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Romuald''s Cave', 'b74dd953b075a4c7807b175d46669e2f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -300000"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33451", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0019:chunk-0001: description \"Romuald''s Cave (Croatian: Romualdova pećina) is a cave in western Istria County, Croatia, containing the oldest known cave paintings in southeast Europe, dating to around 35,000 years ago [1]. The site also preserves traces of both animal and human Upper Paleolithic habitation [1]. Although excavations began in the late 19th century, the paintings were only discovered in 2010 by Professor Darko Komšo, with findings published in Antiquity in 2019 [1].\" -> \"Romuald''s Cave is located on the eastern slopes of the Lim channel, at an altitude of 106 m [1]. Beginning with the end of 19th century, it was excavated multiple times by various archaeologists [1]. It gained notability in the 1980s with the work of Professor Mirko Malez, who was the first to note the existence of Upper Paleolithic stone tools [1]. Subsequent research revealed further stone tools and animal remains from Pleistocene and Holocene, as well as ceramics, fauna and human skeletal remains from both the Bronze and Iron Age [1]. A total of 44 paintings were found in Roumald''s Cave [1]. The paintings, all of which were made with red pigment, stretch between 32–46 m from the entrance, and are divided into four panels: three on the left and one on the right wall [1]. 28 out of 44 paintings are located on the left panel L2, which also contains all four of the cave''s figurative depictions [1]. Two of the four figurative depictions are of animals: a bison and an ibex [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95317", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95318", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-35000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246929", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347223", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347224", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-300000''"}]'::jsonb),
