s, all of which were made with red pigment, stretch between 32–46 m from the entrance, and are divided into four panels: three on the left and one on the right wall [1]. 28 out of 44 paintings are located on the left panel L2, which also contains all four of the cave''s figurative depictions [1]. Two of the four figurative depictions are of animals: a bison and an ibex [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95317", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95318", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-35000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246929", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347223", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347224", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-300000''"}]'::jsonb),
