re town, uncovering sixty houses, the cemetery, a road system connecting everything and a central building which she called \"the palace\" [1]. The town itself is centered around the palatial complex which is located on the central-West side of the town [1]. During the Middle Minoan IB period (1925–1875 B.C.E.) substantial construction began which was later destroyed in the Middle Minoan II period (1875–1700 B.C.E.) [1]. Rebuilding occurred in the Middle Minoan III period, which included the palace complex [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Castle/palace'' -> ''Town''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145351", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/277be4f6/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/277be4f6/Gournia_024.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/277be4f6/Gournia_024.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/277be4f6/Gournia_Minoan_Palace_1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355595", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Town'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
