June solstice. The 2003 Thomson-Ziegler expedition extensively mapped the complex and concluded it served as an important rest stop and roadside shrine on the Inca trail, forming part of the ceremonial network supporting Machu Picchu.\" -> ''An Inca archaeological complex approximately 5 km west of Machu Picchu in the Cusco Region, Peru, first discovered by Hiram Bingham in 1912 [1] [2]. The site contains over 80 structures across a 4 by 2 km area, including a remarkable 145-foot corridor with 6-foot walls aligned at 65 degrees toward Machu Picchu, pointing to the sunrise during the June solstice [3]. The 2003 Thomson-Ziegler expedition extensively mapped the complex and concluded it served as an important rest stop and roadside shrine on the Inca trail, forming part of the ceremonial network supporting Machu Picchu [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235648", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''1401''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235649", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Religious''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:339344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-002-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/28163f7d/Patallacta from Inca Trail.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2817ce5e-3b43-445e-9a10-d4115a7036bb'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2817ce5e-3b43-445e-9a10-d4115a7036bb:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Barranc de Gàfols', '83c47f0b09823af8bbe8e357a1253e60', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 130 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2006:chunk-0001: description ''Barranc de Gàfols (also called Pomeralet) is an archaeological site near Ginestar on the west bank of the river Ebro in Catalonia, Spain. It is one of the most significant Early Iron Age sites in the region, with continuous occupation from the Late Bronze Age through the First Iron Age. Discovered in 1988 and excavated from 1990 to 1998, the site revealed a small organized settlement of at least 13 enclosures separated by three rectilinear streets, dated to around 590-580 BC. The settlement shows early use of moulded mudbrick construction and evidence of Phoenician trade contacts from the Straits area.'' -> ''The Barranc de Gàfols, also referred as Pomeralet, is an archaeological site in Ginestar, Catalonia [1]. It is one of the most important First Iron Age sites in Catalonia, since it presents a continuous occupation since the Last Bronze Age [1]. The site is located 1 km south of Ginestar, in the west bank of the river Ebro [1]. The site was first occupied during the Late Bronze Age, when cottages were established [1]. During the First Iron Age, relatively complex rectangular and trapezoid buildings were planned, with the creation of at least 17 households and 3 streets [1]. Some of these buildings correspond to private households, since a fireplace has been found in each one of the structures, except one which has been identified as a common building devoted to agricultural activities, due to the presence of stone mills [1]. In 1990, excavation works began in Gàfols and continued until 1998 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95347", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95348", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95349", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145368", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2817ce5e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2817ce5e/Barranc de Gàfols kiln.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235650", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246945", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246946", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2817ce5e/Barranc de Gàfols kiln.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2817ce5e/Barranc_de_Gàfols_back_buildings.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355596", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-