cross; small and large ships; animals (deer and dogs), as well as various other images [1]. Small strokes in the rowing ship symbolise the crew members [1]. The \"hook\" on the ship image indicates a Lur [1]. The unusual image of a man carrying a ship is almost exactly the same as the depiction of shipbearer on another rock face in Bohuslän [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95367", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95368", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246951", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246952", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/291542d5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/291542d5/Strömstad Massleberg Skee 614-1 IMG 8921 ID 10159506140001.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347239", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347240", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('29440d54-9b26-4f92-9f0c-b7573373d12c'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:29440d54-9b26-4f92-9f0c-b7573373d12c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Cave of La Pasiega', '217c153ff732d9b3f3d1c9158ee3cac6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Rock art'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 29 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33469", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0019:chunk-0001: description ''The Cave of La Pasiega in Puente Viesgo, Cantabria, was discovered in 1911 by Hugo Obermaier and Paul Wernert. Spanning approximately 400 metres with four main galleries, it contains more than 700 images including paintings, engravings, and petroglyphs. About 40% depict animals such as deer, horses, ibex, and bison, while the rest are abstract symbols including tectiforms and a notable ladder-shaped sign dated to around 64,000 years ago, attributed to Neanderthals. A UNESCO World Heritage Site since 2008 as part of the Cave of Altamira and Paleolithic Cave Art of Northern Spain, the cave remains permanently closed to preserve its art.'' -> \"Cueva de La Pasiega, or Cave of La Pasiega, situated in the Spanish municipality of Puente Viesgo, is one of the most important monuments of Paleolithic art in Cantabria [1]. The recorded remains belong mainly to the Upper Solutrean and the Lower Magdalenian ages, although older objects are also found [1]. Throughout the cave are many ''walls'' with paintings and with engraved or incised images [1]. There are representations of equines (horses), cervids (deer, male and female) and bovines (cattle) [1]. There are also many abstract symbols (idiomorphs), suggesting patterns of repeated characters [1]. The scientific discovery of the La Pasiega can be credited to Werner and Hugo Obermaier [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145415", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/29440d54/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/29440d54/Cueva_de_la_Pasiega,Puente_Viesgo..webp''"}]'::jsonb),
