f Christianity in Late Antiquity [1]. T. A. B. Spratt visited the site for two days in 1842 to copy inscriptions and drew a plan [1]. A 1998 study of coins in the Antalya Museum led to the identification of the name of Kitanaura [1]. The acropolis of Kitanaura was located on a hill extending in an east–west direction and surrounded by remains of structures to its south and west [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96293", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96294", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145477", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2ac1dae4/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246967", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347258", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347259", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''1'' -> ''-323''"}]'::jsonb),
