 vertebrate remains, including the Kudaro cave bear.'' -> ''Kudaro is a complex of Paleolithic cave sites in the highlands of Georgia, located at approximately 1,600 meters above sea level [1]. The caves contain Lower Paleolithic Acheulean artifacts including bifaces, choppers, and sidescrapers [1] [2] [3]. Radiothermoluminescent dating of the Acheulean layer (5c) yielded dates of 360,000 years ago [4]. The caves also yielded Middle Pleistocene vertebrate remains, including the Kudaro cave bear [5] [6].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246971", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246972", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347261", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: lat ''42.190763629610124'' -> ''42.519722''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347262", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: lon ''43.438469873003335'' -> ''43.634167''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355602", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Cave'' -> ''Cave Structures''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357097", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357098", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-358050''"}]'::jsonb),
