 Magdalenian culture of the Upper Palaeolithic, but the cave was probably inhabited before that time [1]. The Tito Bustillo Cave has been designated a World Heritage Site, as part of the Cave of Altamira and Paleolithic Cave Art of Northern Spain, and it has 12 prehistorical paintings [1]. The oldest of these paintings shows human figures and is around 33,000 years old [1]. Apart from the paintings, some objects from the Magdalenian period were perfectly preserved [1]. The most important ones are some harpoons made of bone and a carved staghorn of a goat head [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/60/Tito_Bustillo_entrada.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2bf713bc/Cueva Tito Bustillo (01) Arqueoloxicu.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308689", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2bf713bc/Cueva Tito Bustillo (01) Arqueoloxicu.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2bf713bc/Tito_Bustillo_entrada.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2c05946f-80d4-4caf-8294-f1e2948d69b9'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2c05946f-80d4-4caf-8294-f1e2948d69b9:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Atella', '87f6c55ca5dff4137f8c0b039886b5d6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 316 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33513", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0020:chunk-0001: description ''Atella was an ancient Oscan city in Campania, located 20 km north of Naples [1]. One of the oldest cities in Campania, it was among the first to receive Roman citizenship (civitas) [1]. The Via Atellana crossed the city, connecting Cumae to the southwest and Capua to the northeast [1]. A section of this Roman road still exists today under the same name in Frattaminore [1]. Archaeological excavations have uncovered city walls, private houses, and the \"garden of the Lucceii\" [1]. It gave its name to the Fabula Atellana, a form of early Roman farcical comedy [2][3].'' -> \"Atella was an ancient Oscan city of Campania, located 20km directly north of Naples [1]. The ruins of the city walls, private houses, the so-called garden of Virgil and many tombs remain, on sites in the comuni of Frattaminore, Orta di Atella, Sant''Arpino and Succivo [1]. Atella was a city of Oscan origin, one of the oldest in Campania and one of the first to have obtained the Roman civitas [1]. It was crossed by the Via Atellana, which led southwest to Cumae and northeast to Capua [1]. Atella is not mentioned until the Second Punic War, when, although an independent city striking its own coinage, it was allied with Capua and the other Campanian cities in siding with Carthage after the battle of Cannae [1]. It was occupied by Rome in 210 BC, the chief citizens executed and the survivors enslaved or exiled to Calatia; the city was refounded as a home for the refugees from Nuceria [1]. In the 1st century BC, Cicero speaks highly of it and appears to have been its patron; it continued into imperial times as a municipium [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96305", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96306", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96307", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145540", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2c05946f/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236513", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236514", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: site_type None -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355603", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
