rks, a form of ancient rock art. The site is registered in the Danish Sites and Monuments Record and rated in near-perfect structural condition.\" -> \"Stenseby is a Neolithic passage grave (jaettestue) near St Bodil''s Church on the Danish island of Bornholm [1] [2]. In 1882, schoolteacher and archaeologist J. A. Jorgensen excavated the tomb, uncovering several hundred amber beads, flint tools, a sandstone axe, and decorated pottery [2] [3]. Later excavations in the 1920s yielded a Bronze Age pot [2] [3]. The site is registered in the Danish Sites and Monuments Record [3] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236521", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321262", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/2c621de8/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2c621de8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2c621de8/BodilskerStationSporside.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
