 [1]. Based on their typology, the materials found in the excavation, and study of their magnetic properties, archaeologists have dated the ovens 1 and 2 to the 1st and 2nd centuries AD [1]. The name Fornaca, documented for the first time in 1290 at the castle of Speculum Vilassar, gives clues about the antiquity of the area of industrial production [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145605", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Catalonia_VilassarDeDalt_FornsRomansFornaca_Forns1I2_B.JPG/400px-Catalonia_VilassarDeDalt_FornsRomansFornaca_Forns1I2_B.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2cc719f3/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
