icance. Other hypotheses propose stone flour production via spinning wheels or natural erosion from glacial meltwater.'' -> ''Sliprannor i Gantofta is a sandstone outcrop near Helsingborg in Scania, Sweden, covered with grooves along the Raa river valley escarpment [1] [2]. Once thought to be marks from sharpening weapons, modern scholars have disproven this theory [3] [4]. Other hypotheses propose stone flour production [3] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308713", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2d12562b/Grooves Gantofta 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d12562b/Sliprännor_Gantofta_2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347277", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347278", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2d28d660-358d-4f4b-a99c-57d5b7395bc4'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2d28d660-358d-4f4b-a99c-57d5b7395bc4:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Nichoria', '4dca1d316f41b3932b5ff9cfe5f2e748', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 87 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80754", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2007:chunk-0001: description ''Nichoria is a Bronze Age settlement on a ridgetop in Messenia, southwestern Peloponnese, approximately 30 km northwest of the palace of Pylos. Inhabited from the Neolithic period (c. 6000 BCE) through the Bronze Age, it became a major Mycenaean regional center with tholos tombs, megaron structures, and storage facilities. Reaching 5 hectares at its peak, it featured a Pylos-style megaron. Nichoria is notable as one of the few Greek sites that remained occupied through the Dark Ages, providing key evidence for the post-Mycenaean transition.'' -> ''Nichoria is a site in Messenia, on a ridgetop near modern Rizomylos, at the northwestern corner of the Messenian Gulf [1]. During the Helladic period it was part of the Mycenaean civilisation [1]. Nichoria became subordinate to Pylos and lost the use of its megaron [1]. Nichoria was a major outpost of Pylos\\''s \"Trans-Aigolaia\" province [1]. Nichoria was destroyed in the same event which claimed the main palace at Pylos [1]. The University of Minnesota Messenia Expedition under William Andrew McDonald surveyed the area in the 1960s, and began excavating Nichoria in 1969 [1]. On the foot of the Nichoria acropolis there was discovered a burial circle, comprising a collective burial of 7 people; it was in use until the LH IIIA period, when the adjacent large tholos tomb was built [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96326", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96327", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-2000'' -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145617", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/Entrance_Tholos_Tomb_at_Nichoria.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d28d660/Entrance_Tholos_Tomb_at_Nichoria.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
