haeologist, E. H. Rogers in the 1930s [1]. A partial excavation uncovered eighteen stones arranged into nine standing pairs [1]. Near the stones, Rogers discovered flint tools and evidence indicating human occupation of the site during the Mesolithic, Neolithic and Early Bronze Age eras [1]. In 1932, the tallest standing stone measured 40cm in height above the silt, and the rows were determined to be 56m in length [1]. By 1983, only seven stones were visible above the mud and the remaining stones disappeared from view over the next several years [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145622", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/Location_of_Yelland_Stone_Rows.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247332", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321283", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d61ebea/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2d61ebea/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d61ebea/Location of Yelland Stone Rows.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347279", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 150