 the location.'' -> ''Zukczyn is a village in Gmina Pruszcz Gdanski, Pomeranian Voivodeship, northern Poland within the historic region of Pomerania [1]. The settlement dates back to prehistoric times, with three documented archaeological sites comprising two settlements and a cemetery from the Iron Age [1]. The area was part of the broader Pomeranian culture, known for its distinctive face urns and stone-cist burial traditions during the Hallstatt period [1] [2] [3]. An early medieval settlement also constitutes an archaeological site at the location [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247334", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333719", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d765805/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347281", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347282", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
