sted to have been formed by removed stones [1]. The stones are of squarish granite of approximately 1.22 metres in height and around .50 metres wide [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96341", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96342", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247339", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247340", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347283", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347284", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
