nt in the region of Sparta consists of pottery dating from the Middle Neolithic period, found in the vicinity of Kouphovouno some two kilometres south-southwest of Sparta [1]. At its peak around 500 BC, Sparta had some 20,000–35,000 citizens, plus numerous helots and perioikoi [1]. In 464 BC, a violent earthquake occurred along the Sparta faultline destroying much of what was Sparta and many other city-states in ancient Greece [1]. Sparta never fully recovered from its losses at Leuctra in 371 BC and the subsequent helot revolts [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146217", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2e53c7cf/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2e53c7cf/Ancient_sparta_theater.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355605", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2e974e22-9f31-4d6c-a258-0195f444f533'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2e974e22-9f31-4d6c-a258-0195f444f533:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Heelstone Ditch', '993354a47bbb89f06789f5113e9cc33a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82620", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2066:chunk-0001: description ''Heelstone Ditch is a roughly circular earthwork surrounding the Heel Stone at Stonehenge, England [1]. The ditch has steep sloping sides ending in a narrow flat base, measuring approximately 1.2 metres deep and 1.1 metres wide, with a diameter of roughly 9.7 metres [1]. It lies about 3.7 metres from the base of the Heel Stone, though it remains unclear whether there was an intentional relationship between the two features [1].'' -> \"Heelstone Ditch is a roughly circular feature surrounding the Heel Stone at Stonehenge [1]. It is not known if there was an intended relationship between the ditch and the heelstone although it is likely that the stone was in place either before or at the same time as the ditch [1]. It has steep sloping sides which end at a narrow flat base, and is approximately 4 ft deep and 3.5 ft wide [1]. A broad arcing trench found in 1923 by Lt-Col William Hawley 9 ft wide cuts this ditch from the West, deepening towards the stone [1]. Against the Heelstone Ditch is rammed chalk filled Stonehole 97, whose missing stone is known as Heelstone''s twin although it is possible that the stone in Stonehole 97 was moved and is now the stone known as the Heelstone [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96362", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Earthwork'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247343", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347285", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347286", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
