 stone is known as Heelstone''s twin although it is possible that the stone in Stonehole 97 was moved and is now the stone known as the Heelstone [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96362", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Earthwork'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247343", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347285", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347286", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
