ean trade routes, it is believed to be the ancient city of Bicourgion described by Ptolemy around 100 AD. Metal objects and Celtic artifacts were discovered during road construction from 1838, and the Steinsburg Museum was built in 1929 on the saddle between the twin basalt peaks.'' -> ''The Oppidum Steinsburg is the remains of a major Celtic fortified settlement on the Kleiner Gleichberg in South Thuringia, Germany [1] [2]. Dating to approximately 2,500 years ago, it covered about 68 hectares [3] [4] [5]. Metal objects and Celtic artifacts were discovered during road construction from 1838, and the Steinsburg Museum was built on the saddle between the twin basalt peaks [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247347", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247348", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309342", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2eeaa376/Steinsburg-022.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2eeaa376/Kleiner_Gleichberg_Hildburghausen_Basaltfelder_(1_von_4).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357103", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357104", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-1200''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2f0e58ba-3b2f-4f39-828f-b5d4935121b3'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:2f0e58ba-3b2f-4f39-828f-b5d4935121b3:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Kanheri Caves', 'f56336d20c42ad47796dc926284ca4c3', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cave Structures'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 19 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33547", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0021:chunk-0001: description \"A group of caves and rock-cut Buddhist monuments carved into a massive basalt outcrop in the forests of Sanjay Gandhi National Park on Salsette Island, western outskirts of Mumbai, India[1]. The complex contains sculptures, relief carvings, paintings, and inscriptions dating from the 1st century CE to the 10th century CE[1]. The name Kanheri derives from the Sanskrit Krishnagiri, meaning ''black mountain''[1].\" -> ''The Kanheri Caves are a group of caves and rock-cut monuments, cut into a massive basalt outcrop in the forests of the Sanjay Gandhi National Park, on the island of Salsette in the western outskirts of Mumbai, India [1]. They contain Buddhist sculptures and relief carvings, paintings and inscriptions, dating from the 1st century CE to the 10th century CE [1]. The cave complex comprises one hundred and nine caves [1]. Rock-cut channels above the caves fed rainwater into cisterns, which provided the complex with water [1]. Most of the caves were Buddhist viharas, meant for living, studying, and meditating [1]. The larger caves, which functioned as chaityas, or halls for congregational worship, are lined with intricately carved Buddhist sculptures, reliefs, pillars and rock-cut stupas [1]. A 494-495 CE inscription found at Kanheri mentions the Traikutaka dynasty [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96371", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146240", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/Kanheri_Caves_(17).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236537", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309351", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/Kanheri_Caves_(17).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/Kanheri_Caves_prayer_hall.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
