yas, or halls for congregational worship, are lined with intricately carved Buddhist sculptures, reliefs, pillars and rock-cut stupas [1]. A 494-495 CE inscription found at Kanheri mentions the Traikutaka dynasty [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96371", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146240", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/Kanheri_Caves_(17).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236537", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309351", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/Kanheri_Caves_(17).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f0e58ba/Kanheri_Caves_prayer_hall.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
