Empire [1]. The fort stood on a hill overlooking a reach of sea which has since been drained to form the Romney Marsh [1]. The construction of the Saxon Shore-era fort can be dated to the late 270s, as is evidenced by its late-style characteristics [1]. The southern side of the fort is wholly missing, and elsewhere the remains have been moved at various angles, while little evidence of interior structures (remains of a bath and possibly the principia) survives [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96373", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146241", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c2/Archaeological_excavations_of_the_East_Gate_of_Portus_Lemanis_in_1976_-_retouched.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f217cc8/Lemanis Osttor FM.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247349", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309354", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2f217cc8/Lemanis Osttor FM.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f217cc8/Archaeological_excavations_of_the_East_Gate_of_Portus_Lemanis_in_1976_-_retouched.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345665", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345666", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: 