 Albans). The village has been continuously settled since at least Saxon times and appears in the Domesday Book.\" -> \"Redbourn is a village in Hertfordshire, England, on the line of Roman Watling Street, with archaeological evidence spanning from the Iron Age to the Roman period [1] [2]. Southwest of the village lies the Aubreys, an Iron Age hill fort enclosure [1]. To the north, a complex of Roman temples was excavated at Friar''s Wash by Channel 4''s Time Team in 2008, situated in the hinterland of the important Romano-British town of Verulamium (St Albans) [1] [3] [4]. The village has been continuously settled since at least Saxon times and appears in the Domesday Book [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247353", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247354", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347291", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347292", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
