firm natural deposition rather than human construction. Some have speculated it is a dolmen, though no archaeological evidence supports this.'' -> ''A massive pink granite glacial erratic perched atop five smaller supports in North Salem, Westchester County, New York [1] [2]. Deposited by retreating glaciers, its granite composition does not match local bedrock and likely originated from the Hudson Highlands [1] [2] [3]. Some have speculated it is a dolmen, though no archaeological evidence supports this [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304083", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}]'::jsonb),
