th other Roman remains in the city it makes the Archaeological Ensemble of Tarraco, which was listed in the UNESCO World Heritage Sites in 2000 [1]. It was built starting from 73 AD, by order of Emperor Vespasian, and remained in use until the 5th century [1]. The area consisted of a square dedicated to worship and a larger one for performances, in addition to the lower enclosure where the circus was located [1]. The worship enclosure was the seat of the concilium and was located in the highest part of the city, which today is occupied by the Cathedral, the Cathedral Square, and other buildings [1]. This was an impressive square measuring 153 meters by 136 meters, surrounded by a perimeter wall that was 9 meters high [1]. This wall supported the roof of a portico with columns, approximately 11 meters wide, which encircled the entire square [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146274", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/Tarragona.Pretorio.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3030e8d3/Plaza del Pallol - Arco de Entrada.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309367", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3030e8d3/Plaza del Pallol - Arco de Entrada.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3030e8d3/Tarragona.Pretorio.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('305ccaba-91b3-4679-b1bc-bd894c81dfee'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:305ccaba-91b3-4679-b1bc-bd894c81dfee:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''7'' restored on Alepotrypa Cave', '0188a3fb5037f39131681d5379143513', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 8 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 4 content link(s), 1 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33553", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0021:chunk-0001: description ''Alepotrypa Cave is a major Neolithic site on the Mani Peninsula, Peloponnese, Greece, stretching 300 meters with six chambers ending in an underground lake [1]. Used from roughly 6000 to 3200 BC for habitation, burial, and ritual, it contains remains of at least 170 individuals [1]. Notable finds include rare silver jewelry, Melian obsidian blades, painted pottery, and the famous \"Embracing Skeletons\" dating to the 4th millennium BC [1][2]. It is one of the largest Neolithic burial sites in Europe [1].'' -> ''The Alepotrypa Cave is a Neolithic-period archaeological site on the Mani Peninsula of the Peloponnese in southern Greece [1]. Used for burial and cult purposes, it is one of the largest burial sites ever found in Europe [1]. Two adult human skeletons dubbed \"the Embracing Skeletons of Alepotrypa\" were found at the site, from a burial dating to the 4th millennium BC; remains from at least 170 separate persons have also been uncovered [1]. The Alepotrypa Cave was also inhabited by early farmers [1]. The site was excavated between 1978 and 2005, after which the project was largely put on hold due to lack of funding [1]. The cave is a natural limestone cavity in a dry, rocky landscape, about 20 meters above sea level and 50 meters from the current Mediterranean shoreline [1]. This karstic formation stretches roughly 300 meters in length and 50 meters in width, running east to west [1]. Finds from the excavation include Late Neolithic stone, pottery and clay vessels, jewelry and weapons [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-6000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146275", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324993", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/Diros-cave-greece 16269357444 o.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
