05, after which the project was largely put on hold due to lack of funding [1]. The cave is a natural limestone cavity in a dry, rocky landscape, about 20 meters above sea level and 50 meters from the current Mediterranean shoreline [1]. This karstic formation stretches roughly 300 meters in length and 50 meters in width, running east to west [1]. Finds from the excavation include Late Neolithic stone, pottery and clay vessels, jewelry and weapons [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-6000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146275", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324993", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/305ccaba/Diros-cave-greece 16269357444 o.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
