emple features bas-relief sculptures of spirals and domesticated animals, and the lower portion of a colossal statue of a skirted figure. The Central Temple is unique in Malta for its six-apse plan. Designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1992, the temples have been protected by shelters since 2015.'' -> ''Discovered in 1913 by farmer Lorenzo Despott, excavations were led by Sir Themistocles Zammit from 1915 to 1919 [1]. The highly decorated South Temple features bas-relief sculptures of spirals and domesticated animals, and the lower portion of a colossal statue of a skirted figure [1]. The Central Temple is unique in Malta for its six-apse plan [1] [2]. Designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1992, the temples have been protected by shelters since 2015 [3].''"}]'::jsonb),
