d up to 30 km wide [1]. In the area around Independence Fjord there are traces of two paleo-Eskimo cultures that were named Independence I culture and Independence II culture after the fjord [1]. The traces of ancient human settlements in the area have been the subject of research since the beginning of the 20th century [1]. North of the fjord, in southern Peary Land, there are remains of dwellings with elliptical floor plan, built by Early Paleoeskimo Independence I culture [1]. These people used tools made from rocks and bones, and subsisted from hunting wildlife like musk oxen and Arctic hares [1]. Bones of musk oxen hunted down in Peary Land show that the area was inhabited at 2000 BC [1]. The oldest discoveries are dated at 2400 BC [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114975", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146319", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31ba0428/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31ba0428/Fjord Independance vue du nord.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355608", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('31cb23a8-36ad-4fdc-8fe8-cfca39285d66'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:31cb23a8-36ad-4fdc-8fe8-cfca39285d66:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Ħaġar Qim', '0272c95930710645bdc3eaf84b1226c4', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Megalithic structures'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 10 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82686", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2068:chunk-0001: description ''Megalithic temple complex in Qrendi, Malta, dating to approximately 3600-3200 BC, making it among the oldest freestanding temples in the world. Built from globigerina limestone, the complex features a trilithon entrance, porthole doorways cut from single megaliths, and a massive 20-ton entrance stone. Discovered in 1839, further excavations in 1885 yielded fertility-associated statuettes and a limestone altar, now housed at the National Museum of Archaeology in Valletta. Designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1992 as part of the Megalithic Temples of Malta, with protective shelters erected in 2009 to slow deterioration.'' -> ''The Megalithic Temples of Malta are among the most ancient religious sites on Earth, described by the World Heritage Sites committee as \"unique architectural masterpieces.\" In 1992 UNESCO recognized Ħaġar Qim and four other Maltese megalithic structures as World Heritage Sites [1]. The megalithic complex of Ħaġar Qim is located on the southern edge of the island of Malta, on a ridge capped in soft globigerina limestone [1]. The temple\\''s façade is characterized by a trilithon entrance, outer bench and orthostats [1]. The Ħaġar Qim complex consists of a main temple and three additional megalithic structures beside it [1]. The northern temple is the oldest part of Ħaġar Qim, containing an oval chamber with a semi-circular apse on each side [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/Complejo_de_Ħaġar_Qim,_isla_de_Malta,_Malta,_2021-08-25,_DD_69.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309391", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/Complejo_de_Ħaġar_Qim,_isla_de_Malta,_Malta,_2021-08-25,_DD_69.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/Facade_Hagar_Qim.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
