n soft globigerina limestone [1]. The temple\\''s façade is characterized by a trilithon entrance, outer bench and orthostats [1]. The Ħaġar Qim complex consists of a main temple and three additional megalithic structures beside it [1]. The northern temple is the oldest part of Ħaġar Qim, containing an oval chamber with a semi-circular apse on each side [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/Complejo_de_Ħaġar_Qim,_isla_de_Malta,_Malta,_2021-08-25,_DD_69.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309391", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/Complejo_de_Ħaġar_Qim,_isla_de_Malta,_Malta,_2021-08-25,_DD_69.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31cb23a8/Facade_Hagar_Qim.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
