aptive figures, and symbolic weaponry [1]. These martial artistic themes have led archaeologists to hypothesize that the complex served as military barracks or a warrior training academy for the powerful pre-Hispanic city [1]. The complex consists of multiple rooms arranged around courtyards, reflecting the urban planning typical of Teotihuacán''s apartment compounds [1].\" -> \"Palace Atetelco is an archaeological complex within the ancient city of Teotihuacán, located in the Valley of Mexico northeast of modern-day Mexico City [1] [2] [3]. The complex consists of multiple rooms arranged around courtyards, reflecting the urban planning typical of Teotihuacán''s apartment compounds [3] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236556", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: site_type None -> ''Palace''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247381", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347311", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
