uter one 1.5 metres deep and the inner one 2.3 metres deep, with indications of a bank that once stood between them [1]. The pits in the middle were postholes for timbers that would have been almost 1 m in diameter [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: lat ''52.58972381357498'' -> ''52.605571''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114988", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: lon ''1.3231785396147067'' -> ''1.30667''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114989", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arminghall'' -> ''https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henge_von_Arminghall''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146348", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/334be182/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309424", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url None -> \"/data/images/wiki/334be182/St_Mary''s_church_Arminghall_Norfolk_(4785329366).webp\""}]'::jsonb),
