ns in 441 AD [1]. Archaeological excavations have revealed late antique baths and partially explored Roman, early Byzantine and Gepid necropolises [1][2].'' -> ''Ancient Roman city of Margus situated on the right bank of the Great Morava River near its confluence with the Danube, in the Roman province of Moesia Superior [1] [2]. In late antiquity, Margus served as a crucial Danube river crossing point [3] [4]. Byzantine and Hunnic envoys met at Margus for treaty negotiations [1] [3] [5]. The city was captured and destroyed by the Huns in 441 AD [3] [5]. Archaeological excavations have revealed late antique baths and partially explored Roman, early Byzantine and Gepid necropolises [3] [6].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343664", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/336a2e13/Margum ausgrabung 2011 (1).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
