    ('353aa183-ed5a-4fa8-8894-3f3ff922cb58'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:353aa183-ed5a-4fa8-8894-3f3ff922cb58:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Pomeroy Wood', 'dcc57bdb27f24af2252710adf03a3548', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fort'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82748", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2070:chunk-0001: description ''Pomeroy Wood is a 1st-century AD Roman military site near Honiton in Devon, probably a fort or marching camp, though its exact type remains inconclusive. Discovered during improvements to the A30 Honiton-Exeter road in the late 1990s, excavations revealed an earth and timber rampart flanked by two deep ditches with narrow ankle-breaker slots at their bases. Preserved biological evidence indicates the garrison included a cavalry unit. Samian ware pottery fragments were also recovered from the site.'' -> ''Pomeroy Wood is the site located near Honiton in Devon of a Roman military site of unknown type, probably either a fort or a marching camp, though archaeological investigations have proved inconclusive [1]. The site was investigated during improvements to the A30 Honiton to Exeter road in the late 1990s [1]. A rampart made of earth and timber was found and outside were two deep ditches with narrow ankle breakers at their bases [1]. Preserved biological finds indicate that the garrison included a cavalry unit [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97152", "u