]. The cap stone measures 13ft X 10ft with 5ft thickness and is supported by pillar stones nearly 6ft tall [1]. Excavations in the 1830''s produced a cremation urn and a flint arrowhead [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97157", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97158", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236579", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236580", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/355d25f2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/355d25f2/Goward Dolmen.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
