1]. It was replaced with a newer and larger structure located farther to the west, which included a wooden gate to be shut at night [1]. This gate was enlarged again in 1472 and 1511, and then damaged in the Great Fire of London in 1666 [1]. Although the City gates had ceased to have any modern function apart from decoration, it was replaced along with Ludgate, Newgate, and Temple Bar with a stone gate in 1672 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97184", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97185", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> ''1415''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146971", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/MoorHouse.jpg/400px-MoorHouse.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/36d0cdd3/Moorgate_Hollar.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
