 50 kilometres from the Pacific Ocean [1]. Its southern acropolis complex was destroyed in 1997 by urban development and the main groups are now covered by sugar cane fields [1]. The site''s geologic context is volcanic; it is located just south of an active stratovolcano, Fuego volcano [1]. The site contains monumental architecture in its acropolis as well as a probable sweatbath and obsidian workshops [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84200", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84201", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146990", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/37999fa3/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/37999fa3/El Baúl 20.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247429", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247430", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309492", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/37999fa3/El Baúl 20.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/37999fa3/ElBaulSt.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348078", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348079", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('37c35150-d91b-44bb-a039-48783357de8e'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '10', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:37c35150-d91b-44bb-a039-48783357de8e:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''8'' restored on Kosmaj', '4ea225cad00f16ceff0ce76196d56457', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 10 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 5 content link(s), 21 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33629", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0023:chunk-0001: description \"Kosmaj is a mountain 40 km south-east of Belgrade, Serbia, that served as a major Roman mining centre from the 2nd century AD. Administered by procurator Babenius, the mines contain an estimated 100 ancient shafts extending 2 km below ground, yielding silver, iron, and lead. Production peaked under Trajan and Marcus Aurelius, and the Balkans became the Roman Empire''s primary silver source from the mid-2nd to mid-4th century. Excavations in the 1970s-80s uncovered mining necropoleis and a hidden Roman mine complex.\" -> ''Kosmaj is a mountain south of Belgrade [1]. In Roman period, Kosmaj was an important mining center, but today the mining activities ceased completely [1]. Evidence suggests that the iron ore was extracted even in the pre-Roman period [1]. In July 2000, during the excavations for the new sports complex in Babe, a spring was discovered in the valley of the Pruten creek [1]. Moreover, during the excavation, a hidden entry into the vast complex of Roman mines was discovered, too, being obscured for centuries [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116178", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: lat ''44.46572402189206'' -> ''44.513415''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116179", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: lon ''20.565609240999216'' -> ''20.499206''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116180", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Mine/quarry'' -> ''Mine''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116181", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kosmaj'' -> ''https://oxrep.classics.ox.ac.uk/popup.php?ste=2101''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/37c35150/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:339509", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-003-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/37c35150/World War I memorial on Kosmaj 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355615", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Mine'' -> ''Mine/quarry''"}]'::jsonb),
