ntain plateau at an altitude of 1,770 metres and occupies an area of about 7 hectares on the left side of the canyon of the River Dar, a tributary of the river Vorotan [1]. The Carahunge monument consists of the central circle, the north arm, the south arm, the north–east alley, the chord across the circle, and separated standing stones [1]. The site is rich with stone settings, burial cists and standing stones [1]. In total, 223 stones have been identified [1]. The stones are basalt, eroded by time and covered with moss and lichen of many colours [1]. The heights of the stones above ground-level varies from 0.5 to 3 m, and their weights range up to 10 tons [1]. Zorats Karer was investigated in 2000 by archaeologists from the Institut für Vorderasiatische Archäologie, LMU Munich, as part of a field survey of prehistoric sites in southern Armenia [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97202", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141462", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-01a_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141463", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-01a_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147017", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3807e5f9/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3807e5f9/02 - 2025.8 Zorac Karer 001.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309501", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3807e5f9/02 - 2025.8 Zorac Karer 001.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3807e5f9/Zorats_Karer_2008,_part_of_the_stone_circle.webp''"}]'::