 Intermediate Period (AD 1000-1450), it emerged after the collapse of the Tiwanaku civilization. The site covers roughly 30 hectares and features multiple concentric dry-stone walls enclosing a central plaza, circular domestic structures, chullpas (funerary towers), and agricultural terraces. It was declared part of Peru''s National Cultural Heritage on 17 July 2001.\" -> \"Tanqa Tanqa is a major archaeological pukara (fortified hilltop settlement) of the Lupaca culture, located at an elevation of 3,974 m [1]. Dating to the Late Intermediate Period (AD 1000-1450), it emerged after the collapse of the Tiwanaku civilization [1]. The site covers roughly 30 hectares and features circular domestic structures, chullpas (funerary towers), and agricultural terraces [1] [2]. It was declared part of Peru''s National Cultural Heritage on 17 July 2001 [3] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236632", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''1200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: site_type None -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
