    ('3aa70cf2-d56b-4401-8a60-2cd12131827c'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:3aa70cf2-d56b-4401-8a60-2cd12131827c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Koongine Cave', 'ec4403ea808301dac8b6e89c985acfb8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33671", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0024:chunk-0001: description ''Koongine Cave is an archaeological site in the Limestone Coast of South Australia, situated in a low limestone ridge about 4 km from the coastline. The cave was occupied for approximately 2,000 years during the Pleistocene-Holocene transition, leaving up to 2 m of sediment rich in artefacts. Its stratified deposits define the Gambieran Industry, characterized by large convex scrapers. Indigenous Australian finger markings and more recent petroglyphs adorn the cave walls, stratified by travertine deposits.'' -> ''Koongine Cave is located in the Limestone Coast of South Australia [1]. The cave is situated in a limestone ridge approximately 4 km from the coastline [1]. It was occupied approximately 10,000 years ago for a period of approximately 1,500 years leaving up to 2 m of sediments behind, rich in artefacts and ecofacts [1]. Finger markings made by Indigenous Australians can be found on the walls of the cave [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''< 45