 Birka and the western districts of Lake Mälaren. The fortification lies within Görvälns nature reserve [3].\" -> \"Gåseborg is a prehistoric hillfort in the Lake Mälaren district in Sweden [1]. The scientists don''t know for certain, but most likely it was built to supervise and control the water fairway below the fort, probably sometime during the late iron age [1]. Several major fairways passed right here and from this place the local man in power could control the traffic to Uppsala, Sigtuna, Birka and the western districts of Lake Mälaren [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97261", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97262", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> ''500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147119", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/Gåseborg, framför yttre stenmuren, 2015a.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309558", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/Gåseborg, framför yttre stenmuren, 2015a.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/Gåsborg_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
