rways connecting Uppsala, Sigtuna, Birka and the western districts of Lake Mälaren. The fortification lies within Görvälns nature reserve [3].\" -> \"Gåseborg is a prehistoric hillfort in the Lake Mälaren district in Sweden [1]. The scientists don''t know for certain, but most likely it was built to supervise and control the water fairway below the fort, probably sometime during the late iron age [1]. Several major fairways passed right here and from this place the local man in power could control the traffic to Uppsala, Sigtuna, Birka and the western districts of Lake Mälaren [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97261", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97262", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> ''500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147119", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/Gåseborg, framför yttre stenmuren, 2015a.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309558", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/Gåseborg, framför yttre stenmuren, 2015a.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b4ceaf0/Gåsborg_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('3b512b0e-f4d7-4d81-8467-87796cdf405a'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:3b512b0e-f4d7-4d81-8467-87796cdf405a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Burgstallkogel, Sulm Valley', '220e0fb784ae540c456a7a1660ffe64a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 286 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83242", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2074:chunk-0001: description ''The Burgstallkogel is a 458-metre hill near the confluence of the Sulm and Saggau rivers in southern Styria, Austria, that hosted a major Hallstatt-period settlement from the 9th to 6th centuries BC. Surrounding the hill is the Sulmtal Necropolis, one of the largest Iron Age burial grounds in continental Europe, originally comprising around 2,000 tumuli ranging from 2 to over 40 metres in diameter. Four princely burial mounds near Kleinklein -- Hartnermichelkogel 1 and 2, Pommerkogel, and Krollkogel -- contained exceptionally rich grave goods including bronze masks and armor. Unlike the Western Hallstatt zone where intact inhumation prevailed, all burials here involved cremation before deposition in stone chambers.'' -> \"The Burgstallkogel is a hill situated near the confluence of the Sulm and the Saggau river valleys in Southern Styria in Austria, about 30 km south of Graz between Gleinstätten and Kleinklein [1]. The hill hosted a significant settlement of trans-regional importance from 800 BC to about 600 BC [1]. In contrast to the grave mounds in the Western Hallstatt zone where the deceased were mostly buried intact, all Burgstallkogel dead were cremated, frequently together with some of their personal articles [1]. Besides being larger than most other necropolises in the Eastern Hallstatt area, the Sulm valley necropolis is set apart by the fact that preserved non-aristocratic burials far outnumber the nobility''s graves [1]. The Kröllkogel was the last hill grave to be set up for a chieftain ruling the Burgstallkogel settlement, most likely dating to the first half of the 6th century BC [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116210", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Mound/tumulus'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116211", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgstallkogel_(Sulm_valley)'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgstallkogel''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/Neolithic_reconstructions_Burgstallkogel_02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309561", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/Neolithic_reconstructions_Burgstallkogel_02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/Sulm_valley_tumulus.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355621", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('3b512b0e-f4d7-4d81-8467-87796cdf405a'::uuid, 'rarity_score', '25', '40', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:3b512b0e-f4d7-4d81-8467-87796cdf405a:rarity_score', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: rarity_score ''40'' restored on Burgstallkogel, Sulm Valley', '220e0fb784ae540c456a7a1660ffe64a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "rarity_score = 25 from mystery 1, cultural_influence 10"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83242", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2074:chunk-0001: description ''The Burgstallkogel is a 458-metre hill near the confluence of the Sulm and Saggau rivers in southern Styria, Austria, that hosted a major Hallstatt-period settlement from the 9th to 6th centuries BC. Surrounding the hill is the Sulmtal Necropolis, one of the largest Iron Age burial grounds in continental Europe, originally comprising around 2,000 tumuli ranging from 2 to over 40 metres in diameter. Four princely burial mounds near Kleinklein -- Hartnermichelkogel 1 and 2, Pommerkogel, and Krollkogel -- contained exceptionally rich grave goods including bronze masks and armor. Unlike the Western Hallstatt zone where intact inhumation prevailed, all burials here involved cremation before deposition in stone chambers.'' -> \"The Burgstallkogel is a hill situated near the confluence of the Sulm and the Saggau river valleys in Southern Styria in Austria, about 30 km south of Graz between Gleinstätten and Kleinklein [1]. The hill hosted a significant settlement of trans-regional importance from 800 BC to about 600 BC [1]. In contrast to the grave mounds in the Western Hallstatt zone where the deceased were mostly buried intact, all Burgstallkogel dead were cremated, frequently together with some of their personal articles [1]. Besides being larger than most other necropolises in the Eastern Hallstatt area, the Sulm valley necropolis is set apart by the fact that preserved non-aristocratic burials far outnumber the nobility''s graves [1]. The Kröllkogel was the last hill grave to be set up for a chieftain ruling the Burgstallkogel settlement, most likely dating to the first half of the 6th century BC [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116210", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Mound/tumulus'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116211", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgstallkogel_(Sulm_valley)'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgstallkogel''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/Neolithic_reconstructions_Burgstallkogel_02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309561", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/Neolithic_reconstructions_Burgstallkogel_02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3b512b0e/Sulm_valley_tumulus.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355621", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
