d their westward expansion into the Slavonian plains.'' -> ''Sarvas is a village in eastern Slavonia, Croatia, east of Osijek, containing a Scordisci archaeological site dating to the late La Tene period [1]. Excavated during rescue operations in the 1970s and 1980s, the site was part of the broader Scordisci settlement network in the Vinkovci area [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247797", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247798", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348099", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348100", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-6200''"}]'::jsonb),
