    ('3c47ded2-01b0-4789-bf6e-defb171ddd43'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:3c47ded2-01b0-4789-bf6e-defb171ddd43:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Midea, Argolid', '105a00156b742d0f0ad5f266e18d2b5b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116219", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116220", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-4800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309573", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3c47ded2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3c47ded2/Midea.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:336507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4300:chunk-0001: description ''Midea was one of the three principal Mycenaean centres in the Argolid alongside Mycenae and Tiryns, occupying the highest Mycenaean acropolis at 270m elevation. The citadel is enclosed by massive cyclopean walls measuring 450m long, 5-7m wide, and up to 7m high, with two monumental gates. Excavations from 1939 to 2009 uncovered Linear B inscriptions, faience necklaces, ivory inlays, and a steatite mould for gold and glass beads, confirming it as an administrative and craft production centre. The site was destroyed by an earthquake around 1200 BC.'' -> ''Midea was one of the three principal Mycenaean centres in the Argolid alongside Mycenae and Tiryns, occupying the highest Mycenaean acropolis at 270m elevation [1]. The citadel is enclosed by massive cyclopean walls measuring 450m long, 5-7m wide, and up to 7m high, with two monumental gates [1] [2]. Excavations from 1939 to 2009 uncovered Linear B inscriptions, ivory inlays, and a steatite mould for gold and glass beads, confirming it as an administrative and craft production centre [1] [2] [3]. The site was destroyed around 1200 BC [2].''"}]'::jsonb),
