rgaret Murray in 1930 and declared a National Historical Monument in 1931, Trepuco is now part of the UNESCO-inscribed Talayotic Menorca.'' -> ''Trepuco is one of the largest Talayotic settlements in Menorca, covering over 4 hectares [1] [2]. Its central talayot measures more than 26 metres in diameter and 8 metres in height, while the taula sanctuary features a nearly five-metre-high T-shaped megalith [1] [3] [4]. Around the 5th century BCE the village was enclosed by a Cyclopean wall with square defensive towers [3]. The settlement was likely destroyed during the Second Punic War [3]. Excavated by Margaret Murray in 1930 and declared a National Historical Monument in 1931, Trepuco is now part of the UNESCO-inscribed Talayotic Menorca [1] [3] [5].''"}]'::jsonb),
