ock above a creek, measure 2 × 3 m each [1]. Written in Old Persian, Neo-Babylonian and Neo-Elamite, except for the different royal name, the contents of the two inscriptions are identical; Ahura Mazda receives praise, and lineages and conquests are listed [1]. The site received its name from locals, who believed that the inscriptions contained the secret code to a hidden treasure [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97298", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97299", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247823", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309601", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3d801ecb/Cuneiform Inscriptions of Darius and Xerxes - Ganjnameh - Outside Hamadan - Western Iran - 01 (7423532748).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3d801ecb/Ganj_Nameh-Hamedan.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348122", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348123", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-10000'' -> ''-550''"}]'::jsonb),
