tion_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3eee3fb1/Roman well near the Muntham Court Romano-British site.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3eee3fb1/View_of_Muntham_Court_Romano-British_site.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:336595", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4301:chunk-0001: description \"The Muntham Court Romano-British site is a Scheduled Ancient Monument on the western edge of Findon village in West Sussex, England. Excavated between 1954 and 1956, the site revealed an Iron Age settlement overlaid by a Romano-British shrine, with occupation spanning the 1st to 4th centuries AD. Features include house structures, trackways, field boundaries, and a circular temple or shrine on the hilltop. A 76m-deep Roman well lies to the south, and excavations produced the bronze ''Muntham Boar'' plaque, now displayed in Worthing Museum.\" -> \"The Muntham Court Romano-British site is a Scheduled Ancient Monument on the western edge of Findon village in West Sussex, England [1] [2]. Features include house structures, trackways, field boundaries, and a circular temple or shrine on the hilltop [1]. A well lies to the south, and excavations produced the bronze ''Muntham Boar'' plaque, now displayed in Worthing Museum [1] [3].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348136", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348137", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
