s [1]. The origin of the name is unknown, however local folklore describes their use by Robin Hood and Little John to play quoits [1]. The name is known to have been used since the 19th century appearing on a tithe map created in 1844 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247839", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247840", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348138", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348139", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
