ead were buried in cemeteries [1]. People slept on woollen mats and fur and made clothes of wool, flax and leather [1]. The figurines found not only represent deities but many show the daily life of the inhabitants while crude pottery finds appear to have been made by children [1]. Women are depicted in short tops and skirt wearing jewellery [1]. In 2008, a copper axe was found at Pločnik that was dated to 5,500 BC [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147835", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/%D0%9F%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA_01.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/412a1f97/Плочник_01.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
