 m diameter) forming a kerb around a low cairn. Excavations in 1997 revealed that the stone circles replaced two earlier concentric rings of oak wooden posts dating to c. 2872-2350 BC, making it one of only 15 concentric stone circles identified in England. Evidence of burning was found in the central cairn, with a possible cist at its center.'' -> ''Oddendale Stone Circle is a Neolithic-to-Bronze Age concentric stone circle near Shap in Cumbria [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348161", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348162", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354771", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354772", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
