 34 Shap granite boulders (27.1 m diameter) and an inner ring of 23 stones (7.4 m diameter) forming a kerb around a low cairn. Excavations in 1997 revealed that the stone circles replaced two earlier concentric rings of oak wooden posts dating to c. 2872-2350 BC, making it one of only 15 concentric stone circles identified in England. Evidence of burning was found in the central cairn, with a possible cist at its center.'' -> ''Oddendale Stone Circle is a Neolithic-to-Bronze Age concentric stone circle near Shap in Cumbria [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348161", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348162", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354771", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354772", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('424a8ef0-74a3-48ab-bdaf-8df3d957e36c'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:424a8ef0-74a3-48ab-bdaf-8df3d957e36c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Rouffignac Cave', '8dce4bd01281e631016fb4e2661c3f8a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28163", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0085:chunk-0001: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-11000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34373", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0026:chunk-0001: description ''Rouffignac Cave, known as the \"Cave of the Hundred Mammoths,\" is located in the Dordogne department of France and contains over 250 engravings and paintings dating to approximately 13,000 years ago during the Magdalenian period. The cave features 158 mammoth depictions, comprising roughly 30% of all mammoths in Paleolithic art worldwide. The Grand Plafond ceiling gathers 66 animals in a single composition. Extending over 8 km, it is one of Europe\\''s largest decorated caves. Classified as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1979, visitors explore via electric train to preserve the artwork.'' -> ''The Rouffignac cave, in the French commune of Rouffignac-Saint-Cernin-de-Reilhac in the Dordogne département, contains over 250 engravings and cave paintings dating back to the Upper Paleolithic [1]. The Rouffignac cave was mentioned in 1575 by François de Belleforest [1]. Famous archeologists such as Henri Breuil, André Glory and Édouard-Alfred Martel had visited the cave in the early 20th century, but it was only in 1956 that Louis-René Nougier and Romain Robert, two prehistorians from the Pyrenees, rediscovered and confirmed the cave art [1]. The artistic representations in the cave were mainly executed as engravings or black contour drawings [1]. Reconnaissance excavations in front of the entry of the cave found traces of human occupations (several fireplaces, animal bones and stone tools) dating back to the Mesolithic and to the Neolithic [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98006", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98007", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-11000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147882", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/Grotte_de_Rouffignac_-_Entr%C3%A9e_-_20090924.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/424a8ef0/Grotte_de_Rouffignac_-_Entrée_-_20090924.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236698", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-11000''"}]'::jsonb),
