ions also revealed a stone structure believed to have been part of an early Christian baptistery, suggesting the site may have had later religious significance[1].\" -> \"St Laurence School - Roman Villa is an archaeological site in Bradford-on-Avon, Wiltshire, England [1] [2]. Minor excavations in 1976 revealed the presence of a Roman villa beneath the school''s sports fields [1] [2]. A major excavation in 2003 uncovered Roman-era floor mosaics and walls belonging to the villa complex [1] [3]. The excavations also revealed a stone structure believed to have been part of an early Christian baptistery, suggesting the site may have had later religious significance [1] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Villa'' -> ''Residence/villa/farmhouse''"}]'::jsonb),
