la complex[1]. The excavations also revealed a stone structure believed to have been part of an early Christian baptistery, suggesting the site may have had later religious significance[1].\" -> \"St Laurence School - Roman Villa is an archaeological site in Bradford-on-Avon, Wiltshire, England [1] [2]. Minor excavations in 1976 revealed the presence of a Roman villa beneath the school''s sports fields [1] [2]. A major excavation in 2003 uncovered Roman-era floor mosaics and walls belonging to the villa complex [1] [3]. The excavations also revealed a stone structure believed to have been part of an early Christian baptistery, suggesting the site may have had later religious significance [1] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Villa'' -> ''Residence/villa/farmhouse''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('44def22f-dca7-4075-a555-d64821a0d882'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:44def22f-dca7-4075-a555-d64821a0d882:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''2'' restored on El Tortuguero', '64a5a7e224f5b3b76505b216a2f08f47', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44327", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0090:chunk-0001: description \"Located in southernmost Tabasco, Mexico, El Tortuguero was a Classic period Maya city (500-1000 AD) that used the B''aakal emblem glyph, the same title used by the powerful site of Palenque[1]. Despite its historical significance, El Tortuguero has been heavily damaged by looting and modern development; in the 1960s, a cement factory was built directly atop the site[1].\" -> \"Tortuguero (or El Tortuguero) is an archaeological site in southernmost Tabasco, Mexico which supported a Maya city during the Classic period [1]. The site is noteworthy for its use of the B''aakal emblem glyph also found as the primary title at Palenque [1]. Because of its mid-20th century destruction, little is known about the dynastic lineage of this site [1]. Its history is linked to that of the kingdom of Palenque, as the rulers of Tortuguero used the same emblem glyph as Palenque [1]. Monument 6 from Tortuguero has recently generated discussion as it includes the only known inscription depicting the end of the current 13-Bak''tun era in 2012 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98041", "url": "remediation_ch