dral [1]. To mark the 1,900th anniversary of York''s founding, the column was reassembled and erected in Minster Yard in 1972 [1]. The column is approximately 9.5 metres in height [1]. It is made up of eight cylindrical drums of Magnesian Limestone, a common building material in the region during the Roman period [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/Roman_column%2C_York%2C_2023.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/4561c396/Roman column, York 2015.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4561c396/Roman column, York 2015.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/4561c396/Roman_column,_York,_2023.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
