are now called ''E-Groups'' throughout Mesoamerica. In 378 AD, the warrior Siyaj K''ahk from Teotihuacan conquered Uaxactun and Tikal, marking a major political transformation.\" -> \"Uaxactun is an ancient Maya ceremonial center in the Peten department of Guatemala, located 19 km north of Tikal within the Maya Biosphere Reserve [1]. In 378 AD, the warrior Siyaj K''ahk conquered Uaxactun and Tikal, marking a major political transformation [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355637", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
