    ('482a2a89-7c40-4f4d-a411-ab99de88b701'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:482a2a89-7c40-4f4d-a411-ab99de88b701:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Mulri Hills', '5bed80701450ac95369866c856b45d72', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83502", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2082:chunk-0001: description ''Mulri Hills are located in Gulshan Town, Karachi, Sindh, Pakistan, forming offshoots of the Kirthar Range [1]. The highest point reaches approximately 528 metres (1,732 ft) in the extreme north [1]. These barren hills lack vegetation and feature wide intervening plains, dry river beds, and ancient water channels [1]. Archaeological excavations by the University of Karachi have discovered Late Palaeolithic and Mesolithic sites at the Mulri Hills, constituting one of the most significant prehistoric sites in the region [1].'' -> ''The Mulri Hills are located in Gulshan Town, Karachi, Sindh, Pakistan [1]. The Late Palaeolithic and Mesolithic sites found by Karachi University team on the Mulri Hills, in front of Karachi University Campus, constitute one of the most important archaeological discoveries made in Sindh during the last fifty years [1]. The last hunter-gatherers, who left abundant traces of their passage, repeatedly inhabited the Mulri Hills [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'