9", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248260", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:336927", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4305:chunk-0001: description ''Near the hamlet of Clayhanger in Devon lies the site of a Roman fort at Cudmore Farm, overlooking a tributary of the River Batherm. Considered the best-surviving Roman fort in southwest England, it is rectangular, approximately 100 metres across each side, with an 8-metre rampart and four outer ditches. Cropmarks inside the site reveal building locations, and Roman tile and samian ware have been recovered. Scheduled as a monument on 7 March 1994, the fort mostly lies in the parish of Bampton.'' -> ''Near the hamlet of Clayhanger in Devon lies the site of a Roman fort at Cudmore Farm, overlooking a tributary of the River Batherm [1]. Considered the best-surviving Roman fort in southwest England, it is rectangular, approximately 100 metres across each side, with an 8-metre rampart and four outer ditches [1]. Roman tile and samian ware have been recovered [1]. Scheduled as a monument, the fort mostly lies in the parish of Bampton [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348204", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> ''43''"}]'::jsonb),
