 known fully alphabetic cuneiform script using only 30 characters, and excavations yielded texts in multiple languages with parallels to Hebrew biblical poetry. The city was a vital trade hub distributing grain to Hittite courts and exchanging copper with Cyprus and the Aegean.\" -> ''Ugarit was a major ancient port city at Ras Shamra in northern Syria [1] [2] [3]. The site features a grand royal palace with multiple courtyards, plus two acropolis temples dedicated to Baal and Dagan [1] [2]. Excavations yielded texts in multiple languages with parallels to Hebrew biblical poetry [4] [5] [6]. The city was a vital trade hub [3] [5].''"}]'::jsonb),
