n are 11.9 metres by 10.7 metres [1]. Its original width is unknown as it was moved in 1861 due to an intersecting hedge [1]. Two of the stones were broken in the manoeuvre [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98125", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98126", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148691", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4a42b149/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/4a42b149/1006714-DuloeStoneCircle (1).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237549", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237550", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310405", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4a42b149/1006714-DuloeStoneCircle (1).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/4a42b149/Duloe Stone Circle - geograph.org.uk - 1242170.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4a4dcea2-c940-416e-a217-b397396179e1'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:4a4dcea2-c940-416e-a217-b397396179e1:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Cefn Bryn', '13d9f204d6836ef76a88ee5102002474', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Cairn'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 35 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34445", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0028:chunk-0001: description ''Cefn Bryn is an 8 km long Old Red Sandstone ridge on the Gower Peninsula, south Wales, rising to 188 m and known as the \"backbone of Gower\". It is one of the richest archaeological landscapes in South Wales, with evidence of human activity from at least the 4th-3rd millennium BC. The most prominent feature is Maen Ceti (Arthur\\''s Stone), a Neolithic burial chamber dating to c. 2500 BC with a massive 25-ton capstone measuring 12 feet across supported by upright stones. Over sixty Bronze Age cairns have been discovered beneath bracken on the ridge, and a temporary settlement from the early 3rd millennium BC has been excavated near Arthur\\''s Stone.'' -> ''Cefn Bryn is an ancient ridge in Britain [1]. It is a 5-mile-long Old Red Sandstone ridge in south Wales, in the heart of the Gower Peninsula [1]. Just north of the ridge summit of Cefn Bryn, there is a Neolithic burial ground, known as \"Arthur\\''s Stone\" [1]. Beneath the bracken on the hill over sixty cairns have been discovered [1]. Most of these are likely to be no more than collections of stones cleared by local farmers; but just north-west of Arthur\\''s Stone three prominent cairns have been excavated that prove their ancient role - the largest being Great Cairn, a circular heap of stones above a central grave [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116383", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cefn_Bryn'' -> ''https://cadwpublic-api.azurewebsites.net/reports/sam/FullReport?id=3758''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148692", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4a4dcea2/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/4a4dcea2/Arthur''s_stone,_near_Swansea.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-2300''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4a4dcea2-c940-416e-a217-b397396179e1'::uuid, 'rarity_score', '29', '32', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:4a4dcea2-c940-416e-a217-b397396179e1:rarity_score', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: rarity_score ''32'' restored on Cefn Bryn', '13d9f204d6836ef76a88ee5102002474', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "rarity_score = 29 from mystery 5, cultural_influence 7"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34445", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0028:chunk-0001: description ''Cefn Bryn is an 8 km long Old Red Sandstone ridge on the Gower Peninsula, south Wales, rising to 188 m and known as the \"backbone of Gower\". It is one of the richest archaeological landscapes in South Wales, with evidence of human activity from at least the 4th-3rd millennium BC. The most prominent feature is Maen Ceti (Arthur\\''s Stone), a Neolithic burial chamber dating to c. 2500 BC with a massive 25-ton capstone measuring 12 feet across supported by upright stones. Over sixty Bronze Age cairns have been discovered beneath bracken on the ridge, and a temporary settlement from the early 3rd millennium BC has been excavated near Arthur\\''s Stone.'' -> ''Cefn Bryn is an ancient ridge in Britain [1]. It is a 5-mile-long Old Red Sandstone ridge in south Wales, in the heart of the Gower Peninsula [1]. Just north of the ridge summit of Cefn Bryn, there is a Neolithic burial ground, known as \"Arthur\\''s Stone\" [1]. Beneath the bracken on the hill over sixty cairns have been discovered [1]. Most of these are likely to be no more than collections of stones cleared by local farmers; but just north-west of Arthur\\''s Stone three prominent cairns have been excavated that prove their ancient role - the largest being Great Cairn, a circular heap of stones above a central grave [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116383", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cefn_Bryn'' -> ''https://cadwpublic-api.azurewebsites.net/reports/sam/FullReport?id=3758''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148692", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4a4dcea2/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/4a4dcea2/Arthur''s_stone,_near_Swansea.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-2300''"}]'::jsonb),
