orth-west of Arthur\\''s Stone three prominent cairns have been excavated that prove their ancient role - the largest being Great Cairn, a circular heap of stones above a central grave [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116383", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cefn_Bryn'' -> ''https://cadwpublic-api.azurewebsites.net/reports/sam/FullReport?id=3758''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148692", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4a4dcea2/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/4a4dcea2/Arthur''s_stone,_near_Swansea.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-2300''"}]'::jsonb),
