g it one of the oldest known settlement areas in the region. These sites are part of the Rydno Archaeological Reserve, a complex spanning from Skarżysko-Kamienna to Wąchock, containing several hundred former Paleolithic sites. Archaeological evidence from the area includes stone tools and other artifacts from the Stone Age period.'' -> ''Marcinków is a village in Gmina Wąchock, Starachowice County, Świętokrzyskie Voivodeship, south-central Poland [1]. The village was the location of several Paleolithic industrial sites [1] [2]. These sites are part of the Rydno Archaeological Reserve, a complex spanning from Skarżysko-Kamienna to Wąchock, containing several hundred former Paleolithic sites [1] [2]. Archaeological evidence from the area includes stone tools and other artifacts from the Stone Age period [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:339704", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-004-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/4a59d4e4/Marcinków (przystanek kolejowy) 7.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348205", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348206", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-3000000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4a87bc78-0813-4110-aa1e-3818326bee00'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '10', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:4a87bc78-0813-4110-aa1e-3818326bee00:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''10'' restored on Cave of the Guanches', 'f05bc17ebfd87c4a2c8fd6917dc4d02d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Cave Structures'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44347", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0091:chunk-0001: description ''A protected archaeological site in the municipality of Icod de los Vinos on the north coast of Tenerife, Canary Islands, Spain, designated as a Bien de Interes Cultural. The cave complex of connected chambers preserves the earliest known Guanche settlements on Tenerife, with ceramics dated to the 6th century BCE providing the oldest chronologies in the Canary Islands. Researchers believe it served as a residence for the menceyes, the traditional Guanche leaders. Excavations yielded hand-made pottery, bone awls, caprid remains, marine shells, and a human mandible. Finds are held in the Museo Guanche in Icod de los Vinos and the British Museum.'' -> ''The Cave of the Guanches, or Archaeological area of the Cave of the Guanches, is an important archaeological site located in the north of the island of Tenerife (Canary Islands, Spain) [1]. The protected archaeological environment is in the municipality of Icod de los Vinos and revolves around the Cave of the Guanches [1]. This archaeological area is where the earliest Guanche autochthonous settlements on the island of Tenerife have been found [1]. It has provided the oldest chronologies of the Canary Islands [1]. These have been dated to the 6th century BCE, according to analysis carried out on ceramics that were found inside [1]. The area was in aboriginal times a village of natural caves and huts (now disappeared), which were located at the top of a cliff, about 125 m above sea level [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116389", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: lat ''28.377135967085778'' -> ''28.383278''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116390", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: lon ''-16.723035630895534'' -> ''-16.700256''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116391", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> ''Cave''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355639", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Cave'' -> ''Cave Structures''"}]'::jsonb),
