tury BC theatre seating 3,200, an odeon, agora, and temples. Conquered by Persia around 540 BC, it later surrendered to Alexander the Great in 334 BC. Rediscovered by Charles Fellows in 1839, the site remains largely unexcavated and is on UNESCO\\''s Tentative List.'' -> ''Pinara was one of the six principal cities of the Lycian League [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
