had 53 large boundary stones, is 34 metres long and 8 to 11 metres wide (39 stones have survived) [1]. In the north-east were two transverse dolmens, of which only one is well preserved [1]. It is 1.4 metres high, 1.8 metres long and 1.1 metres wide [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117538", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117539", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-5000'' -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117540", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobbin'' -> ''https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gro%C3%9Fsteingrab_Nobbin''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149505", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Riesenberg_Nobbin.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5077f16f/Riesenberg_Nobbin.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
