le commerce, but became the central point from which Augustus and Tiberius carried on their undertakings against the Pannonians and Illyrians [1]. Tiberius did much to enlarge and embellish the town, which as early as that time seems to have been made a colonia, for Pliny mentions it as such: in the time of Septimius Severus it received fresh colonists [1]. The town contained an imperial mint, which produced coins under a series of emperors between 262 and 383 AD [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98855", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98856", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Sisak_Fortress.jpg/400px-Sisak_Fortress.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/50debb04/Roman_ruins_in_Sisak.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248301", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248302", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348237", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348238", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
