useum [1]. It lies approximately 50 m from the present coastline, situated on raised beaches with a southeastern slope [1]. The area elevation ranges between 9 m (30 ft)and 13 m (43 ft) above mean sea level [1]. This part of the island that contains the archaeological site, did not show signs of later occupation by Dorset culture or Thule culture [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117547", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117548", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nipisat_Island'' -> ''https://tidsskrift.dk/meddrgroenland_man_soc/article/view/147038''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355648", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
