ated in 1 B.C., functioned as such for two centuries, although partial restorations were necessary during that time [1]. Prior to the theatre, in the area where it is currently located, there was a Roman house built at the end of the second century B.C., which was intentionally demolished for the construction of the Roman Theater in the time of Augustus [1]. After a fire that caused a large part of its architectural framework to disappear, in the 5th century A.D. what was left standing of the Theater was dismantled and its architectural elements were used to build a market [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149540", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/39/Teatro_romano_de_Cartagena%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2022-07-16%2C_DD_07.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/51e00207/Teatro_romano_de_Cartagena,_España,_2022-07-16,_DD_07.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
