2].\" -> \"Tipasa (c. 6th c. BC – 6th c. AD) began as a trading post on Algeria''s central coast before Rome transformed it into a strategic colonial base for conquering Mauretania [1] [2]. The site preserves a unique layered heritage—Phoenician, Roman, palaeochristian and Byzantine ruins standing together [1]. UNESCO inscribed Tipasa as a World Heritage Site in 1982, listing it as in danger from 2002–2006 before successful conservation efforts removed it from the danger list [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355650", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('52258395-f830-4181-bccb-8d5e37d2e440'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:52258395-f830-4181-bccb-8d5e37d2e440:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Dun Telve', '1557eacb0742829e0b18f685ec79d280', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start -550"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34501", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0029:chunk-0001: description ''Dun Telve is an Iron Age broch near Glenelg in the Scottish Highlands, and one of the best-preserved brochs in Scotland, standing over 10 metres high with a diameter exceeding 20 metres. Two concentric drystone walls are tied together by large horizontal slabs forming gallery floors, with a winding stone staircase providing access to upper levels. Among the earliest monuments passed into State care in 1885, it is one of only four Scottish brochs retaining heights approaching their original form, alongside Mousa and Dun Carloway. The broch was likely robbed for stone in 1722, probably for construction of Bernera Barracks, and underwent permanent stabilization works around 1914 by the Ministry of Works.'' -> ''Dun Telve (Scottish Gaelic: Dùn Teilbh) is an iron-age broch located about four kilometres southeast of Kirkton, the main village of the community of Glenelg, Inverness-shire in the Highland Region of Scotland [1]. It is one of the best preserved brochs in Scotland [1]. Dun Telve stands on the north bank of the Abhainn a’ Ghlinne Bhig, in the lower reaches of Gleann Beag [1]. The broch consists of a drystone tower which measures 18.3 metres in diameter, and currently stands to a maximum height of 10.2 metres to the west and northwest [1]. The external walls are 4.3 metres thick at the base and 1.2 metres thick at the top [1]. On the south side of the entrance passage is a small side-chamber, sometimes called a \"guard cell\" [1]. Access up the tower is by a winding stone stair, and openings at intervals once gave access to the upper floors [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98881", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98882", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149550", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/Dun Telve - Interior view.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237605", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310519", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/Dun Telve - Interior view.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/Dun Telve - geograph.org.uk - 188336.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348245", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-400'' -> ''-550''"}]'::jsonb),
