nn Beag [1]. The broch consists of a drystone tower which measures 18.3 metres in diameter, and currently stands to a maximum height of 10.2 metres to the west and northwest [1]. The external walls are 4.3 metres thick at the base and 1.2 metres thick at the top [1]. On the south side of the entrance passage is a small side-chamber, sometimes called a \"guard cell\" [1]. Access up the tower is by a winding stone stair, and openings at intervals once gave access to the upper floors [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98881", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98882", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149550", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/Dun Telve - Interior view.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237605", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310519", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/Dun Telve - Interior view.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/52258395/Dun Telve - geograph.org.uk - 188336.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348245", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-400'' -> ''-550''"}]'::jsonb),
