ediation_change_log:311146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/54bbb6a0/02025_2389_Zyndram''s_Hill_A_3700-year-old_mysterious_stronghold.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/54bbb6a0/Góra_Zyndrama._Prace_na_stanowisku_archeologicznym.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:337236", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4309:chunk-0001: description \"Zyndram''s Hill (Gora Zyndrama) in Maszkowice, southern Poland, is a prehistoric fortified settlement in the Beskid Wyspowy range of the Northern Carpathians. Radiocarbon dating places its earliest phase to 1750-1700 BC, when it was surrounded by massive dry-stone defensive walls 2-3 meters wide, representing the oldest known stone fortification in Poland and one of the earliest outside the Mediterranean. The site was occupied during the Early Bronze Age (1750-1550 BC) by the Mierzanowice culture, the Late Bronze and Early Iron Age (950-400 BC), and the La Tene period (200-50 BC). Only about 20% of the plateau has been excavated, with ongoing research by Jagiellonian University revealing pottery, bronze artifacts, and evidence of long-distance Mediterranean contacts.\" -> \"Zyndram''s Hill (Gora Zyndrama) in Maszkowice, southern Poland, is a prehistoric fortified settlement in the Beskid Wyspowy range of the Northern Carpathians [1]. The site was occupied during the Early Bronze Age (1750-1550 BC), the Late Bronze and Early Iron Age (950-400 BC), and the La Tene period (200-50 BC) [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355853", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
