t Buryan in Cornwall, considered one of the best-preserved fogous in the county. Unusual for having more than one entrance, it features a main passage with classic dry-stone and lintel construction plus a side chamber. Excavation yielded Iron Age pottery and a carved figure with a raised arm holding an unidentified object, possibly a spear. A 1996 Time Team investigation discovered remains of an early Iron Age house enclosed by an oval wall adjacent to the fogou, suggesting ritual or ceremonial use.'' -> ''Boleigh Fogou is an Iron Age underground dry-stone passage near St Buryan in Cornwall, considered one of the best-preserved fogous in the county [1] [2] [3]. Unusual for having more than one entrance, it features a main passage with classic dry-stone and lintel construction [1] [2]. Excavation yielded Iron Age pottery [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348996", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348997", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('55727fad-d494-42c3-9463-dc8c1b54d331'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:55727fad-d494-42c3-9463-dc8c1b54d331:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Illerup Ådal', '3f29b95dce052559d5a5b0850ab6471b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Archaeological site'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 15 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28323", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0111:chunk-0001: site_type ''Geological interest'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34533", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0030:chunk-0001: description ''A river valley and major Iron Age weapon sacrifice site near Skanderborg in East Jutland, Denmark. Excavated from 1950-1956 and 1975-1985, the site yielded over 15,000 items including weapons and personal equipment from 200-500 AD, with only 40% of the sacrifice area explored. The largest deposit, dating to c. 205 AD, contained 300 spear points (two inscribed with the runic name Wagnijo), plus shields, belts, combs, and the remains of four horses. The weapons are interpreted as enemy equipment captured after victories and thrown into the lake as votive offerings to the gods. It is one of 25 such weapon sacrifice sites in Denmark and southern Sweden.'' -> ''Illerup Ådal is a river valley and archeological site located near Skanderborg in East Jutland, Denmark [1]. The oldest deposit in Illerup Ådal contained 300 spear points, two with the name Wagnijo written in runes, plus shields, belts, and scabbards [1]. In addition, about 129 tinderboxes, and 124 combs were unearthed [1]. The first archaeological findings at the river valley of Illerup Ådal were revealed in 1950, during some drainage work [1]. The area was subsequently excavated from 1950 till 1956 and again from 1975 to 1985 [1]. During the excavations more than 15,000 items, mainly Iron Age weapons and personal equipment from 200 to 500 AD, were found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/IllerupAadal mod vest.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311152", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/IllerupAadal mod vest.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/IllerupAadal_mod_oest.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
