ame Wagnijo written in runes, plus shields, belts, and scabbards [1]. In addition, about 129 tinderboxes, and 124 combs were unearthed [1]. The first archaeological findings at the river valley of Illerup Ådal were revealed in 1950, during some drainage work [1]. The area was subsequently excavated from 1950 till 1956 and again from 1975 to 1985 [1]. During the excavations more than 15,000 items, mainly Iron Age weapons and personal equipment from 200 to 500 AD, were found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/IllerupAadal mod vest.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311152", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/IllerupAadal mod vest.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/55727fad/IllerupAadal_mod_oest.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
