ures a temple with 17 stone monoliths distributed around a ceremonial platform. Carved stones depict the sun god Tata Inti with eleven solar rays, the Andean serpent (Katari), and the Andean wildcat (Titi). The complex includes a solar gateway, astronomical observatory, burial structure, and stone staircases. On June 21st, the site hosts celebrations of the Andean New Year (Pachakuti). It was declared a National Cultural Heritage of Peru.\" -> \"Intini Uyu Pata (also called Inti Uyu) is an archaeological site in Peru''s Puno Region, Yunguyo Province, between the districts of Ollaraya and Unicachi [1] [2]. The site belongs to the Lupaca society of the Aymara domain and features a temple with 17 stone monoliths distributed around a ceremonial platform [2]. Carved stones depict the sun god Tata Inti with eleven solar rays, the Andean serpent (Katari), and the Andean wildcat (Titi) [2]. The complex includes a solar gateway, astronomical observatory, burial structure, and stone staircases [3]. On June 21st, the site hosts celebrations of the Andean New Year (Pachakuti) [2]. It was declared a National Cultural Heritage of Peru [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349000", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349001", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5614b867-438c-4c38-9a43-e2d04abe6dc0'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5614b867-438c-4c38-9a43-e2d04abe6dc0:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Vallée des Merveilles', '254a2582d931d491b685d2e17f177fb8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Petroglyphs'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44393", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0092:chunk-0001: description \"The Vallee des Merveilles in the Mercantour National Park of southern France contains over 35,000 Bronze Age rock engravings spread across 40 square kilometres, making it Europe''s largest open-air petroglyph collection after Val Camonica. Located on the slopes of Mont Bego in the Maritime Alps, the carvings depict cattle, weapons, anthropomorphic figures, and geometric patterns dating from approximately 3300 to 1200 BC. Systematic study began in 1967 under archaeologist Henry de Lumley, who theorised the engravings were created by a Mediterranean people who revered the bull and considered Mont Bego sacred.\" -> ''The Vallée des Merveilles, also known in Italian as the Valle delle Meraviglie, is a part of the Mercantour National Park in southern France [1]. It holds the largest quantity of open-air Bronze Age petroglyphs in Europe, after Val Camonica in Italy [1]. The valley is located near the Italian border, in the rugged mountains of the Argentera massif within the Maritime Alps, between Saint-Martin-Vésubie and Tende [1]. The petroglyphs (rock engravings), located on stone outcrops within the valley, were first identified by British amateur archaeologist Clarence Bicknell in 1881 [1]. Between 1897 and 1902, Bicknell copied and catalogued more than 10,000 drawings [1]. Suns, stars and spirals are represented [1]. Some anthropomorphic figures have been found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150142", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Vall%C3%A9e.merveilles.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5614b867/Vallée_des_Merveilles_101.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311167", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5614b867/Vallée_des_Merveilles_101.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5614b867/Vallée.merveilles.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
