s), located on stone outcrops within the valley, were first identified by British amateur archaeologist Clarence Bicknell in 1881 [1]. Between 1897 and 1902, Bicknell copied and catalogued more than 10,000 drawings [1]. Suns, stars and spirals are represented [1]. Some anthropomorphic figures have been found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150142", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/Vall%C3%A9e.merveilles.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5614b867/Vallée_des_Merveilles_101.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311167", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5614b867/Vallée_des_Merveilles_101.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5614b867/Vallée.merveilles.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
