ed in a relatively small or restricted area by people who lived there in the Jeulmun pottery period [1]. It was excavated three times by archaeologists of the National Museum of Korea from 1969 and was found to be among the oldest Jeulmun middens so far discovered in the southern part of the Korean Peninsula [1]. The presence of Yunggimun (appliqué-pattern) pottery indicates the site was occupied for a time between 8000-7000 BP, but many absolute dates generated from carbon that was excavated from the site indicate the site was also occupied in the Middle (c. 3500 BC) and Late (c. 2000 BC) Jeulmun sub-periods [1]. A variety of artifacts, including three types of pottery, and tools made of bone and stone were uncovered [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98945", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98946", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-9000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150148", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/Dongsam-dong_Shell_Midden.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237636", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237637", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/565483ad/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325029", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/565483ad/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/565483ad/Dongsam-dong Shell Midden.webp''"},