    ('577f59ce-ea47-4d39-a1f0-c5a0fd6e84d1'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '10', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:577f59ce-ea47-4d39-a1f0-c5a0fd6e84d1:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''10'' restored on Brown Clee Hill', 'f7b9b5978978c9d2bc8dc0edfe7f2a60', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start -800"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80872", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2011:chunk-0001: description \"At 540 metres, the highest hill in Shropshire and home to three Iron Age hillforts, of which only Nordy Bank survives intact. The univallate fort occupies a spur on the hill''s western side, enclosing an oval area of 3.2 hectares (260 m by 200 m) probably dating to the late Bronze Age or early Iron Age, around 400 BC. The other two forts at Abdon Burf and Clee Burf were largely destroyed by dolerite quarrying in the 19th and 20th centuries. Nordy Bank is a scheduled monument within the Shropshire Hills Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty.\" -> \"Brown Clee Hill is the highest hill in the rural English county of Shropshire [1]. Several Iron Age hill forts are dotted around the Clee Hills [1]. Nordy Bank is the last ''intact'' survivor of three hill forts on Brown Clee [1]. The other two, at Abdon Burf and Clee Burf, have been largely lost to quarrying activity [1]. Nordy Bank occupies a sloping ridge top site and its ramparts are up to three metres high [1]. It was built some time in the British Iron Age first millennium BC and gives a commanding view of the local countryside [1].\""}, {"sour