te": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/57ced914/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/57ced914/Beacon Hill - geograph.org.uk - 409967.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:337381", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4311:chunk-0001: description ''Beacon Hill is a Bronze Age hill fort site in Charnwood Forest, Leicestershire, rising to 248 m above sea level. Defensive earthworks discovered near the summit confirmed the presence of a fortified settlement believed to be up to 3,000 years old. In 1858, bronze jewellery, an axe, and a spearhead were unearthed at the site, now displayed at Charnwood Museum in Loughborough. The monument includes a slight univallate hillfort, a linear boundary, and an enclosure, and is legally protected as a Scheduled Ancient Monument by Historic England.'' -> ''Beacon Hill is a hill fort site in Charnwood Forest, Leicestershire, rising to 248 m above sea level [1] [2] [3]. The monument includes a slight univallate hillfort, a linear boundary, and an enclosure, and is legally protected as a Scheduled Ancient Monument by Historic England [4] [5] [6] [7].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349025", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
