s region[1]. The site contains ancient ruins of a Cucuteni-Trypillian culture settlement dating to the 5th millennium to early 4th millennium BC (c. 5000–3500 BC)[1][2]. Archaeological excavations have uncovered remains of this Neolithic-Eneolithic civilization known for its large settlements and elaborate ritual practices[2]. The village lies approximately 30 km northwest of Chernivtsi and about 530 km southwest of Kyiv[1].'' -> ''Shypyntsi (Ukrainian: Шипинці) is a village in Chernivtsi Raion, Chernivtsi Oblast, Ukraine, situated on the left bank of the Prut River in the Dniester Hills region [1]. The site contains ancient ruins of a Cucuteni-Trypillian culture settlement dating to the 5th millennium to early 4th millennium BC [1]. Archaeological excavations have uncovered remains of this Neolithic-Eneolithic civilization known for its large settlements [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345682", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345683", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25o_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357046", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25o_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-5000''"}]'::jsonb),
