ka River[1]. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by the National Institute of Culture[1].'' -> ''Pumamarka (Aymara and Quechua: puma meaning \"cougar\" and marka meaning \"village\", i.e. \"puma village\") is an archaeological park in Peru\\''s Cusco Region, situated in the San Sebastián District on the left bank of the Pumamarka River [1]. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by the National Institute of Culture [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:340454", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-005-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/58486903/Palacio Pumamarka, San Sebastián (2021) 04.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('58733868-7f7f-42e3-9d30-2fb9feb7fd05'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:58733868-7f7f-42e3-9d30-2fb9feb7fd05:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''6'' restored on Biannus', 'a88736023f46001d542ddcd34f067632', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84638", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2092:chunk-0001: description ''Biannus (or Biannos, Bienna) was an inland polis (city-state) of ancient Crete, listed among the 22 cities of Crete in the 6th-century Byzantine geographer Hierocles [1]. Located in eastern Crete, the city stood 170 stadia from Hierapytna and 270 stadia from Leben according to the Stadiasmus Maris Magni [1]. According to myth, the city derived its name from the violent contest between the giants Otus and Ephialtes and Ares, which allegedly occurred nearby [1]. The city minted its own coins during the Hellenistic period, evidence of its political and economic significance [1].'' -> ''Biannus or Biannos, or Biennus or Biennos, also Bienna, was an inland town and polis of ancient Crete [1]. It appears in the list of 22 cities of Crete of the sixth-century Byzantine geographer Hierocles [1]. According to the Stadiasmus Maris Magni, it was 170 stadia from Hierapytna and 270 stadia from Leben [1]. The contest of Otus and Ephialtes with Ares is said to have taken place near this city [1]. From this violent conflict the city is said to have derived its name [1]. The town minted coins in the Hellenistic perio