undations, a 1st-century pottery kiln, and a Byzantine basilica.'' -> ''The Macedonian Tower in Edirne, Turkey, is the sole surviving corner bastion of the Roman fortress built by Emperor Hadrian in the 2nd century AD when he founded the city as Hadrianopolis [1] [2] [3]. The rectangular castrum featured towers on all four corners [2] [3]. A wooden clock tower was built atop the Roman tower, later replaced in stone, but it was severely damaged by the 1953 earthquake and destroyed with dynamite that same year [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:340469", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-005-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/59a722b9/Edirne Roman Walls and Macedonian Tower 0210.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
