istinguishes this mountain from higher peaks surrounding it is its position within the Cotahuasi Canyon, one of the deepest canyons in the world [2]. The summit features an archaeological site dating to 1-500 AD, reflecting pre-Columbian activity in this region [3]. From its peak, visitors enjoy panoramic views of the canyon and adjacent mountains. Local communities venerate Huiñao as an apu, a sacred mountain spirit in Andean belief systems.'' -> ''Huiñao is a mountain in the Andes of Peru in the Cotahuasi District of La Unión Province, Arequipa Region [1]. What distinguishes this mountain from higher peaks surrounding it is its position within the Cotahuasi Canyon, one of the deepest canyons in the world [1] [2]. The summit features an archaeological site [1]. From its peak, visitors enjoy panoramic views of the canyon and adjacent mountains [1]. Local communities venerate Huiñao as an apu, a sacred mountain spirit in Andean belief systems [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349047", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> ''600''"}]'::jsonb),
