Arthurian literature, was identified with the Val de Rauco in the 19th century, the megalithic site near the Gurvant valley took the name of Hotié de Viviane [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99947", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99948", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5b182764/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5b182764/Val Sans Retour - Hotié de Viviane.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237681", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237682", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-3355''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311268", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5b182764/Val Sans Retour - Hotié de Viviane.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5b182764/La_Maison_de_Viviane.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
