    ('5bf42cbd-5082-43a3-b064-91ca60423e51'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5bf42cbd-5082-43a3-b064-91ca60423e51:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Camel Carving Site', '539f68bec58198a1ff76b966257097b1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Rock relief/carving'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 4 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84756", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2095:chunk-0001: description ''The Camel Carving Site near Sakaka in al-Jawf Province, Saudi Arabia, contains some of the oldest large-scale animal reliefs in the world, dating to the 6th millennium BCE. The site features 21 carvings including 17 life-sized camel reliefs and 2 equid figures, all produced using Neolithic stone tools. Discovered in 2016 and studied by an international Saudi-French-German team, radiocarbon dating places occupation between 5200 and 5600 BCE. The site has suffered from erosion, vandalism, and agricultural irrigation damage.'' -> ''The Camel Carving Site is considered one of the most prominent archaeological sites of Prehistoric Arabia [1]. It dates to the Neolithic period of the Al-Jawf region in modern-day Saudi Arabia, specifically located in the eastern center of Sakaka Governorate [1]. The site \"likely has the oldest known surviving large-scale animal reliefs in the world\", differing in execution from the rock art common throughout Saudi Arabia [1]. The site is also considered among Saudi Arabia\\''s oldest rock art sites, which typically feature two-dimensional carvings in both prominent and recessed styles [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99978", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Petroglyphs'' -> ''Rock relief/carving''"}]'::jsonb),
