allock road is nearby [1]. It is estimated to be 4,000-years-old, dating from the Bronze Age [1]. The largest stone is Rannach Chruim Duibh and is over 4m high and weighs 40 tonnes [1]. The entrance of the circle is aligned with the rising sun at the summer solstice [1]. A short distance to the north-north east of the main stone circle, is a second smaller circle, also constructed of large stones [1]. To the north of this is a large leaning standing stone [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100000", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/LoughGurStoneCircle-Apr2012.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311303", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/LoughGurStoneCircle-Apr2012.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/Grange_stone_circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
