gh Gur, 4 km north of Bruff [1]. The Limerick-Kilmallock road is nearby [1]. It is estimated to be 4,000-years-old, dating from the Bronze Age [1]. The largest stone is Rannach Chruim Duibh and is over 4m high and weighs 40 tonnes [1]. The entrance of the circle is aligned with the rising sun at the summer solstice [1]. A short distance to the north-north east of the main stone circle, is a second smaller circle, also constructed of large stones [1]. To the north of this is a large leaning standing stone [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100000", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/LoughGurStoneCircle-Apr2012.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311303", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/LoughGurStoneCircle-Apr2012.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d1b5446/Grange_stone_circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5d252b0e-96d1-4857-9883-72f508cabcd9'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5d252b0e-96d1-4857-9883-72f508cabcd9:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Badshot Lea Long Barrow', '57ccb01dad4f12d36b9dab53a9bab972', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Barrow'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 33 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84764", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2095:chunk-0001: description ''The only known Neolithic long barrow in Surrey, England, also called Farnham Long Barrow, probably built in the 4th millennium BC. Discovered in 1936 by W.F. Rankine, it was excavated by Alexander Keiller and Stuart Piggott before quarrying could destroy it. The earthen tumulus was approximately 43 m long with flanking side ditches. Finds included Neolithic pottery sherds, a polished flint axe fragment, and leaf-shaped arrowheads. Described in 1987 as \"the most impressive Neolithic feature yet located\" in Surrey.'' -> ''Badshot Lea Long Barrow, also known as Farnham Long Barrow, was an unchambered long barrow located near the village of Badshot Lea in the south-eastern English county of Surrey [1]. Although representing part of an architectural tradition of long barrow building that was widespread across Neolithic Europe, the Badshot Lea Long Barrow is the only known example in Surrey [1]. Built out of earth, the long barrow consisted of a tumulus flanked by side ditches [1]. A timber post was embedded into the eastern end of the mound [1]. By the mid-1930s, chalk quarrying adjacent to the long barrow had destroyed much of its southern side [1]. In 1936, local resident W. F. Rankine discovered ox bones and stone arrow-heads in the vicinity of the site [1]. An excavation was launched under the directorship of Alexander Keiller and Stuart Piggott [1]. The northern and southern sides of the tumulus were flanked with flat-bottomed, parallel ditches [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100001", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100002", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d252b0e/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237701", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237702", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
