ccupation of Menorca (end of the 2nd and 1st centuries BC) [1]. The site presents a great state of preservation as several of its structures show [1]. The most significant ones are three talayots or truncated-shape towers built with the cyclopean construction technique, the sanctuary, several hypogea, a large pit possibly for the storage of goods, and other remains, such as a stretch of a wall [1]. The easternmost talayot has an oval layout and its base is 19 meters in diameter [1]. Its façade is somewhat concave and is oriented to the South [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100005", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100006", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100007", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150945", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/Sacudiacremadahypogeum.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d316e03/Sa Cudia Cremada Hypogeum 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248797", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248798", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311309", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d316e03/Sa Cudia Cremada Hypogeum 2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d316e03/Sacudiacremadahypogeum.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349070", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_f