the Bronze Age, and contains several burial mounds in the form of cairns and bowl barrows [1]. Dunkery Hill was part of the \"Royal Forest of Exmoor\", established by Henry II according to the late 13th-century Hundred Rolls [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117680", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunkery_Hill'' -> ''https://www.exmoorher.co.uk/Monument/MEM22803''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150946", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/Dunkery Beacon memorial.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/Dunkery Beacon memorial.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/Dunkery_Beacon_summit_cairn.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
