ay [1]. The site has been visited by humans since the Bronze Age, and contains several burial mounds in the form of cairns and bowl barrows [1]. Dunkery Hill was part of the \"Royal Forest of Exmoor\", established by Henry II according to the late 13th-century Hundred Rolls [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117680", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunkery_Hill'' -> ''https://www.exmoorher.co.uk/Monument/MEM22803''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150946", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/Dunkery Beacon memorial.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/Dunkery Beacon memorial.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d3974ac/Dunkery_Beacon_summit_cairn.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5d3ec998-b314-4e52-bf91-3f2a90f8afaf'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5d3ec998-b314-4e52-bf91-3f2a90f8afaf:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Rough Tor', '3f5e1a1bd0189914f5d74e743f3398c1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 87 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84792", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2096:chunk-0001: description \"Rough Tor is an archaeologically rich tor on Bodmin Moor, Cornwall, standing at 400 metres above sea level as Cornwall''s second highest point. The summit features a Neolithic tor enclosure encircled by rough stone walls aligned with natural outcrops, with terraces believed to be foundations of circular wooden houses. Over 100 Bronze Age hut circles cluster on its southern slopes, representing more than a thousand years of settlement across multiple phases. Nearby lie the Fernacre and Stannon stone circles, numerous cairns, and a memorial to the 43rd Wessex Division.\" -> ''Rough Tor, or Roughtor (Cornish: Torr Garow), is a tor on Bodmin Moor, Cornwall, England, United Kingdom [1]. The site comprises the tor summit and logan stone, a Neolithic tor enclosure, many Bronze Age hut circles, and some contemporary monuments [1]. The summit of Rough Tor once had a Neolithic tor enclosure [1]. The summit is encircled by rough stone walls that align with natural stone outcroppings on the tor [1]. The walls would have originally completely encircled the tor and would have had numerous stone lined openings [1]. The Rough Tor enclosure is located in an area containing numerous upstanding monuments and other Bronze Age sites, such as Fernacre stone circle, which is only 200 metres from the site [1]. On the southern slopes of Rough Tor, there are the remains of numerous stone hut circles, set around three or four enclosures that may have held stock [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117681", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117682", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117683", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Earthwork'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150947", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/Iron_age_remains%2C_Rough_Tor_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1096814.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d3ec998/Roughtor Bodmin Moor-2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237707", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237708", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355861", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
