 high and 9 metres (30 ft) wide, and is covered on its south-east face with numerous petroglyphs, including depictions of horses and ibex [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35783", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Natural feature'' -> ''Petroglyphs''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100010", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100011", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248799", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248800", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349072", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349073", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5d5f1cc8-18af-42b2-860a-65862b328498'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5d5f1cc8-18af-42b2-860a-65862b328498:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Bremetennacum', 'cf78d1c17c6e12fa03769b033bdaa07c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fort'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44421", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0093:chunk-0001: description ''Bremetennacum Veteranorum was a Roman auxiliary fort at modern Ribchester in Lancashire, guarding a crossing of the River Ribble. First built in timber around AD 72-73 by Legio XX Valeria Victrix, it was rebuilt in stone in the early 2nd century and remained occupied until the 4th century. The fort covered about 6 acres and was garrisoned for much of its life by Sarmatian cavalry, stationed in Britain by Marcus Aurelius in AD 175. Its most famous find is the Ribchester Helmet, an elaborate bronze cavalry parade mask discovered in 1796 as part of a hoard. The site is a Scheduled Monument.'' -> ''Bremetennacum, ([brɛmɛˈteːnːakʊm]), or Bremetennacum Veteranorum, was a Roman fort on the site of the present day village of Ribchester in Lancashire [1]. The site guarded a crossing-point of the River Ribble [1]. For most of its existence the fort was garrisoned by Sarmatian auxiliaries, first stationed in Britain by Marcus Aurelius in 175 [1]. Pottery evidence indicates that the fort was occupied for most of the 4th century until the end of the Roman period [1]. The fort was renovated in the late 1st century AD and was rebuilt in stone in the early 2nd century [1]. Several altars were discovered from the Roman fort, including ones dedicated to the Matres and Moguns [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d5f1cc8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d5f1cc8/Ribchester bath house.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333862", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d5f1cc8/Ribchester bath house.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d5f1cc8/Roman_Relics_Ribchester_01.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
