ick construction ramps are still visible inside the great court. Despite its incomplete state, it serves as the main entrance to the Karnak temple complex today.'' -> ''The First Pylon of Karnak is the monumental entrance to the Precinct of Amun-Re, built by Nectanebo I during the 30th Dynasty (380-362 BC) but never completed [1] [2] [3]. It measures 113 metres wide and 15 metres thick, with the south tower reaching approximately 31.65 metres and the north tower about 21.70 metres, against a projected height of 38-40 metres [1] [2]. The mud brick construction ramps are still visible inside the great court [1] [2]. Despite its incomplete state, it serves as the main entrance to the Karnak temple complex today [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355862", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Gate'' -> ''Gate/archway/bridge''"}]'::jsonb),
