    ('5e1bd6c1-43bd-4a34-a7ae-7ea240f9f7b2'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5e1bd6c1-43bd-4a34-a7ae-7ea240f9f7b2:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on La Chapelle-aux-Saints', '1c231e18416430461bc002719adf4db0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80910", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2012:chunk-0001: description ''A cave site in Correze, central France, where the first recognized Neanderthal burial was discovered on 3 August 1908 by brothers Jean and Amedee Bouyssonie. The adult male skeleton, dating to roughly 50,000 years ago, was intentionally buried in a pit in the cave floor, providing the earliest evidence of mortuary ritual among Neanderthals. The individual died in his 30s despite surviving severe osteoarthritis, tooth loss, and a healed rib fracture, suggesting a social network that supported injured group members. Over 1,000 Mousterian flint tools and fauna including reindeer, horse, and rhinoceros remains were also recovered.'' -> ''The La Chapelle-aux-Saints cave, bordering the Sourdoire valley, revealed many archeological artifacts belonging to the late Mousterian techno-complex, including the first ever recognized Neanderthal burial discovered on 3 August 1908 [1]. The Bouffia Bonneval is the site of the discovery in 1908 of the Man of La Chapelle-aux-Saints, a site listed as a historical monument by decree of March 11, 1981 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117697", "ur