ion ''Gilwern Hill, about 5 km southeast of Llandrindod Wells in Powys, Wales, hosts a Neolithic-Bronze Age stone circle of approximately 14 stones, half of which have fallen. The hill also features two prehistoric stone rows at its southern end, each terminating in a large stone over 2 metres high. A separate standing stone of the needle type stands in peaty ground on the hill. The site is composed of Ordovician volcaniclastic rocks forming part of the Builth Inlier, also notable for trilobite fossils.'' -> ''The site is composed of Ordovician volcaniclastic rocks forming part of the Builth Inlier, also notable for trilobite fossils [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:340514", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-005-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/5e53212a/Gilwern Hill - geograph.org.uk - 4142783.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349080", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349081", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2300''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5e5354ff-e651-496a-a9bb-cf779d3cc501'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:5e5354ff-e651-496a-a9bb-cf779d3cc501:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Caer Drewyn', '96b0922f25014a738cbd0f4f2dc3a215', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start -800"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28058", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0060:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30413", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2097:chunk-0001: description ''Early Iron Age hillfort dating to around 500 BC, perched on a spur above the confluence of the River Dee near Corwen, Denbighshire. Unusually built largely of stone rather than earthen banks, the fort encloses about 3 hectares behind a large stone rampart with entrances on the west and north sides, a guard chamber within the north-east entrance, and a deep defensive ditch. The site saw later military use: Owain Gwynedd reportedly occupied it against Henry II in 1165, and Owain Glyndwr is said to have mustered troops here in 1400 after being proclaimed Prince of Wales.'' -> ''Caer Drewyn is an early Iron Age hillfort to the north of the town of Corwen, Denbighshire [1]. Caer Drewyn is the most southerly hillfort in the Clwydian Range and Dee Valley Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty [1]. It is situated on the spur of a hill between Llangollen and Corwen, commanding the valley junction and fertile plain at the confluence of the River Dee and the River Alwen [1]. The earliest structure was a small enclosure built against a natural rock outcrop [1]. A later, larger fortress was surrounded by a dry-stone wall, probably derived from the abundant scree in the area, and does not have the earthen ramparts of other local hillforts [1]. Caer Drewyn is an Iron Age fort dating back to about 500 BC, however it was in use as a defensive position long after this [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100027", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100028", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151008", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5e5354ff/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5e5354ff/Bryngaer_Geltaidd_Caer_Drewyn_Celtic_Hillfort_near_Corwen,_from_the_air;_2023_35.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237711", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237712", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349082", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349083", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
