ntains some 3,500 underground chambers carved into soft chalk, including 800 bell-shaped caves, used as cisterns, oil presses, columbaria (dovecotes), baths, stables, and burial areas across more than 2,000 years of habitation [1] [2]. Archaeological finds include a Roman-Byzantine amphitheatre, a Byzantine church, mosaics, and burial caves [1]. The cave complex was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2014 [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355864", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
