ia Reiche, a German-born mathematician who devoted over 50 years to studying and conserving the Nazca Lines. After her death in 1998 at age 95, the house was converted into a museum displaying her research materials, maps, blueprints, and archaeological finds. A waxwork of Reiche sits at her workspace, and she is buried on the grounds. The Nazca Lines she helped protect were designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1994.'' -> ''A waxwork of Reiche sits at her workspace, and she is buried on the grounds [1] [2]. The Nazca Lines she helped protect were designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1994 [3] [4].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:340529", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-005-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/5ed144bd/Maria Reiche Nazca.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
