    ('616719a2-c7ee-4162-b6f6-da52b85dbc4a'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:616719a2-c7ee-4162-b6f6-da52b85dbc4a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Matilo', 'a575a61973e958f7cf9871d8a9163050', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fort'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0233:chunk-0001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fortress/citadel''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84890", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2099:chunk-0001: description ''Matilo was a Roman fort (castellum) in modern-day Leiden, positioned on the southern banks of the Oude Rijn. It served to protect the Roman borders in the province of Germania Inferior [1]. On the Peutinger map, it lies between the encampments of Albaniana and Praetorium Agrippinae (Valkenburg) [1]. The seventh-century Ravenna Cosmography cites the name in the accusative case as Matellionem [1].'' -> \"Matilo or Matilone was once a Roman fort (castellum) in modern-day Leiden [1]. Positioned on the southern banks of the Oude Rijn, it served to protect the Roman borders in the province of Germania Inferior (Limes Germanicus) [1]. On the Peutinger map, it lies between the encampments of Albaniana (Alphen aan den Rijn) and Praetorium Agrippinae (Valkenburg) [1]. The first Romans arrived at the site in 47 AD as part of a larger operation to reinforce the Germanic lines [1]. In order to increase the efficiency of supply chains and communication lines within his army, general Gnaeus Domitius Corbulo had a canal built (known as the Fossa Corbulonis, or Corbulo''s Canal), connecting the Meuse and Rhine [1]. Matilo was erected there, at the meeting place of the Oude Rijn and the newly dug canal, because of its strategic importance [1]. Archaeological evidence seems to suggest that the Romans only constructed the fort itself somewhere at around 70 AD, whereas a small watchtower might have taken its place in the years before [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117747", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151112", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/616719a2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/616719a2/Matilo 20131017 oostkant 1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
