ocks from the immediate vicinity [1]. The oval chamber measures 10.8 to 9.8 metres, is paved and has a large fire spot in the middle [1]. In the south-west of the chamber a short aisle branches off to the right and leads to an unusually well-preserved staircase in the wall [1]. Finds included saddle and rotary querns, a potential stone ''lamp'' and several sherds of coarse pottery [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100095", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100096", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151121", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/Tappoch_Broch_-_southern_side_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1024967.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/61f1e287/Torwood_2025_(83).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249201", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249202", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311397", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/61f1e287/Torwood_2025_(83).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/61f1e287/Tappoch Broch - southern side - geograph.org.uk - 1024967.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
