hree different types of grave, a barrow, and a field wall system [1]. The area around the south and west flanks of Loughermore Mountain was first recorded as being an area with a significant number of ancient monuments in Ordnance Survey memoirs in 1835 [1]. However, many of these monuments have been damaged or destroyed [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100101", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249204", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325244", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/62406daa/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/62406daa/Wedge Tomb at Ballygroll.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
