nt in southern Quintana Roo, Mexico, about 1.1 km northwest of the main group. The complex features a large, high platform base supporting several multi-chambered buildings, with the main building dividing others between two terraces. During the Early Classic period, temples and elite residences were constructed at Lamay as Dzibanche became a major political center linked to the Kaanu''l (Serpent Kings) dynasty. The complexes are connected by sacbeob causeways up to 2.5 km long.\" -> \"Lamay is an ancient Maya architectural complex forming part of the larger Dzibanche settlement in southern Quintana Roo, Mexico [1]. Dzibanche became a major political center linked to the Kaanu''l (Serpent Kings) dynasty [2]. The complexes are connected by sacbeob causeways up to 2.5 km long [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349103", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349104", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
