nity of the River Medway, now known as the Medway Megaliths [1]. It lies near to both Chestnuts Long Barrow and Coldrum Long Barrow on the western side of the river [1]. The ruin attracted the interest of antiquarians in the early 18th century, and was studied by local archaeologists in the 20th [1]. Upon construction, the barrow would have been about 60 metres long [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151685", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/632852aa/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/632852aa/Addington Long Barrow, north side of road 07.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312030", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/632852aa/Addington Long Barrow, north side of road 07.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/632852aa/Addington_Long_Barrow,_north_side_of_road_01.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
