tury BC [1]. It is believed the stele once stood as part of the peribolos of the Aglaureion [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100137", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100138", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/642f4059/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/642f4059/Aglaureion Acropolis of Athens.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249227", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249228", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312051", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/642f4059/Aglaureion Acropolis of Athens.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/642f4059/The_Sanctuary_of_Aglaurus_on_April_28,_2021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349117", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349118", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('643c0a08-cde9-4a47-a05c-a1f72227f772'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:643c0a08-cde9-4a47-a05c-a1f72227f772:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Cellars of Diocletian''s Palace', '8357f96ef09dcb73c09ca541fec8c1fc', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Castle/palace'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84974", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2101:chunk-0001: description \"The Cellars of Diocletian''s Palace are substructures at the southern end of the 3rd-century AD palace in Split, Croatia, representing some of the best-preserved Roman substructures of their kind in the world. Built to elevate the emperor''s private apartments, they also served as storage for foodstuffs and wine, with a remnant of a large wine press still visible. In the Early Middle Ages, refugees adapted parts as residential areas. In 2024, archaeologists discovered a hidden passageway beneath Hrvojeva Street sealed for over 500 years, connecting to the cellars. The palace complex is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\" -> ''The Cellars of Diocletian\\''s Palace, sometimes referred to as the \"basement halls\", is a set of substructures, located at the southern end of Diocletian\\''s Palace (now the southernmost part of Split\\''s Old Town), that once held up the private apartments of Emperor Diocletian and represent one of the best preserved ancient complexes of their kind in the world [1]. Archeological research on the substructures over the past 70 years has revealed evidence of new structures, predating the palace by two centuries [1]. During the later Roman empire, the function of the cellars was partly to elevate the Emperor\\''s chambers on the floor above, but they were also the storage area for foodstuffs and wine for the Palace [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/643c0a08/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/643c0a08/Split_D81_3061_(37903099964).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333898", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/643c0a08/Split_D81_3061_(37903099964).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/643c0a08/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
