    ('648d388d-8532-4605-9345-1b656640455e'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:648d388d-8532-4605-9345-1b656640455e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Fleam Dyke', 'a0b34dff4262482b4295e6c308c5605d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Earthwork'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 11 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34823", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0034:chunk-0001: description ''Fleam Dyke is a linear earthwork spanning 4.8 km (3 mi) between Fulbourn and Balsham in Cambridgeshire, constructed between AD 330 and 510 [1]. The earthwork rises 7 metres high from ditch to bank, with its west-facing ditch suggesting construction by invading Saxons as a defensive barrier [1]. In the later Anglo-Saxon period, it served as the boundary of the Flendish Hundred administrative division [1]. Near Mutlow Hill, the earthwork passes a Bronze Age burial mound dating to approximately 2000 BC [1].'' -> ''Fleam Dyke is a linear earthwork between Fulbourn and Balsham in Cambridgeshire, initiated some time between AD 330 and AD 510 [1]. The dyke is located near Cambridge, between Fulbourn and Balsham [1]. It forms a barrier across an open chalkland ridge, bounded near Fulbourn by marshy fenland and near Balsham by 90-metre-high formerly wooded hills [1]. It is three miles long and seven metres high from ditch to bank [1]. In the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries Anglo-Saxon weapons and burials were found [1]. An excavation in 1991, on occasion of widening the A11 road, established by radiocarbon dating that it had been built in several phases, the first between AD 330 and 510, and the last between AD 450 and 620 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151701", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/648d388d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/648d388d/Fleam dyke near Balsham, Cambridgeshire. - panoramio (1).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
