_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4317:chunk-0001: description ''A large basaltic rock carving at the archaeological complex of Zonzamas on Lanzarote, Canary Islands, interpreted as a prehistoric lunisolar calendar with 12 solar and 13 lunar months, similar in structure to the ancient Egyptian calendar. Six carved channels represent the first six Canarian months of the Atxano year, which began at the summer solstice. The site is associated with the aboriginal Guanche/Majo culture and is argued to predate Punic or Roman contact, pointing to an Atlantic Bronze Age megalithic cultural horizon. Cart-ruts and Iberian-Guanche rock inscriptions found nearby further suggest a complex pre-classical prehistory for the islands.'' -> ''A large basaltic rock carving at the archaeological complex of Zonzamas on Lanzarote, Canary Islands, interpreted as a prehistoric lunisolar calendar with 12 solar and 13 lunar months, similar in structure to the ancient Egyptian calendar [1] [2]. The site is associated with the aboriginal Guanche/Majo culture and is argued to predate Punic or Roman contact, pointing to an Atlantic Bronze Age megalithic cultural horizon [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349125", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349126", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('64cf6ee2-708e-47c4-a2a6-0ec195d4917e'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:64cf6ee2-708e-47c4-a2a6-0ec195d4917e:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Goodaver Stone Circle', '742b9866dc2848e31baa5095091e06c0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -2500"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44453", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0094:chunk-0001: description \"Goodaver Stone Circle is a Bronze Age monument on Bodmin Moor in Cornwall, England, situated on Shepherd''s Hill at about 306 m altitude. The near-circular arrangement measures approximately 32 m in diameter and consists of around 23 end-set granite slabs ranging from 0.8 to 1.3 m in height. The site was extensively reconstructed in 1906 by Rev. A.H. Malan, before which only three stones remained standing, raising questions about the accuracy of current stone positions. It aligns with Craddock Moor Circle for summer solstice sunset observations.\" -> ''Goodaver stone circle or Goodaver circle is a stone circle located in the parish of Altarnun, near Bolventor on Bodmin Moor in Cornwall [1]. The stones are generally rectangular and measure between 0.6 metres and 1.6 metres high by 1.45 feet wide [1]. Reverend A. H. Malan discovered the circle in 1906 when only three stones remained standing [1]. Local farmers supplied workers to erect the fallen stones in their current position and it is clear that several stones were inverted, spaced incorrectly with some reversed faces and possibly in the wrong places [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100825", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249239", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249240", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349128", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
