aced atop moai statues. The soft, iron oxide-rich volcanic stone was intensively quarried between the 14th and 17th centuries, with roughly one-third of the crater consumed for pukao production. Beyond pukao, artisans also carved small statues, water containers, and moai eyes from this material. Red held sacred significance in Rapanui culture, associated with mana (spiritual power).'' -> ''Puna Pau is a small extinct volcanic crater on Easter Island that served as the sole quarry for the red scoria (hani hani) used to carve pukao -- the cylindrical topknots placed atop moai statues [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355874", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Quarry'' -> ''Mine/quarry''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357187", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357188", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> ''1250''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('66004bcf-8b17-4b3b-8dd0-ab55d21a1bd3'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:66004bcf-8b17-4b3b-8dd0-ab55d21a1bd3:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Jhukar-jo-Daro', '0f03ef16756d85d2955469684a7fd265', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Mound/tumulus'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80938", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2013:chunk-0001: description ''Jhukar-jo-Daro is a Chalcolithic mound site in Larkana District, Sindh, covering approximately 10 hectares with two main mounds separated by 300 feet. Excavated by N.G. Majumdar in 1927-28, it is the type site for the Jhukar Phase (c. 1900-1300 BCE), a post-urban regional variant of the Indus Valley Civilization. Finds include distinctive bichrome pottery, terracotta figurines, carnelian beads, geometric seals, and about 50 mud-brick rooms. The site illuminates the transition from urban Mature Harappan centers to decentralized settlements during the Localization Era.'' -> ''The Jhukar-jo-Daro is the highest mud mound in Larkana, located at a distance of 6 miles (10 kilometers) from Larkana city towards west near to village Mithodero on the left of the Larkana-Mehar Road (N55 National Highway) in Larkana District, Sindh, Pakistan [1]. It was explored and excavated by renowned archaeologist N. G. Majumdar in 1928 [1]. The remains of late Harappan culture of Chalcolithic period were discovered here at Jhukar-Jo-Daro [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151731", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66004bcf/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66004bcf/Jhukar mound 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238566", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: lat ''27.558571064634943'' -> ''27.559972''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238567", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: lon ''68.21095016352173'' -> ''68.126261''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323025", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66004bcf/Jhukar mound 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66004bcf/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325250", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66004bcf/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66004bcf/Jhukar-jo-Daro.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
