 in 1754 showing eighteen stones standing and one fallen, and at some time in the next hundred years a Cornish hedge was constructed through the circle [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100839", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100840", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-2400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151740", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66b6fcb0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66b6fcb0/Boscawen-Un (01).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312087", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66b6fcb0/Boscawen-Un (01).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66b6fcb0/Boscawen-Un_stone_circle_2011.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('66be5990-dc1f-47f2-bc11-367354a63a14'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:66be5990-dc1f-47f2-bc11-367354a63a14:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on First Ancient Theatre, Larissa', '3608e6bd8bfd85ab6a3f666ab330c7f9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Theatre'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 28 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2013:chunk-0001: description ''The First Ancient Theatre of Larissa, built in the early 3rd century BC during the reign of Philip V of Macedon, is the largest theater in Thessaly with a capacity of around 10,000. Beyond performances, it hosted meetings of the Thessalian Koinon, the supreme administrative body of the region. In the 1st century BC it was converted into a Roman arena by removing front rows to widen the orchestra. The theater was in use for six centuries until earthquakes in the 3rd-4th century AD caused its collapse. Restoration costing 5.9 million euros repositioned over 15,000 marble pieces, and the theater reopened in 2023.'' -> ''The First Ancient Theatre of Larissa was built in the center of the ancient city of Larissa, during the reign of king Philip V of Macedon, towards the end of the 3rd century BC [1]. The theatre was in use for six centuries until the end of the 3rd century AD (or the beginning of the 4th century AD) when its operation stopped abruptly [1]. During the first centuries, the theatre was used for two purposes: in addition to theatrical performances, it also hosted the meetings of the highest regional authority, the so-called Koinon of Thessaly [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151741", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66be5990/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66be5990/Ancient-theater.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312090", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/66be5990/Ancient-theater.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/66be5990/Λάρισα,_αρχαίο_Θέατρο_Α_4.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
