_change_log:337863", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4317:chunk-0001: description ''Brean Down Fort is a Victorian Palmerston Fort built 18 m above sea level on the Brean Down headland in Somerset, constructed between 1864 and 1871 to defend the Bristol Channel approaches to Bristol and Cardiff. Armed with seven 7-inch guns from Woolwich, it was garrisoned by 50 Royal Artillery personnel. The fort never saw combat. In 1897, Guglielmo Marconi used the site to set a new distance record of 14 km for wireless transmission over open sea. Its active service ended when the No. 3 magazine containing 3 tons of gunpowder exploded on 6 July 1900. Restored by the National Trust from 2002, it is now open to the public.'' -> ''Brean Down Fort is a Victorian Palmerston Fort built 18 m above sea level on the Brean Down headland in Somerset, constructed between 1864 and 1871 to defend the Bristol Channel approaches to Bristol and Cardiff [1]. Armed with seven 7-inch guns from Woolwich, it was garrisoned by 50 Royal Artillery personnel [1]. The fort never saw combat [1]. In 1897, Guglielmo Marconi used the site to set a new distance record of 14 km for wireless transmission over open sea [1]. Its active service ended when the No. 3 magazine containing 3 tons of gunpowder exploded on 6 July 1900 [1]. It is now open to the public [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355875", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
