 is to be found in Arsameia, the burial site and the associated cultic area for Antiochus'' father Mithridates [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118841", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118842", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> ''-300''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118843", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355876", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
