 findings at Lake Mungo have been Mungo Man and Mungo Woman [1]. Mungo Woman was only partially cremated before the remainder of her bones were crushed [1]. The first evidence of human occupation in Lake Mungo was revealed after an excavation of two Lake Mungo trenches contained 11 silcrete flakes [1]. Fish otoliths have been recovered from hearths in Lake Mungo [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100861", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100862", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151767", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/68677772/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/68677772/Lake_Mungo_lunette.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249259", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249260", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349133", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349134", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-48050''"}]'::jsonb),
