    ('695ddb9f-70cb-4e8a-9020-4bebf0b06227'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:695ddb9f-70cb-4e8a-9020-4bebf0b06227:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Tomb of Cyrus the Great', '95409dc4ab52b9e807b0294fe2fb2bc2', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 24 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85080", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2104:chunk-0001: description \"The Tomb of Cyrus the Great (c. 530 BC) at Pasargadae is the mausoleum of the founder of the Achaemenid Empire. The structure measures approximately 13.75 x 12.25 m and stands about 11 m high, consisting of a six-step stone platform topped by a gabled burial chamber. Built of white limestone blocks, the chamber once housed a gold sarcophagus, Cyrus''s arms, jewelry, and a ceremonial cloak. Part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Pasargadae, the tomb is considered the oldest base-isolated structure in the world, demonstrating early earthquake engineering.\" -> \"The tomb of Cyrus the Great is located in Pasargadae, which was the first capital city of his Achaemenid Empire and is now an archaeological site in the Fars Province of Iran [1]. The tomb of Cyrus is located in the southern corner of the site, which was once the royal park of Pasargadae and is built of yellowish-white limestone, probably from the Sivand mine [1]. The tomb building has been resistant to natural and unnatural factors for 2,500 years and is still standing in Pasargad plain [1]. Its main base or foundation is a stone platform whose design forms a rectangular square with a length of 13.35 m and a width of 12.3 m [1]. This building consists of two completely separate parts: a six-step stone platform, and a room with a gabled roof over the sixth step [1]. The total height of the building is a little over 11 m [1]. The design of Cyrus''s tomb is credited to Mesopotamian or Elamite ziggurats, but the cella is usually attributed to Urartu tombs of an earlier period [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151781", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/Pasargad_Tomb_Cyrus3.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/Tomb_of_Madre_Suleiman.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323044", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/Tomb_of_Madre_Suleiman.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325253", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/Pasargad Tomb Cyrus3.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
