rs and is still standing in Pasargad plain [1]. Its main base or foundation is a stone platform whose design forms a rectangular square with a length of 13.35 m and a width of 12.3 m [1]. This building consists of two completely separate parts: a six-step stone platform, and a room with a gabled roof over the sixth step [1]. The total height of the building is a little over 11 m [1]. The design of Cyrus''s tomb is credited to Mesopotamian or Elamite ziggurats, but the cella is usually attributed to Urartu tombs of an earlier period [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151781", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/Pasargad_Tomb_Cyrus3.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/Tomb_of_Madre_Suleiman.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323044", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/Tomb_of_Madre_Suleiman.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325253", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/695ddb9f/Pasargad Tomb Cyrus3.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
