aves beneath it, surrounded by a deep defensive ditch carved directly into rock on all four sides [1]. Building remains and a water well have been documented within the castle complex [1].'' -> ''Cimdin Kalesi is a fortress built on a rocky hill in southeastern Turkey [1] [2]. Constructed of hard limestone with white cut stone walls and bastions, the castle was used by Byzantine, Arab, and Akkoyunlu forces [3]. The interior was filled with rubble stone, and the western entrance features large caves beneath it, surrounded by a deep defensive ditch carved directly into rock on all four sides [1] [3]. Building remains and a water well have been documented within the castle complex [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349141", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349142", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''101'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355878", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Castle'' -> ''Castle/palace''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('69b83929-86e2-4a3e-8e0d-2418db5192ed'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:69b83929-86e2-4a3e-8e0d-2418db5192ed:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Königsaue', '942f466655caec2c199a9aecb7fc027a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -78050"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34861", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0035:chunk-0001: description ''Konigsaue is a Middle Palaeolithic site in Saxony-Anhalt, Germany, discovered in 1963 by Dieter Mania during rescue excavations in an open-pit lignite mine. Dating to approximately 80,000 BP during the Eemian interglacial, it was a seasonal Neanderthal hunting camp on the shore of paleo-lake Aschersleben, yielding three archaeological horizons with Mousterian and Micoquian tool assemblages. The site is renowned for two birch tar pieces (1.35g and 0.83g) representing the oldest known synthetic substance, whose chemical analysis revealed Neanderthals used sophisticated underground distillation rather than simple above-ground methods, evidencing cumulative cultural evolution.'' -> ''Königsaue is also a middle palaeolithic find spot [1]. It dates to about 80.000 BP [1]. Three settlement layers can be distinguished, separated by limnic sediments [1]. Ca. 6000 flints have been excavated, including a few bifacially worked knives and small pointed hand axes of Micoquien type [1]. Layers A and C belong to the Micoquien, B to the Mousterian [1]. Animal bones show that Mammoth, woolly haired rhino, horses, red deer and reindeer were hunted [1]. The most famous finds from Königsaue are two pieces of birch-pitch, one of which shows the partial finger-print of a Neanderthal [1]. It shows the impression of a piece of wood as well and was thus used for hafting a composite tool [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100885", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-78000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/69b83929/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249267", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249268", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343799", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/69b83929/View to Neu Königsaue (Aschersleben).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357221", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357222", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-78050''"}]'::jsonb),
