es, red deer and reindeer were hunted [1]. The most famous finds from Königsaue are two pieces of birch-pitch, one of which shows the partial finger-print of a Neanderthal [1]. It shows the impression of a piece of wood as well and was thus used for hafting a composite tool [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100885", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-78000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/69b83929/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249267", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249268", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343799", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/69b83929/View to Neu Königsaue (Aschersleben).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357221", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357222", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-78050''"}]'::jsonb),
