uted to the UNESCO World Heritage designation of the Stora Alvaret landscape.'' -> ''Alby is a village on the island of Oland, Sweden, with one of the oldest settlements on the island, dating to the Mesolithic era around 7000-6000 BC [1]. The earliest settlers, known archaeologically as the Alby People, built wooden huts on the edge of a prehistoric lagoon and subsisted by hunting, fishing, and gathering [1]. The nearby Hulterstad grave field contains over 170 burials [1]. The Alby Mesolithic village contributed to the UNESCO World Heritage designation of the Stora Alvaret landscape [1] [2].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('69ef4043-f69f-4f87-b422-09eb53a72950'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:69ef4043-f69f-4f87-b422-09eb53a72950:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Cave del Valle, Cantabria', '6f0bccb6f37cd8e8e1405bc9fb386e7e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85086", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2104:chunk-0001: description ''Prehistoric cave in the municipality of Rasines, Cantabria, northern Spain, serving as the source of the Rio Silencio. The underground system known as Caballos-Valle spans 60.2 km of passage with 447 m of elevation change, making it the longest cavity in the region and second longest in Spain. In 1905, priest Lorenzo Sierra discovered Azilian harpoons, Upper Magdalenian spear points, and other bone tools documenting human occupation from c. 7000 BC. In 1983, a rock carving depicting a goat head in frontal view was found, attributed to the Upper Final Magdalenian period (c. 12,000 years old). The site now operates as a Paleolithic Park featuring the cave vestibule and a life-size mammoth recreation.'' -> \"Cave del Valle (Spanish: Cueva del Valle, The Valley''s Cave), locally also known as La Viejarrona (Old Girl), is located near El Cerro Village in the municipality of Rasines in Cantabria, northern Spain [1]. The cave is the source of the Silencio River, a tributary of the Rio Ruahermosa, which in turn is a tributary of the Asón River [1]. Documented are Azilian harpoons and scrapers, Upper Magdalenian spear points and other bone tools [1]. Stone tools include chisels and various types of scrapers [1]. A perforated and decorated stick of archaeological interest was found at this site, but is now lost [1]. The cave of the valley is recognized as one of the longest explored caves in the world with more than 40 mi yet explored [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100890", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100891", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-7000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238592", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238593", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-7000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312138", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/69ef4043/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/69ef4043/Cueva_del_Valle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
