{"source": "remediation_change_log:337944", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4318:chunk-0001: description ''Mawk\\''allaqta (Quechua: mawk\\''a \"ancient\" + llaqta \"place\") is an archaeological site in the Nunoa District, Melgar Province, Puno Region of southern Peru. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by the National Institute of Culture. It is one of at least six sites bearing the name Mawk\\''allaqta across Peru\\''s highland regions, reflecting the Quechua naming convention for ancient settlements.'' -> ''Mawk\\''allaqta (Quechua: mawk\\''a \"ancient\" + llaqta \"place\") is an archaeological site in the Nunoa District, Melgar Province, Puno Region of southern Peru [1] [2]. The site was declared a National Cultural Heritage (Patrimonio Cultural) of Peru by the National Institute of Culture [1]. It is one of at least six sites bearing the name Mawk\\''allaqta [3].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6a111273-edf6-44f2-b282-a7ac9477aa98'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:6a111273-edf6-44f2-b282-a7ac9477aa98:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Teufelsstein, Haardt', '836e03e6e1bb2bc77a97562a85303624', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85090", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2104:chunk-0001: description ''The Teufelsstein is a sandstone monolith approximately 2.5 metres tall and 4 metres wide, situated atop a 317 m hill near Bad Durkheim in the Palatinate Forest. Five steps are carved into the rock leading to a hollow interpreted as a sacrifice bowl, with a channel or \"blood groove\" running down the side. The stone bears Celtic Iron Age cup marks and grooves, as well as later medieval crosses and geometric signs, indicating the site remained spiritually significant across many centuries. The monolith rises above the remnants of an ancient Celtic ring wall, suggesting it served as a sacred ceremonial center.'' -> ''The Teufelsstein in the Haardt mountains, near the Palatine county town of Bad Dürkheim in the German state of Rhineland-Palatinate, is a hill 317 m above sea level [1]. On its domed summit is a monolith of the same name (which means \"Devil\\''s Rock\") [1]. Traces of human activity on the rock indicate that it acted as a cult object in former times [1]. The Teufelsstein, which gave the hill its name, is a rock formation about 2.50 metres high and up to 4 metres wide [1]. Five steps have been carved into the rock, staircase-fashion, leading to the top where there is a hollow which is thought to be a sacrifice bowl for religious rites of its former, probably Celtic users and from which a blood channel runs down the rock by the steps [1]. In addition, the rock has numerous symbols carved into it, dating to various periods [1]. As well as sun wheels, runes and Roman letters there are several markings that recall the stonemason\\''s marks of the 12th and 13th centuries [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151817", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Teufelsstein_%28Pfalz%29.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6a111273/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249271", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249272", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6a111273/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6a111273/Teufelsstein (Pfalz).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349145", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
