d up to 4 metres wide [1]. Five steps have been carved into the rock, staircase-fashion, leading to the top where there is a hollow which is thought to be a sacrifice bowl for religious rites of its former, probably Celtic users and from which a blood channel runs down the rock by the steps [1]. In addition, the rock has numerous symbols carved into it, dating to various periods [1]. As well as sun wheels, runes and Roman letters there are several markings that recall the stonemason\\''s marks of the 12th and 13th centuries [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151817", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Teufelsstein_%28Pfalz%29.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6a111273/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249271", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249272", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6a111273/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6a111273/Teufelsstein (Pfalz).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349145", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
