ttle community of Bella Flores north of Singa [1]. Wat''a is situated at a height of about 3,889 metres on top of a mountain which is bordered by the little rivers Tawlli and Aqu [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118881", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: lat ''-9.367109446811607'' -> ''-9.357669''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118882", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: lon ''-76.7925678178729'' -> ''-76.809532''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118883", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152272", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Wata_(Huánuco)_01078.jpg/400px-Wata_(Huánuco)_01078.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6b730ea0/Huata 00612.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249289", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249290", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349159", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349160", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6bb12b0e-f96b-4243-a96f-395cc7c5d317'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:6bb12b0e-f96b-4243-a96f-395cc7c5d317:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Karla Buddha Caves', 'd4938f8d37f11ccaf7cfbfa6e0353cb0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cave Structures'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 19 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85124", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2105:chunk-0001: description ''A complex of ancient Buddhist rock-cut caves near Lonavala in Maharashtra, India, about 60 km from Pune, developed between the 2nd century BC and the 5th century AD. The site comprises 16 caves built by the Mahasamghika school of Buddhism. Its Great Chaitya hall (Cave 8), completed around 120 AD, is the largest rock-cut chaitya in India at 45 metres long and 14 metres high, with 37 octagonal pillars and original teak wood roof timbers. The caves contain donatory inscriptions from merchants, monks, and rulers including Nahapana. A protected monument under the Archaeological Survey of India.'' -> ''The Karla Caves, Karli Caves, Karle Caves or Karla Cells, are a complex of ancient Buddhist Indian rock-cut caves at Karli near Lonavala, Maharashtra [1]. The shrines were developed over the period from the 2nd century BCE to the 5th century CE [1]. The caves were historically associated with the Mahāsāṃghika sect of Buddhism which had great popularity in this region of India, as well as wealthy patronage [1]. The caves house a Buddhist monastery dating back to the 2nd century BC [1]. The main cave, called the Great Chaitya cave, or Cave No. 8, features a large, intricately carved chaitya within a prayer hall [1]. This is the largest rock-cut chaitya in India, measuring 45 metres long and up to 14 metres high [1]. The hall features sculptures of both males and females, as well as animals such as lions and elephants [1]. Numerous donors, mainly local merchants, several of them Yavanas, as well as numerous Buddhist monks and nuns, provided donations for the construction of the chaitya cave, as recorded by their dedicatory inscriptions [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152278", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/KarlaCavesStatue1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312163", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/KarlaCavesStatue1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/Karla_caves_Chaitya.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6bb12b0e-f96b-4243-a96f-395cc7c5d317'::uuid, 'rarity_score', '40', '34', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:6bb12b0e-f96b-4243-a96f-395cc7c5d317:rarity_score', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: rarity_score ''34'' restored on Karla Buddha Caves', 'd4938f8d37f11ccaf7cfbfa6e0353cb0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "rarity_score = 40 from mystery 6, cultural_influence 10"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85124", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2105:chunk-0001: description ''A complex of ancient Buddhist rock-cut caves near Lonavala in Maharashtra, India, about 60 km from Pune, developed between the 2nd century BC and the 5th century AD. The site comprises 16 caves built by the Mahasamghika school of Buddhism. Its Great Chaitya hall (Cave 8), completed around 120 AD, is the largest rock-cut chaitya in India at 45 metres long and 14 metres high, with 37 octagonal pillars and original teak wood roof timbers. The caves contain donatory inscriptions from merchants, monks, and rulers including Nahapana. A protected monument under the Archaeological Survey of India.'' -> ''The Karla Caves, Karli Caves, Karle Caves or Karla Cells, are a complex of ancient Buddhist Indian rock-cut caves at Karli near Lonavala, Maharashtra [1]. The shrines were developed over the period from the 2nd century BCE to the 5th century CE [1]. The caves were historically associated with the Mahāsāṃghika sect of Buddhism which had great popularity in this region of India, as well as wealthy patronage [1]. The caves house a Buddhist monastery dating back to the 2nd century BC [1]. The main cave, called the Great Chaitya cave, or Cave No. 8, features a large, intricately carved chaitya within a prayer hall [1]. This is the largest rock-cut chaitya in India, measuring 45 metres long and up to 14 metres high [1]. The hall features sculptures of both males and females, as well as animals such as lions and elephants [1]. Numerous donors, mainly local merchants, several of them Yavanas, as well as numerous Buddhist monks and nuns, provided donations for the construction of the chaitya cave, as recorded by their dedicatory inscriptions [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152278", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/KarlaCavesStatue1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312163", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/KarlaCavesStatue1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6bb12b0e/Karla_caves_Chaitya.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
