    ('6be9a7f1-53c8-447b-8c63-d6cc40f2281e'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:6be9a7f1-53c8-447b-8c63-d6cc40f2281e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Font-de-Gaume', 'bdcac988912d1512e5c8b7f01f26e351', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0231:chunk-0001: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-17000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30428", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80964", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2014:chunk-0001: description ''Font-de-Gaume is a cave near Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil in the Dordogne department of southwest France. The cave contains prehistoric polychrome cave paintings and engravings dating to the Magdalenian period, approximately 17,000 years old [1]. Discovered in 1901, more than 200 images have been identified, including representations of mammoths, bison, horses, and reindeer [1]. Along with other nearby prehistoric archaeological sites, Font-de-Gaume was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1979 as the Prehistoric Sites and Decorated Caves of the Vézère Valley [1].'' -> ''Font-de-Gaume is a cave near Les Eyzies in the Dordogne department of south-west France [1]. The cave contains prehistoric polychrome cave paintings and engravings dating to the Magdalenian period [1]. The paintings were discovered by Denis Peyrony, a local schoolmaster, on 12 September 1901 [1]. The paintings in the cave at Font-de-Gaume were the first to be discovered in the Périgord province [1]. Prehistoric people living in the Dordogne Valley first settled in the mouth of Font-de-Gaume around 25,000 BC [1]. The cave mouth was inhabited at least sporadically for the next several thousand years [1]. To date, 230 figures have been recorded in the cave, and it is thought that more are still to be revealed [1]. The rock art in Font-de-Gaume includes depictions of more than 80 bison, approximately 40 horses, and more than 20 mammoths [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152281", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6be9a7f1/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6be9a7f1/Font-de-Gaume_entree.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
