 [1]. Also found were two Anglo-Saxon burials which had been cut into the top of the existing mound [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100929", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249658", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312172", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6c689af9/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6c689af9/Lyneham Longbarrow - geograph.org.uk - 3144.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
