ring petroglyphs on the boulder with patterns on ceramics from the region suggests that the petroglyphs, made over the Late Archaic soapstone extraction scars, date somewhere between the Middle Woodland and late Mississippian culture periods, roughly 200 CE to 1400 CE [1]. Judaculla Rock retains a special significance for the Cherokee [1]. Judaculla Rock contains approximately 1,548 motifs [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100938", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1'' -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152315", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6cb8a98b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6cb8a98b/Judaculla Rock May 30 2021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312184", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6cb8a98b/Judaculla Rock May 30 2021.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6cb8a98b/Judaculla_Rock,_Caney_Fork,_NC_Aug_2019.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6cc29702-81c5-4a0a-bc3e-a62de9545b3a'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:6cc29702-81c5-4a0a-bc3e-a62de9545b3a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Pusharo', 'da92e8876944c70f0a3a8ceb37835071', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Petroglyphs'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 5 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34879", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0035:chunk-0001: description \"The Petroglyphs of Pusharo are an extensive ancient rock art site deep within Peru''s Manu National Park, along the Palotoa River. The carvings cover a perpendicular rock face over 30 meters long, reaching heights of 2.7 meters, and are estimated to be 1,000-2,000 years old. The deeply incised images depict geometric patterns, animal motifs including jaguars and serpents, and human figures, possibly linked to the Machiguenga or other Amazonian groups. Recognized as archaeological heritage by Peru''s National Institute of Culture in 2003.\" -> ''The Petroglyphs of Pusharo constitute a unique and extensive ancient rock art archaeological site in southeastern Peru\\''s Manú National Park, an expanse of rain forest that still contains unexplored and little known areas [1]. A smattering of adventurers began to arrive at the site in the 1950s, and in 1969 it was visited by the Peruvian physician Dr. Carlos Neuenschwander Landa [1]. In 1991 the party of North American explorer Gregory Deyermenjian arrived at Pusharo [1]. The site has since been visited and studied by rock art scholar Rainer Hostnig [1]. The site is made up of an array of deeply incised rock carvings that cover up to a height of 9 feet, a perpendicular rock face that is over 100 feet long and 75 feet high [1]. Its location is on the south shore of the Río Palatoa (designated on some maps at this location as the Porotoa, and known by others as the Palatoa Chico) [1]. The petroglyphs contain elements such as heart-shaped faces, some with double borders, spirals, zigzags, suns, \"curlicue Xs\" and others that defy verbal description [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152316", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/6cc29702/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238609", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238610", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}]'::jsonb),
