close to the upper Lamorna River [1]. The barrow is a circular mound of earth and stones, measuring up to 20 feet in diameter [1]. The mound is surrounded and retained by a border of large granite blocks [1]. It contains a rectangular stone-lined chamber measuring 7.5 ft long by 4 ft wide and 3 ft high [1]. The chamber is roofed with two capstones: a third capstone was removed at some point [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312193", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6d28ceb7/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6d28ceb7/Brane burial chamber - geograph.org.uk - 1040.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
