ture (c. 5500-4800 BC), one of the earliest town-states in the Near East [1] [2] [3]. The city became the capital of the Abbasid Caliphate from 836 to 892 AD, stretching 32 km along the river [1] [4]. Designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2007, Samarra has been on the List of World Heritage in Danger since inscription, with 80% of the site still unexcavated [5].''"}]'::jsonb),
