ption ''Lakhan-Jo-Daro is one of the largest cities of the Indus Valley civilization, located near Sukkur in Sindh, Pakistan, roughly 120 km southwest of Mohenjo-Daro. Covering over 300 hectares, the site rivals Mohenjo-Daro in scale. Carbon-14 testing by the University of Groningen dated samples to approximately 3,960 years old, and deep excavations revealed artifacts predating Mohenjo-Daro. Finds include terracotta wheels, stone weights, copper items, seals, and a faience mirror factory.'' -> ''Lakhan-Jo-Daro is one of the largest cities of the Indus Valley civilization, located near Sukkur in Sindh, Pakistan [1] [2] [3]. Carbon-14 testing by the University of Groningen dated samples to approximately 3,960 years old [4]. Finds include stone weights, copper items, seals, and a faience mirror factory [5] [6] [7].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349903", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349904", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
