"url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4320:chunk-0001: description ''Lakhan-Jo-Daro is one of the largest cities of the Indus Valley civilization, located near Sukkur in Sindh, Pakistan, roughly 120 km southwest of Mohenjo-Daro. Covering over 300 hectares, the site rivals Mohenjo-Daro in scale. Carbon-14 testing by the University of Groningen dated samples to approximately 3,960 years old, and deep excavations revealed artifacts predating Mohenjo-Daro. Finds include terracotta wheels, stone weights, copper items, seals, and a faience mirror factory.'' -> ''Lakhan-Jo-Daro is one of the largest cities of the Indus Valley civilization, located near Sukkur in Sindh, Pakistan [1] [2] [3]. Carbon-14 testing by the University of Groningen dated samples to approximately 3,960 years old [4]. Finds include stone weights, copper items, seals, and a faience mirror factory [5] [6] [7].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349903", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349904", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6de0d66c-8252-46f9-9f71-dd6210234681'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:6de0d66c-8252-46f9-9f71-dd6210234681:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Isturitz and Oxocelhaya Caves', 'b84c6f6a4fc903db435e80c05e16b69b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80974", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2015:chunk-0001: description ''Isturitz and Oxocelhaya Caves in southwestern France contain a remarkable stratigraphy spanning Neanderthal and modern human occupation [1]. Excavations revealed a Neanderthal mandible alongside Aurignacian, Solutrean and Magdalenian artifacts [1]. The site features cave paintings and bone flutes, making it one of the few French Paleolithic sites with both art and musical instruments [1]. Located on Gaztelu hill in the Arberoue Valley, the caves sit at the crossroads of the French Basque Country and Lower Navarre in the foothills of the Pyrenees [1].'' -> ''The Isturitz and Oxocelhaya caves are an important Paleolithic site where a Neanderthal mandible was found, as well as later modern human finds associated with the Aurignacian, Solutrean and Magdalenian [1]. They also include cave paintings and bone flutes [1]. The caves are located in the Gaztelu hill in the Arberoue Valley in the foothills of Pyrenees, in Lower Navarre, a traditional region of the department of Pyrénées-Atlantiques, southwestern France, part of the French Basque Country [1]. The Isturitz cave is divided into two parts: the Hall of Saint-Martin and the Main Hall or Hall of Isturitz [1]. The most common human remains from Isturitz are cranial vaults, which have been cut-marked and modified to create drinking cups, dating from the Magdalenian [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100959", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100960", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152338", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/The entery of Isturitz and Oxocelhaya caves (2024).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238625", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-80000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/The entery of Isturitz and Oxocelhaya caves (2024).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/The_entry_of_the_cave_of_Isturitz.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
