rn France, part of the French Basque Country [1]. The Isturitz cave is divided into two parts: the Hall of Saint-Martin and the Main Hall or Hall of Isturitz [1]. The most common human remains from Isturitz are cranial vaults, which have been cut-marked and modified to create drinking cups, dating from the Magdalenian [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100959", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100960", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152338", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/The entery of Isturitz and Oxocelhaya caves (2024).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238625", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-80000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/The entery of Isturitz and Oxocelhaya caves (2024).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6de0d66c/The_entry_of_the_cave_of_Isturitz.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
