 dating to approximately 4000-3000 BC. Discovered on 6 August 1909 by Francesco Samarelli and Angelo Mosso, with further excavations by Michele Gervasio in 1910, the corridor-type tomb is nearly 10 metres long with a burial chamber 1.80 m high, roofed by a capstone measuring 2.40 x 3.80 m. Excavations uncovered eight human skeletons, pottery, stone knives, obsidian blades, and a bronze falera. In 2011 UNESCO recognized it as a Heritage Witness to a Culture of Peace.'' -> ''Discovered on 6 August 1909 by Francesco Samarelli and Angelo Mosso, with further excavations by Michele Gervasio in 1910, the corridor-type tomb is nearly 10 metres long with a burial chamber 1.80 m high [1] [2] [3]. Excavations uncovered pottery, stone knives, obsidian blades, and a bronze falera [2] [4]. In 2011 UNESCO recognized it as a Heritage Witness to a Culture of Peace [4] [5].''"}]'::jsonb),
