url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4321:chunk-0001: description ''The Cave of Bacinete (Cueva de Bacinete) is located in Los Alcornocales Natural Park near Los Barrios in Andalusia, southern Spain. It contains prehistoric rock art depicting animals, people, and symbols created using natural pigments. The art spans multiple periods: semi-schematic paintings in dark red from the early Neolithic, and white schematic paintings from the late Neolithic to Metal Age. Declared a Property of Cultural Interest in 1985, it is one of only eight rock shelters in southern Spain physically protected for its rock art.'' -> ''The Cave of Bacinete (Cueva de Bacinete) is located in Los Alcornocales Natural Park near Los Barrios in Andalusia, southern Spain [1]. It contains prehistoric rock art depicting animals, people, and symbols created using natural pigments [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349923", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349924", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('7054234a-ec07-477d-afe0-df191dbca303'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '10', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:7054234a-ec07-477d-afe0-df191dbca303:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''10'' restored on Newspaper Rock State Historic Monument', '416e87766bdb81c9934b4175225adefc', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0036:chunk-0001: description ''(1st–5th c. AD) Newspaper Rock State Historic Monument is a Utah state monument featuring one of the largest and most dense collections of petroglyphs in North America [1]. The rock panel is located in San Juan County, Utah [1]. Located along State Route 211, it lies 45 km (28 mi) northwest of Monticello and 85 km (53 mi) south of Moab [1].'' -> ''Newspaper Rock State Historic Monument is a Utah state monument featuring a rock panel carved with one of the largest known collections of petroglyphs [1]. It is located in San Juan County, along Utah State Route 211 [1]. The 200-square-foot (19 m2) rock is a part of the vertical Wingate sandstone cliffs that enclose the upper end of Indian Creek Canyon, and is covered by hundreds of petroglyphs—one of the largest, best preserved and easily accessed groups in the Southwest [1]. People of the Archaic, Basketmaker, Fremont, and Ancestral Puebloan cultures carved petroglyphs on Newspaper Rock from around the beginning of the current era until about 1300 [1]. Ute, Navaho, and Anglo people have also left carvings on the rock in historic times [1]. There are over 650 rock art designs [1]. The drawings on the rock are of different animals, human figures, and symbols [1]. These carvings include pictures of deer, buffalo, and pronghorn [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101007", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101008", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152416", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Newspaper_Rock_closeup.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7054234a/Newspaper_Rock_closeup.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249701", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249702", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345693", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345694", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
