d a hillfort on top of the hill named \"Sigiburg\" in 775 AD; two years later the Saxons failed with a reconquest of Sigiburg [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118946", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118947", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''700''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118948", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Castle''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syberg'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigiburg''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152419", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Syberg_2012-03-11-6107.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/70762563/Dortmund Syburg - Syberg (Ruhrbrücke Dortmunder Straße) 01 ies.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331836", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/70762563/Dortmund Syburg - Syberg (Ruhrbrücke Dortmunder Straße) 01 ies.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/70762563/Ruine Hohensyburg, Blick vom Vincketurm.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355885", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Castle'' -> ''Castle/palace''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('708e01e6-3b2f-4c7f-924b-42e319169c68'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:708e01e6-3b2f-4c7f-924b-42e319169c68:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Archaeological Site of Pnyx', '9d25fc3f78aac6ae290336d29e0c4434', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Archaeological site'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85258", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2109:chunk-0001: description \"Rocky hill less than 1 km west of the Acropolis where the Athenian democratic assembly (ekklesia) met from as early as 507 BC, making it one of the earliest known sites of democratic governance. A carved stone bema served as the speakers'' platform where Pericles, Themistocles, and Demosthenes addressed citizens. Three construction phases span the 5th to late 4th century BC, after which assemblies moved to the Theatre of Dionysus.\" -> ''The Pnyx is a hill or hillside in central Athens [1]. The Pnyx is located less than 1 kilometre west of the Acropolis and about 2 km south-west of the Syntagma Square in the centre of Athens [1]. Pericles, Aristides and Alcibiades spoke here, within sight of the Parthenon [1]. Here Demosthenes delivered his vilifications of Philip II of Macedon [1]. The Pnyx is a small, rocky hill surrounded by parkland, with a large flat platform of eroded stone set into its side, and by steps carved on its slope [1]. It was the meeting place of one of the world\\''s earliest known democratic legislatures, the Athenian ekklesia, and the flat stone platform was the bema, the \"stepping stone\" or speakers\\'' platform [1]. In 1910, excavations began at the site by the Greek Archaeological Society and confirmed the site as the Pnyx [1]. Large-scale excavations were conducted at times between 1930 and 1937 by Homer Thompson [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118950", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152420", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/708e01e6/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/708e01e6/Ancient ruins on the Pnyx on September 19, 2020.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312262", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/708e01e6/Ancient ruins on the Pnyx on September 19, 2020.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/708e01e6/Pnyx_Bema_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
