. The site occupies a strategic position along the Han River floodplain, likely serving defensive and administrative functions for ancient settlements in the region[1].'' -> ''Located at the edge of the Han River in present-day Songpa-gu district, this flat earthen wall forms a long oval shape extending north-south and slightly leaning eastward [1]. The massive structure encompasses a circumference of approximately 3.5 kilometers (2.2 miles), making it one of the larger known earthworks from the Korean Three Kingdoms period [1] [2] [3].''"}]'::jsonb),
