e": "remediation_change_log:325265", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7111f8f1/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7111f8f1/Ashhole Cavern Brixham.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338241", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4322:chunk-0001: description ''Ash Hole Cavern is a limestone cave system in Brixham, Devon, with evidence of human habitation dating back to the Neolithic period [1][2]. Archaeological excavations have uncovered several artefacts, including pottery fragments and tools, indicating prolonged human use of the site [2]. The cave is situated in Devonian-age limestone and consists of an east-west-orientated passage [3]. It has been a scheduled monument since 1966, offering valuable insights into prehistoric and Roman-period activity in south Devon [1][2].'' -> ''Ash Hole Cavern is a limestone cave system in Brixham, Devon, with evidence of human habitation dating back to the Neolithic period [1]. Archaeological excavations have uncovered several artefacts, including pottery fragments, indicating prolonged human use of the site [1]. The cave is situated in Devonian-age limestone [1]. It has been a scheduled monument since 1966 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349929", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''1'' -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('7155aa5a-4eff-4b1d-a105-b15d17b786c6'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:7155aa5a-4eff-4b1d-a105-b15d17b786c6:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Kirkdale Cave', 'f5d04b638dddf6d2e9b2f14d0b7537c1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Cave Structures'', ''Undated'') is shared by 45 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44511", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0096:chunk-0001: description ''Kirkdale Cave is a fossil site near Kirkbymoorside in the Vale of Pickering, North Yorkshire, England. Discovered by quarry workers in 1821, it contained fossilised bones of hippos, elephants, cave hyenas, cave lions, and rhinoceroses dating to the Eemian interglacial around 121,000 years ago. It is one of the northernmost sites where hippopotamus remains have been found. William Buckland analysed the cave in December 1821, determining the bones were brought by hyenas who used it as a den, and was awarded the Copley Medal in 1822 for his landmark paper.'' -> ''Kirkdale Cave is a cave and fossil site located in Kirkdale near Kirkbymoorside in the Vale of Pickering, North Yorkshire, England [1]. William Buckland analyzed the cave and its contents in December 1821 and determined that the bones were the remains of animals brought in by hyenas who used it for a den, and not a result of the Biblical flood floating corpses in from distant lands, as he had first thought [1]. The fossil bones found in the cave included those of straight-tusked elephants, hippopotamuses, the narrow-nosed rhinoceros, cave hyena, cave lion, Irish elk, brown bears, red deer and fallow deer [1]. The fossilized remains were embedded in a silty layer sandwiched between layers of stalagmite [1]. The entrance to the cave was found by limestone quarry workers in the summer of 1821 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101665", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101666", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-121000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152438", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7155aa5a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7155aa5a/Kirkdale Cave - geograph.org.uk - 1072214.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304103", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}]'::jsonb),
