 [1]. The site, discovered in 1981, is a Late Minoan IIIA tholos tomb [1]. At least 9 burials were made here [1]. Artefacts found included a gold necklace which contained 28 rosettes of gold, fifteen seal stones, amulets, bronze weapons and bronze utensils [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118965", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Cemetery'' -> ''Tomb''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:340724", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-005-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/71f6f6f1/Head of a warrior wearing boar tusk helmet carved of hippopotamus ivory from Phylaki, 1375-1300 BCE, Archaeological Museum of Chania (Crete).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
