n as an indication of clearance in advance of arable farming, but the Crawley Edge field unusually includes a barrow cremation mound among the cairns [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101686", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249723", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249724", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('72f50344-3b9f-4390-929c-78d72d7a6e01'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '9', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:72f50344-3b9f-4390-929c-78d72d7a6e01:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''7'' restored on Banc Du', '6e5e965b10bef6d3ea8ce08e82278744', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 9 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 4 content link(s), 2 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85300", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2110:chunk-0001: description ''Banc Du is a Neolithic causewayed enclosure on the summit of Foel Eryr at 334m OD in the Preseli Hills, Pembrokeshire, Wales. The site occupies a flat-topped promontory projecting southwards. First identified during aerial photographic survey in 1990, it comprises two non-concentric, incomplete earthworks defining a roughly oval hilltop area, amidst a series of cultivation features and abandoned trackways.[1]'' -> ''Banc Du is a prominent, fairly flat-topped southwards-projecting promontory of Foel Eryr, at about 334m OD at the west end of the Preseli Hills in north Pembrokeshire, Wales [1]. First spotted during an aerial photographic survey of the region in 1990, this hilltop enclosure consists of two non-concentric and incomplete earthworks that define a roughly oval area around the hilltop [1]. There is a crag-line on the south-east side and steep slopes to the south and west [1]. Although small scale, Banc Du has profound implications for the understanding of occupation of the area in the fourth and third millennia BC [1]. The first confirmed neolithic enclosure in Wales and the mid west of Britain, it is also notable for the fact that visible earthworks survive at ground level [1]. When first built, it would have been contemporary with the great megalithic tombs such as the long barrow at Pentre Ifan just 7.5 km to the north, and the passage grave at Bedd yr Afanc 6 km to the north-east [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152962", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/72f50344/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343814", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/72f50344/Cerrig ar rostir ger Banc Du - Stones on moorland near Banc Du - geograph.org.uk - 7905287.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
