884).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:338311", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4323:chunk-0001: description ''Perthi-Duon is a Neolithic portal dolmen located west of Brynsiencyn on Anglesey, Wales, dating to around 3500 BC. The collapsed burial chamber consists of a 2.5m by 1.8m capstone resting on two fallen stones. It is one of eighteen stone chambered monuments within a 1.5km corridor along the Menai Straits, and its architecture appears to be a blueprint for other portal dolmens in the Irish Sea Province. A 2014 excavation led by Dr. George Nash uncovered a compacted-stone kidney-shaped cairn mound surrounding the chamber, with an east-west oriented entrance. Bodies were likely deposited as cremated remains or disarticulated skeletal material.'' -> ''Perthi-Duon is a Neolithic portal dolmen located west of Brynsiencyn on Anglesey, Wales, dating to around 3500 BC [1] [2]. The collapsed burial chamber consists of a 2.5m by 1.8m capstone resting on two fallen stones [1]. It is one of eighteen stone chambered monuments within a 1.5km corridor along the Menai Straits, and its architecture appears to be a blueprint for other portal dolmens in the Irish Sea Province [2]. A 2014 excavation led by Dr. George Nash uncovered a compacted-stone kidney-shaped cairn mound surrounding the chamber [1] [2]. Bodies were likely deposited as cremated remains or disarticulated skeletal material [2].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('74a81d2a-f0a4-482b-ae66-15b51bbdb7ee'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:74a81d2a-f0a4-482b-ae66-15b51bbdb7ee:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Tillya Tepe', 'c13e03dd902dd1300803aec4fcf7cd0e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Necropolis/tombs complex'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 24 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0037:chunk-0001: description \"Tillya Tepe is a necropolis in northern Afghanistan''s Jowzjan Province near Sheberghan, consisting of six burial mounds dating to the 1st century BC–1st century AD [1]. Excavated in 1978 by a Soviet-Afghan team led by archaeologist Viktor Sarianidi, the site yielded the famous Bactrian gold hoard—approximately 20,600 gold, silver, and ivory artifacts including ornaments, coins, and jewelry [1][2]. The graves contained five women and one man, buried with extremely rich jewelry that demonstrates the wealth and international connections of ancient Bactria [1][2].\" -> ''Tillya tepe, Tillia tepe or Tillā tapa is an archaeological site in the northern Afghanistan province of Jowzjan near Sheberghan, excavated in 1978 by a Soviet-Afghan team led by the Soviet archaeologist Viktor Sarianidi [1]. The hoard found there is often known as the Bactrian gold [1]. The hoard is a collection of about 20,600 ornaments, coins and other kinds of artifacts, made of gold, silver, ivory, etc., that were found in six burial mounds erected for five women and one man, with extremely rich jewelry, dated to around the 1st century BCE-1st century CE [1]. The ornaments include necklaces set with semi-precious stones, belts, medallions and a crown [1]. Several coins dated up to the early 1st century CE, with none dated later, suggest a 1st-century CE date for the burial [1]. A silver coin was found in one of the tombs from the reigns of the Parthian king Mithridates II, who ruled c.\\u2009123–88 BCE [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101708", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101709", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/Tillya_Tepe_crown.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/74a81d2a/Tillya_Tepe_crown.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238682", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238683", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-1000''"}]'::jsonb),
