k-0001: description ''Norchia is an ancient Etruscan city and necropolis near Vetralla in northern Lazio, established as a satellite settlement of the powerful city of Tarquinia along the Via Clodia. Inhabited since the Bronze Age, it reached its peak between the 4th and 2nd centuries BC. The rock-cut tombs, carved from tuff cliffs, include distinctive dice-shaped tombs and Doric temple-facade tombs with carvings of ritual processions, Etruscan demons, and Gorgon heads. The plateau above preserves ruins of a medieval castle and the Romanesque church of San Pietro.'' -> ''Norchia is an ancient Etruscan city and necropolis near Vetralla along the Via Clodia [1]. Inhabited since the Bronze Age, it reached its peak between the 4th and 2nd centuries BC [1] [2]. The rock-cut tombs, carved from tuff cliffs, include distinctive dice-shaped tombs and Doric temple-facade tombs with carvings of processions, Etruscan demons, and Gorgon heads [1] [3] [4]. The plateau above preserves ruins of a medieval castle and the church of San Pietro [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355886", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Necropolis'' -> ''Necropolis/tombs complex''"}]'::jsonb),
