ption ''Lismore Fields is a prehistoric settlement near the River Wye in Buxton, Derbyshire, discovered in 1984 by the Trent and Peak Archaeological Trust while searching for a Roman road. Excavations revealed a Mesolithic timber roundhouse and two Early Neolithic longhouses, among the best-preserved examples in Britain. Building 1 dates to 3800-3650 BC and Building 2 to 3650-3350 BC. The site yielded one of the largest cereal assemblages from any Early Neolithic site in England, possibly representing the earliest evidence of cereal cultivation in the British Isles. It is a protected Scheduled Monument.'' -> ''Lismore Fields is a prehistoric settlement near the River Wye in Buxton, Derbyshire, discovered in 1984 by the Trent and Peak Archaeological Trust while searching for a Roman road [1]. Excavations revealed two Early Neolithic longhouses, among the best-preserved examples in Britain [2]. Building 1 dates to 3800-3650 BC and Building 2 to 3650-3350 BC [2]. The site yielded one of the largest cereal assemblages from any Early Neolithic site in England, possibly representing the earliest evidence of cereal cultivation in the British Isles [2]. It is a protected Scheduled Monument [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349960", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349961", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4501'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355887", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('76220eb6-d405-4d79-a0a7-d36c4809094f'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:76220eb6-d405-4d79-a0a7-d36c4809094f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Shrub''s Wood Long Barrow', '108c81e4f608a40f7c0e24b81ceef62b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Barrow'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 33 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2112:chunk-0001: description \"Shrub''s Wood Long Barrow is an unchambered long barrow located near Elmsted in Kent, southeastern England[1]. Constructed in the fourth millennium BCE during Britain''s Early Neolithic period, it was built by a pastoralist community shortly after the introduction of agriculture to Britain[1]. The earthwork consists of a sub-trapezoidal tumulus flanked by side ditches[1]. As an unchambered long barrow, it lacks an internal burial chamber, representing an early form of Neolithic monument construction in southern England[1].\" -> \"Shrub''s Wood Long Barrow is an unchambered long barrow located near to the village of Elmsted in the south-eastern English county of Kent [1]. It was probably constructed in the fourth millennium BCE, during Britain''s Early Neolithic period [1]. Although representing part of an architectural tradition of long-barrow building that was widespread across Neolithic Europe, Shrub''s Wood Long Barrow belongs to a localised regional variant of barrows produced in the vicinity of the River Stour [1]. Shrub''s Wood Long Barrow was discovered in the late 1960s, although it has yet to undergo thorough archaeological investigation [1]. The barrow stands on a sandy sub-soil that is part of the Lenham Beds [1]. At its eastern end, the long barrow is 2 metres high, and a little less than that at its western end [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101742", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101743", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153064", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Slope_of_Shrub%27s_Wood_Long_Barrow.jpg'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/76220eb6/Slope_of_Shrub''s_Wood_Long_Barrow.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238691", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:238692", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
