monument [1]. The settlement covered most of a small knoll on the limestone pavement of the scar [1]. A walled enclosure surrounded most of the knoll and, on the western side, the eight-foot thick walls extended the steep escarpment of the knoll to form a significant obstacle [1]. The area enclosed is about 1.25 acres [1]. There were about a dozen stone huts built into the walls of the enclosure so that the central space was open [1]. The wall was constructed from orthostats which enclosed rubble [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101750", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101751", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101752", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249763", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249764", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355888", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('767b931c-d5d6-4da3-80fd-bdd8b72f8663'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:767b931c-d5d6-4da3-80fd-bdd8b72f8663:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''9'' restored on Tašmajdan Park', '15c0b2d9c09c8473378d11170ee97891', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Mine/quarry'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44523", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0096:chunk-0001: description ''Tasmajdan Park in Belgrade, Serbia sits atop ancient Roman limestone quarries used from the 1st to 4th centuries AD to supply building materials for Singidunum (Roman Belgrade). The name derives from Turkish tas (stone) and majdan (mine). The quarrying created an extensive network of underground tunnels and catacombs, later used as a cemetery (1826-1886) and a German military bunker in WWII capable of sheltering 1,000 soldiers. Declared a cultural monument in 2021.'' -> \"Tašmajdan Park, colloquially Tašmajdan or simply just Taš, is a public park and the surrounding urban neighborhood of Belgrade, the capital of Serbia [1]. Almost two millennia ago, Romans were extracting stone from the quarry located in the area for the building of Belgrade''s predecessor, Singidunum and for many surviving sarcophagi from that period [1]. It was recorded that the Romans used this stone for the construction of the city''s aqueduct in 69 AD [1]. The castrum of Singidunum had tall walls, built from the white Tašmajdan limestone [1]. The caves under Tašmajdan are 6 to 8 million years old [1]. Remains of the Roman aqueduct are found in the caves [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:119012", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Quarry''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153068", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Tašmajdan_Park.jpg/400px-Tašmajdan_Park.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/767b931c/Миоценски_спруд_Ташмајдан,споменик_природе,_Београд,_021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355889", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Quarry'' -> ''Mine/quarry''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('767b931c-d5d6-4da3-80fd-bdd8b72f8663'::uuid, 'rarity_score', '35', '41', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:767b931c-d5d6-4da3-80fd-bdd8b72f8663:rarity_score', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: rarity_score ''41'' restored on Tašmajdan Park', '15c0b2d9c09c8473378d11170ee97891', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "rarity_score = 35 from mystery 7, cultural_influence 7"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44523", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0096:chunk-0001: description ''Tasmajdan Park in Belgrade, Serbia sits atop ancient Roman limestone quarries used from the 1st to 4th centuries AD to supply building materials for Singidunum (Roman Belgrade). The name derives from Turkish tas (stone) and majdan (mine). The quarrying created an extensive network of underground tunnels and catacombs, later used as a cemetery (1826-1886) and a German military bunker in WWII capable of sheltering 1,000 soldiers. Declared a cultural monument in 2021.'' -> \"Tašmajdan Park, colloquially Tašmajdan or simply just Taš, is a public park and the surrounding urban neighborhood of Belgrade, the capital of Serbia [1]. Almost two millennia ago, Romans were extracting stone from the quarry located in the area for the building of Belgrade''s predecessor, Singidunum and for many surviving sarcophagi from that period [1]. It was recorded that the Romans used this stone for the construction of the city''s aqueduct in 69 AD [1]. The castrum of Singidunum had tall walls, built from the white Tašmajdan limestone [1]. The caves under Tašmajdan are 6 to 8 million years old [1]. Remains of the Roman aqueduct are found in the caves [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:119012", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Quarry''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153068", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Tašmajdan_Park.jpg/400px-Tašmajdan_Park.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/767b931c/Миоценски_спруд_Ташмајдан,споменик_природе,_Београд,_021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355889", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Quarry'' -> ''Mine/quarry''"}]'::jsonb),
