    ('775adc1b-7af2-4452-824b-5cc575b2ec8c'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:775adc1b-7af2-4452-824b-5cc575b2ec8c:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Zemun', 'e7801731bee57e94c77b81a1d0a021ae', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -4000"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81018", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2016:chunk-0001: description ''Zemun, now part of Belgrade, Serbia, has been inhabited since the Neolithic period (4500-3000 BC), with early residents living in dugouts that gave the settlement its name. The Celtic Scordisci founded the fortified settlement of Taurunum around 85 BC on the Gardos plateau overlooking the Danube. After Roman conquest, Taurunum became a port city and seat of the Danube Roman fleet (classis Flavia Pannonica), serving as a fortified trading town on the route to Constantinople. The Celts built the first fortifications, followed by the Romans, while surviving wall remnants date to the Middle Ages.'' -> ''The area of Zemun has been inhabited since the Neolithic period [1]. Baden culture graves and ceramics like bowls and anthropomorphic urns were found in the town [1]. The first Celtic settlements in Taurunum area originate from the 3rd century BC when the Scordisci occupied several Thracian and Dacian areas of the Danube [1]. The Scordisci founded both Taurunum and Singidunum across the Sava [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101771", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-