    ('775deb7e-4de9-46c9-936c-9de468d21192'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:775deb7e-4de9-46c9-936c-9de468d21192:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Kinđa', 'd66c40b3284ad34a89441f689648227e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44525", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0096:chunk-0001: description ''Kinđa is a Copper Age kurgan (burial mound) in northeastern Vojvodina, Serbia, near the town of Kikinda. Its summit reaches 91 m altitude, with the mound rising 5-6 m above the surrounding plain, making it one of the highest points in Serbian Banat. Believed to be the tomb of an important individual, it is the largest kurgan in Serbia and the centerpiece of a cluster of burial mounds that make Kikinda one of the richest Eneolithic heritage sites in the country. An alternative theory attributes its construction to the Cumans in the 13th century. In 2017, heavy machinery destroyed the northeastern part of the mound beyond repair.'' -> ''Top of Kinđa is at an altitude of 91 m, with the mound itself being elevated 5.3 m to 6 m above the surrounding ground [1]. The mound is earthen, circular and has a diameter of 50 m [1]. Kinđa is the largest and was one of the best preserved kurgans in Serbia [1]. Based on its monumental size, it is believed that Kinđa is the tomb of someone very important [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101775", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-w