n in 1977 excavated 3.5 acres of the site [1]. The modern excavations discovered an Iron Age site beneath the Roman villa [1]. The villa was constructed in the 3rd-century AD, though some evidence suggests 2nd-century activity at the site as well [1]. Coins on the site date from AD 270–355 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101784", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: site_type ''Residence/villa/farmhouse'' -> ''Villa''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Villa'' -> ''Residence/villa/farmhouse''"}]'::jsonb),
