 row and an embanked enclosure [1]. One of the first archaeological surveys of Bodmin Moor, including Craddock Moor Circle was carried out c. 1800 by Nicholas Johnson and Peter Rose [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101802", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101803", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250129", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250130", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349982", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('78c9f0a2-2247-4159-87ce-9a0e69e88e28'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:78c9f0a2-2247-4159-87ce-9a0e69e88e28:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Tremeca', '2523a9594c72edee03b528987342312f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0038:chunk-0001: description \"Tremeca is a Neolithic and Bronze Age dolmen burial chamber located approximately 600 meters northwest of the village of Casaglione in Corse-Sud, Corsica, France. The dolmen features a distinctive semicircular capstone and is part of Corsica''s broader megalithic heritage, which corresponds to the early European Megalithic Culture. The site is in near-perfect condition but requires a long walk to reach, situated in a landscape rich with related megalithic monuments including other dolmens and menhirs.\" -> ''Tremeca is an archaeological site in Corsica [1]. The site is located in west-central Corsica, near Casaglione [1]. Tremeca was first described by the archaeologist Roger Grosjean in his 1966 overview of prehistoric Corsican sites [1]. The ancient dolmen stands in the narrowest part of a small plateau; it is approximately hemispherical in its design, supported by four rough-hewn granite blocks capped with a slab [1]. The structure of the dolmen opens toward the southeast [1]. Its design is rudimentary when compared to menhirs and other nearby structures [1]. The region has not been extensively excavated, with one of the few nearby megalithic sites being that of Monte Lazzo [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101804", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101805", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250131", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250132", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
