ward the southeast [1]. Its design is rudimentary when compared to menhirs and other nearby structures [1]. The region has not been extensively excavated, with one of the few nearby megalithic sites being that of Monte Lazzo [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101804", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101805", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250131", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250132", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
