flutes from the Geissenklösterle cave, dated around c.\\u200943,150–39,370 BP, are the oldest musical instruments ever found [1]. The 41,000 to 39,000-year-old Lion-man and the 42,000 to 41,000-year-old Venus of Hohle Fels are the oldest confirmed sculptures in the world [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84245", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153818", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-017: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7bfb0158/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7bfb0158/Die Bocksteinhöhle im Lonetal. 02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250155", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250156", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313064", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7bfb0158/Die Bocksteinhöhle im Lonetal. 02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7bfb0158/Hohler_Fels_Eingang_Gang_Steg.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350003", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350004", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-41050''"}]'::jsonb),
