    ('7d24f980-7f63-4e6a-8bb1-1f83d16435f2'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:7d24f980-7f63-4e6a-8bb1-1f83d16435f2:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Achilleion, Thessaly', 'e5e3b0baff62fde7fc509a9e16f46cba', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85554", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2117:chunk-0001: description ''Achilleion is a Neolithic settlement in Thessaly, Greece, dating to approximately 6400–5600 BCE, making it among the earliest Neolithic sites in the country [1]. A Greek-American team excavated the site in 1973–1974 under the direction of Marija Gimbutas, who published the results in 1989 [2]. Four occupation phases (Achilleion I–IV) were defined based on stratigraphy, radiocarbon dates, and analysis of over 100,000 pottery sherds, covering about 800 years of early to classical Sesklo culture [3].'' -> ''Achilleion is an early Neolithic site in Thessaly, Greece [1]. It was partly excavated in the 1970s [1]. Achilleion is a stratified Early and Middle Neolithic tell of 200 x 260 m [1]. Excavations were led by archaeologist Marija Gimbutas in cooperation with D. Theocharis and yielded valuable information on the mounds stratigraphy, chronology, settlement phases, architecture, material culture and environment [1]. The well-preserved material culture of Achilleion includes all find categories typical of Early Neolithic sites in Thessaly, such as pottery, bone tools, personal ornaments, and both ground and chipped stone tools [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102517", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355900", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
