lendorf_frontview_retouched_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('7e97d2a5-3f87-44fc-9ad0-f0d5a2d84cab'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '10', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:7e97d2a5-3f87-44fc-9ad0-f0d5a2d84cab:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''10'' restored on Huerfano Butte (Arizona)', 'cc6f02b770d534c17b77a96b8176d726', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Rock art'', ''1000 - 1500 AD'') is shared by 8 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29619", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0315:chunk-0001: period_start ''1000'' -> ''1100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29620", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0315:chunk-0001: site_type ''Petroglyphs'' -> ''Rock art''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35852", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''1100'' -> ''1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85590", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2118:chunk-0001: description ''Huerfano Butte (\"Orphan Butte\") is a prehistoric Hohokam archaeological site on the western flank of the Santa Rita Mountains in Pima County, Arizona, utilized from c. 1100 CE. The granite outcrops feature about fifty bedrock mortars, metates, and approximately two dozen petroglyphs painted in red hematite depicting human and animal forms and concentric circles. In 1965, Tani Bahti discovered a pottery jar containing over 1,450 turquoise beads and pendants plus carved glycimeris shell artifacts, now housed at the Arizona State Museum. The site is restricted access to protect its cultural resources.'' -> ''Huerfano Butte (English: \"Orphan Butte\") is a small rocky butte located on the western flank of the Santa Rita Mountains in southeastern Pima County, Arizona [1]. Huerfano Butte and the surrounding area were utilized by the Hohokam as early as circa 1100 CE [1]. Shallow bedrock forces ground water to surface in a small pool located in a wash on the south side of the butte [1]. Exposed outcrops of granite on either side of the wash have about fifty bedrock mortars, at least two small bedrock metates, and numerous smaller cupules [1]. Along the same wash is a vertical stone surface with approximately two dozen weathered pictographs painted in red hematite [1]. In 1965, Huerfano Butte gained public notoriety when a young girl discovered an extensive prehistoric jewelry cache while on a picnic with her family [1]. While exploring cracks and crevices on the butte, the young girl discovered a small pottery jar filled with about 1,500 turquoise and glycimeris shell beads and pendants [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153935", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-017: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7e97d2a5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7e97d2a5/Huerfano_Butte_Arizona_Bedrock_Metate.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323230", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7e97d2a5/Huerfano_Butte_Arizona_Bedrock_Metate.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7e97d2a5/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325280", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7e97d2a5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7e97d2a5/Huerfano Butte Pima County Arizona.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
