e Age date, containing a cremation and food vessel [1]. Gib Hill is part of a complex of prehistoric monuments with Arbor Low [1]. The Neolithic barrow at Gib Hill was probably the first element in the complex [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102576", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-8000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154495", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/80770c65/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/80770c65/Gib hill barrow with several markers visible.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250201", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250202", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
