o around the turn of the eras [1]. The Ringwall (circular rampart) was one of the largest and most elevated in eastern Hesse [1]. It originally had three gates, only one of which — the Tor am Kälberhutstein — was passable by wagons [1]. The main fortification was a 1,300 metres long stone wall that surrounded the north, east and south sides of the hill at its base [1]. It was discovered as ancient in origin by R. Virchow (1821–1902) [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120217", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milseburg'' -> ''https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oppidum_Milseburg''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154546", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Rhoen_Milseburg.jpg/400px-Rhoen_Milseburg.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/81ee931d/Rhoen Milseburg.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('820bbc57-f448-4e1a-8912-d097977fd739'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:820bbc57-f448-4e1a-8912-d097977fd739:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Apodoulou', '140c9f554fa644843cb31fc7180e625c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 130 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35067", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0040:chunk-0001: description ''Apodoulou is a Minoan settlement in the Amari basin of Crete, located 450 metres above sea level overlooking the Libyan Sea[1]. The site was inhabited from the Late Neolithic period through the Late Minoan era, with the main building complex in use during Middle Minoan III (c. 1950-1600 BC)[2]. The settlement was destroyed by fire at the end of Middle Minoan II around 1700 BC, though habitation continued afterward[2].'' -> ''Apodoulou is the archaeological site of an ancient Minoan mansion or ceremonial building on Crete [1]. It overlooks the Libyan Sea from an altitude of 450 metres above sea level [1]. Apodoulou was first excavated by Spyridon Marinatos in 1934 [1]. The area was inhabited from Late Neolithic times to the Late Minoan period, and the building was in use in the Middle Minoan III period [1]. The site has yielded Linear A inscriptions on a basin and fragments of a stone cylindrical jar, as well as a small golden axe [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102613", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-w