ong the Main, to date only one south of Obernburg am Main has been identified [1]. North of the Main the limes initially runs through the marshy terrain of the Schifflache and Bulau before linking up with the Wetterau Limes [1]. At the crossing of the Main at Großkrotzenburg a Roman bridge has been identified from post sockets [1]. In the south it extended in its early period to Obernburg or Wörth [1].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('833d2de9-5bc4-425d-b5a5-111d742c8f0d'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:833d2de9-5bc4-425d-b5a5-111d742c8f0d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Hadži-Prodan''s Cave', '0af2554c9fa10cb620465dd867b372db', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85694", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2121:chunk-0001: description \"The Hadži-Prodan''s Cave is a Paleolithic archaeological site and national natural monument in the village Raščići, 7 km from Ivanjica in western Serbia[1]. The entrance sits at 630 m altitude, 40 m above the Rašćanska river valley, facing south[1]. This 345 m cave formed in Late Cretaceous Senonian limestone[1]. Excavations yielded prehistoric pottery shards, Pleistocene faunal fossils including Cave bear remains, and Iron Age artifacts[1]. The cave is named for Hadži-Prodan, a 19th-century Serbian revolutionary[1].\" -> ''The Hadži-Prodan\\''s Cave is an archaeological site of the Paleolithic period and a national natural monument, located in the village Raščići around 7 km from Ivanjica in western central Serbia [1]. The 345 m long cave was formed during the Late Cretaceous in \"thick-bedded to massive\" Senonian limestone [1]. Hadži Prodanova has been the subject of research and study in speleological and archaeological literature for over a century [1]. In 2003 a 2.5 m deep trench of 16 m2 was dug in the entrance, the main cavern and the internal part of the cave plateau [1]. Only fifteen Palaeolithic artifacts were discovered inside the cave [1]. However, Hadži Prodanova and the nearby Šalitrena Cave are so far the only cave sites in the Central Balkan mountains, that have produced evidence for human presence in a Gravettian and/or Epigravettian cultural context [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102642", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102643", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-50000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154569", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/833d2de9/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/833d2de9/Crkva Arhangela Gavrila kraj Hadži Prodanove pećine u Lisi, Ivanjica 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302156", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302157", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''-3000000''"}]'::jsonb),
