four granite standing stones and several fallen [1]. The Stripple stones were excavated in 1905 by H. St. George Gray who found a burnt flint, three flint flakes, an ox bone and some charcoal and oak timbers in the surrounding ditch [1]. He also detected an entrance from this facing southwest, directly towards the Trippet stones [1]. Gray noted that the stones had only been set approximately 1.5 feet deep into the ground [1]. The vallum surrounding the circle has three semi-lunar projections facing towards the northwest, northeast and east [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102671", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154598", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ac/Stripple_Stones_henge_and_stone_circle_%28geograph_6416860%29.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8426a941/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250601", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250602", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350053", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350054", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2900''"}]'::jsonb),
