es Act of 1975. Systematic excavation of Dabarkot has been deemed essential for understanding Balochistan''s archaeological sequence.\" -> ''Dabarkot, or Dabar Kot, is a tell site of the Indus Civilization in Balochistan, Pakistan [1]. It is situated in Duki district [1]. Various artifacts and figurines excavated from the area show a Harappan connection of the site [1]. The Dabarkot mound is 500 yards in diameter showing the settlement was large in size and of considerable significance [1]. Excavations from the site recovered various artifacts including stone beads, copper pieces, a gold pin, sheet metal, and large mud bricks [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:239656", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s006: lat ''30.3405882793553'' -> ''30.083333''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:239657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s006: lon ''69.00001436725573'' -> ''68.683333''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:340829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-005-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/8442fc68/Harappan elephant figurine - Dabarkot - BM.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355906", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
