e with a diameter of 40 kilometres [1]. The sedimentary rock exposed in this dome ranges in age from Late Proterozoic within the center of the dome to Ordovician sandstone around its edges [1]. The Richat Structure is the location of exceptional accumulations of Acheulean artifacts [1]. These Acheulean archaeological sites are located along wadis that occupy the outermost annular depression of this structure [1]. Pre-Acheulean stone tools also have been found in the same areas [1]. Sparse and widely scattered Neolithic spear points and other artifacts have also been found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120225", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120226", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304117", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}]'::jsonb),
