he area she found great amounts of painted and unpainted pieces of pottery, stone tools made from Silex and Obsidian, seashells, and bones of mammals and fish as well as plaster [1]. In the same year, Geoffrey Bibby dated the pottery to the Ubaid period and suggested further investigation on the site [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:239660", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s006: site_type None -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350057", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: site_type ''Settlement'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
