large brick-based stupa and numerous terracotta reliefs now displayed in major world museums [1]. Clay tablets containing the Buddhist formula \"Ye Dharma Hetu\" in 7th-8th century script were also found [1]. The stupa was decorated using terracotta sculptures representing the Buddha [1]. According to Henry Cousens, the Kahu-Jo-Daro site was significantly damaged when railway contractors in colonial-era Sindh carted off large quantities of the ancient bricks to use them as track ballast [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154748", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8838f1fa/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8838f1fa/KAHO J DARO.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:239687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s006: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313866", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8838f1fa/KAHO J DARO.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8838f1fa/Buddha,_da_mirpur_khas,_sindh_(pakistan),_410_dc_ca.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
