doleritic stones came from nearby Stapeley Hill [1]. Many of them are now missing and others are fallen [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103370", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103371", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155250", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Mitchell%27s_Fold_5.jpg'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/88c87513/Mitchell''s Fold Stone Circle Sunrise (5319635644).webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313878", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/88c87513/Mitchell''s Fold Stone Circle Sunrise (5319635644).webp\" -> \"/data/images/wiki/88c87513/Mitchell''s_Fold_5.webp\""}]'::jsonb),
