    ('89bdbe2c-a19b-484d-b6ef-2ed464b1311b'::uuid, 'mystery', '2', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:89bdbe2c-a19b-484d-b6ef-2ed464b1311b:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''9'' restored on Chaa Creek', '06a7b38cd09fff3c040370b61f2540fb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 2 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 159 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81066", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2018:chunk-0001: description ''Chaa Creek is a tributary of the Macal River in the Cayo District of western Belize, with Maya ruins that remain largely unexcavated in its catchment basin. In 1997, a survey led by Anabel Ford of Harvard University employed ground-penetrating radar and surface surveys, identifying over 20 unexcavated structures in and near the Chaa Creek area. The site encompasses over 70 recorded archaeological features within a 500-acre area, including structural mounds indicative of residential areas and agricultural terraces adapted to the riverine landscape. Chaa Creek is posited to be a satellite settlement of Xunantunich, the major Maya ceremonial centre nearby that peaked around 600-900 AD with a population of some 10,000 people.'' -> ''Chaa Creek is a tributary of the Macal River in the Cayo District in western Belize [1]. It is near the site of an ancient Maya settlement [1]. Initial investigation and surveying of the site was done from 1992 to 1994 under the auspices of the Xunantunich Archaelogical Project [1]. Excavations were conducted in 1995 and 1997 