The site preserves the Seokbinggo, a Joseon-era stone ice storage facility. It is part of the Gyeongju Historic Areas, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.'' -> ''Wolseong or Wolseong Palace was a royal palace of Silla [1]. It was located in what is now Gyeongju [1]. The palace was used during the Silla and Unified Silla periods [1]. The palace gets its names from the approximate outline of the palace walls, which were shaped like a crescent moon [1]. It is also called Banwolseong or Sinwolseong or Jaeseong, which means where the king resides [1]. The South Korean government has also designated the palace ruins as Historic Site No. 16 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120354", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: site_type ''Castle/palace'' -> ''Palace''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banwolseong'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseong''"}]'::jsonb),
