    ('8d0fb4aa-7eda-4d61-a313-5f270a2f5b8c'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:8d0fb4aa-7eda-4d61-a313-5f270a2f5b8c:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Batik Sehir Kekova', '26490a54f64b9de8fcea9c193cc9195f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81088", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2019:chunk-0001: description \"The Sunken City of Dolichiste lies submerged off Kekova Island along Turkey''s Mediterranean coast. This ancient Lycian city, dating from the 14th century BC to the 2nd century AD, preserves remarkable underwater structures including a harbour, pier, Roman bath (hammam), fish sauce workshops, residential houses, cisterns, churches, chapels and a military tower. The island of Kekova, historically known as Dolichiste, covers 4.5 km² and is uninhabited today [1].\" -> ''Kekova is a small Turkish island near Demre district of Antalya province which faces the villages of Kaleköy (ancient Simena) and Üçağız (ancient Teimioussa) [1]. On its northern side are the partly sunken ruins of Dolchiste/Dolikisthe, an ancient town which was destroyed by an earthquake during the 2nd century [1]. Rebuilt and still flourishing during the Byzantine Empire period, it was finally abandoned because of Arab incursions [1]. The Tersane (meaning \"dockyard\", as its bay was the site of an ancient city Xera and dockyard, with the ruins of a Byzantine church) is at the northwest of the island [1].''"}, {"source": "re