escribed on maps as a settlement [1]. Situated some 208 metres above sea level, overlooking the River Exe, it is most likely to be an Iron Age Hill fort or enclosure [1]. While the earthworks do not appear as pronounced as others nearby at Huntsham Castle, Cranmore Castle and Cadbury Castle they are still in a classical layout typical of an Iron Age hill fort or enclosure [1]. These other Devon Hill forts are all in plain view from the centre of the enclosure [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103441", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103442", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250698", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350868", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350869", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('8e4f5b3f-25dd-471f-96e4-4398f89754bd'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:8e4f5b3f-25dd-471f-96e4-4398f89754bd:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Cueva de Bolomor', '79bf6165b77545b2fd4a091ea960c25d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85948", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2128:chunk-0001: description ''Cueva de Bolomor (Bolomor Cave) is a karst cave near Tavernes de la Valldigna in the Valencian Community, Spain, occupied over three main periods between 350,000 and 120,000 years ago. Four Neanderthal remains have been recovered since excavations began in 1989: a fibula fragment, two teeth, and a nearly complete adult parietal bone. The 17-layer stratigraphy preserves evidence of diverse subsistence practices including hunting of ungulates, tortoises, birds, and young elephants, along with fifteen hearths ranging from 250,000 to 100,000 years old. Pollen analysis revealed the Neanderthals lived amid hazel shrubs, strawberry trees, carob trees, and chestnuts in a mild Mediterranean climate.'' -> ''Cueva de Bolomor, or Bolomor Cave, is an archaeological site near Tavernes de la Valldigna in the Valencian Community, Spain [1]. It was occupied over a long period of time, between 350,000 and 120,000 years ago [1]. Four Neanderthal remains have been recovered in excavations that were begun in 1989: a fragment of a fibula, two teeth, and a nearly complete parietal bone from an adult [1]. All date from the late Middle/early Late Pleistocene [1]. The cave today is more a rock shelter, of about 35 metres in length and 17 metres wide, and 20 metres deep with an irregular interior [1]. Archaeologists recognize a stratigraphy of 17 layers [1]. Three main periods of occupation are recognized: 350,000 years ago, 200,000 to 150,000 years ago, and 120,000 years ago [1]. Human occupants ate a wide variety of animals, including ungulates of all sizes, besides tortoises and birds [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103444", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-350000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-300000''"}]'::jsonb),
