bula, two teeth, and a nearly complete parietal bone from an adult [1]. All date from the late Middle/early Late Pleistocene [1]. The cave today is more a rock shelter, of about 35 metres in length and 17 metres wide, and 20 metres deep with an irregular interior [1]. Archaeologists recognize a stratigraphy of 17 layers [1]. Three main periods of occupation are recognized: 350,000 years ago, 200,000 to 150,000 years ago, and 120,000 years ago [1]. Human occupants ate a wide variety of animals, including ungulates of all sizes, besides tortoises and birds [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103444", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-350000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-300000''"}]'::jsonb),
