 and Mesolithic periods, and in the Bronze Age [1]. A maxilla (almost complete, with a number of teeth), a molar, a fibula, and four fragments of a cranium belonging to two humans were found between 2000 and 2003, in what appeared to be a layer from the Mousterian [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103460", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103461", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-100000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251046", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:341459", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-006-001: thumbnail_url None -> \"/data/images/wiki/8ef67a96/Talla lítica, conjunt de la cova Foradà, Museu Arqueològic d''Oliva.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350874", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350875", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''1'' -> ''-300000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('8f0bd6a2-46b6-46cb-afbb-efd18b2471d8'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:8f0bd6a2-46b6-46cb-afbb-efd18b2471d8:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Yereruyk Archaeological Site', '28f5987aee22aa6c35973873a4fb7af1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Church/cathedral'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 12 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2129:chunk-0001: description ''One of the earliest surviving Armenian Christian monuments, this basilica near the village of Anipemza in Shirak Province was built in the 5th century by the Kamsarakan princely family. Constructed from pink tuff stone on an elevated stepped foundation, the three-aisled basilica features a large columned hall and ornately carved southern portal. An inscription identifies it as a martyrial sanctuary dedicated to Saint John the Baptist and Saint Stephen. Added to the UNESCO World Heritage Tentative List in 1995, the basilica is considered a key to understanding the origins of Armenian ecclesiastical architecture. It was severely damaged in the 1988 earthquake.'' -> ''Yererouk, also Yereruyk or Ererouk, is an ancient Armenian church near the village of Anipemza in the Shirak Province of Armenia [1]. Yererouk was built on a plateau near the Akhurian River, which defines the frontier with Turkey, about 5 km southeast of the ancient city of Ani [1]. Yererouk means quivering in the Armenian language [1]. According to Toros Toramanian, Yererouk is a clear and perhaps the earliest example of the basilica style of the Armenian church buildings that are constructed on pillars [1]. The church was surrounded with thick walls [1]. From the surrounding buildings, underground rooms and the water reservoir, it becomes clear that the church was the centre of a developed residential community [1]. Yererouk Basilica is similar to Syrian basilicas in the architectural system and in the sculptural decoration [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Church''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155398", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/%D4%B5%D6%80%D5%A5%D6%80%D5%B8%D6%82%D5%B5%D6%84%D5%AB_%D5%8F%D5%A1%D5%B3%D5%A1%D6%80_05.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8f0bd6a2/Երերույքի_Տաճար_03.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313960", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8f0bd6a2/Երերույքի_Տաճար_03.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8f0bd6a2/Երերույքի_Տաճար_05.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355917", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Church'' -> ''Church/cathedral''"}]'::jsonb),
