 ruined state with much fallen debris [1]. The entrance is blocked with stones but the lintel over the inner end is still apparent [1]. There appear to be two guard cells on either side of the entrance passage [1]. Internally four mural cells can be seen, two of which are dumb-bell shaped with short passages between the two halves [1]. Borgarfjörð, the \"fjord of the borg\" was so named by the Norse on account of the broch [1]. The broch was visited by George Low in the 18th century, when he noted a number of cells in the base of the wall, and he stated that a hollow, galleried wall began above these [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251063", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251064", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350892", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('90bf9ebf-4050-433f-aaef-3b31dd3053d6'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:90bf9ebf-4050-433f-aaef-3b31dd3053d6:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Balberta', '8f076dd6a0a082b1bdf810bdbd73b897', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -400"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86000", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2130:chunk-0001: description ''Balberta is a major Maya archaeological site on the Pacific coastal plain of southern Guatemala, dated to the Early Classic period [1]. It is the only known major site on the Guatemalan Pacific coastal plain with exposed Early Classic architecture that has not been buried under later Late Classic construction [1]. The site was related to the nearby settlement of San Antonio, located 6 km to the west [1].'' -> ''Balberta is a major Mesoamerican archaeological site on the Pacific coastal plain of southern Guatemala, belonging to the Maya civilization [1]. It has been dated to the Early Classic period and is the only known major site on the Guatemalan Pacific coastal plain to have exposed Early Classic architecture that has not been buried under posterior Late Classic construction [1]. Balberta first appears to have been occupied in the Late Preclassic period, when it was a small site of minor importance [1]. After a period of rapid growth it became one of the largest Early Classic sites on the Guatemalan Pacific coast and reached the height of its power between AD 200 and AD 400 [1]. It traded with the distant metropolis of Teotihuacan in the Valley of Mexico [1]. At its height Balberta demonstrated true state-level political organisation and dominated a wide swathe of the Guatemalan coast [1]. Balberta was suddenly abandoned around AD 400 [1]. The site core consists of 22 structures occupying an area of 18 hectares [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103487", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103488", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103489", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/90bf9ebf/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: site_type None -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251065", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251066", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''1'' -> ''-400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355920", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
