3 following the abduction of his mother [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155971", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/918025af/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/918025af/Broch of Mousa from the Sea.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9190f012-5a73-4f94-9f39-9c870a7bdf4c'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9190f012-5a73-4f94-9f39-9c870a7bdf4c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Shap Stone Avenue', '8b864d665ba98ce35a15f24f0405b6bf', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Road/avenue/trackway'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 4 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29457", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0290:chunk-0001: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-3200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35881", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-3200'' -> ''-4500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36867", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0045:chunk-0001: description ''The Shap Stone Avenue is a largely destroyed Late Neolithic megalithic complex near Shap in Cumbria, England, dating to approximately 3200-2500 BC. Before its destruction it was one of the largest megalithic monuments in Europe, comparable to Avebury. The avenue extends almost 2.5 km in a southeast-to-northwest arc, constructed primarily from local pink granite, with the Thunder Stone and Goggleby Stone as notable glacial erratics. Two stone circles anchor the complex: Kemp Howe at the southern end and Carl Loft to the northwest. English Heritage has recorded only 14 surviving stones, as centuries of agricultural development and stone-blasting from the 18th century onward progressively dismantled the monument.'' -> \"Shap Stone Avenue sits near the centre of the Eden Valley, Cumbria [1]. It is broadly grouped into a category of monuments dubbed by Aubrey Burl, as ''Cumbrian Circles'': large, uncluttered enclosures of stone [1]. The monuments around Shap form a northwest alignment with several monuments in the Eden Valley [1]. A significant burial cairn, known as ''Skellaw Hill'', is found at the avenue''s northern end, though most stones have now been lost [1]. The Goggleby Stone is about ten feet high and has a cup mark on its north face [1]. Tom Clare suggests that the avenues date to the Late Neolithic period (approximately 3,200 - 2,500 BC), based upon evidence supplied by the Goggleby Stone [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103504", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103505", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155973", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/Goggleby_Stone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1889779.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9190f012/Googleby stone Shap uk - panoramio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240613", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240614", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-3200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314017", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9190f012/Googleby stone Shap uk - panoramio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9190f012/Goggleby Stone - geograph.org.uk - 1889779.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
