alley, Cumbria [1]. It is broadly grouped into a category of monuments dubbed by Aubrey Burl, as ''Cumbrian Circles'': large, uncluttered enclosures of stone [1]. The monuments around Shap form a northwest alignment with several monuments in the Eden Valley [1]. A significant burial cairn, known as ''Skellaw Hill'', is found at the avenue''s northern end, though most stones have now been lost [1]. The Goggleby Stone is about ten feet high and has a cup mark on its north face [1]. Tom Clare suggests that the avenues date to the Late Neolithic period (approximately 3,200 - 2,500 BC), based upon evidence supplied by the Goggleby Stone [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103504", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103505", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155973", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/Goggleby_Stone_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1889779.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9190f012/Googleby stone Shap uk - panoramio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240613", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240614", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-3200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314017", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9190f012/Googleby stone Shap uk - panoramio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9190f012/Goggleby Stone - geograph.org.uk - 1889779.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
