ne"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104224", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156089", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Salter%27s_Nick%2C_Shaftoe_Crags_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1941480.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251115", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251116", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334606", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/94fc8fb4/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345709", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345710", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('94fd509a-71e9-4a1e-b235-4eb91b1cacca'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:94fd509a-71e9-4a1e-b235-4eb91b1cacca:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Mamshit National Park', 'd5ff0eeb16aade2cf4ecb6c3880fa8d3', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 316 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86144", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2134:chunk-0001: description ''Mamshit (also Mampsis) was a Nabataean caravan stop that later became a Byzantine city in the Negev Desert[1]. Strategically positioned on the Incense Road, it connected Southern Arabia through Edom and the Arabah to Mediterranean ports and to Jerusalem via Beersheba and Hebron[1]. The settlement covers approximately 10 acres (40,000 m2), making it the smallest but best-preserved ancient city in the Negev[1]. Its once-luxurious houses feature distinctive architecture not found in any other Nabataean city[1].'' -> \"Mampsis or Memphis, today Mamshit, Kurnub, is a former Nabataean caravan stop and Byzantine city [1]. In the Nabataean period, Mampsis was an important station on the Incense Road, connecting Southern Arabia through Edom, the Arabah and Ma''ale Akrabim, to the Mediterranean ports, as well as to Jerusalem via Beersheba and Hebron [1]. The city covers 10 acres and is the smallest but best restored ancient city in the Negev Desert [1]. Mampsis was founded in the 1st century BCE as trade post between Petra and Gaza [1]. In 106, after the city was annexed to the Roman Empire, a Roman garrison was stationed there to guard part of the southern border of the empire and large dams were built around it [1]. Two churches were discovered in Mampsis [1]. The western St. Nilus Church has a mosaic floor with colorful geometric patterns, birds, a fruit basket, and five dedications in Greek [1]. The biggest hoard ever found in Israel was discovered in Mampsis, consisting of 10,500 silver coins with a total weight of 72 kg [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121498", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156092", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/94fd509a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/94fd509a/A Flour Mill in Mamshit IMG 6111.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314065", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/94fd509a/A Flour Mill in Mamshit IMG 6111.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/94fd509a/Mamshit.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355924", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
