e excavators cite radiocarbon dates which establish Pernil Alto as the oldest known inland and sedentary agricultural village in the Central Andes of Peru and Bolivia [1]. The date at which agriculture became the main source of subsistence for the inhabitants of Pernil Alto was 3300 BCE [1]. Pernil Alto was discovered in 2001 by the German Archaeological Institute [1]. Pernil Alto is located on a terrace approximately 10 metres above the irrigated valley of the Rio Grande de Nazca River at an elevation of 400 metres [1]. The most important cultivated crops were sweet potatoes and lima beans [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/Palpa_Province%2C_Peru_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323417", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/97443726/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325309", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/97443726/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/97443726/Palpa Province, Peru - panoramio (2).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
