    ('9789696d-6670-42d8-a76a-bd73fd3ca2c0'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9789696d-6670-42d8-a76a-bd73fd3ca2c0:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Church of Saint George, Sofia', '1d424d8911e7fff142e9c2ebcbc9a2d4', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Church/cathedral'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 12 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86216", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2136:chunk-0001: description ''The Church of Saint George is a Late Antique red brick rotunda in Sofia, Bulgaria. Built in the early 4th century CE as Roman baths, it was converted into a Christian church within the ancient walls of Serdica, which served as the capital of Dacia Mediterranea during the Roman and Byzantine periods [1]. It is considered the oldest surviving building in modern Sofia and remains in use by the Bulgarian Orthodox Church [1].'' -> ''The Church of Saint George is a late antique red brick rotunda in Sofia, Bulgaria [1]. Built in the early 4th century CE as Roman baths, it became a church inside the walls of Serdica, capital of ancient Dacia Mediterranea during the Roman and Byzantine eras [1]. The building, a cylindrical domed structure built on a square base, is famous for the 12th-, 13th-, and 14th-century frescoes inside the central dome [1]. Three layers of frescoes have been discovered, the earliest dating from the 10th century [1]. Frescoes of 22 prophets over two metres tall crown the dome [1]. Painted over during the Ottoman era, when the building was used as a mosque, these frescoes were only uncovered and restored in the 20th century [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156693", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9789696d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9789696d/C-SvetiGeorgi001.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314719", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9789696d/C-SvetiGeorgi001.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9789696d/StGeorgeRotundaSofia.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
