    ('990741ec-f247-483a-8b8e-29f634e63f96'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:990741ec-f247-483a-8b8e-29f634e63f96:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Deva Victrix', '0003612c29f2d216c95f3f8f8c6c1241', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Fortification'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86238", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2136:chunk-0001: description ''Deva Victrix was a legionary fortress and settlement in the Roman province of Britannia, located on the site of modern Chester, England [1]. The fortress was originally built by Legio II Adiutrix during the 70s AD as Roman forces advanced north against the Brigantes [1][2]. It was later rebuilt and expanded by Legio XX Valeria Victrix, which gave the fortress its lasting name [1]. A major reconstruction took place in the early 3rd century [1]. The legion remained stationed at Deva until the late 4th or early 5th century, when the fortress fell into disuse as Roman authority in Britain declined [1][3].'' -> \"Deva Victrix, or simply Deva, was a legionary fortress and town in the Roman province of Britannia on the site of the modern city of Chester [1]. The fortress was built by the Legio II Adiutrix in the 70s AD as the Roman army advanced north against the Brigantes, and rebuilt completely over the next few decades by the Legio XX Valeria Victrix [1]. In the early 3rd century the fortress was again rebuilt [1]. A civilian settlement, or canaba, grew around the fortress [1]. Chester''s Roman Amphitheatre, south-east of the fortress, is the largest-known military amphitheatre in Britain [1]. The civilian settlement remained after the Romans departed, eventually becoming the present-day city of Chester [1]. The fortress contained barracks, granaries, headquarters, military baths, and an unusual elliptical building which had it been finished may have been intended to act as the governor of Britain''s headquarters [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156716", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/Camp de légion de Deva Victrix.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/Camp de légion de Deva Victrix.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/990741ec/ChesterCan4.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
