orm [1]. The monument has a stepped facade, but the original shape was probably rounded or conical, with the stonework covered in clay and turf [1]. The site was excavated in the 1840s by George Petrie [1]. He did not uncover any human remains or other finds at the time and suggested that the burial monument had been filled with rubble and abandoned [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156766", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Wideford_Hill_Chambered_Cairn_showing_original_entrance.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9a219745/Wideford Hill Chambered Cairn entrance from inside.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314761", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9a219745/Wideford Hill Chambered Cairn entrance from inside.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9a219745/Wideford_Hill_Chambered_Cairn_showing_original_entrance.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
