ir by hand into the shape of a cross as a Christian monument [1]. Two niches for figures have been chiselled into the rock, each surrounded by holes [1]. Today, the cross is about 3.5 metres high [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104343", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156857", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9bedafde/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9bedafde/Fraubillenkreuz ferschweiler plateau eifel 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240707", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240708", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334642", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9bedafde/Fraubillenkreuz ferschweiler plateau eifel 2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9bedafde/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9bf7ac31-4f48-4bbc-ad4b-cbef11d994b9'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9bf7ac31-4f48-4bbc-ad4b-cbef11d994b9:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Huckhoe Settlement', '3d68229dbfdc7f231984d25183d4c1c7', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 286 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0077:chunk-0001: description ''Huckhoe Settlement is an archaeological site in Northumberland, England, near the village of Bolam approximately 11 km (7 miles) west of Morpeth[1]. Excavations revealed at least four phases of occupation dating from the early Iron Age (6th century BC) to the post-Roman period (6th century AD)[1]. It is designated as a scheduled monument[1].'' -> ''Huckhoe Settlement is an archaeological site in Northumberland, England, near the village of Bolam and about 7 miles (11 km) west of Morpeth [1]. The site shows occupation, in at least four phases, dating from the early Iron Age (6th century BC) to the post-Roman period (6th century AD) [1]. The site is on an oval promontory, steep on the north and west sides, above a tributary of the River Wansbeck [1]. There is a low earth and stone bank forming an enclosure, 94 metres north-east to south-west by 72 metres north-west to south-east, with an entrance of width 5 metres on the east side, and slight traces inside of roundhouses and courtyard walls [1]. This is thought to be a re-occupation in the Romano-British period, of an Iron Age defended settlement [1]. Traces of a palisaded enclosure were uncovered, consisting of three concentric palisades of oak [1]. A sample was radio-carbon dated to about 580 BC: the early Iron Age [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355934", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
