sented as evidence for the early development of agriculture, but this is now deprecated [1]. The site is situated at an elevation of 650 m above sea level on a hillside overlooking a small stream [1]. It was excavated in the mid-1960s by Chester Gorman [1]. Human presence at the site is documented from the Upper Paleolithic to the early Neolithic, but the primary occupation layers represent Hoabinhian hunter-gatherers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:341594", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-006-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/9c64a3f6/Spirit Well Cave 1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
