    ('9c827589-5230-48e4-bf6b-fb7dee9e7c35'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9c827589-5230-48e4-bf6b-fb7dee9e7c35:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Inti Punku', '6f9511cb11a2053be779af4576d1ff64', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1000 - 1500 AD'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86338", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2139:chunk-0001: description ''Inti Punku is an archaeological site in Peru\\''s Cusco Region, situated at the end of the famous Incan Trail. This fortress served as the main entrance to Machu Picchu, controlling access to the sacred city [1]. The site features massive carved stone steps and pillars that formed a gateway checkpoint [1]. Today, it marks the final destination for trekkers completing the Inca Trail, offering panoramic views of Machu Picchu below [1]. The name Inti Punku translates to \"Sun Gate\" in Quechua [1].'' -> ''Inti Punku or Intipunku is an archaeological site in the Cusco Region of Peru that was once a fortress of the sacred city, Machu Picchu [1]. Inti Punku was once the main entrance to Machu Picchu, in particular it was the primary approach from the then capital city of Cusco to the southeast [1]. Inti Punku is dedicated to the cult of the Inti, the Sun god [1]. The altitude of the climb to Inti Punku from Machu Picchu is 290 m [1]. It is a wide archaeological site with windows and gates that are held up by terraces [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_chang