    ('9cb8e16e-1f97-47da-b7f9-558216c9b543'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9cb8e16e-1f97-47da-b7f9-558216c9b543:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Chalkotheke', 'feaa666253805b89941f52888a2a1ec4', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (None, ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28495", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0148:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-450''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30464", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30901", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:gap-0007:chunk-0001: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81130", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2021:chunk-0001: description ''The Chalkotheke was a large rectangular treasury building on the Athenian Acropolis, erected soon after 400 BC to store bronze and metal possessions of the city. Located southwest of the Parthenon adjacent to the south wall, it measured approximately 43 m long and 14 m wide, fronted by a Doric portico of 4.5 m width. Ancient inscriptions record it housed bronze vessels for religious processions, military equipment including helmets and shields from victories, bronze statues, ritual objects such as kraters and braziers, and weights and measures. Only scant limestone foundations and rock-cut foundation trenches survive today.'' -> ''The Chalkotheke (Greek for \"bronze store\") was a structure on the Athenian Acropolis, Greece [1]. Its name and function are only known from 4th century BC inscriptions [1]. One decree orders the listing of all objects stored in the Chalkotheke and the erection of a stele inscribed with that list in front of the building [1]. Remains of a structure discovered to the east of the sanctuary of Artemis Brauronia and immediately to the southwest of the Parthenon have been suggested to be those of the Chalkotheke [1]. Only scant limestone foundations and rock-cut foundation trenches survive [1]. The building stood in front of the southern Acropolis wall and was circa 43 m long and 14 m wide [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121585", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
