    ('9d230dae-1f9b-4d16-a2a0-cce28ff32c56'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9d230dae-1f9b-4d16-a2a0-cce28ff32c56:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Cetina', 'b309061b1a999666ab6d46743be5d155', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Mound/tumulus'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 14 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29342", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0275:chunk-0001: site_type ''Mound/tumulus'' -> ''Natural feature''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Natural feature'' -> ''Mound/tumulus''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86342", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2139:chunk-0001: description ''The Cetina culture is an Early Bronze Age culture (c. 2200-1500 BC) named after archaeological sites along the Cetina River in central Dalmatia, Croatia. It is mainly known from its funerary practices: the dead were buried in stone tumuli, placed in a crouched position in stone chests or as cremated remains in clay urns, typically as single burials at the centre of the mound. The Cetina Valley preserves a string of settlements from the early Neolithic through the Iron Age, with some occupying entire river islands up to 1.5 hectares in size. Over 60 swords and 30 Greco-Illyrian helmets from the mid-first millennium BC were recovered from the river near Trilj, suggesting ritual deposition. Cetina culture finds extend to the central Dalmatian islands, Albania, southern Italy, and Greece.'' -> ''The Cetina Valley and the narrow passage at Klis have always functioned as a principal trade route between the Croatian coast and hinterland [1]. The earliest evidence for agricultural activity is from the Early Neolithic in the upper part of the valley [1]. In the Early Bronze Age the Cetina culture, a geographically pervasive group with contacts throughout the Adriatic basin, became dominant [1]. Extensive mound fields are recorded on the lower valley slopes at several locations around Cetina, Vrlika and Bajagić [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121586", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetina'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetina_culture''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9d230dae/hero.webp'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
