eposition. Cetina culture finds extend to the central Dalmatian islands, Albania, southern Italy, and Greece.'' -> ''The Cetina Valley and the narrow passage at Klis have always functioned as a principal trade route between the Croatian coast and hinterland [1]. The earliest evidence for agricultural activity is from the Early Neolithic in the upper part of the valley [1]. In the Early Bronze Age the Cetina culture, a geographically pervasive group with contacts throughout the Adriatic basin, became dominant [1]. Extensive mound fields are recorded on the lower valley slopes at several locations around Cetina, Vrlika and Bajagić [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121586", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetina'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetina_culture''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9d230dae/hero.webp'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9d3a0f75-ce6d-4778-891e-e3fc60310f76'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9d3a0f75-ce6d-4778-891e-e3fc60310f76:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Acropolis Museum', '4fca20bca1b1dd5abfe30fd8d24ed361', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2139:chunk-0001: description \"The Acropolis Museum is a 21,000 sq m archaeological museum at the foot of the Athens Acropolis, designed by Bernard Tschumi and opened on 20 June 2009. It houses over 4,000 artifacts from the Acropolis spanning the Bronze Age to Byzantine periods. The top-floor Parthenon Gallery recreates the dimensions of the temple''s frieze, while five original Caryatids from the Erechtheion are displayed on the first floor, with an empty space left for the sixth held by the British Museum. The building rests on over 100 concrete pillars above excavated ancient Athenian ruins visible through glass floors.\" -> ''The Acropolis Museum is an archaeological museum focused on the findings of the archaeological site of the Acropolis of Athens [1]. The museum was built to house every artifact found on the rock and on the surrounding slopes, from the Greek Bronze Age to Roman and Byzantine Greece [1]. The Acropolis Museum also lies over the ruins of part of Roman and early Byzantine Athens [1]. The museum was founded in 2003, while the Organization of the Museum was established in 2008 [1]. It opened to the public on 20 June 2009 [1]. More than 4,250 objects are exhibited over an area of 14,000 square metres [1]. The museum is located by the southeastern slope of the Acropolis hill, on the ancient road that led up to the \"sacred rock\" in classical times [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104364", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156931", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9d3a0f75/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9d3a0f75/New_Acropolis_Museum_5.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251499", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251500", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9d3a0f75/New_Acropolis_Museum_5.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9d3a0f75/ACMA_Moschophoros.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345711", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345712", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
