, points to sunset at the equinoxes [1]. Many of the stones have quartz inclusions and many small pieces of quartz are associated with the circle [1]. In 1959 the site was excavated and a central pit containing charcoal and cremated bone was found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104370", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104371", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251503", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251504", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:341624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-006-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/9db1409d/BohonaghSteinkreis.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350969", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9e17ecc2-7c59-4f03-bea4-8d32de261d3e'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9e17ecc2-7c59-4f03-bea4-8d32de261d3e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Yarim Tepe', '044bb54b8a797f5fb56ec2ca34468701', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2140:chunk-0001: description \"Yarim Tepe is an archaeological site in Iraq''s Sinjar valley, 7 km southwest of Tal Afar, representing an early farming settlement dating to approximately 6000 BC [1]. The multi-hill site documents the cultural sequence from the Hassuna culture through the Halaf period to the Ubaid culture [1].\" -> ''Yarim Tepe is an archaeological site of an early farming settlement that goes back to about 6000 BC [1]. It is located in the Sinjar valley some 7km southwest from the town of Tal Afar in northern Iraq [1]. The site consists of several hills reflecting the development of the Hassuna culture, and then of the Halaf and Ubaid cultures [1]. The settlement was investigated between 1969 and 1976, and later by the Soviet archaeological expedition under the leadership of Rauf Munchaev and Nikolai Merpert [1]. Yarim Tepe II is a settlement of the Halafian culture, belonging to the fifth millennium BC [1]. Metal was already quite common at Yarim Tepe; as many as 21 examples of worked copper or copper ore were found in the lower levels of the settlement [1].''"}