    ('9ee5d047-1345-405a-a689-4624365e0104'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '10', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:9ee5d047-1345-405a-a689-4624365e0104:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''8'' restored on Kot Diji', '1cde79a92aad36027f8997642ede2fef', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 10 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 5 content link(s), 3 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2140:chunk-0001: description \"Kot Diji is an archaeological site representing an early phase of the Indus Valley Civilization, with occupation dating to approximately 3300 BCE [1]. Located about 45 km south of Khairpur in Sindh, Pakistan, the site sits on the east bank of the Indus River, directly opposite Mohenjo-daro [1]. The remains are divided into two areas: a citadel on elevated ground and a surrounding outer area [2]. The Pakistan Department of Archaeology conducted excavations in 1955 and 1957, with F.A. Khan''s 1954-55 excavation revealing the formative Kot Dijian cultural assemblage that predates the mature Indus Civilization [1][3].\" -> \"The excavation at Kot Diji during 1954-55 by F. A. Khan revealed convincing evidence of the early or formative stage of the Indus civilisation in the cultural assemblage called Kot Dijian [1]. Kot Diji is the type site, i.e. the first excavated site of this type of culture, for the Kot Diji Culture which belongs to the Early Harappan Phase of the Indus Valley Civilisation, c.3300-2800 BCE [1]. The site covers 2.6 hectares (6.4 acres) [1]. The earliest occupation of this site is termed ''Kot Dijian'', which is pre-Harappan, or early formative Harappan [1]. The houses and fortifications were made from unbaked mud-bricks [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157525", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9ee5d047/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314858", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/9ee5d047/Kot_diji.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
