reported by Robert Raikes in 1963 [1]. It was excavated, between 1968 and 1974, before the well known sites of Mehrgarh or Nausharo by the French archaeological mission team led by Jean Marie Casal [1]. According to the excavator, this site was occupied from c.1800 BCE to 800 BCE [1]. The site has some very early ironwork and iron artefacts [1]. The excavator records three phases of unbroken occupation in Safi pirak [1]. The earliest indubitable evidence of domestic horse comes from Safi Pirak, during period I (c.1700 BC) [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157577", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Old_mithri_graveyard.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1174754/Painted_Water_Pitcher,_Pirak.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314900", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a1174754/Painted_Water_Pitcher,_Pirak.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1174754/Old_mithri_graveyard.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
