 [1]. The site of Pirak was first reported by Robert Raikes in 1963 [1]. It was excavated, between 1968 and 1974, before the well known sites of Mehrgarh or Nausharo by the French archaeological mission team led by Jean Marie Casal [1]. According to the excavator, this site was occupied from c.1800 BCE to 800 BCE [1]. The site has some very early ironwork and iron artefacts [1]. The excavator records three phases of unbroken occupation in Safi pirak [1]. The earliest indubitable evidence of domestic horse comes from Safi Pirak, during period I (c.1700 BC) [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157577", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Old_mithri_graveyard.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1174754/Painted_Water_Pitcher,_Pirak.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314900", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a1174754/Painted_Water_Pitcher,_Pirak.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1174754/Old_mithri_graveyard.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('a1428be8-db83-4d05-be49-9ee85ed77689'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:a1428be8-db83-4d05-be49-9ee85ed77689:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''6'' restored on Menir da Cabeça do Rochedo', '25153e085b5d882f5b17536d297938a9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -4000"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37005", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0048:chunk-0001: description ''A Neolithic limestone menhir located on a hill near Portelas, approximately 5 km north of Lagos in the Algarve, Portugal. The cylindrical, obelisk-shaped stone features faint serpentiform (wavy, spiral-like) carvings along its length. It was originally part of a group of eight similar monuments, of which it is the sole survivor in its original location; the others were relocated by Lagos municipality for preservation. Unlike other Algarve menhirs, it did not serve funerary purposes, and its original function remains debated.'' -> \"The Menir da Cabeça do Rochedo is an obelisk-like monument made from limestone, located just north of the town of Lagos [1]. Dating back to the early Neolithic, and of a considerable weight and size, it has a cylindrical shape and a decorative spiral-like engraving that''s faintly discernible [1]. It was part of a group of eight other similar monuments, of which just one is still standing in its original location [1]. The rest were taken by Lagos''s city hall for preservation [1]. Just like other Menhirs found in the Algarve, the Cabeça do Rochedo Menir did not serve funerary purposes, and the end it served is still debated [1]. The monument is located at a hill just outside of Portelas, 6 km north of Lagos [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121630", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121631", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240760", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325319", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a1428be8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1428be8/Menir da Cabeça do Rochedo - Lagos - 10-05-2018.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-2000'' -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
