 [1]. Just like other Menhirs found in the Algarve, the Cabeça do Rochedo Menir did not serve funerary purposes, and the end it served is still debated [1]. The monument is located at a hill just outside of Portelas, 6 km north of Lagos [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121630", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121631", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240760", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325319", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a1428be8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1428be8/Menir da Cabeça do Rochedo - Lagos - 10-05-2018.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-2000'' -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('a1435e3d-4c9d-410e-992e-842f24dfba16'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:a1435e3d-4c9d-410e-992e-842f24dfba16:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Priddy Circles', 'ff61a37442d0a9e74132e61635e9983e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Earthwork'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44903", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0102:chunk-0001: description ''Priddy Circles are four circular earthwork enclosures near Priddy on the Mendip Hills in Somerset, each nearly 200m in diameter, stretching over 1.2km. Their external rather than internal ditches make them unique among British henges. Excavations (1956-1959) revealed banks with stone cores and concentric rings of posts lined with stakes and hurdles. Though undated by artifacts, they appear contemporary with Stonehenge, c. 2500-2180 BC. Recent research suggests they may predate henges and served a different function. The southernmost circle suffered damage in 2012, resulting in a fine for the landowner.'' -> \"Priddy Circles are a linear arrangement of four circular earthwork enclosures near the village of Priddy on the Mendip Hills in Somerset [1]. The circles have been listed as Scheduled Ancient Monuments, and described as ''probable Neolithic ritual or ceremonial monuments similar to a henge'' [1]. The enclosures range in diameter from 185 to 194 m [1]. Three of the circles are closely spaced in a nearly straight line, while the fourth is 350 m to the north and somewhat out of line with the other three [1]. The total arrangement is spread over roughly 1.2 km [1]. The four circles each consist of a flat circular area surrounded by a bank and external ditch enclosure with more than one entrance [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157589", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/Priddy_circles.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a1435e3d/Priddy_circles.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
