eolithic creations [1]. They were estimated in the Vršac City Museum to belong to the Vinča culture and are estimated to be 6500 years old [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121663", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121664", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121665", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: site_type ''Geoglyphs'' -> ''Earthwork''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251543", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251544", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345713", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345714", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
