ce [1]. An inscription dedicated to Demeter and the Kore indicates that the site also housed a temple dedicated to them [1]. Only the stage and the chorus area (orchestra) were completed; the semi-circular seating area (koilon) and the side entrances were left incomplete, apparently due to inability to fund their completion [1]. The koilon is divided by 14 stairs into thirteen tiers, each with two rows of low seats of grey-white marble; the rest were never completed, and probably wooden seats were used instead [1]. The orchestra has a diameter of 29.7 metres and is composed of two layers of stamped earth mixed with gravel [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157733", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/60/Second_Ancient_Theater_of_Larissa_2.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a55ddaef/Théâtre B de Larissa.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314973", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a55ddaef/Théâtre B de Larissa.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a55ddaef/Second_Ancient_Theater_of_Larissa_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
