ninsula in commemoration of their joint victory with the Lacedaemonians against the Athenians [1]. In 424 B.C., in the course of the Peloponnesian War, the Spartan general Brasidas managed to persuade Acanthos, an ally of Athens on the Chalcidice peninsula, to defect from their alliance [1]. Then, the Acanthians sided with the Lacaedemonians and fought against Athens [1]. From the booty of the battles, including the battle of Lyncestis, they built a treasury in the sanctuary of Apollo at Delphi, commemorating the joint victory [1]. Plutarch in his \"Life of Lysander\" mentions the dedicatory inscription: Brasidas and the Acanthians from the Athenians [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122809", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-424'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122810", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240802", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:240803", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-422''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('a71bf02d-0df6-4b15-8436-be73a43950f4'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:a71bf02d-0df6-4b15-8436-be73a43950f4:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Roman Theatre, Tarraco', 'fab2d7f8e18a8f975fdc1b411d2fa7f6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Theatre'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 28 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86548", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2145:chunk-0001: description ''The Roman Theatre of Tarraco was a Roman theatre built in Tarraco –present-day Tarragona, Spain–, the capital of the Roman province of Hispania Tarraconensis. Constructed at the end of the 1st century BC during the reign of Augustus, it was located in the area of the local forum and the port and was used for Roman theatrical performances.[1]'' -> ''The Roman Theatre of Tarraco is a Roman theatre in the Roman colonia of Tarraco –present-day Tarragona, Spain–, capital of the Roman province of Hispania Tarraconensis [1]. Despite much of it having been destroyed during the 20th century, the remains of three fundamental parts of the structure are still visible; the cavea, the orchestra and the scaena [1]. The theatre was built during the time of Augustus at the end of the 1st century BC as part of the monumentalization of the forum of the colony [1]. The building was in use until the end of the 2nd century, at which point it ceased to function as a theater and was repurposed for other uses [1]. In the 3rd century, following a fire within the compound, new buildings were constructed in the monumental area adjacent to the theater using materials salvaged from the theater itself [1]. Today, only the first five rows of seating around the orchestra remain intact [1]. Archaeological excavations within the theater and its vicinity have unearthed significant artifacts, including capitals, friezes, columns, sculptures, and more [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158276", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/Teatre_Rom%C3%A0_de_Tarragona-4.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a71bf02d/Teatre Romà de Tarragona-1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a71bf02d/Teatre Romà de Tarragona-1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a71bf02d/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
