    ('a945d5ef-bbbf-42bd-be5b-27c25eda9df1'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:a945d5ef-bbbf-42bd-be5b-27c25eda9df1:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Archaeological Site of La Ribera de Algaida', '51abc4e6aaa38a481d77c143dcc0deaa', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86616", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2147:chunk-0001: description ''One of the most important archaeological sites in Almeria, Spain, spanning 20-30 hectares near Aguadulce and occupied from the late Copper Age through the Roman era. The settlement originated during the Argaric Bronze Age culture and later served as a Phoenician trading port. Under Rome it was known as Turaniana, cited in the Antonine Itinerary as a mansion on the road from Castile to Malacca. Discovered in 1859 and declared a Bien de Interes Cultural in 1991, it remains one of the longest continuously occupied sites in southeastern Spain.'' -> ''The archaeological site of La Ribera de Algaida or Ribera de Turaniana is located in Aguadulce (Almería), Spain and discovered in 1859 [1]. The site is one of the most important human settlements in the history of Almería, Spain, due to its size and long-term occupation [1]. It has an area of 20 to 30 hectares (49 to 74 acres), and was occupied during the late Copper Age (from the Argaric culture until the Roman Era) [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105210", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26