erving it [1]. Archaeologists have discovered large quantities of burnt flints, mounds of timbers and pits dug into the ground [1]. Wood from this era does not normally preserve well in land environments, so the quantity of wood found at Bouldnor makes the site of international importance [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105221", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: site_type ''Underwater structures'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158396", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323559", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/Bouldnor.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355950", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
