s deposited silt and mud onto the original land surface, covering and preserving it [1]. Archaeologists have discovered large quantities of burnt flints, mounds of timbers and pits dug into the ground [1]. Wood from this era does not normally preserve well in land environments, so the quantity of wood found at Bouldnor makes the site of international importance [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105221", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: site_type ''Underwater structures'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158396", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323559", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a9a32ee2/Bouldnor.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355950", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s002: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('a9a3d2fe-0f58-4627-a34d-124e0190d7e8'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:a9a3d2fe-0f58-4627-a34d-124e0190d7e8:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on El Zotz', 'dc252cb6a9c3b15dd32e04d967e39079', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 316 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2147:chunk-0001: description \"El Zotz is a Maya archaeological site in Guatemala''s Petén Basin, situated about 20 km west of Tikal and 26 km west of Uaxactun [1]. The site derives its name from the abundant bat colonies inhabiting caves in neighboring cliffs [1]. Located within San Miguel la Palotada National Park, which borders Tikal National Park, El Zotz flourished during the Classic Period [1]. The site features numerous unexcavated mounds and ruins [1].\" -> \"El Zotz is a Mesoamerican archaeological site of the pre-Columbian Maya civilization, located in the Petén Basin region around 20 kilometres west of the major center of Tikal and approximately 26 kilometres west of Uaxactun [1]. It is so called because of the large number of bats living in caves in the nearby cliffs (the original Mayan name was Pa''Chan) [1]. The apogee of El Zotz appears to have been brief, spanning about one hundred years during the later Early Classic and the early part of the Late Classic, experiencing an intense burst of construction activity including the building of palaces and pyramids [1]. A stela from Bejucal indicates that the Teotihuacan-linked general Siyaj K''ak'' was the overlord of the king of El Zotz [1]. El Zotz has at least two principal ceremonial centres [1]. The main ceremonial centre lies within the site core while the second of these is in an area known as El Diablo [1]. The architecture at the site is massive and the stonework of excellent quality [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105222", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105223", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105224", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158399", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a9a3d2fe/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241639", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241640", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241641", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: site_type None -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356151", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
