Northern Ireland [1]. The circle measures around 35 m in diameter and includes 50 or more small, upright stones, with a maximum height of 1.8 m [1]. The excavation was conducted between 20 - 27 September 1937 and 7 - 16 June 1938 by Professor Albert Giffen, a Dutch archaeologist, and Miss Mary McMurray Gaffikin, an archaeology expert from Newcastle, County Down [1]. The excavation uncovered a partially curbed long cairn 21 metres in length by 9 metres wide within the stone circle [1]. There were cists at both the east and west ends with the west end later augmented with two more chambers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105926", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105927", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158480", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ac2c74ff/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ac2c74ff/4 Ballynoe Stone Circle 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ac2c74ff/4 Ballynoe Stone Circle 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ac2c74ff/Ballynoe_(27),_September_2009.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ac3877a0-04fc-4049-b918-ebf41b0a1501'::uuid, 'antiquity', '2', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:ac3877a0-04fc-4049-b918-ebf41b0a1501:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Cerro Pátapo Ruins', 'c2737c6039d97c04280ec60c77def016', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 2 from period_start 700"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86680", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2149:chunk-0001: description ''The Cerro Pátapo ruins, also called Northern Wari ruins, are the remains of a pre-Columbian city located near present-day Chiclayo, Peru[1]. The settlement was built by the Wari (Huari) culture, which flourished from 350 CE to 1000 CE along the coast and extending into the highland regions[1]. These northern Wari ruins are distinguished from the major Wari archaeological sites found in the Ayacucho Region to the south[1].'' -> ''The Cerro Pátapo ruins or Northern Wari ruins are the remains of a pre-Columbian city near the site of present-day Chiclayo, Peru [1]. The ruins are primarily of the Wari (Huari) culture [1]. The discovery was announced on 16 December 2008 by the lead archeologist, Cesar Soriano [1]. The city was part of the Wari Empire, which ruled parts of the Andes Mountains, mostly in south-central Peru [1]. The site is remarkably well preserved due to the dry desert climate [1]. The site includes evidence of human sacrifice, with special spots set aside and a pile of bones at the bottom of a cliff [1]. Well-preserved remains have been found of one young woman [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105928", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105929", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251943", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s015: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251944", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s015: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351811", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351812", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''1'' -> ''700''"}]'::jsonb),
