ting until 1913 [1]. Apart from the petroglyphs, wall paintings, 15000 stone tool fragments and around 6000 animal bones of 60 species were unearthed and recorded [1]. Human occupation took place over a period spanning 60,000 years from the Mousterian, the Chatelperronian, the Aurignacian and into the Gravettian cultures [1]. Most animals carved on the walls of the cave are represented in pairs [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: lat ''45.016780434339054'' -> ''45.038978''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: lon ''-0.48329038780693007'' -> ''-0.50178''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122897", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122898", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-80000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159136", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-024: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/18/Entr%C3%A9e_de_Pair-non-Pair.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/af919ba9/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('afac29e1-ce20-4266-8f23-7bb05390ac64'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:afac29e1-ce20-4266-8f23-7bb05390ac64:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''9'' restored on Grotta di Cocceio', '2e830d1026a8d9e67c09aa1ed43a83ae', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Road/avenue/trackway'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 4 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86780", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2152:chunk-0001: description ''The Grotta di Cocceio is an ancient Roman tunnel dating from 38-36 BC, stretching nearly 1 km through the tuff stone of Monte Grillo [1]. It connected Lake Avernus with Cumae, linking the volcanic crater lake to the ancient Greek colony [1]. The tunnel was constructed by architect Lucius Cocceius Auctus at the command of Marcus Agrippa, who was transforming Lake Avernus into the military port known as Portus Julius [1].'' -> ''The Grotta di Cocceio is an ancient Roman tunnel nearly a kilometre in length connecting Lake Avernus with Cumae and dating from 38-36 BC [1]. It was burrowed through the tuff stone of Monte Grillo by the architect Lucius Cocceius Auctus at the command of Agrippa who was in the process of converting the Lake into a military port, the Portus Julius [1]. The tunnel was wide enough to allow the passage of two wagons [1]. The Avernus side of the passage was decorated with a colonnade and had many statues in niches hewn into the tuff walls of the entrance [1]. The tunnel is also known as the Grotta della Pace, in reference to a Spanish captain, Pietro de Pace, who made use of the tunnel in 1508–1509 to plunder the ruins of Cumae, which, at the time, still bore many rich items [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122899", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Road''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159140", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-024: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/afac29e1/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/afac29e1/Grotta_di_Cocceio_-_uscita_via_Arco_Felice_Vecchio_(2018)_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315756", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/afac29e1/Grotta_di_Cocceio_-_uscita_via_Arco_Felice_Vecchio_(2018)_01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/afac29e1/Grotta_di_Cocceio_1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356159", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''Road'' -> ''Road/avenue/trackway''"}]'::jsonb),
