 Period and was a ceremonial center on the central highlands of Peru, on the Ayacucho Valley [1]. The ceremonial center was similar to Cerro Secchin and the centers were built in a U-shape of alternating sized stones [1]. On the site there were semicircle temple structures on artificial mounds which indicates some sort of priestly figure was used [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106031", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106032", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241723", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241724", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-1200''"}]'::jsonb),
