    ('b40d492a-193f-422b-bd42-559624dd2079'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '10', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:b40d492a-193f-422b-bd42-559624dd2079:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''10'' restored on Virnamäki', '1cd81d136ecf9d027bd39c6d90b2a25a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Cemetery'', ''500 - 1000 AD'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37311", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0052:chunk-0001: description ''Virnamäki is an Iron Age hill and ancient monument area in Turku, Finland [1]. This archaeological site served as both a dwelling area and contains cremation cemeteries beneath the ground surface [1]. The location features multiple stones with cup marks and the Komosten kummut—two natural mounds with Iron Age dwelling traces [1]. A 1.5 km nature trail traverses the site, including a 250-meter cultural landscape section along the Aurajoki river [1]. The entire area is protected under the Finnish Antiquities Act (Muinaismuistolaiki) [1].'' -> ''Virnamäki is a hill and glade ancient monument area from the Iron Age in Turku, Finland [1]. In addition to having been a dwelling site, the area is also known for its cremation cemeteries under level ground and also multiple stones with cup marks [1]. The area is protected under the Finnish Antiquities Act [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122944", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:1