}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122945", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''550''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122946", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: site_type ''Monument'' -> ''Cemetery''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-025: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/Virnam%C3%A4en_muinaisj%C3%A4%C3%A4nn%C3%B6salue.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b40d492a/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b427d092-8349-4f90-b2e9-6fb6036fb3e2'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:b427d092-8349-4f90-b2e9-6fb6036fb3e2:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Sofia', 'c757ba61f39fcc5e208b535eb6b83958', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:91838", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2210:chunk-0001: description ''Sofia, the capital of Bulgaria, occupies a site with nearly 7,000 years of continuous habitation. Known as Serdica in antiquity, it was established by the Thracian Serdi tribe around the 5th century BC in the fertile Sofia Valley. Conquered by Rome in 29 BC, the city flourished as Ulpia Serdica under Emperor Trajan and received fortified walls with towers under Marcus Aurelius around 175 AD. In 311 AD Emperor Galerius issued the Edict of Serdica there, one of the first decrees ending Christian persecution. Archaeological remains including Roman streets, baths, an early Christian basilica, and 4th-6th century houses are preserved in the Serdica Metro Station complex, uncovered during construction from 2010-2012.'' -> ''Unlike most European capitals, Sofia does not straddle any large river, but is surrounded by comparatively high mountains on all sides [1]. The Neolithic village in Slatina dating to the 5th–6th millennium BC is documented [1]. Another neolithic settlement was founded in the 3rd–4th millennium BC near the site of the modern National Art Gallery, which has been the traditional centre of the city ever since [1]. The earliest tribes who settled were the Thracian Tilataei [1]. In 339 BC Philip II of Macedon destroyed and ravaged the town for the first time [1]. Serdica became part of the First Bulgarian Empire during the reign of Khan Krum in 809 [1]. The city centre contains many remains of ancient Serdica that have been excavated and are on public display, including Complex Ancient Serdica, eastern gate, western gate, city walls, thermal baths [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106126", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159912", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-025: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/Festung_Serdica_Sofia_20090405_006.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b427d092/Festung_Serdica_Sofia_20090405_006.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241773", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241774", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-7000''"}]'::jsonb),
