ns, representing nearly 500 years of continuous occupation from the 1st to the 5th century AD [1][2].'' -> ''Thibilis was a Roman and Byzantine era town in what was Numidia but is today northeast Algeria [1]. The site has extensive Roman and Byzantine ruins [1]. The numerous Latin inscriptions discovered on the site of Thibilis provided indications on the status and magistrates of this city: during the Early Empire, Thibilis was first a pagus dependent on the Cirtaian confederacy which united Cirta, Rusicade, Chullu and Milève [1]. Enjoying a certain autonomy, the city was administered by two magistri of annual mandate, assisted by one or two aediles [1]. Thibilis gained the rank of municipality headed by two duumviri between 260 and 268 which corresponds to the period estimated for the dissolution of the confederacy [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160057", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-025: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/Announa_-_Arc_de_triomphe_-_Mieusement.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b9024baf/Thibilispan01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252423", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252424", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316512", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/b9024baf/Thibilispan01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b9024baf/Announa_-_Arc_de_triomphe_-_Mieusement.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351906", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351907", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb