eing performed [1]. Between the Bouleuterion and Sibyl''s Rock in the sanctuary of Apollo in Delphi there is a narrow pass leading to the fountain which the dragon Python was supposedly guarding [1]. In front of the rocks marking the pass, a round square is formed, called Halos (literally: a threshing floor), where several rituals were taking place [1]. Among these rituals was the Septerion (Σεπτήριον), the ritual re-enactment of the murder of Python by Apollo, taking place once every eight years [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252435", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252436", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351916", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351917", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
