    ('bbde3c09-ac95-4fe7-b9d9-1be1fd6452fb'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '7', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:bbde3c09-ac95-4fe7-b9d9-1be1fd6452fb:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''5'' restored on Glevum', 'a86e6c397c40542334ea689f704f1948', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 7 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 0 content link(s), 3 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2161:chunk-0001: description ''Glevum was a Roman fort that became a colonia (a settlement for retired legionaries) in AD 97 [1]. Today, the site is occupied by modern Gloucester, the county town of Gloucestershire, England [1]. The Roman name Glevum survives in local usage, including the 26-mile Glevum Way long-distance footpath that encircles the city [1].'' -> ''Glevum was originally a Roman fort in Roman Britain that became a \"colonia\" of retired legionaries in AD 97 [1]. Today, it is known as Gloucester, in the English county of Gloucestershire [1]. In AD 97, the city was designated a colonia by the Emperor Nerva [1]. The legionaries were given farmland in the surrounding district, and could be called upon as a Roman auxiliary armed force [1]. The city was built within the legionary fortress and used the same rectilinear street plan and ramparts [1]. A large and impressive administrative basilica and forum market-place were built in the town, as well as many fine homes with mosaic floors [1]. Excavations at Gloucester\\''s New Market Hall in the 1960s showed that Romano-British occupation of the town may have continued in some form into the sub-Roman period, even if the town\\''s population may have been greatly reduced [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160663", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/bbde3c09/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316564", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/bbde3c09/Detail_of_mosaic_from_Chedworth.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
