    ('bc85d3d5-a47e-4c4d-be70-aaa1c18915d1'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:bc85d3d5-a47e-4c4d-be70-aaa1c18915d1:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''3'' restored on Crkvine, Stubline', '40ff90cb8ec7b357b65d2266361a9d30', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 5 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 0 content link(s), 1 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87128", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2162:chunk-0001: description ''Crkvine (Serbian Cyrillic: Црквине, meaning \"church ground\") is a Neolithic archaeological site in the village of Stubline, Obrenovac municipality, Belgrade, Serbia. The settlement dates to the 5th millennium BC and represents an important component of the Vinča culture, one of the most significant Neolithic cultures in Southeast Europe. Archaeological research at the site began in 1962 and continued intermittently, uncovering remains of dwellings, tools, and pottery characteristic of the Vinča culture. In 2014, the locality was officially declared a cultural monument of Serbia, recognizing its historical and archaeological significance for understanding Neolithic life in the Balkans.[1][2][3]'' -> ''Crkvine is a Neolithic locality and an archaeological site in the village of Stubline in the municipality of Obrenovac [1]. The Neolithic settlement is dated to the 5th millennium BC and was part of the Vinča culture [1]. The research of the site began in 1962 and the locality was declared a cultural monument in 2014 [1]. Crkvine is situated on a mild slope, bounded by the creeks of Izvorac and Trstenica [1]. The houses were built in rows, forming something of a street-like map [1]. Almost 50,000 whole or fragmented artifacts were found so far in Crkvine [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/bc85d3d5/Crkvine 0593.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
