014 [1]. Crkvine is situated on a mild slope, bounded by the creeks of Izvorac and Trstenica [1]. The houses were built in rows, forming something of a street-like map [1]. Almost 50,000 whole or fragmented artifacts were found so far in Crkvine [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/bc85d3d5/Crkvine 0593.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('bc89e53c-a9e6-465e-9cc9-4a6f844b9589'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:bc89e53c-a9e6-465e-9cc9-4a6f844b9589:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Lang Rongrien Rock Shelter', '1601a6b58b8a88810fb69e6a1ebe3a22', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37391", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0054:chunk-0001: description \"Lang Rongrien is a rock shelter and Hoabinhian habitation site in the upland Krabi River valley of southern Thailand, dating to 39,000–28,000 years before present [1]. Excavated in 1974 under Douglas Anderson''s direction, the site yielded rich Pleistocene archaeological finds despite some disturbance from soil collection [1][2]. Access remains difficult, requiring either a steep trail below the shelter or a narrow ridge approach from the north [1].\" -> ''The Hoabinhian hunter-gatherers who lived at the Lang Rongrien rock shelter used the site as a temporary habitation site [1]. The oldest use for the rock shelter was as a campground for hunters in the late Pleistocene epoch [1]. The excavated areas of the Lang Rongrien rock shelter have been divided into ten stratigraphic layers, or cultural deposit layers [1]. The eighth and ninth layers are similar to each other, with charcoal remains, stone artifacts and flakes, and animal bones that are scattered about among these layers [1]. The oldest pieces of charcoal found in the lower most layers where human habitation is seen have been dated to around 39,000 years ago [1]. Charcoal pieces from the upper layers have been dated to about 9,000 years ago [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106948", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-38000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/bc89e53c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/bc89e53c/Lang_Rongrien_Exterior_1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252783", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252784", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334726", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/bc89e53c/Lang_Rongrien_Exterior_1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/bc89e53c/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351924", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351925", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
