    ('be29b127-7a5f-48fe-b1f9-ad4f67fe9c55'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:be29b127-7a5f-48fe-b1f9-ad4f67fe9c55:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Marid Castle', 'ce38c5200096ed9473ccbcb13242248e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Castle/palace'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87166", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2163:chunk-0001: description ''Marid Castle is a historic military fortress in Dumat al-Jandal, Al-Jawf region, Saudi Arabia, about 50 km from Sakaka [1]. Built in the first century AD, it is among the oldest surviving castles in the Arabian Peninsula [1]. The fortress was first mentioned in the third century during Queen Zenobia\\''s campaign against Dumat al-Jandal and Tayma, when her troops were unable to capture it [1]. Legend records her remark: \"Marid has rebelled, and Ablaq has glorified\" [1]. The castle sits on a hill commanding strategic views of the surrounding desert landscape.'' -> ''Marid Castle is a historic military fortress located in the city of Dumat al-Jandal in the Al-Jawf region of Saudi Arabia, about 50 km from Sakaka [1]. The castle stands on a hill rising about 620 metres above sea level and overlooks the city of Dumat al-Jandal in the Al-Jawf region from the western side [1]. Marid Fortress is generally dated to the 1st century AD on the basis of Roman–Nabataean pottery recovered during excavations [1]. The earliest written mention of the castle dates to the third century AD, when Queen Zenobia of Palmyra is reported to have besieged Dūmat al-Jandal and Tayma without being able to capture the fortress [1]. The castle was originally rectangular in plan but is now oval in shape [1]. The castle has two storeys: the lower built in stone and the upper in mudbrick [1]. Inside the castle are two wells, and the floors contain rooms used by the garrison for guard duty, shooting positions and observation [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160739", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/Marid Castle, Dumat al-Jandal, Saudi Arabia, ca. 1st cent. CE (1).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/Marid Castle, Dumat al-Jandal, Saudi Arabia, ca. 1st cent. CE (1).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/Marid_Castle_IMG_7070.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
