a of Palmyra is reported to have besieged Dūmat al-Jandal and Tayma without being able to capture the fortress [1]. The castle was originally rectangular in plan but is now oval in shape [1]. The castle has two storeys: the lower built in stone and the upper in mudbrick [1]. Inside the castle are two wells, and the floors contain rooms used by the garrison for guard duty, shooting positions and observation [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160739", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/Marid Castle, Dumat al-Jandal, Saudi Arabia, ca. 1st cent. CE (1).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/Marid Castle, Dumat al-Jandal, Saudi Arabia, ca. 1st cent. CE (1).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/be29b127/Marid_Castle_IMG_7070.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
