 and earthworks, suggesting that all were contemporary [1]. It also manages to overlook the confluence of the rivers Lowman and Exe and the forded crossings on those rivers, which a higher position would not allow [1]. The Ordnance Survey Map of Southern Britain in the Iron Age shows Cranmore as the largest enclosure in Devon (along with Hillsborough) at over 15 acres [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106978", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252803", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252804", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351938", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('be5e8af5-aaee-4119-9572-a66ee691f455'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:be5e8af5-aaee-4119-9572-a66ee691f455:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Devil''s Lair', 'd2e784632c4299b79906accf8ad610f9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -46050"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44993", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0105:chunk-0001: description \"Devil''s Lair is a single-chamber cave of about 200 m² formed in Quaternary dune limestone on the Leeuwin‑Naturaliste Ridge, 5 km from the modern Western Australian coast[1]. The deposit reaches 660 cm depth with over 100 distinct layers intercalated with flowstone[1]. Since 1973, excavations in the cave centre have uncovered 10 trenches, with archaeological evidence—including hearths, bone, and stone artefacts—extending to 350 cm depth at layer 30[1]. The site demonstrates human habitation of Southwest Australia beginning 50,000 years before present[1].\" -> \"Devil''s Lair is a single-chamber cave with a floor area of around 200 square metres that formed in a Quaternary dune limestone of the Leeuwin–Naturaliste Ridge, 5 kilometres from the modern coastline of Western Australia [1]. Archaeological evidence for intermittent human occupation extends down about 350 centimetres to layer 30, with hearths, bone, and stone artefacts found throughout [1]. The site is named for the remains of the locally extinct Sarcophilus harrisii (Tasmanian devil), uncovered there [1]. Devil''s Lair is important as one of the earliest sites of human occupation in Australia [1]. The site boasts a rich history, occupation of the site dating back to more than 40,000 years ago [1]. Excavations at Devil''s Lair have yielded early human ornaments in the form of three ground bone beads dating to 19,000–12,700 years BP [1]. These beads were made from the limb-bones of macropods and were manufactured by cutting the bone shafts into short segments and grinding them smooth on abrasive stone [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106980", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106981", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160744", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/be5e8af5/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252805", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252806", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-46050''"}]'::jsonb),
