    ('bfcc8547-38c2-4af1-bb54-79a47c79daea'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:bfcc8547-38c2-4af1-bb54-79a47c79daea:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Basilica of Constantine', '7d2b4588887b2ed99e2581377f1630bb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Church/cathedral'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 12 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87200", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2164:chunk-0001: description ''The Aula Palatina, also called Basilica of Constantine, in Trier, Germany, is a Roman palace basilica and early Christian structure built between AD 300 and 310 during the reigns of Constantius Chlorus and Constantine the Great[1].'' -> ''The Aula Palatina, also called Basilica of Constantine, at Trier, Germany, is a Roman palace basilica and an early Christian structure built between AD 300 and 310 during the reigns of Constantius Chlorus and Constantine the Great [1]. The basilica contains the largest extant hall from classical antiquity [1]. The hall has a length of 67 m, a width of 26.05 m and a height of 33 m [1]. The Aula Palatina generally follows the standard architectural plan of earlier basilicas, with a lack of columns in the interior and an open, box-like shape [1]. It is unique in its addition of a transverse vestibule reminiscent of a narthex [1]. The basilica was made of solid brick, with black-and-white marble floors, and was equipped with a floor and wall-heating system [1]. The basilica was originally part of a palace complex and was not a free-standing building, but had other smaller buildings (such as a forehall, a vestibule and some service buildings) attached to it [1]. The outer courtyard and railings on the first and second stories of the basilica no longer exist, but overall it is remarkably well preserved [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160788", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/bfcc8547/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/bfcc8547/2017-06-03 14-26-37 ILCE-6500 DSC02094 DxO Redo PL4 (50786261297).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316635", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/bfcc8547/2017-06-03 14-26-37 ILCE-6500 DSC02094 DxO Redo PL4 (50786261297).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/bfcc8547/Trier_-_Aula_Palatina.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
