ert Way of the Ordnance Survey with no supporting evidence [1].\" -> ''The Harrow Way is another name for the \"Old Way\", an ancient trackway in the south of England, dated by archaeological finds to 600–450 BC, but probably in existence since the Stone Age [1]. The Old Way ran from Seaton in Devon to Dover [1]. The eastern part of the Harrow Way from Farnham, Surrey, later known as the Pilgrims\\'' Way, runs on or parallel to the North Downs Way National trail [1]. The Harrow Way can be traced from Rochester and alternative Channel ports on the Straits of Dover [1]. In Dorset, the Harrow Way can be traced through the villages of Halstock and Corscombe, where it is known as Common Lane [1]. At the Halstock end, a short length was realigned to form the access for a Roman villa (which was built on the site of a late Iron Age farmstead) [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c06cb387/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252827", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252828", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c070b6b0-3fd2-4d6c-acbe-105539188253'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c070b6b0-3fd2-4d6c-acbe-105539188253:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Eartham Pit, Boxgrove', '565db9563b84577a639f4302eb1bd34d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -478050"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30805", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-uk-parts: country ''United Kingdom'' -> ''England''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87234", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2165:chunk-0001: description ''Eartham Pit (Boxgrove) is a Lower Palaeolithic site in West Sussex, England, dating to approximately 480,000 years ago during the Middle Pleistocene. It contains the oldest human remains found in Britain, known as \"Boxgrove Man,\" believed to be Homo heidelbergensis. The site provides rare direct evidence of hunting and butchering activities, making it one of Europe\\''s oldest locations showing such behavior [1].'' -> ''The Boxgrove Palaeolithic site is a complex of internationally important Lower Palaeolithic archaeological sites in the former Eartham Quarry, north-east of Boxgrove in West Sussex, dating to around 480,000 years ago during the Middle Pleistocene [1]. Boxgrove is also one of the oldest sites in Europe with direct evidence of hunting and butchering by early humans [1]. The site was discovered by Andrew Woodcock and Roy Shephard-Thorn in 1974 [1]. Parts of the site complex were later excavated between 1982 and 1996 by a team led by Mark Roberts of the Institute of Archaeology, University College London [1]. The site is now some 10 kilometres inland and 35–43.5 metres above present sea level, because of later tectonic uplift of the area after the deposition of the Boxgrove site [1]. Numerous species of animals, including snails, fish, lizards, amphibians including frogs and salamanders, and 50 species of mammals have been found at the site [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107889", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107890", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-480000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c070b6b0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c070b6b0/Boxgrove_handaxe.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252830", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:332893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c070b6b0/Boxgrove_handaxe.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c070b6b0/Eartham Pit, Boxgrove.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352725", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352726", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-478050''"}]'::jsonb),
