 in the Buzeir cave [1]. Within the framework of Intas 2000 programme, European scholars such as Henry de Lumley conducted scientific research in Buzeyir cave in September-October 2002 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-70000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252831", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252832", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-3000000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c097eec0-60d9-4c1c-84f7-16e869dd5ccd'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c097eec0-60d9-4c1c-84f7-16e869dd5ccd:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Swinside', '4ee97d59bcd9fac5cfb864fe6d62c0ad', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -2900"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0105:chunk-0001: description ''Swinside (also known as Sunkenkirk and Swineshead) is a Neolithic-Bronze Age stone circle on Swinside Fell, part of Black Combe in southern Cumbria, North West England. One of approximately 1,300 stone circles in the British Isles and Brittany, it was constructed during a megalithic tradition spanning 3300 to 900 BC [1]. The ring measures about 26.8 metres (93.8 ft) in diameter [1].'' -> ''Swinside, which is also known as Sunkenkirk and Swineshead, is a stone circle lying beside Swinside Fell, part of Black Combe in southern Cumbria [1]. The stone circle at Swinside is located in the south-west corner of the Lake District in the ancient district of Millom, 5 miles north of the town of Millom [1]. The stones used in the construction of Swinside were porphyritic slate collected from the adjacent fells, and are of the type that was known locally as \"grey cobbles\" by the 20th century [1]. Swinside\\''s builders included a well defined entrance, 2.1 m wide, at the south-eastern side, which is defined by the placing of two large portal stones outside the circumference of the circle [1]. Such portal openings can also be found at Long Meg and Her Daughters, 64 km to the northeast in the Eden Valley [1]. In 1901, the Cumberland & Westmorland Antiquarian & Archaeological Society sponsored the first archaeological excavation at Swinside [1]. The excavators reported finding a lump of charcoal and a piece of decayed bone as well as some modern coins in the turf layer [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160831", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8c/Swinside_Stone_Circle_02.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c097eec0/Swinside Stone Circle 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252834", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316650", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c097eec0/Swinside Stone Circle 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c097eec0/Swinside_Stone_Circle_02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357319", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2900''"}]'::jsonb),
