-> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252852", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4501''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352736", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352737", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4501'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c22fa6c5-6691-4f76-a6fe-83ee0b7e0dbf'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c22fa6c5-6691-4f76-a6fe-83ee0b7e0dbf:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''8'' restored on Boskednan Stone Circle', 'f35bc010c6c323a5343180f98b79ca07', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -2500"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0106:chunk-0001: description ''Boskednan Stone Circle, traditionally known as the Nine Maidens, is a late Neolithic or early Bronze Age monument located 6.4 km northwest of Penzance in Cornwall, England. The circle originally comprised up to 22 granite uprights around a 69 m perimeter, of which 10 survive today -- six standing, one partially exposed, and three fallen. In 2009, archaeologists re-erected two of the fallen stones. Excavations by W. C. Borlase uncovered a cist and funerary urn nearby, dating to the early Bronze Age. The site likely served a ceremonial or ritual purpose for the megalithic communities of Penwith.'' -> ''Boskednan stone circle is a partially restored prehistoric stone circle near Boskednan, around 4 miles northwest of the town of Penzance in Cornwall [1]. The megalithic monument is traditionally known as the Nine Maidens or Nine Stones of Boskednan, although the original structure may have contained as many as 22 upright stones around its 69-metre perimeter [1]. The stones form a roughly circular shape about 22 metres across [1]. Archaeologists believe the circle originally contained around twenty-two stones placed around the edge of the ring [1]. Today ten stones survive [1]. Stone circles such as that at Boskednan, were erected in the late Neolithic or in the early Bronze Age by representatives of a Megalithic culture [1]. The first mention of the stone circle in modern times, in 1754, is found in the work Antiquities, historical and monumental, of the County of Cornwall by William Borlase [1]. William Copeland Borlase, a descendant of the earlier Borlase, conducted excavations and found a cist and a funerary urn near the stone circle, dating from the early Bronze Age [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107926", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107927", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161358", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c22fa6c5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c22fa6c5/Boskednan stone circle-2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252853", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252854", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316689", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c22fa6c5/Boskednan stone circle-2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c22fa6c5/Boskednan_stones_at_sunset_penwith.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345733", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fi