re than 600 prehistoric engravings of animals and symbols, the two galleries in the cave were crucial in the re-evaluation of the mental and technical capabilities of these prehistoric humans around the turn of the 20th century [1]. In 1979 the cave was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List as part of the Prehistoric Sites and Decorated Caves of the Vézère Valley [1]. Formed by an underground river, the cave is approximately 300 m long with an average width of 1 m [1]. Long used as a stable by local peasants who regularly found Magdalenian artifacts in the cave, the cave and its content remained unstudied by scientists for a long period [1]. It was officially discovered in September 1901 by pre-historians Denis Peyrony, Abbé Breuil, and Louis Capitan [1]. Radiocarbon dating of bones found in the cave indicate the cave was inhabited by Cro-Magnon people 13,680–11,380 years ago [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107934", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107935", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-11680'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c292f83a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c292f83a/Guide leaflet (1901) (14764048431).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242741", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242742", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-12000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316692", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c292f83a/Guide leaflet (1901) (14764048431).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c292f83a/Ent