 the Middle Mumun, some 950 years before the first state-level societies formed in Korea [1]. The settlement is dated by pottery, pit-house types, and an AMS radiocarbon date to the Late Middle Mumun Pottery Period (c. 700–550 BC) [1]. Test excavations were conducted in 1997 [1]. The site contains a megalithic cemetery with 63 burials, some of them with artifacts of high-status, 25 raised-floor buildings, including the two largest raised-floor buildings in Korean prehistory, 5 ditches, 1 palisade, and 27 pit-houses [1]. The megalithic cemetery is notable for a number of high-status burials and an interconnected series of low ‘pavement’ features made of rounded river cobbles that link the burials together [1]. Some of the artifacts excavated from the cemetery include two rare Liaoning-style bronze daggers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107966", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107967", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: site_type ''Cemetery'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161434", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c434e091/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242757", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242758", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-700''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: site_type None -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356187", "url": "remediation_change_log", 