igned north-west to south-east, and is immediately south-east of the south-western terminus of the Dorset Cursus [1]. The second barrow, a short distance along the ridge to the south-east, is also aligned north-west to south-east [1]. It is rectangular, 30 by 18 metres, and 2.4 metres high [1]. The south-eastern barrow was excavated in 1933 by C. D. Drew and Stuart Piggott, and carefully restored [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161469", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/c4ee2569/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252883", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c50a5a61-0ce6-4e28-a525-b19a21140a30'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c50a5a61-0ce6-4e28-a525-b19a21140a30:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Maen Llia', '41be259ed2211c7390138582051ace4d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 33 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81282", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2027:chunk-0001: description ''Maen Llia is a Bronze Age standing stone on moorland in Bannau Brycheiniog (Brecon Beacons) National Park, Powys, Wales. Composed of Old Red Sandstone conglomerate, it stands 3.7 m high and 2.8 m wide, with an estimated 1.2-1.8 m buried below ground. CADW dates its erection to 2300-800 BCE. The stone likely served as a waymarker along an ancient route that later became the Roman road Sarn Helen. Local legend claims it walks down to the River Llia to drink when the sun is low.'' -> ''Maen Llia is a standing stone which sits on moorland at grid reference SN924192 in the Brecon Beacons National Park in Powys [1]. The stone which is a large piece of intraformational conglomerate from the Old Red Sandstone measures 3.7 m high by 2.8 m wide by 0.9 m [1]. It is roughly diamond-shaped and is partly moss-covered [1]. It sits on a purpose made stone and earth mound [1]. It is thought to date from the Bronze Age or later Neolithic [1]. The stone is a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107993", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107994", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161470", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c50a5a61/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c50a5a61/Maen Llia (27181951346).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242770", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316747", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c50a5a61/Maen Llia (27181951346).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c50a5a61/Menhir_Brecon_Beacon_02.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
