kerton in Lincolnshire, England in 1826 [1]. The shield is now in the British Museum [1]. The bronze facings show evidence of having been reworked [1]. Originally a leather silhouette of a long-legged wild boar would have been riveted to the shield around the central dome, as indicated by small rivet holes and staining of the shield [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124172", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161484", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Witham_Shield_cutout.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5c5f2da/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
