    ('c8e0a91d-298d-40f1-aef8-f8503e44b05a'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '8', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c8e0a91d-298d-40f1-aef8-f8503e44b05a:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''6'' restored on Fen Causeway', '312af890de3c3235c552fc471e69c121', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 8 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 5 content link(s), 1 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87420", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2171:chunk-0001: description ''A Roman road crossing the Cambridgeshire and Norfolk fens, linking Ermine Street near Peterborough in the west to Denver, Norfolk in the east, spanning 39 km. The road was raised above the marshy terrain on gravel and reached widths of up to 18 metres. In places it follows the crest of natural watercourse levees, creating a sinuous course rather than the typical Roman straight alignment. First recorded by Dugdale in 1772, a cross-section of the road can be viewed at the Flag Fen archaeological site near its western end.'' -> ''Fen Causeway or the Fen Road is the modern name for a Roman road of England that runs between Denver, Norfolk in the east and Peterborough in the west [1]. Its path covers 24 miles, passing March and Eldernell before joining the major Roman north–south route Ermine Street west of modern-day Peterborough [1]. It provided a link from the north and west of England to East Anglia [1]. The road is thought to have been raised above the marshy fens using gravel, with a width of up to 60 feet [1]. Towards its western end it is close to the Bronze Age route across Flag Fen [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108064", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108065", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242806", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242807", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:343964", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-010-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/c8e0a91d/Fen Causeway underpass, Cambridge - geograph.org.uk - 5275920.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
