    ('c8ec86a6-5e59-47c9-a1be-51db69a2f0d7'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c8ec86a6-5e59-47c9-a1be-51db69a2f0d7:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Castlerigg Stone Circle', '9d9f80926d8d52f94152d4eb8783b91b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Stone circle'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 8 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45243", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0107:chunk-0001: description ''Castlerigg Stone Circle sits on a prominent hill east of Keswick in the Lake District National Park, North West England [1]. It is one of approximately 1,300 stone circles in the British Isles and Brittany, constructed during the Late Neolithic to Early Bronze Age (3200-2500 BC) as part of a megalithic tradition [1].'' -> ''Castlerigg stone circle (alternatively Keswick Carles, or Carles) is situated on a prominent hill to the east of Keswick, in the Lake District National Park, North West England [1]. The stones are glacial erratic boulders composed of volcanic rock from the Borrowdale Volcanic Group [1]. Castlerigg sits on a deposit of glacial till, and it is likely that the boulders were originally part of this deposit [1]. The stones are set in a flattened circle, measuring 32.6 metres at its widest and 29.5 metres at its narrowest [1]. The heaviest stone has been estimated to weigh around 16 tons and the tallest stone measures approximately 2.3 metres high [1]. There is a 3.3 metre wide gap in its northern edge, which may have been an entrance [1]. Castlerigg stone circle was one of the monuments included in the Ancient Monuments Protection Act 1882 [1]. It thus became one of the first scheduled monuments [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162091", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/1011362 Castlerigg stone circle St. John''s Castlerigg and Wythburn 20240526 0001.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:332941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-002: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/1011362 Castlerigg stone circle St. John''s Castlerigg and Wythburn 20240526 0001.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/Castlerigg Stone Circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
