well preserved, and engravings of great antiquity occur [1]. Engravings of both figurative and abstract styles are found throughout Quinkan country [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108731", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-25000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162111", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ef/Quinkan5.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253233", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253234", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317448", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/Quinkan5.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c9a49774-6211-499c-b80c-9dbeec95b47c'::uuid, 'total_power', '28', '27', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c9a49774-6211-499c-b80c-9dbeec95b47c:total_power', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: total_power ''27'' restored on Quinkan Rock Art', '5895872d92692cebc07495ec39cefb58', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "total_power = 28 from antiquity + fortification + cultural_influence + mystery + legacy = 10 + 2 + 10 + 5 + 1"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0107:chunk-0001: description ''Quinkan Rock Art is a significant body of Aboriginal rock art found among sandstone escarpments near Laura, Queensland. The art features unique representations of \"Quinkans\" rendered through painting and engraving techniques. Quinkan Country was inscribed on the Australian National Heritage List on 10 November 2018 [1].'' -> ''Quinkan rock art refers to a large body of locally, nationally and internationally significant Aboriginal rock art in Australia of a style characterised by their unique representations of \"Quinkans\" (an Aboriginal mythological being, often spelt \"Quinkin\"), found among the sandstone escarpments around the small town of Laura, Queensland [1]. Quinkan Country was inscribed on the Australian National Heritage List on 10 November 2018 [1]. The Australian Heritage Commission\\''s 1980 entry on the register of the national estate describes the Quinkan rock art as being located across 230,000 hectares of rugged sandstone plateaux and escarpments 4 km south east of Laura and 50 km west of Cooktown [1]. The paintings are generally large and well preserved, and engravings of great antiquity occur [1]. Engravings of both figurative and abstract styles are found throughout Quinkan country [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108731", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-25000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162111", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ef/Quinkan5.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253233", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253234", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317448", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9a49774/Quinkan5.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c9ab63ba-44f8-4e52-aec1-2e305191abf6'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:c9ab63ba-44f8-4e52-aec1-2e305191abf6:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''9'' restored on Thor''s Cave', 'f605ad127e310fed95718dddfde14c55', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0058:chunk-0001: description ''Thor\\''s Cave is a natural cavern located in the Manifold Valley of the White Peak in Staffordshire, England [1]. Situated in a steep limestone crag, the cave entrance forms a symmetrical arch 7.5 metres wide and 10 metres high, prominently visible around 80 metres above the valley floor [1]. It is classified as a karst cave and can be reached by an easy stepped path from the Manifold Way [1]. Archaeological evidence dates its use to approximately 9650 BC, making it a Mesolithic-period site [2]. A second entrance known as the \"West Window\" leads to Thor\\''s Fissure Cavern [1].'' -> \"Thor''s Cave is a natural cavern located at SK09865496 in the Manifold Valley of the White Peak in Staffordshire [1]. It is classified as a karst cave [1]. Located in a steep limestone crag, the cave entrance, a symmetrical arch 7.5 metres wide and 10 metres high, is prominently visible from the valley bottom, around 80 metres below [1]. Excavations in 1864–65 and 1927–35 found human and animal remains, stone tools, pottery, amber beads, and bronze items within Thor''s Cave and the adjacent Thor''s Fissure Caver