ads, and bronze items within Thor''s Cave and the adjacent Thor''s Fissure Cavern [1]. The caves are estimated to have contained the burial sites of at least seven people [1]. The finds suggest the cavern was occupied from the end of the Palaeolithic period, with more intensive use during the Iron Age and Roman periods [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108733", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-9650'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162112", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/Thor%27s_cave.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9ab63ba/Thor’s Cave, Wetton, Ashbourne, Staffordshire, Explore - Flickr - cattan2011.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253235", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253236", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-4501''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317451", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c9ab63ba/Thor’s Cave, Wetton, Ashbourne, Staffordshire, Explore - Flickr - cattan2011.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/c9ab63ba/Thor''s_cave.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352793", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352794", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4501'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
