 archaeological site on the hillsides of Mount Santa Trega, in the southwestern Galician municipality of A Guarda [1]. The site is strategically located overlooking the mouth of the river Miño, at 341 meters above sea level [1]. Santa Trega is a ''Castro-Roman'' settlement [1]. It was inhabited between 100 BC and 100 AD, in a period when the process of Romanisation of the northwest of the Iberian Peninsula had already begun [1]. Despite this, the construction system reflects techniques that respect the Castro tradition and has seen very little Roman influence [1]. This style is dominated by the use of circular structures [1]. Proof of human presence approximately 2,000 years before the settlement was built is confirmed by petroglyphs or rock engravings in various locations [1]. In 1862, the first recorded archaeological discovery was a bronze sculpture of Hercules found by stonemasons [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124234", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: lat ''41.90306258189035'' -> ''41.8927''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124235", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: lon ''-8.875190269054976'' -> ''-8.8698''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124236", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162115", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c9ea41a4/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9ea41a4/2014 Castro de Santa Trega. A Guarda. Galiza-17.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317457", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c9ea41a4/2014 Castro de Santa Trega. A Guarda. Galiza-17.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c9ea41a4/2014_Castro_de_Santa_Trega._Galiza.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356194", 