 theatre was deactivated, and the stones used to construct the city walls [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108752", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108753", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162148", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9c/Termas_romanas_Alto_da_Cividade.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/cab346d8/TERMAS ROMANAS DE MAXIMINOS 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242825", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317475", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/cab346d8/TERMAS ROMANAS DE MAXIMINOS 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/cab346d8/Termas_romanas_Alto_da_Cividade.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352798", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352799", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-100'' -> ''1''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('cac95409-52f9-4a26-bf59-fd7af98d054e'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:cac95409-52f9-4a26-bf59-fd7af98d054e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Anim Synagogue', '01f751f14d8523d8abe524f6c29207fd', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Religious'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87464", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2172:chunk-0001: description ''A 4th-7th century CE basilical synagogue at Horvat Anim (Khirbet Ghuwein al-Tahta) in the southern Hebron Hills, Israel. The rectangular hall measures approximately 14.5 by 8.5 metres, oriented toward Jerusalem, with hewn stone walls surviving to 3.5 metres. Excavated by Z. Ilan and Dan Urman in 1988-89, revealing preserved eastern lintels, mosaic pavement traces beneath a later stone floor, and inscription fragments. Later converted to a mosque in the early Islamic period. The site reflects the large Jewish village of Anaya during the Roman-Byzantine era.'' -> ''The site is identified with the lower of the two historical settlements known as Anim/Anaia from Biblical times and Late Antiquity and preserves the remains of the Anim Synagogue [1]. Archaeological remains of a rectangular, basilical synagogue date its main phase to the 4th–7th centuries CE, with later conversion to a mosque in the early Islamic period [1]. Excavations by Z. Ilan and Dan Urman (1988–89) reported standing hewn-stone walls to c. 3.5 m, an eastern entrance with preserved lintels, traces of a mosaic pavement beneath a later stone floor, and inscription fragments [1]. The synagogue at Lower ʽAnim is paired historically with a Byzantine-era church on the hill east of Upper ʽAnim, reflecting the Christianisation patterns of the South Hebron Hills in late antiquity [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''Religious''"}]'::jsonb),
