    ('cc7e7e8a-ad91-4001-9849-bfcd41168369'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:cc7e7e8a-ad91-4001-9849-bfcd41168369:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Slate Hill Settlement', 'a08f5ca6d3943aedfe0a7b52ace72cc3', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 286 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87506", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2173:chunk-0001: description ''Slate Hill Settlement is an Iron Age defended settlement on a hilltop near Bolam, approximately 11 km west of Morpeth in Northumberland, England. The semi-circular enclosure measures 98m by 62m and is defended by four ramparts of stone and earth, about 5 metres wide and 1.4 metres high, though the eastern ramparts have been damaged by quarrying. First constructed in the 7th-5th centuries BC, the settlement would have contained stone or timber roundhouses for a single family group with space for livestock. A quern for grinding corn was recorded at the site. It is designated as a Scheduled Monument (entry 1011834).'' -> ''Slate Hill Settlement is an archaeological site in Northumberland, England, near the village of Bolam and about 7 miles west of Morpeth [1]. The site, a defended settlement dating from the Iron Age, is a scheduled monument [1]. The site is regarded as an example of a type of defended settlement of the Iron Age, first constructed in the 7th to 5th centuries BC in the northern uplands of what is now England, sometimes located on hilltops [1]. On Slate Hill there are four concentric ramparts, terraced on the sloping hillside, in a semicircle forming on the north and west sides of an enclosure; quarrying has affected the east side where one rampart remains [1]. The ramparts, of stone and earth, are about 5 metres (16 ft) wide and 1.4 metres (4 ft 7 in) high [1]. On the south side a steep slope provides defence [1]. The enclosure within the defences is about 98 metres west to east and 62 metres north to south [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124281", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124282", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124283", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162233", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Settlement_earthworks_-_geograph.org.uk_-_387809.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/cc7e7e8a/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253251", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253252", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356198", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
