e in the Koksu River valley of historic Zhetysu, southeastern Kazakhstan [1] [2]. Located in piedmont steppes above the Zhalgyzagash River, it was occupied by transhumant pastoralists who mainly herded sheep and goats and likely used the site for winter residence [1]. Burial practices transitioned from cist graves to kurgan burials over time [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: site_type ''Residence/villa/farmhouse'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
