]. Typical of most cave art, there are no paintings of complete human figures, although there are two partial \"Venus\" figures: one within a niche or vestibule of the End Chamber, and the other on a roughly conical or dental-shaped pendant several metres away; both are composed of what appears to be a vulva attached to an incomplete pair of legs [1]. Above the pendant Venus, and in contact with it, is a bison head, which has led some to describe the composite drawing as a Minotaur [1]. There are a few panels of red ochre hand prints and hand stencils made by blowing pigment over hands pressed against the cave surface [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162873", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-029: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ce8a19e4/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ce8a19e4/Etologic horse study, Chauvet cave.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317558", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ce8a19e4/Etologic horse study, Chauvet cave.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ce8a19e4/Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ce979635-b9c3-4645-838d-a7a30da06854'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:ce979635-b9c3-4645-838d-a7a30da06854:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Broch of Culswick', '91e627f53a30fee7577d0ae89841c35c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Minaret/tower'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 13 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28676", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0178:chunk-0001: site_type ''Minaret/tower'' -> ''Fortification''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Fortification'' -> ''Minaret/tower''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87578", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2175:chunk-0001: description ''The Broch of Culswick is an unexcavated coastal Iron Age tower in the Shetland Islands, Scotland. Standing about 3 metres tall on a rock platform, it has panoramic views of Foula and Vaila islands, Fitful Head, and Fair Isle to the south. Its most distinctive feature is a massive triangular lintel stone over the entrance, which remains partly filled with rubble. Historical drawings from 1774 and 1805 show the structure survived remarkably well until those dates[1].'' -> ''The Broch of Culswick is an unexcavated coastal broch in the Shetland Islands of Scotland [1]. Much rubble has fallen into the centre [1]. This broch has a massive triangular lintel stone over the entrance, which is partly filled with rubble [1]. Drawings by Low in 1774 and Skene in 1805 reveal that the structure survived very well up to those dates [1]. The Broch of Culswick is located a kilometre west of Culswick in the parish of Sandsting [1]. It is on top of a steep, smooth knoll near cliffs and the sea [1]. The main entrance is clearly visible but debris nearly fills the passage [1]. A \"guard cell\" was visible to the right of the main entrance [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108830", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108831", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243678", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-500''"}]'::jsonb),
