s as a fortified site (acropolis) [1]. Occupation ceased in the LHIIIb period, and the acropolis was never significantly resettled after this time [1]. This gap in the occupation of the site lasted from LHIIIb until the 8th century BCE [1]. An epigram in the Anthologia Graeca concerns the offerings of childish playthings a nubile young girl dedicates to Artemis on the eve of marriage; many such tokens have been recovered from the spring at Brauron [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108840", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108841", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243682", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243683", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-5000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317567", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ced822e8/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ced822e8/Brauron-2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ceff34a3-d6a5-4d8c-8c58-4a8cc27460a5'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:ceff34a3-d6a5-4d8c-8c58-4a8cc27460a5:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Bull-Leaping Fresco', '0112c3137913022b25d4051f6635917f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (None, ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2028:chunk-0001: description ''(c. 1450-1400 BC) The Bull-Leaping Fresco is the most completely restored of several stucco relief panels originally located on the upper-story east wall of the Minoan palace at Knossos, Crete[1]. It depicts a bull-leaping scene with three figures—a bull, a leaper, and an attendant—rendered in polychrome hues including white, pale red, dark red, blue, and black[1]. The panels represent mature Minoan art, dating no earlier than MM III, and were likely destroyed during the palace’s destruction in LM II, possibly by earthquake[1].'' -> ''The Bull-Leaping Fresco is the most completely restored of several stucco panels originally sited on the upper-story portion of the east wall of the Minoan palace at Knossos in Crete [1]. It shows a bull-leaping scene [1]. Although they were frescos, they were painted on stucco relief scenes [1]. In Minoan chronology, their polychrome hues – white, pale red, dark red, blue, black – exclude them from the Early Minoan (EM) and early Middle Minoan (MM) Periods [1]. They are, in other words, instances of the \"mature art\" created no earlier than MM III [1]. The flakes of the destroyed panels fell to the ground from the upper story during the destruction of the palace, probably by earthquake, in Late Minoan (LM) II [1]. The subject is common in Minoan art, one of a number depicting the handling of bulls [1]. A proposed reconstruction by M. Cameron has four very similar scenes, each with a left-facing bull and three human figures, one upside-down over the bull\\''s back, and then one at each end, the ones at the front holding the bull\\''s horns [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: lat ''35.33874235298766'' -> ''35.29806''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: lon ''25.136955125206935'' -> ''25.16306''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124332", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1450''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Rock relief/carving'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334795", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ceff34a3/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ceff34a3/Bull leaping minoan fresco archmus Heraklion (cropped).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
