er words, instances of the \"mature art\" created no earlier than MM III [1]. The flakes of the destroyed panels fell to the ground from the upper story during the destruction of the palace, probably by earthquake, in Late Minoan (LM) II [1]. The subject is common in Minoan art, one of a number depicting the handling of bulls [1]. A proposed reconstruction by M. Cameron has four very similar scenes, each with a left-facing bull and three human figures, one upside-down over the bull\\''s back, and then one at each end, the ones at the front holding the bull\\''s horns [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: lat ''35.33874235298766'' -> ''35.29806''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: lon ''25.136955125206935'' -> ''25.16306''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124332", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1450''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Rock relief/carving'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334795", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ceff34a3/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ceff34a3/Bull leaping minoan fresco archmus Heraklion (cropped).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
