) in diameter [1]. The Cornwall and Scilly Historic Environment Record describes it as a central domed structure, containing cists and with a pit beneath, surrounded by an outer cairn also containing cists [1]. An entrance grave is located in the external side of the outer cairn [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108897", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108898", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163041", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-029: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d2db72cb/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d2db72cb/Carn Gloose aka Ballowall Barrow, St Just, Cornwall.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243715", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243716", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317627", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d2db72cb/Carn Gloose aka Ballowall Barrow, St Just, Cornwall.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d2db72cb/Ballowall Barrow, near St Just - geograph.org.uk - 660261.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('d2dd6e95-7f9a-4d6c-bd8e-a00f39d1f1f5'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:d2dd6e95-7f9a-4d6c-bd8e-a00f39d1f1f5:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''6'' restored on Allahdino', '655b201ebe742a923ac6f96a647a7530', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -2600"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81352", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2029:chunk-0001: description ''Allahdino is the smallest known Indus Valley Civilization site, a 1.4-hectare unfortified Harappan settlement located 40 km east of Karachi, Pakistan. Excavated by Walter Fairservis in 1973-1975, it dates to the Mature Harappan period (c. 2500-2000 BC) and was abandoned around 2000 BC. Finds include mud-brick houses, cattle figurines, clay carts, and evidence that cattle served as a measure of wealth and prestige.'' -> ''Allahdino is a small village belonging to the Harappan period, located 40 kilometres east of Karachi [1]. It is an unfortified settlement of 1.4 hectares, established in a coastal area of Pakistan [1]. This small but well-organised settlement was abandoned by c. 2000 BCE [1]. Several mud-brick houses, sometimes built on stone platforms were excavated from this site [1]. A large multiroomed house with a mudbrick platform was also excavated [1]. One building had three wells, with diameters of 60 cm to 90 cm [1]. Large quantities of copper objects, triangular terracotta cakes, seals, small terracotta jars with profusions of gold, silver, bronze and other ornaments were found [1]. A belt containing 36 carnelian beads was found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108899", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108900", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163042", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-029: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d2dd6e95/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243717", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243718", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352863", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352864", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354793", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354794", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-2600''"}]'::jsonb),
