 of Attalos was subsequently built over the top of its foundations [1]. Traces of the structure were revealed by American excavations in the 1950s, but were covered over shortly thereafter when the Stoa of Attalos was rebuilt [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109671", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163691", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/Athens_Agora_Law_Court_%28Square_Peristyle%29.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7a107f8/Athens Agora Law Court (Square Peristyle) 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d7a107f8/Athens Agora Law Court (Square Peristyle) 2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7a107f8/Athens_Agora_Law_Court_(Square_Peristyle).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
