 of Sylt in Schleswig-Holstein [1]. The megalithic Harhoog burial chambers were originally located near the mud-flats between Keitum and Tinnum [1]. The stones were moved to the area near the Tipkenhoog on the coast near Keitum in 1954, when Sylt Airport was under development [1]. The chambers contain parallel and transverse sections [1]. The graves at Harhoog are dated to the Neolithic and belonged to ancient settlements of the island''s Funnelbeaker culture, probably around 3000 BC [1]. Harhoog dolmen is an extended dolmen, under Ernst Sprockhoff''s six-category classification; the other five types are simple dolmen, great dolmen, passage grave, long barrows (without a burial chamber) and cist [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109678", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d7c375d0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7c375d0/Harhoog vom Tipkenhoog.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243755", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243756", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d7c375d0/Harhoog vom Tipkenhoog.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7c375d0/Megalithic_grave_Harhoog_in_Keitum,_Sylt,_Germany.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
