nt is a cairn, a burial mound constructed largely from stone, and is one of the largest known burial monuments in northern Europe [1]. In its restored form, the circular cairn measures about 75 metres across and 3.5 metres high [1]. Near its centre is a cist, a stone-built burial chamber approximately 4 metres long and 1.5 metres wide [1]. The principal cist is formed from ten upright stone slabs, eight of which are decorated with petroglyphs on the surfaces facing the burial chamber [1]. The carvings depict people, ships, birds, fish, horses, axes, circular symbols and figures playing lurs [1]. Only a small quantity of human remains survived within the principal cist because the monument had been looted before archaeological excavation [1]. Radiocarbon dating showed that the burials took place during at least three separate periods between approximately 1400 and 800 BCE [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163701", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Rock_carving_Kivik_Sweden.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7c688fd/0228Kungagraven Kivik.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318334", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d7c688fd/0228Kungagraven Kivik.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7c688fd/Rock_carving_Kivik_Sweden.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('d7e1cd9a-7861-459a-8454-5631dbbadf8b'::uuid, 'antiquity', '10', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:d7e1cd9a-7861-459a-8454-5631dbbadf8b:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Grotte de Gabillou', '9acae2c165afd60972df459d734e7b6c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 10 from period_start -3000000"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87774", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2182:chunk-0001: description ''The Grotte de Gabillou (also Grotte de las Agnelas) is a cave in Sourzac, Dordogne, Nouvelle Aquitaine, France, containing Paleolithic prehistoric ornaments[1]. Its sediments date from the Maastrichtian era[1]. The cave remains a private property[1].'' -> ''The Grotte de Gabillou also known as Grotte de las Agnelas is a cave in France in which prehistoric ornaments stemming from the Paleolithic period exist [1]. It is situated in the commune of Sourzac in the department of Dordogne [1]. The cave was discovered either in 1940 or in 1941 and subsequently its discovery was announced to the Historical and Archaeological Society of Perigord [1]. It was classified as a historic monument on the 20 July 1942 [1]. The cave is seated in the valley of the Isle river near Mussidan [1]. The length of the cave is twenty-seven meters, with slim passages of between fifty and sixty cm wide [1]. The cave contains more than 200 ornaments, fifty-six horses, twenty-one reindeers, eighteen birds, twelve bisons, eight ibex and some bears and rabbits [1]. A remarkable example is the ornament known as The Sorcerer, which is described as a horned and bearded man-like figure with a foot and leg which resembles the one of a human [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109679", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109680", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163703", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/d7e1cd9a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/d7e1cd9a/Crocuta crocuta cave art - Le Gabillou cave.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253693", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s019: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253694", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s019: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352908", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352909", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-3000000''"}]'::jsonb),
