st hominin specimen in the Central Balkans recovered through controlled excavations with firm stratigraphic context [1]. Remains in Velika Balanica make it one of the oldest localities in Europe where transition from the Lower to Middle Paleolithic is recorded [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109729", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-525000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/da2f5fea/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/da2f5fea/Balanica_BH1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302204", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''-300000''"}]'::jsonb),
