erchants, and early Christians [1]. The city began to decline in the mid-1st century AD as the emperors Claudius and Trajan expanded the port of Ostia in Latium to provide a direct gateway to the Tiber [1]. The Samnites occupied Dicaearchia in 421 BC after conquering Cumae and may have changed its name to Fistelia [1]. It enjoyed considerable political and commercial autonomy favoured by the excellent position of its port with the Campanian hinterland [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:163800", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-030: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/Amfiteatr_Flawiuszy_w_Pozzuoli.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/da488c94/Johann_Joachim_Faber_Die_Bucht_von_Pozzuoli_bei_Neapel_1829.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/da488c94/Johann_Joachim_Faber_Die_Bucht_von_Pozzuoli_bei_Neapel_1829.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/da488c94/Amfiteatr_Flawiuszy_w_Pozzuoli.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353698", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: lat ''40.84455799856999'' -> ''40.822643''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: lon ''14.093408398482643'' -> ''14.121911''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356218", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
