    ('dbd288ca-6fcc-4eaa-a346-a7b233b33955'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:dbd288ca-6fcc-4eaa-a346-a7b233b33955:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Altendorf Megalithic Tomb', '69c1fb757d5b2cf8751fdd1736d910ca', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Tomb'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 12 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2185:chunk-0001: description ''A Late Neolithic gallery grave of the Wartberg culture near Naumburg in northern Hesse, Germany, dating to c. 3400 BC. The tomb held remains of at least 250 individuals of all ages and both sexes, making it one of the most significant collective burials in Central European prehistory. Research reveals three phases: collective community burials (3250-3100 BC), a hiatus, and later single inhumations (2600-1450 BC). Finds are displayed at the Wolfhagen Country Museum and the State Museum of Kassel.'' -> ''The Altendorf tomb was an important megalithic tomb at Altenburg near Naumburg, northern Hesse, Germany [1]. It was a gallery grave belonging to the Late Neolithic Wartberg culture [1]. The tomb belongs to the Hessian-Westphalian stone cist group, which is part of the Wartberg culture [1]. About 4 m of the monument had been destroyed before systematic excavation took place in 1934 [1]. The tomb, oriented east-south-east to west-north-west was built into a rectangular pit of 17 x 3 m dimensions, with an entrance ramp at the east end [1]. The dead had been placed in the tomb over time, possibly over several centuries [1]. The bones indicated a minimum of 235-250 individuals [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125602", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: site_type ''Necropolis/tombs complex'' -> ''Tomb''"}]'::jsonb),
