o) is an archaeological site in the Pasco Region in Peru [1]. It is located in Daniel Alcides Carrión Province, Yanahuanca District, in the community of the same name [1]. The archaeological site of Astupampa is close to it [1]. The complex was built during the government of Pachakutiq Inka Yupanki [1]. Some of the most interesting buildings at Warawtampu are Inkawasi (\"Inca house\"), Warmiwasi (\"woman house\") and Phaqcha (\"waterfall\"), an altar for water ceremonies [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109782", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164316", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Edificio_Inkawasi.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dc7253ce/Sitio arqueológico Huarautambo (Inkawasi).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243796", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318412", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dc7253ce/Sitio arqueológico Huarautambo (Inkawasi).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dc7253ce/Edificio_Inkawasi.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356222", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
