 spelling Huarautambo) is an archaeological site in the Pasco Region in Peru [1]. It is located in Daniel Alcides Carrión Province, Yanahuanca District, in the community of the same name [1]. The archaeological site of Astupampa is close to it [1]. The complex was built during the government of Pachakutiq Inka Yupanki [1]. Some of the most interesting buildings at Warawtampu are Inkawasi (\"Inca house\"), Warmiwasi (\"woman house\") and Phaqcha (\"waterfall\"), an altar for water ceremonies [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109782", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164316", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Edificio_Inkawasi.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dc7253ce/Sitio arqueológico Huarautambo (Inkawasi).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243796", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: site_type None -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318412", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dc7253ce/Sitio arqueológico Huarautambo (Inkawasi).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dc7253ce/Edificio_Inkawasi.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356222", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('dc789e55-ef9b-4d3e-8a82-075427def6ea'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:dc789e55-ef9b-4d3e-8a82-075427def6ea:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''4'' restored on Acinipo', '27ff94a58a70d4ea00fd30f2d8a4e5ed', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -3000"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43665", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0079:chunk-0001: description \"Acinipo is an archaeological site in Spain''s Málaga province, about 20 km from Ronda. Settlement dates to approximately 3000 BCE, with evidence of continuous occupation through the Bronze Age (1100-750 BC). The Romans arrived in 206 BCE, and some historians believe the city was founded for veterans of Caesar''s legions after the Battle of Munda in 45 BCE [1][2][3][4]. It became a prosperous Roman municipium of the Turdetani people, minting its own coins with agricultural motifs. The 32-hectare city sat at 1,000m elevation and housed 5,000 residents in the first century AD before falling in 429 AD [5][6][7].\" -> \"Acinipo was a city about 20 kilometers from Ronda, in the Spanish province of Málaga, believed to have been founded by retired soldiers from the Roman legions more than 2,000 years ago [1]. The remaining ruins include a Roman theater still in use today [1]. It is sometimes referred to as Ronda la Vieja (Old Ronda) despite the fact that Acinipo and Arunda (the original settlement of Ronda) co-existed for centuries [1]. Some historians assert that Acinipo was created after the battle of Munda (45 BC), fought between the armies of Julius Caesar and the army of Pompey''s two sons [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109783", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109784", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dc789e55/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dc789e55/Acinipo roman theatre - panoramio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243797", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243798", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-45''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318415", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dc789e55/Acinipo roman theatre - panoramio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dc789e55/Teatroacinipo.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345736", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345737", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-45'' -> ''-3000''"}]'::jsonb),
