    ('dea9db29-e9cc-4ebc-b01b-e6f3028fbd4f'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:dea9db29-e9cc-4ebc-b01b-e6f3028fbd4f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''7'' restored on Carn Liath - Broch', '2061a0875693dbe9eb79057023107810', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Minaret/tower'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 13 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2031:chunk-0001: description ''Carn Liath (Grey Cairn) is an Iron Age broch on the eastern shore of the Scottish Highlands near Golspie, Sutherland, dating to the golden age of broch building (c. 300 BC - 200 AD). The drystone tower has an external diameter of 19 metres and stands 3 metres tall today, though it may originally have been three times that height, with a narrow entrance passage, guard cell, and internal stairway between double walls. Excavations revealed a Bronze Age cist burial predating the broch, plus Roman-era finds including a copper-alloy ingot and silver brooch from the 300s-400s AD, indicating long-distance trade contacts. The surrounding enclosure preserves a rare associated village of stone houses contemporary with the broch.'' -> ''Càrn Liath is an Iron Age broch on the eastern shore of the Scottish Highlands, near Golspie, Sutherland [1]. The broch has an external diameter of around 19 metres and an internal diameter of around 10 metres [1]. The broch was first excavated in the 19th century by the Duke of Sutherland, and was initially thought to be a burial cairn [1]. Finds included pottery, flint chips, stone hammers, mortars and pestles, querns, whorls, shale rings, long-handled bone combs, a whale bone club, a silver fibula, steatite cups and an iron blade [1]. The site was excavated again in 1986 [1]. This showed that the site was occupied in the Bronze Age, before the broch was built [1]. A Bronze Age cist burial with a food vessel was discovered [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109821", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109822", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164367", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dea9db29/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dea9db29/Scotland Carn Liath Broch 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243809", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-100''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326231", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dea9db29/Scotland Carn Liath Broch 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dea9db29/Scotland Carn Liath Broch 3.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
