lity of pottery suggests that people lived in the caves [1]. Thereafter, it was used for storage and worship [1]. The cave may have once been a shrine to a female deity - Artemis, Diktynna or perhaps Eileithyia [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254133", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254134", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353740", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353741", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-4000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('decbad37-dc89-4adf-926b-19c94a17e50f'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:decbad37-dc89-4adf-926b-19c94a17e50f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''9'' restored on Ferrier of Tannerre-en-Puisaye', 'ff3008f56183e7b81b6ab07662aa9594', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Mine/quarry'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 3 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87936", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2186:chunk-0001: description ''The ancient Ferrier of Tannerre-en-Puisaye is an iron mining and working site in Burgundy, France, dating from the Gallic and Gallo-Roman periods (7th century BC to 5th century AD) [1]. It is one of two largest ferriers in France and one of the largest in Europe, located in the Yonne department commune of Tannerre-en-Puisaye [1]. Industrial exploitation ceased when the site was designated a French Heritage monument in 1982 [1].'' -> \"The ancient ferrier of Tannerre-en-Puisaye, located in the village of Tannerre-en-Puisaye in Burgundy, France, is a historic site used for mining and working of iron [1]. The works date from the Gallic and Gallo-Roman times [1]. It is one of two largest ferriers in France and one of the largest in Europe [1]. The whole ferrier is spread over 30 ha surface [1]. Three Gallo-Roman wells have been found, each 1.20 m wide and providing 2 m3 per hour [1]. Tannerre''s ferrier, and iron extraction in the area, was active from the Iron Age up to the Middle Ages, with most production taking place during the Roman occupation [1]. In the early times the ore was picked straight from ground surface, with no digging involved [1]. Iron was produced in bloomeries made of clay, using the technique of « direct iron reduction », and forge-wrought on the spot [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109823", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164368", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/decbad37/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/decbad37/Tannerrre-ferrier-Motte-Champlay_1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254135", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254136", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318448", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/decbad37/Tannerrre-ferrier-Motte-Champlay_1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/decbad37/Tannerrre-ferrier-slag_mound_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
