e northeastern corner of the Roman forum in Plovdiv [1]. The Odeon was a rectangular building which comprised typical elements for roofed theatres like skene, orchestra and cavea [1]. The skene was two stories high and built in the Corinthian order which was typical for the period [1]. The Odeon of Philippopolis was discovered in 1988 by the archeologist Z. Dimitrov and Maya Martinova [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164373", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Odeon_plovdiv.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/df0881e1/AncientRomanOdeon-Plovdiv001.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318451", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/df0881e1/AncientRomanOdeon-Plovdiv001.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/df0881e1/Odeon_plovdiv.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
