d both within the circle and around the cairn [1]. These remains were often though not always placed in ceramic urns, and were sometimes deposited alongside other material such as flint tools, small pieces of bronze, and faience beads [1]. The antiquarian Thomas Bateman excavated at the site in 1852, and J. P. Heathcote conducted a second excavation between 1931 and 1933 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110496", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll_Tor_stone_circle,_Derbyshire.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243825", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll_Tor_stone_circle,_Derbyshire.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll tor stone circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('dfe76079-9794-4c48-beef-d80ad9728849'::uuid, 'total_power', '29', '30', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:dfe76079-9794-4c48-beef-d80ad9728849:total_power', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: total_power ''30'' restored on Doll Tor', 'a793401f03e78364a65108a5f6620181', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "total_power = 29 from antiquity + fortification + cultural_influence + mystery + legacy = 6 + 8 + 10 + 4 + 1"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42220", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0063:chunk-0001: description \"Doll Tor is a stone circle situated just west of Stanton Moor near Birchover, Derbyshire, England [1]. Built during the Late Neolithic and Early Bronze Ages, between 3300 and 900 BCE, it belongs to a widespread tradition of stone circle construction that extended across Britain, Ireland, and Brittany [1]. The purpose of such monuments remains unknown, though archaeologists speculate the stones may have represented supernatural entities for the circles'' builders [1].\" -> ''Doll Tor is a stone circle just west of Stanton Moor, near the village of Birchover, Derbyshire in the English East Midlands [1]. Doll Tor is part of a tradition of stone circle construction that spread throughout much of Britain, Ireland, and Brittany during the Late Neolithic and Early Bronze Ages [1]. With a diameter of 7 metres, Doll Tor consists of six upright main stones arranged in a circle [1]. A stone cairn had been added to the east of the circle, perhaps in a second phase of construction [1]. Excavation has revealed that the cremated human remains of several adults and children were buried both within the circle and around the cairn [1]. These remains were often though not always placed in ceramic urns, and were sometimes deposited alongside other material such as flint tools, small pieces of bronze, and faience beads [1]. The antiquarian Thomas Bateman excavated at the site in 1852, and J. P. Heathcote conducted a second excavation between 1931 and 1933 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110496", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll_Tor_stone_circle,_Derbyshire.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243825", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll_Tor_stone_circle,_Derbyshire.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll tor stone circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
