ave been about 209 by 78 feet [1]. Towards the eastern end are the remains of a chamber: a capstone, about 12 by 6 feet, leaning against two upright stones (all of limestone), which formed the false entrance portal to the mound [1]. George Scrope excavated the site from 1854 to 1855, and a report was written by John Thurnam [1]. Four burial chambers were found, three of which contained a total of twenty-six skeletons of adults and children of both sexes [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110504", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110505", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164464", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e0ffa4e7/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e0ffa4e7/Chamber at Lugbury Long Barrow as seen from the West.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243828", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-3700''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326263", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e0ffa4e7/Chamber at Lugbury Long Barrow as seen from the West.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e0ffa4e7/The chamber of Lugbury Long Barrow from the south.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
