uthern European Neanderthals who inhabited the area during the Middle Paleolithic approximately 50,000 years ago [1]. The site was declared a Cultural Asset of National Interest in 2015 [1]. The site is located 6 mi north of the city of Balaguer, Province of Lleida in northeast Spain, above the river Segre at a height of 286 m in the Pyrenees foothills [1]. Excavation probes yielded especially flint and quartzite artifacts typical of Middle Paleolithic Neanderthals [1]. In the excavation sequence, that reached a depth of 1.5 m, bones from various animals of different ecosystems that were part of the diet of Neanderthal groups were found [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110521", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-48000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164477", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/Roca_desl_Bous.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e17ba5d6/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254163", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254164", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353754", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353755", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-48050''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e180ea7b-079b-44f8-88db-128ddc3ee492'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:e180ea7b-079b-44f8-88db-128ddc3ee492:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Tiryns', '169c650c487025f31f74d63228c3b6b0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81376", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2031:chunk-0001: description \"Tiryns is a Mycenaean fortress-citadel in Argolis, Peloponnese, Greece, located 20 km south of Mycenae. Occupation dates to 4500-3000 BC, with its peak between 1400-1200 BC when it became a major Mycenaean center. Mythologically, it is linked to Heracles'' Twelve Labours. The site features massive Cyclopean walls and famous long galleries[1].\" -> ''Tiryns is a Mycenaean archaeological site in Argolis in the Peloponnese [1]. Tiryns was a hill fort with occupation ranging back seven thousand years, from before the beginning of the Bronze Age [1]. It reached its height of importance between 1400 and 1200 BC, when it became one of the most important centers of the Mycenaean world, and in particular in Argolis [1]. Its most notable features were its palace, its Cyclopean tunnels and especially its walls, which gave the city its Homeric epithet of \"mighty walled Tiryns\" [1]. In c. 1300 BC, the citadel and lower town had a population of 10,000 people covering 20–25 hectares [1]. Despite the destruction of the palace in c. 1200 BC, the city population continued to increase and by 1150 BC it had a population of 15,000 people [1]. In the post-palatial LH IIIC period (c.\\u20091180 BC), an extensive deposit of precious items, including gold and silver objects and a fifteenth-century BC Minoan signet ring, was made in a cauldron in Tiryns\\''s lower town [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125656", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-5000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164478", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/Tiryns_-_Cyclopean_masonry.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e180ea7b/Tiryns_-_Cyclopean_masonry.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
