ea was destroyed during the Third Sacred War by Philip II of Macedon in 346 BCE, but it was rebuilt during the following years in the course of the project for the reconstruction of the Phocian citadels [1]. When Pausanias visited Lilaea, in the second century, he reported seeing a theatre, an agora, and baths, with temples of Apollo and Artemis [1]. Lilaea is located near the modern namesake village of Lilaia [1]. Its walls and gates are to the east of the modern settlement [1]. The fortification of the city is evident on the hill \"Pyrgos\" or \"Palaeokastro\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164509", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2aa3754/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2aa3754/Acropolis of Lilaia 3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254177", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254178", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353758", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
