of Achnacroish on the island of Lismore, Scotland [1]. Tirefour Castle is situated on a rocky height on the east coast of the island of Lismore [1]. The broch was probably built in the late Iron Age [1]. It was inhabited during the Roman era as shown by the discovery of an enamel brooch in the foundation layer [1]. Among the finds in the broch was a decorative pin from the 8th century and a Norse pin and rivets, dating from the 11th or 12th century [1]. Tirefour Castle has an almost circular floor plan [1]. The lower floor has a solid, dry stone wall [1]. The wall is on average 3 metres high and survives to a maximum height of 4.9 metres in the southeast corner [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110553", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110554", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/91/Tirefour_Broch_20100929.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2fab8b2/DSCN3763 Tirefour Broch.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254179", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254180", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318531", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2fab8b2/DSCN3763 Tirefour Broch.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2fab8b2/Tirefour_Broch_20100929.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353763", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {