ralian clan of the Gaagudju people, of the Gunwinyguan language group [1]. More than 100,000 artefacts have been excavated, including flaked stone artefacts, ground stone axe heads, grinding stones, animal bones, shellfish remains, ground ochre, charcoal, seeds and human burials [1]. Some of these were buried more than 2.5 metres below the surface [1]. Archaeobotanical investigations have demonstrated the exploitation of plant foods, including seeds, tubers and pandanus nuts [1]. In 1973 archaeologist Johan Kamminga carried out a small-scale test pit excavation to a depth of nearly 2.5 m below surface [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110569", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110570", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-63000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254189", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254190", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353770", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-63050''"}]'::jsonb),
