), and almost on the present-day border with Scotland [1]. Archaeological excavation at Chew Green has uncovered a complex of Roman military camps consisting of a Roman fort, two fortlets, two camps and a section of Roman road [1]. The largest camp structure is a square that encloses about 17 acres with a defensive rampart and ditch [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110607", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110608", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165076", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e65caba7/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e65caba7/Chew Green Roman Fort.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254209", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254210", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:335283", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e65caba7/Chew Green Roman Fort.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e65caba7/Chew Green Roman camp - geograph.org.uk - 14252.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353779", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353780", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-800'' -> ''43''"}]'::jsonb),
