Dalam to the north-east and Wied Żembaq to the south-west [1]. The site was mostly untouched in the late 19th century, with investigations only resuming under the direction of Thomas Ashby and Temi Żammit in 1915 [1]. Ashby''s descriptions remain the principal sources of information on the rustic villa [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110614", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110615", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165083", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/39/Kaccatura_masonry_wall.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6b90e74/Kaccatura_masonry_wall.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254213", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357369", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357370", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''43'' -> ''-200''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e6e23722-1ab1-48ef-bf6f-252a0135097f'::uuid, 'mystery', '2', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:e6e23722-1ab1-48ef-bf6f-252a0135097f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Ancient City of Diana Veteranorum', 'f16eddc8c6c2f3555046a3b8a7ff0d39', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 2 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 180 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88166", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2192:chunk-0001: description \"A Roman-Berber city founded under Emperor Trajan (98-117 AD) to settle veterans of the Legio III Augusta in what is now Ain Zana, Batna Province, Algeria. It grew from a vicus to a municipium, possibly as early as Trajan''s reign. A three-arched triumphal arch erected for Emperor Macrinus in 217 AD still stands at the intersection with the cardo maximus. Other remains include a paved rectangular forum, an aqueduct, and a temple possibly dedicated to the goddess Diana.\" -> ''Diana Veteranorum was an ancient Roman-Berber city in Algeria [1]. It was located around 40 km northwest of Lambaesis and 85 km southwest of Cirta [1]. Diana Veteranorum was founded in the connection with the settling of Roman veterans of the Legio III Augusta in northern Africa under the emperor Trajan (98-117) [1]. In 164/165 AD the legate C. Maesius Picatianus issued the construction of a memorial arch for the emperors Marcus Aurelius and Lucius Verus [1]. Archeological excavations at the site have yielded a large paved rectangular forum and an aqueduct [1]. In the southeastern area, there are also the remains of a temple that may have been dedicated to the goddess Diana [1]. Two arches have been found, the larger one of which features three openings [1]. An inscription on it indicates that it was erected for the emperor Macrinus in 217 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110620", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165089", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/Arc_Diana_Veteranorum.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/Arc_Diana_Veteranorum.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/Les_deux_arcs_de_triomphe.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356232", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e6e23722-1ab1-48ef-bf6f-252a0135097f'::uuid, 'rarity_score', '28', '40', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:e6e23722-1ab1-48ef-bf6f-252a0135097f:rarity_score', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: rarity_score ''40'' restored on Ancient City of Diana Veteranorum', 'f16eddc8c6c2f3555046a3b8a7ff0d39', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "rarity_score = 28 from mystery 2, cultural_influence 10"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88166", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2192:chunk-0001: description \"A Roman-Berber city founded under Emperor Trajan (98-117 AD) to settle veterans of the Legio III Augusta in what is now Ain Zana, Batna Province, Algeria. It grew from a vicus to a municipium, possibly as early as Trajan''s reign. A three-arched triumphal arch erected for Emperor Macrinus in 217 AD still stands at the intersection with the cardo maximus. Other remains include a paved rectangular forum, an aqueduct, and a temple possibly dedicated to the goddess Diana.\" -> ''Diana Veteranorum was an ancient Roman-Berber city in Algeria [1]. It was located around 40 km northwest of Lambaesis and 85 km southwest of Cirta [1]. Diana Veteranorum was founded in the connection with the settling of Roman veterans of the Legio III Augusta in northern Africa under the emperor Trajan (98-117) [1]. In 164/165 AD the legate C. Maesius Picatianus issued the construction of a memorial arch for the emperors Marcus Aurelius and Lucius Verus [1]. Archeological excavations at the site have yielded a large paved rectangular forum and an aqueduct [1]. In the southeastern area, there are also the remains of a temple that may have been dedicated to the goddess Diana [1]. Two arches have been found, the larger one of which features three openings [1]. An inscription on it indicates that it was erected for the emperor Macrinus in 217 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110620", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''City''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165089", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/Arc_Diana_Veteranorum.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/Arc_Diana_Veteranorum.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6e23722/Les_deux_arcs_de_triomphe.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356232", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s003: site_type ''City'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
