inos in 1913 [1]. Recinos considered Kʼatepan to be the most important ceremonial site in the northern Sierra de los Cuchumatanes mountains [1]. Kʼatepan possesses 19 structures clustered in six architectural groups [1]. The main temple measures 8 by 13.5 by 2.5 metres and stands in the centre of a small plaza [1]. A substantial portion of the southeastern corner of the temple has collapsed, revealing a substructure with finely cut stonework, perhaps belonging to its stairway [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110685", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110686", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244702", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: site_type None -> ''Temple complex''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254603", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353809", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''43'' -> ''950''"}]'::jsonb),
