    ('e9f1550f-44ab-4661-b362-0abdb4f33e74'::uuid, 'total_power', '34', '33', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:e9f1550f-44ab-4661-b362-0abdb4f33e74:total_power', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: total_power ''33'' restored on Gallardet Dolmen', '2b015934c6620e3ba1eefabe98b01e65', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "total_power = 34 from antiquity + fortification + cultural_influence + mystery + legacy = 8 + 8 + 10 + 7 + 1"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88254", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2194:chunk-0001: description ''Neolithic passage grave near Le Pouget in the Herault department of Languedoc, France, and one of the largest dolmens in the region. The monument features a 12-metre-long alley within a large tumulus, with a main chamber 6 metres long by 4 metres wide covered by three capstones. The dry-stone-walled structure includes a barrel-vaulted corridor, an ante-chamber, and an oven-door-style entrance only 1 metre wide. The entire passage grave remains enclosed within its original mound, a rare state of preservation for megalithic monuments in southern France.'' -> ''Gallardet Dolmen is a dolmen near the village of Le Pouget in Languedoc [1]. It is a large tumulus, containing a 12 metre long alley [1]. The main chamber, 6 metres long by 4 metres wide, is covered by three large capstones [1]. The entrance is described as being like an \"oven door\", 2 metres high and 1 metre wide [1]. The access corridor is 5 metres long and between 1 and 1.5 metres wide [1]. The corridor leads to an outside chamber which is 2.5 metres long and the same in width [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110690", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110691", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165237", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e9f1550f/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e9f1550f/Le-pouget gallardet 02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244704", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244705", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319261", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e9f1550f/Le-pouget gallardet 02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e9f1550f/Le_Pouget_dolmen_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
