the cliffs on the north side of Mupe Bay [1]. The total enclosed area is about 110 ha [1]. The enormous enclosed area, lack of evidence of settlement in the interior, and the impossibility of effectively defending such a large perimeter, all suggest it was primarily an enclosed pasture for domesticated animals, not a strategic tribal hill fort [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254615", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254616", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353821", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353822", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
