    ('eb482c92-0104-4243-8ae6-0316f0bdec37'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:eb482c92-0104-4243-8ae6-0316f0bdec37:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Dimini', 'b4bcd767e02a87f6bc514443372a3ded', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45397", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0111:chunk-0001: description ''Dimini is a prehistoric settlement near Volos in Thessaly, Greece, with remains dating from before 4500 BC[1]. The site contains both a Neolithic settlement (5th-4th millennium BC) and a later Mycenean settlement[1]. The Neolithic area was discovered in the late 19th century and first excavated by archaeologists Christos Tsountas and Valerios Stais[1]. The settlement was the seat of the ancient municipality of Aisonia, whose name dates back to classical times[1]. Today, Dimini remains the westernmost settlement in the Volos metropolitan area[1].'' -> ''The Dimini area contains both a Mycenean settlement and a Neolithic settlement [1]. The Neolithic settlement in Dimini was discovered near the end of the 19th century and was first excavated by the archaeologists Christos Tsountas and Valerios Stais [1]. Dimini culture is well known for its abstract painted vessels [1]. Dimini ware is characteristic of the Later Neolithic period in eastern Thessaly, although it was traded and imitated outside the region and has been identified as far away as Cakran in Albania [1]. In 1977, George Chourmouziadis continued excavations at the Neolithic settlement [1]. Excavations of the Mycenean settlement in Dimini began in 1980 by V. Adrimi-Sismani [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111362", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111363", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/eb482c92/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/eb482c92/Clay_vase_with_polychrome_decoration,_Dimini,_Magnesia,_Late_or_Final_Neolithic_(5300-3300_BC).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244710", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244711", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-4800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319279", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/eb482c92/Clay_vase_with_polychrome_decoration,_Dimini,_Magnesia,_Late_or_Final_Neolithic_(5300-3300_BC).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/eb482c92/Dimini_DSC_2062a.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
