eriod right up to Late Antiquity [1]. The excavation site at the villa confirms the presence of a thriving olive oil industry on the southern end of the islands [1]. The remains rest on the highest point of a long, flat ridge stretching in an east-west direction [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111381", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165751", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Zejtun_Roman_Villa_(12682983103).jpg/400px-Zejtun_Roman_Villa_(12682983103).jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ebf816e0/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254625", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254626", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353825", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353826", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ec0a83d5-737e-48de-a79c-d709ad794e60'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:ec0a83d5-737e-48de-a79c-d709ad794e60:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Ajanta Caves', 'cced1216e83e2b7ac11569aa48fbac9d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cave Structures'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 19 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81446", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2033:chunk-0001: description ''The Ajanta Caves are 30 rock-cut Buddhist cave monuments located in Aurangabad district, Maharashtra, India, dating from the second century BCE to about 480 CE [1]. A UNESCO World Heritage Site, they contain paintings and rock-cut sculptures considered among the finest surviving examples of ancient Indian art [1]. The caves are particularly renowned for expressive paintings that convey emotions through gesture, pose and form, universally regarded as masterpieces of Buddhist religious art [1].'' -> \"The Ajanta Caves constitute ancient monasteries and worship-halls of different Buddhist traditions carved into a 75-metre wall of rock [1]. The caves also present paintings depicting the past lives and rebirths of the Buddha, pictorial tales from Aryasura''s Jatakamala, and rock-cut sculptures of Buddhist deities [1]. While vivid colours and mural wall paintings were abundant in Indian history as evidenced by historical records, Caves 1, 2, 16 and 17 of Ajanta form the largest corpus of surviving ancient Indian wall-paintings [1]. The Ajanta Caves are mentioned in the memoirs of several medieval-era Chinese Buddhist travelers [1]. The caves are located in the rocky northern wall of the U-shaped gorge of the River Waghur, in the Deccan Plateau [1]. The Ajanta Caves are generally agreed to have been made in two distinct phases; first during the 2nd century BCE to 1st century CE, and second several centuries later [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165752", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/Ajanta_Caves_130.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319294", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/Ajanta_Caves_130.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/Ajanta_(63).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
