emoirs of several medieval-era Chinese Buddhist travelers [1]. The caves are located in the rocky northern wall of the U-shaped gorge of the River Waghur, in the Deccan Plateau [1]. The Ajanta Caves are generally agreed to have been made in two distinct phases; first during the 2nd century BCE to 1st century CE, and second several centuries later [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165752", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/Ajanta_Caves_130.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319294", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/Ajanta_Caves_130.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ec0a83d5/Ajanta_(63).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
