    ('ec4f5013-86b2-45a2-af61-d69b8f863d74'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:ec4f5013-86b2-45a2-af61-d69b8f863d74:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Lagentium', '983d6e7146b8d23f88bda67553023432', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fort'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43119", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0066:chunk-0001: description ''Lagentium was a Roman auxiliary fort and civilian settlement underlying the modern town of Castleford in West Yorkshire, England, built on the south bank of the River Aire near its confluence with the River Calder. Constructed around AD 71 during the Roman conquest of the Brigantes, it sat on the major road between Lindum (Lincoln) and Eburacum (York). The site was an important manufacturing center specializing in enameled metalwork, including spoons, brooches, and water canteens -- the only known spoon-making center in the Western Roman Empire. A glass-making industry also operated there, and the fort served as a station where imperial messengers rested and changed horses.'' -> ''Lagentium or Legiolum was the Roman name for the fort and surrounding civilian settlement which was built around the year 74 by the Roman Empire [1]. The English town of Castleford, West Yorkshire, is now built on what was the fort [1]. The name Lagentium may be of Brittonic origin [1]. The Roman engineers chose Lagentium for its strongly strategic position [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84282", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26a_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Castleford_Legions_-_geograph.org.uk_-_393608.jpg'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
