the first ESR / U-Th chronology for the Cova Negra site and indicates that Neanderthals occupied this site during MIS 8–6, between 273 ± 26 ka and 146 ± 34 ka [1]. These results suggest that human occupation took place at the end of the Middle Pleistocene [1]. The site was discovered by the priest G. Viñes in 1933 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125792", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125793", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-300000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165790", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ed8ffc34/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ed8ffc34/Cova Negra (Xàtiva).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254637", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254638", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353835", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353836", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''1'' -> ''-4501''"}]'::jsonb),
