g Grooved ware and Beaker ware, stone tools, and cremated human bones. The name references the game of quoits, with local legend claiming King Arthur himself played with the capstone. The site is managed by Cadw as a scheduled ancient monument.'' -> ''Carreg Coetan Arthur is a Neolithic dolmen in Newport, Pembrokeshire, Wales [1]. Carreg Coetan Arthur dates from around 3000 BC and is the remains of a Neolithic burial chamber (also known as a quoit) [1]. The remains consist of a 4-metre-long capstone on smaller supporting rocks [1]. It would have originally been earth covered, but this has eroded away [1]. The site is managed by Cadw and it is a scheduled monument [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111427", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111428", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165832", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/eecda91b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/eecda91b/Carreg Coetan Arthur H0a.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244741", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244742", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353841", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353842", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-3650''"}]'::jsonb),
