os Dikaios [1]. The settlement of Khirokitia was situated on the slope of a hill in the valley of the Maroni River, towards the southern coast of the island about 6 km from the sea [1]. Subsistence methods practiced by its Neolithic inhabitants included farming crops like wheat, barley, lentils, peas, horse bean, and vetch, foraging olives, flax, figs, pistachios, plums, and pears, herding sheep, goats, and pigs [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165915", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f1710818/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f1710818/Khirokitia_near_Larnaca_01-2017_img7.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319398", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f1710818/Khirokitia_near_Larnaca_01-2017_img7.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f1710818/Khirokitia3.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
