ecropolis and ancient archeological site in Rabat, Morocco, located on the south side of the Bou Regreg estuary [1]. In the late 13th century the site began to be used as a dynastic necropolis for the Marinid dynasty [1]. By the mid-14th century Marinid sultans had enclosed a part of the site with a new set of walls and built a religious complex inside it to accompany their mausoleums [1]. In the 15th century the necropolis began to decline and it suffered damage over the centuries due to earthquakes and looting [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165956", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/Roman_Ruins_Zawiya_Chellah_Rabat_Nov25_A7CR_08989.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319410", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/Roman_Ruins_Zawiya_Chellah_Rabat_Nov25_A7CR_08989.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/View_of_the_Forum_with_bases_of_honorary_inscriptions_dedicated_to_the_emperors_and_the_great_magistrates_of_the_city,_Sala_Colonia_(32143204794).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
