Site since 2012[1].'' -> ''The Chellah or Shalla is a medieval fortified necropolis and ancient archeological site in Rabat, Morocco, located on the south side of the Bou Regreg estuary [1]. In the late 13th century the site began to be used as a dynastic necropolis for the Marinid dynasty [1]. By the mid-14th century Marinid sultans had enclosed a part of the site with a new set of walls and built a religious complex inside it to accompany their mausoleums [1]. In the 15th century the necropolis began to decline and it suffered damage over the centuries due to earthquakes and looting [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165956", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/Roman_Ruins_Zawiya_Chellah_Rabat_Nov25_A7CR_08989.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319410", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/Roman_Ruins_Zawiya_Chellah_Rabat_Nov25_A7CR_08989.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f2046843/View_of_the_Forum_with_bases_of_honorary_inscriptions_dedicated_to_the_emperors_and_the_great_magistrates_of_the_city,_Sala_Colonia_(32143204794).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('f23a32f2-4b00-4b17-9cfd-2f30f753276e'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:f23a32f2-4b00-4b17-9cfd-2f30f753276e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''8'' restored on Figsbury Ring', '5be30d3123cb90b83671bea2af69c15f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Earthwork'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43159", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0067:chunk-0001: description ''A multi-period earthwork enclosure on a chalk ridge northeast of Salisbury, Wiltshire, with occupation from roughly 2500 BC. The oval hillfort encloses 6.4 hectares with ramparts 18 metres wide and 3.4 metres high, surrounded by a V-shaped ditch. Within lies an earlier Neolithic henge with a flat-bottomed ditch 14 metres wide and 4.5 metres deep. The 1924 Cunnington excavation recovered animal and human bones plus Beaker and Grooved Ware pottery from the inner ditch. A late Bronze Age sword found here in 1704 is now in the Ashmolean Museum. Owned by the National Trust and designated an SSSI.'' -> ''Figsbury Ring is an 11.2 hectare biological Site of Special Scientific Interest in Wiltshire, England [1]. The earthworks of Figsbury Ring are sub-circular and enclose 6.4 hectares of grassland on a chalk ridge in Wiltshire to the north east of Salisbury, in the parish of Firsdown [1]. It is yet to be fully investigated [1]. Small portions of the site were excavated in 1924 by Ben and Maud Cunnington [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111506", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165967", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f23a32f2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f23a32f2/A juniper bush at Figsbury Ring.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319413", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f23a32f2/A juniper bush at Figsbury Ring.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f23a32f2/Figsbury_Ring_3.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
