e part of the Rhine limes [1]. Then around 70 AD, at the time of the Batava revolt, the castellum was completely burned [1]. The archeological site contains the remains of a fort, port, cemetery, and a civilian settlement [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165973", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f28a2d38/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f28a2d38/De countouren van het hoofdgebouw van Castellum Fectio in Bunnk.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('f294fd21-7428-4c73-9810-dae8ff8ee546'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '3', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:f294fd21-7428-4c73-9810-dae8ff8ee546:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: antiquity ''3'' restored on Karakabaklı', '9c0cdae9f32ff44f572f13d781622fe0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43183", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0068:chunk-0001: description ''An ancient agricultural settlement in the Taurus mountains of Cilicia, near Silifke in Mersin Province, Turkey. Founded in the Hellenistic period, it was rebuilt during the Roman and early Byzantine eras, peaking in the 5th-6th centuries. Ruins include two three-aisled basilicas, a two-storey villa with pentagonal tower, two tetrapylon gates, cisterns, and a paved limestone road connecting to the Mediterranean coast. The settlement was abandoned in the 8th century due to Arab invasions.'' -> ''Karakabaklı is an archaeological site in Mersin Province, Turkey [1]. The settlement dates back to Hellenistic age [1]. But it was rebuilt and inhabited during the Roman and early Byzantine ages [1]. It was probably abandoned during the Arab–Byzantine wars in the 7th and 8th centuries [1]. According to Professor Semavi Eyice who has studied on the ruins there are many houses and seven of them are in relatively good condition [1]. Eyice notes that the percentage of standing buildings is higher in Karakabaklı than in most other ancient settlements [1]. The plans of the houses are not standard and they probably belonged to people of different economic status [1]. There are also, basilicas, a tetrapylon, cisterns and a partially unearthed Roman road [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111516", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-300'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165974", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f294fd21/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f294fd21/Karakabaklı7.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302210", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302211", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''330''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319419", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f294fd21/Karakabaklı7.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f294fd21/Karakabaklı.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353871", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353872", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''330'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
