    ('f523b5df-b6a1-4dd9-ab12-59e22b0c7ea0'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '7', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:f523b5df-b6a1-4dd9-ab12-59e22b0c7ea0:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''5'' restored on Osiris Temple, Abydos.', '5c1a2ee82cc113c39896e652135811f3', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 7 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 0 content link(s), 20 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:45459", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0113:chunk-0001: description ''Between the First Dynasty and the Twenty-sixth Dynasty (c. 3000–1500 BC), nine or ten successive temples were built on this sacred site at Abydos[1]. The first structure was a modest rectangular enclosure measuring approximately 9.1 by 15.2 metres (30 × 50 ft), enclosed by a thin wall of unbaked mud brick[1]. A larger temple, roughly 12 metres (40 ft) square with walls about 3 metres (10 ft) thick, was later constructed incorporating one wall of the earlier structure[1]. An outer temenos wall enclosed the entire complex[1]. Abydos, located about 11 km west of the Nile in Upper Egypt, was primarily dedicated to the worship of Osiris.'' -> ''Abydos was one of the oldest cities of ancient Egypt [1]. From earliest times, Abydos was a cult centre, first of the local deity, Khentiamentiu, and from the end of the Old Kingdom, the rising cult of Osiris [1]. From the First Dynasty to the Twenty-sixth Dynasty, nine or ten temples were successively built on one site at Abydos [1]. The first was an enclosure, about 30 ft × 50 ft, enclosed by a thin wall of unbaked bricks [1]. Incorporating one wall of this first structure, the second temple of about 40 ft square was built with walls about 10 ft thick [1]. An outer temenos wall surrounded the grounds [1]. This outer wall was made wider some time around the Second or Third Dynasty [1]. The old temple entirely vanished in the Fourth Dynasty, and a smaller building was erected behind it, enclosing a wide hearth of black ashes [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:166565", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-034: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/AbydosFacade.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319452", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/f523b5df/AbydosFacade.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
