    ('f5893102-13b9-44a0-bc87-8348f7da115c'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:f5893102-13b9-44a0-bc87-8348f7da115c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Heunischenburg', '76d674e2b54644d95298aa4919f9da02', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Fortification'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 10 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0009:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30541", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81482", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2034:chunk-0001: description ''A late Urnfield period stone fortification near Kronach in Upper Franconia, Germany, with its heyday in the 9th century BC, making it the oldest known stone fortification north of the Alps. Located on a 486-metre hill spur, it likely guarded a copper and tin trading route. Finds include about 70% weapons among numerous bronzes, plus needles, razors, and arrowheads -- many undeburred, suggesting high munitions consumption during garrison operations. A wall section and gateway tower were reconstructed in 1986 and 2000.'' -> ''The Heunischenburg is a stone fortification of the late Urnfield period near the Upper Franconian town of Kronach in Germany [1]. Its heyday was in the 9th century BC, making it the oldest stone fortification north of the Alps that is known and archaeologically investigated [1]. The fort is located on a 486-metre-high hill spur of the Wolfsberg [1]. The strong, but small fort and the many weapons found distinguish the Heunischenburg clearly from the great centres of settlement of the late Bronze Age [1]. In the first period (10th century BC) the Heunischenburg was constructed as a palisaded fortification [1]. In the second period (10th century BC) the defences were reinforced with a sandstone wall that probably burned down during a battle [1]. In the third period (9th century) the Heunischenburg was expanded into a strong hillfort [1]. The archaeological dating of the site is based on numerous bronze finds, about 70% of which are weapons [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112215", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fortification''"}]'::jsonb),
