    ('f7f2dac5-0f0a-4cbd-8ac0-c2f1f42311ca'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:f7f2dac5-0f0a-4cbd-8ac0-c2f1f42311ca:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Pešturina', 'a0d2e7a1d2300ec1997d3d03f5cc0e38', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''Cave Structures'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 113 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2203:chunk-0001: description ''Pešturina is a cave in the municipality of Niška Banja in southeast Serbia, located southwest of Jelašnica and 20 km southeast of Niš [1]. Archaeological excavations began in 2006, uncovering artifacts from both the Middle and Upper Paleolithic periods [1]. The remains, identified as belonging to the Mousterian culture, have been dated to between 111,000 BP ± 5,000 and 39,000 BP ± 3,000, making Pešturina one of the latest surviving Neanderthal habitats in Europe [1][2]. The cave has been nicknamed the \"Serbian Atapuerca\" [1].'' -> ''Pešturina (Serbian: Пештурина) is a cave in the municipality of Niška Banja in southeast Serbia [1]. It is located southwest of Jelašnica and 20 km southeast of Niš [1]. Artifacts from the Middle and Upper Paleolithic periods were discovered since the archaeological excavations began in 2006 [1]. The cave is located on the hillock on the northern slopes of the Suva Planina mountain at an altitude of 330 m [1]. Pešturina is one of three caves in a row, the other two being Mala Balanica and Velika Balanica [1].''"}, {"source":