d axe [1]. A field of Mesolithic flint artifacts has been found to the north of Battlegore [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112306", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112307", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112308", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: site_type ''Barrow'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245168", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245169", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245170", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: site_type None -> ''Barrow''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('faf09f30-a927-4d6b-9fd9-14e1ab1b7c81'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:faf09f30-a927-4d6b-9fd9-14e1ab1b7c81:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''4'' restored on Pyrasus', '5b25fdba93d838fe65d14aefb24ada3f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 105 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81520", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2035:chunk-0001: description \"Pyrasus (or Pyrasos) was an ancient Greek polis of Phthiotis in Thessaly, mentioned by Homer in the Catalogue of Ships as ruled by Protesilaus [1]. The city was situated on the Pagasaean Gulf, approximately 20 stadia (3.7 km) from Phthiotic Thebes, and possessed a good harbour [1]. Homer described it as ''Πύρρασον ἀνθεμόεντα, Δήμητρος τέμενος'' (flowering Pyrasus, Demeter''s sacred grove) [1]. By Strabo''s time (early 1st century AD), the original settlement had disappeared, with the town relocated to nearby Demetrium, named after the temple of Demeter mentioned by Homer [1].\" -> ''The site of Pyrasus is within the limits of Nea Anchialos [1]. The only excavation that took place on the hill of Magoula, the ancient acropolis, southeast of Nea Anchialos, shows that the place was inhabited since the Neolithic by fishermen and farmers [1]. Stählin found a walled circuit covered by Byzantine remains near the top of the hill, and other walls similar at its foot [1]. Archaeological remains are scarce and the city is barely known in historical times [1]. An arm of a large statue, which came to light in 1965, was attributed to Demeter [1]. Possibly the most important finding is a small fragment of an old epigraph, discovered in the remains of the great Basilica D with the name Pyrasus, which confirms the location of the town [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112309", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112310", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-6000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245171", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245172", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-6000''"}]'::jsonb),
