    ('fc973357-2176-4ed3-ab9d-fdb783edb192'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:fc973357-2176-4ed3-ab9d-fdb783edb192:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''6'' restored on Castro de Borneiro', '9bc7e5092dce8d947cd7f7914991782d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 316 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81524", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2035:chunk-0001: description ''Castro de Borneiro is an Iron Age hillfort (castro) in Galicia, Spain, occupied from the 4th to the 1st century BC [1][2]. One of the most representative archaeological sites of castrexa culture, it sits just three kilometers from the sea in Cabana de Bergantiños [2]. The settlement exemplifies the Castro culture of Northern Spain, which dates as far back as the 9th century BC [1]. Recent research has uncovered evidence of bonecoal metalworking at the site, revealing specialized iron production techniques during the Iron Age [3]. This textbook example of a walled settlement has undergone several excavations and modifications to accommodate visitors [1].'' -> ''Castro de Borneiro is an archeological site in Galicia, Spain [1]. A castro is an iron-age walled settlement, or oppidum, and the site is an example of remnants of the Castro culture in Northern Spain which dates as far back as the 9th century BCE, though this site was inhabited from the 4th to the 1st century BCE [1]. Castro de Borneiro is located in Castro, which belongs to the parish of Borneiro, in the municipality of Cabana de Bergantiños [1]. The castro, which is located at an altitude of 200 m on an east-facing slope near a stream, was the first Galician castro to have been scientifically dated, using Carbon-14 dating [1]. No signs of Romanization have been found at the site [1]. After being discovered in 1924 by Isidro Parga Pondal and Pérez Bustamante, excavations began in the 1930s, led by Sebastián García-Paz, and were resumed by Jorge Juan Eiroa in the 1970s [1]. To date, a total of 36 structures have been excavated, about three quarters of the total [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:126697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s011: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:167365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-035: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/2333-Castro de Borneiro en Cabana de Bergantiños (Coruña).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:320053", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/2333-Castro de Borneiro en Cabana de Bergantiños (Coruña).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/Castro_de_borneiro_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s004: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
