stro, which belongs to the parish of Borneiro, in the municipality of Cabana de Bergantiños [1]. The castro, which is located at an altitude of 200 m on an east-facing slope near a stream, was the first Galician castro to have been scientifically dated, using Carbon-14 dating [1]. No signs of Romanization have been found at the site [1]. After being discovered in 1924 by Isidro Parga Pondal and Pérez Bustamante, excavations began in the 1930s, led by Sebastián García-Paz, and were resumed by Jorge Juan Eiroa in the 1970s [1]. To date, a total of 36 structures have been excavated, about three quarters of the total [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:126697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s011: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:167365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-035: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/2333-Castro de Borneiro en Cabana de Bergantiños (Coruña).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:320053", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/2333-Castro de Borneiro en Cabana de Bergantiños (Coruña).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/fc973357/Castro_de_borneiro_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:356365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s004: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('fc9edb4c-80d3-4046-a92b-2a0137c419cf'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:fc9edb4c-80d3-4046-a92b-2a0137c419cf:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: mystery ''5'' restored on Cheetham Close', '6326e249609997fd4906f9f058812efe', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Stone circle'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 57 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88628", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2206:chunk-0001: description ''Cheetham Close is a Neolithic to Early Bronze Age stone circle and scheduled ancient monument located in Lancashire, near the boundary with Greater Manchester, England [1]. According to an 1829 article, it was once believed to be a druidical ritual place, and a Roman road passed within 200 yards of the site [1]. The megalith was destroyed in the 1870s when a farmer from Turton sledgehammered the circle [1].'' -> ''Cheetham Close is a megalithic site and scheduled ancient monument located in Lancashire, very close to the boundary with Greater Manchester, England [1]. The megalith was in good condition until a farmer from Turton sledgehammered the circle in the 1870s [1]. The stone circle at Cheetham Close measured about 18.5 metres (61 ft) in diameter [1]. Six stones are definitely part of the circle and other smaller stones are scattered about the place [1]. The monument has been damaged, and the stones fractured [1]. The area was surveyed in 1850 by Dryden, who identified a circle of six stones [1]. In 1871 Greenhalgh identified a seventh stone and drew attention to the destruction of the site [1]. A saddle quern was found in 1954 and the site was scheduled in 1958 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112338", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112339", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:167367", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-035: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/fc9edb4c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/fc9edb4c/Not the most impressive of stone circles - geograph.org.uk - 2385288.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245182", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245183", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-2100''"}]'::jsonb),
