ke Federsee has a depth of 2 metres [1]. The basin of Lake Federsee is famous for its excavations of Stone Age and Bronze Age artifacts [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112347", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112348", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:167432", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-035: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/fd2f475b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/fd2f475b/Abendstimmung am Federsee.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255095", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255096", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354478", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354479", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-11000''"}]'::jsonb),
