    ('ff136c0c-2d3a-4621-b27b-294758b9cc4d'::uuid, 'cultural_influence', '8', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-05-rollback:ff136c0c-2d3a-4621-b27b-294758b9cc4d:cultural_influence', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-05: cultural_influence ''6'' restored on Treasury of Cyrene', '9fb4eccb36c36dcbe06b78297085d74a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "cultural_influence = 8 from description yes, thumbnail yes, 5 content link(s), 1 image(s), source_url yes"}, {"source": "production export 21200f1e3f26a29a (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 5519 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04f''s own export (2026-10-04 19:19:41.515456+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28607", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0168:chunk-0001: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Temple''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32439", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-23_mechanical-journal-reversal-2: site_type ''Temple'' -> ''Megalithic structures''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88690", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2208:chunk-0001: description ''The Treasury of Cyrene was probably the last treasury built within the sanctuary of Apollo at Delphi, dated to ca. 334-322 BC. Constructed in the Doric order with a distyle in antis design, it featured marble from Paros and Mount Pentelikon, with a roof decorated with gargoyles in alternating lion-head and tubular forms. An inscription records that the Cyreneans received the privilege of promanteia in gratitude for donating wheat during a famine. The building was oriented toward the Temple of Apollo and stood on a three-step limestone platform.'' -> ''The Treasury of Cyrene (Treasury of the Cyreneans) was a building in the sanctuary of Apollo in Delphi [1]. The Treasury of Cyrene was probably the last treasury to have been built within the sanctuary of Apollo [1]. It was oriented towards the Temple of Apollo [1]. Its date of construction is estimated at ca. 334–322 BC [1]. It was constructed at the eastern part of the precinct, supported by a base made of limestone and consisting of three steps [1]. The elevation of the treasury was made of two kinds of marble with provenance from Paros and Mount Pentelikon [1]. It was built in the Doric order, distyle in antis, with a vestibule and a cella [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:126721", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s011: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Monument''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:342959", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-008-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/ff136c0c/Treasure of Cyrene 1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
