ry of Cyrene was probably the last treasury to have been built within the sanctuary of Apollo [1]. It was oriented towards the Temple of Apollo [1]. Its date of construction is estimated at ca. 334–322 BC [1]. It was constructed at the eastern part of the precinct, supported by a base made of limestone and consisting of three steps [1]. The elevation of the treasury was made of two kinds of marble with provenance from Paros and Mount Pentelikon [1]. It was built in the Doric order, distyle in antis, with a vestibule and a cella [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:126721", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s011: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Monument''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:342959", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-008-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/ff136c0c/Treasure of Cyrene 1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
